1468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000],"start":"2026-10-08T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall Gallery","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to challenge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynamics, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each piece is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by Danielle Colle. \n\nAbout the Artist\nDanielle Cole is a Toronto-based artist whose collages, composed of vintage graphics, examine domestic roles and consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and featured in CBC Arts, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":null,"image":"VcFllYw-QNwjEH_CMAZzTA","website":"https://daniellecole.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"5757e741-816e-4790-b342-1d410b43a152","name":"Held by Anne Michaels - By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1796774400000],"start":"2026-12-08T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-08T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Held, by 2024 Scotiabank Giller Prize winner Anne Michaels, is a luminous, fragmented novel about love, memory, and the reverberations of war across generations. Beginning on a First World War battlefield, the narrative moves through time and place to explore how desire and grief endure beyond a single lifetime. Michaels – renowned poet and author of Fugitive Pieces—weaves history and intimacy into a work of haunting beauty.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readings, discussions, Q&A, book signings and ASL interpretation, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.\n","categories":["Literary"],"presenter":"City of Toronto","image":"yFdcXkah7XICEeFv7n5Q3A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/216644f0-d05b-410f-a0d0-be3b766b93a8"},{"id":"d1cadd10-a7c4-4d8a-a8c1-8ff10676b23a","name":"Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition","dates":[1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000],"start":"2026-10-08T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall Gallery","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to challenge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynamics, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each piece is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by Danielle Colle. \n\nAbout the Artist\nDanielle Cole is a Toronto-based artist whose collages, composed of vintage graphics, examine domestic roles and consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and featured in CBC Arts, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":null,"image":"VcFllYw-QNwjEH_CMAZzTA","website":"https://daniellecole.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"87eea263-f6fe-4ba1-affb-1062b47334e0","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1779526800000,1780131600000,1780736400000,1781341200000,1781946000000,1782550800000,1783155600000,1783760400000,1784365200000,1784970000000,1785574800000,1786179600000,1786784400000,1787389200000,1787994000000,1788598800000,1789203600000,1789808400000,1790413200000,1791018000000,1791622800000,1792227600000,1792832400000,1793437200000,1794045600000,1794650400000,1795255200000,1795860000000,1796464800000,1797069600000,1797674400000,1798279200000,1798884000000],"start":"2026-05-23T05:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T05:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"St. Lawrence North Market","address":"92 Front St E, Toronto","lat":43.649145,"lng":-79.371526},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visit the Saturday Farmers' Market in the newly redeveloped St. Lawrence Market North building. Discover seasonal produce, baked goods, meats, cheeses, flowers and pantry staples from local vendors all under one roof.","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"a0PsB9WOlmzpz_7ENsYW_A","website":"https://www.stlawrencemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"0db67576-30ee-4429-813f-ea16af7ee2b7","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1779526800000,1780131600000,1780736400000,1781341200000,1781946000000,1782550800000,1783155600000,1783760400000,1784365200000,1784970000000,1785574800000,1786179600000,1786784400000,1787389200000,1787994000000,1788598800000,1789203600000,1789808400000,1790413200000,1791018000000,1791622800000,1792227600000,1792832400000,1793437200000,1794045600000,1794650400000,17952