ronto 2026","dates":[1794668400000],"start":"2026-11-14T10:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-14T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"North York Memorial Community Hall","address":"5110 Yonge Street North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.759875,"lng":-79.411926},"free":false,"low":40,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFree admission to the SignFest Toronto Expo (10:00 AM–5:00 PM). \nThe evening performance featuring SignMark – Final Canada Tour \"One Last Time\" requires a $40 General Admission ticket. ","description":"This is a free public festival celebrating Deaf culture, sign language, accessibility, and inclusion. \n\nThe festival features a free daytime expo with vendors, exhibitors, organizations, presentations, entertainment, and networking opportunities.\n\nIn the evening, internationally acclaimed Deaf rapper and performer SignMark from Finland will perform his Final Canada Tour – \"One Last Time.\" \n\nJoin us for a full day of connection, learning, and celebration in Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":" DEAFest Toronto Inc.","image":null,"website":null,"tickets":"https://signmark2026.eventbrite.ca"},{"id":"51dc73d2-eae3-49fa-ad65-fc700398ae24","name":"Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition","dates":[1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000],"start":"2026-10-08T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall Gallery","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to challenge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynamics, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each piece is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by Danielle Colle. \n\nAbout the Artist\nDanielle Cole is a Toronto-based artist whose collages, composed of vintage graphics, examine domestic roles and consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and featured in CBC Arts, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":null,"image":"VcFllYw-QNwjEH_CMAZzTA","website":"https://daniellecole.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"d425cc8f-0061-488a-b484-fe4dd9081bf9","name":"Disney and Pixar's Finding Nemo","dates":[1795737600000,1795888800000,1795968000000,1795978800000,1796493600000,1796504400000,1796536800000,1797098400000,1797109200000,1797177600000,1797188400000,1797703200000,1797714000000,1797789600000,1797800400000,1797876000000,1797886800000,1797962400000,1797973200000,1798048800000,1798059600000],"start":"2026-11-26T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T16:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Young People's Theatre","address":"165 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5A 3Z4","lat":43.6499984416,"lng":-79.3687420725},"free":false,"low":17,"high":67,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Make your holidays merry with an enchanting family adventure! This splashy musical adaptation of the beloved Pixar film celebrates the love between parents and children in a vivid underwater world.\n\nWhen Nemo, a spirited clownfish with a “lucky fin\" is captured by a diver, his cautious father, Marlin, embarks on an epic rescue mission across the ocean. Guided by the hilariously forgetful Dory, the laid-back sea turtle Crush, and the supportive Tank Gang, father and son must discover the hero within themselves as they navigate the deep to find one another.\n\nBubbling with laughs, toe-tapping songs, and beautiful larger-than-life puppets, Finding Nemo is a joyful musical journey to celebrate the season together.\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances"],"presenter":"Music Theatre International","image":"9Meg9fUkr4hj-hkhVmAA2g","website":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/finding-nemo/","tickets":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/finding-nemo/"},{"id":"f43cf943-5452-43d5-be1d-7db19a51dc5a","name":"Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition","dates":[1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000],"start":"2026-10-08T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall Gallery","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to challenge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynamics, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each piece is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by Danielle Colle. \n\nAbout the Artist\nDanielle Cole is a Toronto-based artist whose collages, composed of vintage graphics, examine domestic roles and consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and featured in CBC Arts, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":null,"image":"VcFllYw-QNwjEH_CMAZzTA","website":"https://daniellecole.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"e1c1f51c-fcc4-48ea-840c-0889dc8e27df","name":"Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition","dates":[1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,17918136