site":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/third-tuesday-nights-free?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=ttnf&utm_content=tourism","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/third-tuesday-nights-free?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=ttnf&utm_content=tourism"},{"id":"95086932-d155-42e2-ae09-2e01735f597e","name":"Teddy Swims: The UGLY Tour","dates":[1791237600000],"start":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Scotiabank Arena","address":"40 Bay St., Toronto, ON M5J 3A5, Canada","lat":43.643518,"lng":-79.379092},"free":false,"low":215,"high":700,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Live at Scotiabank Arena, with special guests \"St. Paul & The Broken Bones and MarcLo\".\n\nTickets on sale now!","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Tour"],"presenter":"AEG Presents ","image":"_6z5BKQxaprohTMfwy_DbQ","website":"https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event/1000648D929F6B7D?utm_medium=affiliate&irgwc=1&afsrc=1&clickid=X21T88UHwxyZTqrS9F3yBySvUkuXM3zvIzLjVQ0&camefrom=CFC_BUYAT_219208&impradid=219208&REFERRAL_ID=tmfeedbuyat219208&wt.mc_id=aff_BUYAT_219208&utm_source=219208-Bandsintown&impradname=Bandsintown&ircid=4272","tickets":null},{"id":"208d1710-09b9-4354-8577-5c096f6625b8","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"610d156e-5b41-4633-9974-6133714e3142","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"4b49eb40-d8ee-49d7-84af-829fc6530a41","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall h