00,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000],"start":"2026-08-06T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Ascent Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visual perceptions of the human gaze are analysed in this dual exhibit created by James Rose and Emmanuel Udeh. Rose depicts various forms of body modification to demonstrate how physical changes can have a sacred, transformative, spiritual effect that exceeds the body’s limitation. Udeh creates technically skilled, conceptually grounded drawings that balance realism with imagination; quiet yet powerful visual meditations explore what it means to watch and be watched.\n\nReception: August 15, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"aT6_lLHg3nQFe3YvB7TNHQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"fb6f2b0e-f094-404e-b16b-13762b5a9cf7","name":"Held by Anne Michaels - By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1796774400000],"start":"2026-12-08T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-08T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Held, by 2024 Scotiabank Giller Prize winner Anne Michaels, is a luminous, fragmented novel about love, memory, and the reverberations of war across generations. Beginning on a First World War battlefield, the narrative moves through time and place to explore how desire and grief endure beyond a single lifetime. Michaels – renowned poet and author of Fugitive Pieces—weaves history and intimacy into a work of haunting beauty.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readings, discussions, Q&A, book signings and ASL interpretation, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.\n","categories":["Literary"],"presenter":"City of Toronto","image":"yFdcXkah7XICEeFv7n5Q3A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/216644f0-d05b-410f-a0d0-be3b766b93a8"},{"id":"5ce4b493-aeae-4480-b50b-af09b28a0f86","name":"Ritual / Still Without Shelter","dates":[1786017600000,1786104000000,1786197600000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786802400000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787407200000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788012000000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000],"start"