":null,"description":"Celebrate emerging voices in art at this annual exhibition, developed in partnership between the City of Toronto and Humber Polytechnic’s Arts Administration & Cultural Management Program. Showcasing early-career artists with focus on IBPOC, persons with disabilities, and 2SLGBTQIAS+, New Vistas highlights bold, fresh perspectives. Witness the creativity shaping the next generation of artists and arts leaders.\n\nReception: December 5, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"prQfzbnWAAkE_8xLZf6hbw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"de7fd87e-1092-418d-882f-1e6d304b94e9","name":"First Wednesday Night Free at the AGO","dates":[1770246000000,1772665200000,1775080800000,1778104800000,1780524000000,1783548000000,1785967200000,1788386400000,1791410400000,1793833200000,1796252400000],"start":"2026-02-04T18:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-02T18:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Art Gallery of Ontario","address":"317 Dundas St W, Toronto, ON, M5T 1G4","lat":43.653511557,"lng":-79.392569777},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTickets for the free general admission must be booked online in advance. They will be released at 10 a.m. the Monday prior to the first Wednesday of the month. Maximum of two tickets may be booked at a time. \nAll visitors including children in strollers require a ticket.","description":"Enjoy the galleries at night.\n\nPlease dress for the weather as the queue for entrance begins outside the AGO. Pack light as wait times for coat check may be longer than usual. Bags larger than a small purse, including backpacks and totes must be left at coat check for a fee. Please refrain from bringing oversized bags. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":null,"image":"bep_Lj3fURjoKwv1k-WPDQ","website":"https://ago.ca/visit/free-wednesday-nights","tickets":"https://visit.ago.ca/?_ga=2.250807618.598114334.1768831088-454920034.1768575201"},{"id":"b02e93da-0676-4cf4-8304-061a4b519b49","name":"Ritual / Still Without Shelter","dates":[1786017600000,1786104000000,1786197600000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786802400000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787407200000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788012000000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000],"start":"2026-08-06T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Ascent Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visual perceptions of the human gaze are analysed in this dual exhibit created by James Rose and Emmanuel Udeh. Rose depicts various forms of body modification to demonstrate how physical changes can have a sacred, transformative, spiritual effect that exceeds the body’s limitation. Udeh creates technically skilled, conceptually grounded drawings that balance realism with imagination; quiet yet powerful visual meditations explore what it means to watch and be watched.\n\nReception: August 15, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"aT6_lLHg3nQFe3YvB7TNHQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"244b6c8b-0722-4a76-913b-aee9ec99c999","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"e0f75fdb-21c6-42d6-abd9-4afb7cf3440d","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"43882940-a892-4b27-bf59-cee1f484921b","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting there is easy with the free shuttle bus picking up next to Broadview Station or take the TTC's 28 bus from Davisville Station.\n\nThe farmers' market is operated by Evergreen, a national non-profit transforming public spaces in our cities to build a healthier future for people and our planet.","categories":["Environmental","Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"g_7hN7bS9geSUWTPQPVycA","website":"https://www.evergreen.ca/evergreen-brick-w