/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"238812b4-7125-41fc-9151-2a7cfbffac46","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"ec15ddfc-c777-47c2-b642-618e15f6694b","name":"Jazz at the Columbus Centre","dates":[1777591800000,1780011000000,1789169400000,1793316600000,1796344200000],"start":"2026-04-30T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-03T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Joseph D. Carrier Art Gallery","address":"901 Lawrence Ave W, North York, ON, M6A 1C3","lat":43.713005,"lng":-79.456742},"free":false,"low":100,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the richness, diversity and enduring appeal of jazz.\n\nBack by popular demand, enjoy ive unforgettable concerts celebrating the richness, diversity, and enduring appeal of jazz. This curated series brings together outstanding Canadian musicians and vocalists to explore iconic recordings, global jazz influences, beloved composers, and seasonal favourites, all presented in an intimate and elegant concert setting.\n\nFrom jazz’s greatest hits and Brazilian bossa nova to the timeless music of George Gershwin, festive holiday swing, and Italian classics reimagined, this series invites audiences to discover the music they love, performed with artistry, imagination, and style.\n\nWhether you’re a devoted jazz fan or a curious first‑time listener, this series offers a welcoming and richly rewarding journey through the sound, history, and spirit of jazz.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre","tickets":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre"},{"id":"3f6c227b-9941-4738-b280-28e15a975f79","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"75b55c80-de82-4418-8f2c-ef976032ecc2","name":"Jack Goodlad Park  - 2:30 to 4:30 p.m.","dates":[1791138600000],"start":"2026-10-04T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Jack Goodlad Park","address":"929 Kennedy Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1K 0B2","lat":43.742303233,"lng":-79.271036705},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels, no registration or reservations are required to participate. The new soccer Play Mobile is dedicated to the world’s most popular game. All ages are invited to learn and celebrate soccer in a fun, supportive environment with no experience required.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"D-JBEvzzMMBRxdflGESP0g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=633","tickets":null},{"id":"9fd82124-48b5-4479-bb22-cfd23b9049bc","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"2aca7aa9-3e87-4ccc-bb19-f49c658786d6","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"9e551f54-722f-4f35-9cbb-5bfa97dc6163","name":"Jazz at the Columbus Centre","dates":[1777591800000,1780011000000,1789169400000,1793316600000,1796344200000],"start":"2026-04-30T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-03T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Joseph D. Carrier Art Gallery","address":"901 Lawrence Ave W, North York, ON, M6A 1C3","lat":43.713005,"lng":-79.456742},"free":false,"low":100,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the richness, diversity and enduring appeal of jazz.\n\nBack by popular demand, enjoy ive unforgettable concerts celebrating the richness, diversity, and enduring appeal of jazz. This curated series brings together outstanding Canadian musicians and vocalists to explore iconic recordings, global jazz influences, beloved composers, and seasonal favourites, all presented in an intimate and elegant concert setting.\n\nFrom jazz’s greatest hits and Brazilian bossa nova to the timeless music of George Gershwin, festive holiday swing, and Italian classics reimagined, this series invites audiences to discover the music they love, performed with artistry, imagination, and style.\n\nWhether you’re a devoted jazz fan or a curious first‑time listener, this series offers a welcoming and richly rewarding journey through the sound, history, and spirit of jazz.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre","tickets":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre"},{"id":"9c4f38e2-d8d1-4056-be0c-44bafaea0c44","name":"74th Open Juried Exhibit","dates":[1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000],"start":"2026-10-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Colour and Form Society presents an exhibit opportunity for their artists to showcase a myriad of talent, and for non-members to be juried into membership of the organization.  The Colour and Form Society was established in 1952 and has played a significant role in the cultural mosaic of Canada—promoting diversity, creative freedom, and independence in art.\n\nReception: November 1, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7mEc5fM1FmfuHLkEV5ODug","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"9d204147-cefa-443f-8db5-e8c3da28d3d0","name":"74th Open Juried Exhibit","dates":[1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000],"start":"2026-10-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Colour and Form Society presents an exhibit opportunity for their artists to showcase a myriad of talent, and for non-members to be juried into membership of the organization.  The Colour and Form Society was established in 1952 and has played a significant role in the cultural mosaic of Canada—promoting diversity, creative freedom, and independence in art.\n\nReception: November 1, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7mEc5fM1FmfuHLkEV5ODug","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"732054ce-808d-4c8c-acc2-cd8beaef695c","name":"Ritual / Still Without Shelter","dates":[1786017600000