410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"902028b5-7b81-4da0-8fbb-7fec352594eb","name":"Jazz at the Columbus Centre","dates":[1777591800000,1780011000000,1789169400000,1793316600000,1796344200000],"start":"2026-04-30T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-03T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Joseph D. Carrier Art Gallery","address":"901 Lawrence Ave W, North York, ON, M6A 1C3","lat":43.713005,"lng":-79.456742},"free":false,"low":100,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the richness, diversity and enduring appeal of jazz.\n\nBack by popular demand, enjoy ive unforgettable concerts celebrating the richness, diversity, and enduring appeal of jazz. This curated series brings together outstanding Canadian musicians and vocalists to explore iconic recordings, global jazz influences, beloved composers, and seasonal favourites, all presented in an intimate and elegant concert setting.\n\nFrom jazz’s greatest hits and Brazilian bossa nova to the timeless music of George Gershwin, festive holiday swing, and Italian classics reimagined, this series invites audiences to discover the music they love, performed with artistry, imagination, and style.\n\nWhether you’re a devoted jazz fan or a curious first‑time listener, this series offers a welcoming and richly rewarding journey through the sound, history, and spirit of jazz.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre","tickets":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre"},{"id":"6113bbc9-223f-4dea-ad55-0513383fa412","name":"Jazz at the Columbus Centre","dates":[1777591800000,1780011000000,1789169400000,1793316600000,1796344200000],"start":"2026-04-30T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-03T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Joseph D. Carrier Art Gallery","address":"901 Lawrence Ave W, North York, ON, M6A 1C3","lat":43.713005,"lng":-79.456742},"free":false,"low":100,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the richness, diversity and enduring appeal of jazz.\n\nBack by popular demand, enjoy ive unforgettable concerts celebrating the richness, diversity, and enduring appeal of jazz. This curated series brings together outstanding Canadian musicians and vocalists to explore iconic recordings, global jazz influences, beloved composers, and seasonal favourites, all presented in an intimate and elegant concert setting.\n\nFrom jazz’s greatest hits and Brazilian bossa nova to the timeless music of George Gershwin, festive holiday swing, and Italian classics reimagined, this series invites audiences to discover the music they love, performed with artistry, imagination, and style.\n\nWhether you’re a devoted jazz fan or a curious first‑time listener, this series offers a welcoming and richly rewarding journey through the sound, history, and spirit of jazz.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre","tickets":"https://www.villacharities.com/culture-heritage/cultural-programming/new-cultural-events/#Jazz-at-the-Columbus-Centre"},{"id":"6ad3aa1e-2dde-4459-a117-b7be3cb9cf2b","name":"Sketch Party","dates":[1769904000000,1771718400000,1774738800000,1777158000000,1779577200000,1781996400000,1784415600000,1786834800000,1789254000000,1792278000000,1795305600000,1797724800000],"start":"2026-01-31T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-19T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Comedy Bar","address":"945 Bloor Street W, Toronto, ON, M6H 1L5","lat":43.66148,"lng":-79.428242},"free":false,"low":23,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each month we're partying HARD and bringing the best sketch comedy this city has to offer, from the hottest up and coming troupes to long time fan favourite troupes and solo acts.\n\nGet ready for a wild night of expecting the unexpected and, of course, sketch comedy. Bring your best party trick and enjoy the vibes. There ain't no party like a S-KETCH PARTY!\n\nYou won’t want to miss this monthly shindig, come party-hardy with us!","categories":["Comedy"],"presenter":null,"image":"IoEFS6qmP2peTL7SwyQW_w","website":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/sketch-party","tickets":null},{"id":"5bf72ab2-1ad4-4088-a614-389055b51441","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"cf71de1e-ef52-4532-94bc-b6f930b8ddf2","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"e7b0ebcb-8060-4605-bc47-218aa4cbbdb2","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"4cf354c4-e1a0-4831-9fc6-26ab0a1e427f","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"e54805db-3ca2-49ad-8d78-5f8ecf9f5005","name":"A Spore on its Journey","dates":[1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,17