ings that balance realism with imagination; quiet yet powerful visual meditations explore what it means to watch and be watched.\n\nReception: August 15, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"aT6_lLHg3nQFe3YvB7TNHQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"3b277951-4c4c-4be6-9687-2dd195f855d5","name":"Ritual / Still Without Shelter","dates":[1786017600000,1786104000000,1786197600000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786802400000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787407200000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788012000000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000],"start":"2026-08-06T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Ascent Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visual perceptions of the human gaze are analysed in this dual exhibit created by James Rose and Emmanuel Udeh. Rose depicts various forms of body modification to demonstrate how physical changes can have a sacred, transformative, spiritual effect that exceeds the body’s limitation. Udeh creates technically skilled, conceptually grounded drawings that balance realism with imagination; quiet yet powerful visual meditations explore what it means to watch and be watched.\n\nReception: August 15, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"aT6_lLHg3nQFe3YvB7TNHQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"5d77bd45-15af-4dfd-a624-7841ef0320b2","name":"The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus by Emma Knight - By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1791327600000],"start":"2026-10-06T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus, by Emma Knight, shortlisted for the 2025 Scotiabank Giller Prize, is a spellbinding debut about friendship, motherhood, first love and the secrets that shape us. Set against the moody backdrop of Edinburgh, the novel follows Pen, a Canadian student unraveling a family mystery while navigating independence and desire. With wit and emotional depth, Knight explores womanhood and the choices that bind us.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readings, discussions, Q&A, book signings and ASL interpretation, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.","categories":["Literary"],"presenter":"City of Toronto","image":"1JKHhOM-wZcXUs7CD2kXfg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4c24b080-834a-499a-8d4f-4dd578c9d279"},{"id":"cb90d913-46c7-4646-a679-264f66c0db55","name":"Ritual / Still Without Shelter","dates":[1786017600000,1786104000000,1786197600000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786802400000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787407200000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788012000000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000],"start":"2026-08-06T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Ascent Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visual perceptions of the human gaze are analysed in this dual exhibit created by James Rose and Emmanuel Udeh. Rose depicts various forms of body modification to demonstrate how physical changes can have a sacred, transformative, spiritual effect that exceeds the body’s limitation. Udeh creates technically skilled, conceptually grounded drawings that balance realism with imagination; quiet yet powerful visual meditations explore what it means to watch and be watched.\n\nReception: August 15, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"aT6_lLHg3nQFe3YvB7TNHQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"1fc6a9f3-e52e-41c8-a9c8-392c032d0f8b","name":"The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus by Emma Knight - By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1791327600000],"start":"2026-10-06T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus, by Emma Knight, shortlisted for the 2025 Scotiabank Giller Prize, is a spellbinding debut about friendship, motherhood, first love and the secrets that shape us. Set against the moody backdrop of Edinburgh, the novel follows Pen, a Canadian student unraveling a family mystery while navigating independence and desire. With wit and emotional depth, Knight explores womanhood and the choices that bind us.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readings, discussions, Q&A, book signings and ASL interpretation, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.","categories":["Literary"],"presenter":"City of Toronto","image":"1JKHhOM-wZcXUs7CD2kXfg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4c24b080-834a-499a-8d4f-4dd578c9d279"},{"id":"1fbd8fcd-9e54-44e0-be15-7db6c72db2e8","name":"The Cabbagetown Farmers Market","dates":[1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000],"start":"2026-05-12T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-20T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cabbagetown Farmers Market ","address":"191 Winchester St, Toronto","lat":43.666948,"lng":-79.362713},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Nestled in the heart of Riverdale Park West – just outside the gates of Riverdale Farm – we’re proud to be Toronto’s first park market. Every Tuesday, we bring together over 30 incredible vendors from across southern Ontario—from Brant County to Prince Edward County—offering farm-fresh produce, artisanal goods, and street food that reflects the vibrant diversity of our city.\n\nThis isn’t just a market—it’s a weekly celebration. Whether you're here for the just-picked produce, a bottle of Niagara wine, or a delicious meal in the park, you’ll find something to love. Stay for the live music, meet your neighbors, and soak in the community vibes. No pretense, no pressure—just fresh flavors, friendly faces, and a little something unexpected every week.\n\nCabbagetown Farmers Market is where Toronto gathers to eat well, shop local, and connect. Come for the food, stay for the community.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"VP43HPFTUlgkeT6FmKC9Fg","website":"https://www.cabbagetownmarket.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"2aaed361-2ec0-47a0-9646-d936140ecc7c","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market","dates":[1778007600000,1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000,1793127600000],"start":"2026-05-05T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Bellwoods Park","address":"1053 Dundas Street West","lat":43.64976901117809,"lng":-79.41732226545297},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market is of modest size and nestled in the north-west corner of the largest green space park in the downtown core. 2026 celebrates it’s 20 years of bringing to the neighbourhood fresh, local, sustainably grown agriculture and food artisans that prioritize local ingredients. It is farmer-focused, favours slow food not fast food and eating at the hearth and home. Human food only. Visit website for more info.  The market is operated by the generosity of part-time seasonal community volunteers. ","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"I3mtanYM-El4GRbb-TAO2A","website":"https://www.tbfm.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"491e9a50-fd88-4d33-a518-01b2b42fa642","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"604219d1-0a49-4a42-9ac8-00cdff02b614","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"6248aeaf-6cc5-4b53-a2a6-ef4dbd8b85c1","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market","dates":[1778007600000,1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000,1793127600000],"start":"2026-05-05T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Bellwoods Park","address":"1053 Dundas Street West","lat":43.64976901117809,"lng":-79.41732226545297},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market is of modest size and nestled in the north-west corner of the largest green space park in the downtown core. 2026 celebrates it’s 20 years of bringing to the neighbourhood fresh, local, sustainably grown agriculture and food artisans that prioritize local ingredients. It is farmer-focused, favours slow food not fast food and eating at the hearth and home. Human food only. Visit website for more info.  The market is operated by the generosity of part-time seasonal community volunteers. ","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"I3mtanYM-El4GRbb-TAO2A","website":"https://www.tbfm.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"d60ec4e1-834b-4553-aedd-8f5ee9dd1ab3","name":"Downsview Park Merchants Market","dates":[1779544800000,1779631200000,1780149600000,1780236000000,1780754400000,1780840800000,1781359200000,1781445600000,1781964000000,1782050400000,1782568800000,1782655200000,1783173600000,1783260000000,1783778400000,1783864800000,1784383200000,1784469600000,1784988000000,1785074400000,1785592800000,1785679200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793455200000,1793545200000,1794063600000,1794150000000,1794668400000,1794754800000,1795273200000,1795359600000,1795878000000,1795964400000,1796482800000,1796569200000,1797087600000,1797174000000,1797692400000,1797778800000,1798297200000,1798383600000,1798902000000,1798988400000,1799506800000,1799593200000,1800111600000,1800198000000,1800716400000,1800802800000,1801321200000,1801407600000,1801926000000,1802012400000,1802530800000,1802617200000,1803135600000,1803222000000,1803740400000,1803826800000,1804345200000,1804431600000,1804950000000,1805032800000,1805551200000,1805637600000,1806156000000,1806242400000,1806760800000,1806847200000,1807365600000,1807452000000,1807970400000,1808056800000,1808575200000,1808661600000,1809180000000,1809266400000],"start":"2026-05-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"40 Carl Hall Rd","address":"40 Carl Hall Rd, North York, ON, M3K 2C1","lat":43.7483766822,"lng":-79.4791132214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Downsview Park Merchants Market is one of Toronto’s vibrant weekend destinations, offering a dynamic indoor marketplace experience for shoppers of all ages. Located in North York, the market features a diverse mix of local vendors offering clothing, accessories, home goods, beauty products, electronics, toys, collectibles, gifts, fresh produce, specialty items, and incredible deals. Visitors can also explore the farmers market section featuring fresh fruits, vegetables, and locally sourced goods, alongside an international food court offering a variety of delicious global cuisines and authentic flavours. With a lively, family-friendly atmosphere, the market is a perfect destination for bargain hunters, families, food lovers, and those looking to support local and small businesses. Open every Saturday and Sunday from 10 AM to 