e the heart of your community!\n\nThe Allan Gardens Farmers’ Market facilitates a direct exchange between local farmers, food producers, artisan makers, and consumers. Everything sold at the market (50%+1) must be grown, sourced, made, and/or prepared in Toronto and the surrounding  area—ensuring that every purchase supports your neighbourhood economy.\n\nJoin us year- round every Saturday from 10am-2pm, in the beautiful Allan Gardens Children’s Conservatory & Teaching Garden. ","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"1_2B-asoDqdvJSyiKMPiaQ","website":"https://www.friendsofallangardens.ca/saturday-farmers-market","tickets":null},{"id":"ef63582d-dceb-405d-9ab2-26726bb97660","name":"Immersion Festival","dates":[1794153600000,1794263400000,1794439800000,1794526200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794958200000,1795131000000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795379400000],"start":"2026-11-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Betty Oliphant Theatre","address":"404 Jarvis St, Toronto, ON M4Y 2G6","lat":43.6643,"lng":-79.3777},"free":false,"low":0,"high":150,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a celebration of Canadian cultural life for audiences and a sought-after performance and networking opportunity for renowned and aspiring artists, with three distinct stage performances, twelve workshops, a dance education roundtable, and community gatherings. Performances and workshops are open to all!\n\nEnjoy The Vanguard Presentation includes commissioned works by Katlyn Addison and Tanya Charles, Travis Knights and Divine Brown, and Nubian Néné. The National Presentation features Ebnflōh Dance Company, Lua Shayenne Dance Company, and N.A.P.P.Y. Dance, while the Next Gen showcase highlights emerging Black youth artists.\n\nOur workshops for youth, beginners, and professionals are led by Kwasi Obeng-Adjei, Reequal Smith, Natasha Powell, and Isaac Gasangwa, exploring diverse Black and diasporic movement practices. \n\nThree gathering events bring together presenters, artists, and academics to connect, exchange ideas, and celebrate Black dance across Canada.","categories":["Dance","Live Performances","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"dance Immersion","image":"sERkkQuapznV_lRLtFWEKw","website":"https://danceimmersion.ca/immersionfestival/","tickets":"https://danceimmersion.ca/immersionfestival/#full-festival-info"},{"id":"64eece07-7caf-4437-be2f-afdd89cbdbde","name":"Immersion Festival","dates":[1794153600000,1794263400000,1794439800000,1794526200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794958200000,1795131000000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795379400000],"start":"2026-11-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Betty Oliphant Theatre","address":"404 Jarvis St, Toronto, ON M4Y 2G6","lat":43.6643,"lng":-79.3777},"free":false,"low":0,"high":150,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a celebration of Canadian cultural life for audiences and a sought-after performance and networking opportunity for renowned and aspiring artists, with three distinct stage performances, twelve workshops, a dance education roundtable, and community gatherings. Performances and workshops are open to all!\n\nEnjoy The Vanguard Presentation includes commissioned works by Katlyn Addison and Tanya Charles, Travis Knights and Divine Brown, and Nubian Néné. The National Presentation features Ebnflōh Dance Company, Lua Shayenne Dance Company, and N.A.P.P.Y. Dance, while the Next Gen showcase highlights emerging Black youth artists.\n\nOur workshops for youth, beginners, and professionals are led by Kwasi Obeng-Adjei, Reequal Smith, Natasha Powell, and Isaac Gasangwa, exploring diverse Black and diasporic movement practices. \n\nThree gathering events bring together presenters, artists, and academics to connect, exchange ideas, and celebrate Black dance across Canada.","catego