ptu open-air pedestrian mall has one of the most eclectic collection of startup businesses in the city.","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"oa2xxPdB_5ibesOE3pMKmA","website":"https://mkt707.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"caca7f84-bfd9-4b16-8043-1fc2eb564b1c","name":"Black Creek Farm Stand & Market","dates":[1781805600000,1782410400000,1783015200000,1783620000000,1784224800000,1784829600000,1785434400000,1786039200000,1786644000000,1787248800000,1787853600000,1788458400000,1789063200000,1789668000000,1790272800000,1790877600000,1791482400000,1792087200000,1792692000000,1793296800000],"start":"2026-06-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Black Creek Community Farm","address":"4929 Jane St, North York, ON M3N 2K8","lat":43.774639106068285,"lng":-79.52128184272664},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week during the growing season, we stock our on-site farm stand with freshly harvested produce from our fields. We ensure a weekly selection that highlights peak seasonal crops. Purchasing from our farm stand is a great way to support BCCF and enjoy delicious Toronto-grown produce.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NRVKLaN_ro4wSC8_vXcsRA","website":"https://blackcreekfarm.ca/en/programs-and-activities/farm-stand-markets","tickets":null},{"id":"68e5c6fa-c6c9-487f-a085-fc2f4c112c34","name":"Black Creek Farm Stand & Market","dates":[1781805600000,1782410400000,1783015200000,1783620000000,1784224800000,1784829600000,1785434400000,1786039200000,1786644000000,1787248800000,1787853600000,1788458400000,1789063200000,1789668000000,1790272800000,1790877600000,1791482400000,1792087200000,1792692000000,1793296800000],"start":"2026-06-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Black Creek Community Farm","address":"4929 Jane St, North York, ON M3N 2K8","lat":43.774639106068285,"lng":-79.52128184272664},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week during the growing season, we stock our on-site farm stand with freshly harvested produce from our fields. We ensure a weekly selection that highlights peak seasonal crops. Purchasing from our farm stand is a great way to support BCCF and enjoy delicious Toronto-grown produce.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NRVKLaN_ro4wSC8_vXcsRA","website":"https://blackcreekfarm.ca/en/programs-and-activities/farm-stand-markets","tickets":null},{"id":"110af083-7bb6-47c5-8479-7e55e384ccfe","name":"Scarborough Farmers' Market","dates":[1780428600000,1781033400000,1781638200000,1782243000000,1782847800000,1783452600000,1784057400000,1784662200000,1785267000000,1785871800000,1786476600000,1787081400000,1787686200000,1788291000000,1788895800000,1789500600000,1790105400000,1790710200000,1791315000000],"start":"2026-06-02T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cynthia Lai - Rosebank Park","address":"1051 Progress Ave, Scarborough, ON M1B 5M2","lat":43.79259399732396,"lng":-79.23363880409994},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Our mission then, as it is now, is to bring nutrient-dense, fairly priced, culturally appropriate, fresh fruits, vegetables, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"9d460590-6a19-4619-9adb-6dad98d629ee","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market","dates":[1778007600000,1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000,1793127600000],"start":"2026-05-05T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Bellwoods Park","address":"1053 Dundas Street West","lat":43.64976901117809,"lng":-79.41732226545297},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market is of modest size and nestled in the north-west corner of the largest green space park in the downtown core. 2026 celebrates it’s 20 years of bringing to the neighbourhood fresh, local, sustainably grown agriculture and food artisans that prioritize local ingredients. It is farmer-focused, favours slow food not fast food and eating at the hearth and home. Human food only. Visit website for more info.  The market is operated by the generosity of part-time seasonal community volunteers. ","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"I3mtanYM-El4GRbb-TAO2A","website":"https://www.tbfm.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"3b1cd1f7-92b9-421e-804c-4dfcf9aeb23d","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market","dates":[1778007600000,1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000,1793127600000],"start":"2026-05-05T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Bellwoods Park","address":"1053 Dundas Street West","lat":43.64976901117809,"lng":-79.41732226545297},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market is of modest size and nestled in the north-west corner of the largest green space park in the downtown core. 2026 celebrates it’s 20 years of bringing to the neighbourhood fresh, local, sustainably grown agriculture and food artisans that prioritize local ingredients. It is farmer-focused, favours slow food not fast food and eating at the hearth and home. Human food only. Visit website for more info.  The market is operated by the generosity of part-time seasonal community volunteers. ","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"I3mtanYM-El4GRbb-TAO2A","website":"https://www.tbfm.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"9877d3da-2154-44a1-86f1-a46ecc5e09e0","name":"Junction Farmers' Market","dates":[1778936400000,1779541200000,1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000,1793451600000],"start":"2026-05-16T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Baird Park","address":"275 Keele St, Toronto, ON M6P 2K5, Canada","lat":43.663023721805715,"lng":-79.46217817047676},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the lively Junction Farmers Market, where every visit is a celebration of fresh, local, and sustainably produced food! Join a vibrant community supporting passionate growers and producers while discovering delicious finds around every corner.\n\nExperience the joy of healthy, accessible food for everyone in and around the Junction—your next great food adventure starts here!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"1QtxyeTQD-ylYXlIjttO-g","website":"https://junctionmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"c88c18ae-a7af-43c5-99f8-3199816a0bfd","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200000,1787598000000,1788202800000,1788807600000,1789412400000,1790017200000,1790622000000,1791226800000,1791831600000,1792436400000,1793041200000],"start":"2026-05-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sorauren Park","address":"50 Wabash Ave, Toronto, ON M6R 1N2, Canada","lat":43.648147722995105,"lng":-79.44310115767041},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This year round farmers' Market operates during the outdoor season, we operate in Sorauren Park which is a beautiful greenspace managed by the City of Toronto and animated by community group, Friends of Sorauren Park. Along with the Farmers’ Market, you’ll find an ice skating rink, dog walking park, community pizza oven, children’s soccer and baseball programmes and even movie nights and an annual pumpkin parade!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"pratsPJvmGxDUcIhkbTofA","website":"https://www.soraurenmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"e89b5453-3372-4054-97a7-761bc568f62a","name":"Allan Gardens Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1777730400000,1778335200000,1778940000000,1779544800000,1780149600000,1780754400000,1781359200000,1781964000000,1782568800000,1783173600000,1783778400000,1784383200000,1784988000000,1785592800000,1786197600000,1786802400000,1787407200000,1788012000000,1788616800000,1789221600000,1789826400000,1790431200000,1791036000000,1791640800000,1792245600000,1792850400000,1793455200000,1794063600000,1794668400000,1795273200000,1795878000000,1796482800000,1797087600000,1797692400000,1798297200000,1798902000000,1799506800000,1800111600000,1800716400000,1801321200000,1801926000000,1802530800000,1803135600000,1803740400000,1804345200000,1804950000000,1805551200000,1806156000000,1806760800000,1807365600000,1807970400000,1808575200000,1809180000000],"start":"2026-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Children's Conservatory","address":"19 Horticultural Ave, Toronto, ON, M5A 2P2","lat":43.661418998,"lng":-79.37480223},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate local food, community, and sustainable agriculture. Discover fresh produce, artisanal products, and small-scale producers - all while connecting with the people who grow and create them.We invite you to come meet the vendors, discover new favourites, and taste the heart of your community!\n\nThe Allan Gardens Farmers’ Market facilitates a direct exchange between local farmers, food producers, artisan makers, and consumers. Everything sold at the market (50%+1) must be grown, sourced, made, and/or prepared in Toronto and the surrounding  area—ensuring that every purchase supports your neighbourhood economy.\n\nJoin us year- round every Saturday from 10am-2pm, in the beautiful Allan Gardens Children’s Conservatory & Teaching Garden. ","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"1_2B-asoDqdvJSyiKMPiaQ","website":"https://www.friendsofallangardens.ca/saturday-farmers-market","tickets":null},{"id":"b7a54eee-4ba8-4ad3-98a9-59093306f739","name":"Allan Gardens Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1777730400000,1778335200000,1778940000000,1779544800000,1780149600000,1780754400000,1781359200000,1781964000000,1782568800000,1783173600000,1783778400000,1784383200000,1784988000000,1785592800000,1786197600000,1786802400000,1787407200000,1788012000000,1788616800000,1789221600000,1789826400000,1790431200000,1791036000000,1791640800000,1792245600000,1792850400000,1793455200000,1794063600000,1794668400000,1795273200000,1795878000000,1796482800000,1797087600000,1797692400000,1798297200000,1798902000000,1799506800000,1800111600000,1800716400000,1801321200000,1801926000000,1802530800000,1803135600000,1803740400000,1804345200000,1804950000000,1805551200000,1806156000000,1806760800000,1807365600000,1807970400000,1808575200000,1809180000000],"start":"2026-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Children's Conservatory","address":"19 Horticultural Ave, Toronto, ON, M5A 2P2","lat":43.661418998,"lng":-79.37480223},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate local food, community, and sustainable agriculture. Discover fresh produce, artisanal products, and small-scale producers - all while connecting with the people who grow and create them.We invite you to come meet the vendors, discover new favourites, and taste the heart of your community!\n\nThe Allan Gardens Farmers’ Market facilitates a direct exchange between local farmers, food producers, artisan makers, and consumers. Everything sold at the market (50%+1) must be grown, sourced, made, and/or prepared in Toronto and the surrounding  area—ensuring that every purchase supports your neighbourhood economy.\n\nJoin us year- round every Saturday from 10am-2pm, in the beautiful Allan Gardens Children’s Conservatory & Teaching Garden. ","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"1_2B-asoDqdvJSyiKMPiaQ","website":"https://www.friendsofallangardens.ca/saturday-farmers-market","tickets":null},{"id":"6ebb5934-e693-46cf-a5c8-01a2c5aa8b1a","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"start":"2026-05-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mel Lastman Square","address":"5100 Yonge St, North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.768067488538286,"lng":-79.41329517024496},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"From Farm to Table. We make it, WE bake it, and grow it for you! The perfect place to shop for fresh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"420d079d-654c-4f58-be18-4852c570e3be","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"start":"2026-05-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mel Lastman Square","address":"5100 Yonge St, North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.768067488538286,"lng":-79.41329517024496},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"From Farm to Table. We make it, WE bake it, and grow it for you! The perfect place to shop for fresh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"b9b7e0fb-d785-450c-a18f-aa2992ceafe7","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"e0d671b2-7de6-4bac-afe1-ebb8f14bdbfb","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"d4290c4d-4330-44b3-ab3b-a65182a98c35","name":"Withrow Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000],"start":"2026-05-30T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Withrow Park ","address":"725 Logan Ave, Toronto, ON M4K 3B9","lat":43.67657084103454,"lng":-79.34742988876354},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Just steps from Danforth Avenue in vibrant Greektown, Withrow Park Farmers’ Market bursts to life every season! Since 2006, it’s been the go-to destination for fresh food, lively music, local art, and a joyful sense of community—celebrating the best of Toronto while championing local farmers, producers, and artisans.\n\nFrom June to October, the park transforms into a buzzing hub of delicious discoveries and vibrant connection. We’re passionate about creating an inclusive, sustainable, and community-powered market where every visit is an adventure—and everyone’s welcome!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"L8DDBTjIOMKrxChhtduF6Q","website":"https://withrowmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"b43023ff-dfd4-400d-91d1-647dc40cd264","name":"Withrow Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000],"start":"2026-05-30T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Withrow Park ","address":"725 Logan Ave, Toronto, ON M4K 3B9","lat":43.67657084103454,"lng":-79.34742988876354},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Just steps from Danforth Avenue in vibrant Greektown, Withrow Park Farmers’ Market bursts to life every season! Since 2006, it’s been the go-to destination for fresh food, lively music, local art, and a joyful sense of community—celebrating the best of Toronto while championing local farmers, producers, and artisans.\n\nFrom June to October, the park transforms into a buzzing hub of delicious discoveries and vibrant connection. We’re passionate about creating an inclusive, sustainable, and community-powered market where every visit is an adventure—and everyone’s welcome!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"L8DDBTjIOMKrxChhtduF6Q","website":"https://withrowmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"c2f44ff7-f0e0-4650-9045-810ebcf6ee27","name":"Market 707","dates":[1779462000000,1779548400000,1779807600000,1779894000000,1779980400000,1780066800000,1780153200000,1780412400000,1780498800000,1780585200000,1780671600000,1780758000000,1781017200000,1781103600000,1781190000000,1781276400000,1781362800000,1781622000000,1781708400000,1781794800000,1781881200000,1781967600000,1782226800000,1782313200000,1782399600000,1782486000000,1782572400000,1782831600000,1782918000000,1783004400000,1783090800000,1783177200000,1783436400000,1783522800000,1783609200000,1783695600000,1783782000000,1784041200000,1784127600000,1784214000000,1784300400000,1784386800000,1784646000000,1784732400000,1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785250800000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785855600000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786460400000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1787065200000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787670000000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788274800000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000],"start":"2026-05-22T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scadding Court Community Centre","address":"707 Dundas St W, Toronto, ON M5T 2W6","lat":43.651713739404556,"lng":-79.40508261942017},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Market 707 is a stretch of sidewalk near Dundas and Bathurst lined with upcycled shipping containers that offer sweet and savoury foods, services, and everything in between. \n\nPresided over by the Scadding Court Community Centre, this impromptu open-air pedestrian mall has one of the most eclectic collection of startup businesses in the city.","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"oa2xxPdB_5ibesOE3pMKmA","website":"https://mkt707.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"3f7ee427-b93d-45c9-b188-06f11c7e9dfe","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market","dates":[1778007600000,1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000,1793127600000],"start":"2026-05-05T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Bellwoods Park","address":"1053 Dundas Street West","lat":43.64976901117809,"lng":-79.41732226545297},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market is of modest size and nestled in the north-west corner of the largest green space park in the downtown core. 2026 celebrates it’s 20 years of bringing to the neighbourhood fresh, local, sustainably grown agriculture and food artisans that prioritize local ingredients. It is farmer-focused, favours slow food not fast food and eating at the hearth and home. Human food only. Visit website for more info.  The market is operated by the generosity of part-time seasonal community volunteers. ","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"I3mtanYM-El4GRbb-TAO2A","website":"https://www.tbfm.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"fecd5eea-2bde-4c8f-8f7e-08385f217f28","name":"The Toronto Flea Market","dates":[1780844400000,1783263600000,1788706800000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-06-07T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Ashbridge Estate","address":"1444 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M4L 1E1","lat":43.665266265,"lng":-79.322771049},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Let us show you how we spend our Sunday’s … we like it slow. we invite you to come and be offline with us, relax outdoors in nature and spend time with some of the best handmade artists + vintage curators around.\n\nInvite your friend and meet us here for coffee + a stroll, come for a solo date to fall back in love with the city, bring a parent for some quality time, or pack up the whole crew and little ones and enjoy our fenced open playground. we promise good time with live music and special treats.\n\nOur vendors are truly something special - some travel as far as thunder bay and Cobourg or Niagara and Hamilton just to vend here. We consider ourselves so lucky to get to bring the east end community (and all who come support) such incredible one-of-a-kind finds.\n\nWe operate seasonally outdoors exclusively, be sure to check out our Instagram for any and all updates. We can't wait to see you.\n","categories":["Artisan","Live Performances","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Q7s9d-8N45DaAEv8PBzrAg","website":"https://www.torontoflea.com","tickets":null},{"id":"728b2e22-fd3d-43ad-9823-a4656638238e","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"start":"2026-05-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mel Lastman Square","address":"5100 Yonge St, North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.768067488538286,"lng":-79.41329517024496},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"From Farm to Table. We make it, WE bake it, and grow it for you! The perfect place to shop for fresh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"287fb046-e9ea-4f2d-bc58-10c2f35375bd","name":"Downsview Park Merchants Market","dates":[1779544800000,1779631200000,1780149600000,1780236000000,1780754400000,1780840800000,1781359200000,1781445600000,1781964000000,1782050400000,1782568800000,1782655200000,1783173600000,1783260000000,1783778400000,1783864800000,1784383200000,1784469600000,1784988000000,1785074400000,1785592800000,1785679200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793455200000,1793545200000,1794063600000,1794150000000,1794668400000,1794754800000,1795273200000,1795359600000,1795878000000,1795964400000,1796482800000,1796569200000,1797087600000,1797174000000,1797692400000,1797778800000,1798297200000,1798383600000,1798902000000,1798988400000,1799506800000,1799593200000,1800111600000,1800198000000,1800716400000,1800802800000,1801321200000,1801407600000,1801926000000,1802012400000,1802530800000,1802617200000,1803135600000,1803222000000,1803740400000,1803826800000,1804345200000,1804431600000,1804950000000,1805032800000,1805551200000,1805637600000,1806156000000,1806242400000,1806760800000,1806847200000,1807365600000,1807452000000,1807970400000,1808056800000,1808575200000,1808661600000,1809180000000,1809266400000],"start":"2026-05-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"40 Carl Hall Rd","address":"40 Carl Hall Rd, North York, ON, M3K 2C1","lat":43.7483766822,"lng":-79.4791132214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Downsview Park Merchants Market is one of Toronto’s vibrant weekend destinations, offering a dynamic indoor marketplace experience for shoppers of all ages. Located in North York, the market features a diverse mix of local vendors offering clothing, accessories, home goods, beauty products, electronics, toys, collectibles, gifts, fresh produce, specialty items, and incredible deals. Visitors can also explore the farmers market section featuring fresh fruits, vegetables, and locally sourced goods, alongside an international food court offering a variety of delicious global cuisines and authentic flavours. With a lively, family-friendly atmosphere, the market is a perfect destination for bargain hunters, families, food lovers, and those looking to support local and small businesses. Open every Saturday and Sunday from 10 AM to 5 PM, Downsview Park Merchants Market combines shopping, food, culture, and community into one exciting weekend experience in Toronto.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"HsINX9unS5aRBvcRR5D6QA","website":"https://www.dpmarket.com","tickets":null},{"id":"cb2c744a-d1c3-47e9-9c41-f29a3be96ceb","name":"Immersion Festival","dates":[1794153600000,1794263400000,1794439800000,1794526200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794958200000,1795131000000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795379400000],"start":"2026-11-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Betty Oliphant Theatre","address":"404 Jarvis St, Toronto, ON M4Y 2G6","lat":43.6643,"lng":-79.3777},"free":false,"low":0,"high":150,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a celebration of Canadian cultural life for audiences and a sought-after performance and networking opportunity for renowned and aspiring artists, with three distinct stage performances, twelve workshops, a dance education roundtable, and community gatherings. Performances and workshops are open to all!\n\nEnjoy The Vanguard Presentation includes commissioned works by Katlyn Addison and Tanya Charles, Travis Knights and Divine Brown, and Nubian Néné. The National Presentation features Ebnflōh Dance Company, Lua Shayenne Dance Company, and N.A.P.P.Y. Dance, while the Next Gen showcase highlights emerging Black youth artists.\n\nOur workshops for youth, beginners, and professionals are led by Kwasi Obeng-Adjei, Reequal Smith, Natasha Powell, and Isaac Gasangwa, exploring diverse Black and diasporic movement practices. \n\nThree gathering events bring together presenters, artists, and academics to connect, exchange ideas, and celebrate Black dance across Canada.","categories":["Dance","Live Performances","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"dance Immersion","image":"sERkkQuapznV_lRLtFWEKw","website":"https://danceimmersion.ca/immersionfestival/","tickets":"https://danceimmersion.ca/immersionfestival/#full-festival-info"},{"id":"e24ad1d6-ed06-45d5-b057-a3ac0b79b7a5","name":"Downsview Park Merchants Market","dates":[1779544800000,1779631200000,1780149600000,1780236000000,1780754400000,1780840800000,1781359200000,1781445600000,1781964000000,1782050400000,1782568800000,17826552000