t reflects the vibrant diversity of our city.\n\nThis isn’t just a market—it’s a weekly celebration. Whether you're here for the just-picked produce, a bottle of Niagara wine, or a delicious meal in the park, you’ll find something to love. Stay for the live music, meet your neighbors, and soak in the community vibes. No pretense, no pressure—just fresh flavors, friendly faces, and a little something unexpected every week.\n\nCabbagetown Farmers Market is where Toronto gathers to eat well, shop local, and connect. Come for the food, stay for the community.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"VP43HPFTUlgkeT6FmKC9Fg","website":"https://www.cabbagetownmarket.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"bd78b239-d115-45dc-a5fb-65ea0e578c48","name":"Withrow Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000],"start":"2026-05-30T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Withrow Park ","address":"725 Logan Ave, Toronto, ON M4K 3B9","lat":43.67657084103454,"lng":-79.34742988876354},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Just steps from Danforth Avenue in vibrant Greektown, Withrow Park Farmers’ Market bursts to life every season! Since 2006, it’s been the go-to destination for fresh food, lively music, local art, and a joyful sense of community—celebrating the best of Toronto while championing local farmers, producers, and artisans.\n\nFrom June to October, the park transforms into a buzzing hub of delicious discoveries and vibrant connection. We’re passionate about creating an inclusive, sustainable, and community-powered market where every visit is an adventure—and everyone’s welcome!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"L8DDBTjIOMKrxChhtduF6Q","website":"https://withrowmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"c74d57fc-e528-467c-9b9d-1ccaf1d6f2df","name":"Withrow Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000],"start":"2026-05-30T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Withrow Park ","address":"725 Logan Ave, Toronto, ON M4K 3B9","lat":43.67657084103454,"lng":-79.34742988876354},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Just steps from Danforth Avenue in vibrant Greektown, Withrow Park Farmers’ Market bursts to life every season! Since 2006, it’s been the go-to destination for fresh food, lively music, local art, and a joyful sense of community—celebrating the best of Toronto while championing local farmers, producers, and artisans.\n\nFrom June to October, the park transforms into a buzzing hub of delicious discoveries and vibrant connection. We’re passionate about creating an inclusive, sustainable, and community-powered market where every visit is an adventure—and everyone’s welcome!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"L8DDBTjIOMKrxChhtduF6Q","website":"https://withrowmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"1f8df394-d68a-45bc-9426-b884d3392bee","name":"27th Annual Planet in Focus International Environmental Film Festival","dates":[1792535400000,1792621800000,1792708200000,1792794600000,1792881000000,1792967400000],"start":"2026-10-20T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Paradise Theater","address":"1006c Bloor Street West, Toronto, ON M6H 1M2","lat":43.661115,"lng":-79.430709},"free":false,"low":15,"high":20,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Don’t miss this lineup of groundbreaking documentary films focusing on the planet we share. \n\nThe festival includes Canadian and international films, a free Industry Conference, a free Family Day Program, special guests, panels and filmmaker QnAs. \n\n","categories":["Cultural","Environmental","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"http://planetinfocus.org","tickets":"https://planetinfocus.org/tickets/"},{"id":"95bf3fec-684b-40b0-8d5e-42bbccd530ce","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"fd4ba3db-8eac-45c6-bb50-1e934c8175a1","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,178007940000