y food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"18be4b3d-f8b5-4e25-be7d-3062ba1ec599","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"7ee5b852-d4d0-4330-b944-693bb4280d5a","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"064613e4-80b3-45e1-a226-83b1f00b96cd","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"06f537f9-e346-47fc-9b8f-48b477b00d82","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"035989c8-641b-45e0-8f25-6562be1e40ed","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community b