 vegetables, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"d6c70d72-b283-4b1e-93c6-e545ba809e69","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"956839d4-5146-4d1a-9351-16d1444c6f0e","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200000,1787598000000,1788202800000,1788807600000,1789412400000,1790017200000,1790622000000,1791226800000,1791831600000,1792436400000,1793041200000],"start":"2026-05-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sorauren Park","address":"50 Wabash Ave, Toronto, ON M6R 1N2, Canada","lat":43.648147722995105,"lng":-79.44310115767041},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This year round farmers' Market operates during the outdoor season, we operate in Sorauren Park which is a beautiful greenspace managed by the City of Toronto and animated by community group, Friends of Sorauren Park. Along with the Farmers’ Market, you’ll find an ice skating rink, dog walking park, community pizza oven, children’s soccer and baseball programmes and even movie nights and an annual pumpkin parade!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"pratsPJvmGxDUcIhkbTofA","website":"https://www.soraurenmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"4e396b1e-4d47-448a-b8fe-7da7540e29e3","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200