Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"de0af28f-0906-4217-adeb-aa02d0336db4","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market","dates":[1778007600000,1778612400000,1779217200000,1779822000000,1780426800000,1781031600000,1781636400000,1782241200000,1782846000000,1783450800000,1784055600000,1784660400000,1785265200000,1785870000000,1786474800000,1787079600000,1787684400000,1788289200000,1788894000000,1789498800000,1790103600000,1790708400000,1791313200000,1791918000000,1792522800000,1793127600000],"start":"2026-05-05T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-27T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Bellwoods Park","address":"1053 Dundas Street West","lat":43.64976901117809,"lng":-79.41732226545297},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Trinity Bellwoods Farmers' Market is of modest size and nestled in the north-west corner of the largest green space park in the downtown core. 2026 celebrates it’s 20 years of bringing to the neighbourhood fresh, local, sustainably grown agriculture and food artisans that prioritize local ingredients. It is farmer-focused, favours slow food not fast food and eating at the hearth and home. Human food only. Visit website for more info.  The market is operated by the generosity of part-time seasonal community volunteers. ","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"I3mtanYM-El4GRbb-TAO2A","website":"https://www.tbfm.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"bf86abce-d1d9-4666-ad9b-7b73cfed8b62","name":"Trinity Bellwoods Fa