es, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"26e0a968-a963-4ee4-9526-11559bad5557","name":"Beach Photo Club Exhibition","dates":[1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000,1795096800000,1795183200000,1795269600000,1795356000000,1795442400000,1795528800000,1795615200000,1795701600000,1795788000000,1795874400000,1795960800000,1796047200000,1796133600000,1796220000000,1796306400000],"start":"2026-11-03T09:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-03T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy this photography exhibition by a diverse group of artists as they present their unique interpretations of our world, from realistic to abstract, including techniques such as macro photography, intentional movement and digital compositing. This collection promises a rich visual experience that reflects the wide-ranging creativity of Beach Photo Club members.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4UNkAN-HEr_AYUwhK0vhfw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"9d66d3ea-76c7-4c4c-8575-7ff206ee72a6","name":"Beach Photo Club Exhibition","dates":[1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000,1795096800000,1795183200000,1795269600000,1795356000000,1795442400000,1795528800000,1795615200000,1795701600000,1795788000000,1795874400000,1795960800000,1796047200000,1796133600000,1796220000000,1796306400000],"start":"2026-11-03T09:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-03T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy this photography exhibition by a diverse group of artists as they present their unique interpretations of our world, from realistic to abstract, including techniques such as macro photography, intentional movement and digital compositing. This collection promises a rich visual experience that reflects the wide-ranging creativity of Beach Photo Club members.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4UNkAN-HEr_AYUwhK0vhfw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"3097b6c6-446a-4c6f-ae3d-5fa8f5c38c66","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting there is easy with the free shuttle bus picking up next to Broadview Station or take the TTC's 28 bus from Davisville Station.\n\nThe farmers' market is operated by Evergreen, a national non-profit transforming public spaces in our cities to build a healthier future for people and our planet.","categories":["Environmental","Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"g_7hN7bS9geSUWTPQPVycA","website":"https://www.evergreen.ca/evergreen-brick-work/activities/saturday-farmers-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"dfc54d77-9d4c-47e0-9898-88b3fab167c3","name":"Sketch Party","dates":[1769904000000,1771718400000,1774738800000,1777158000000,1779577200000,1781996400000,1784415600000,1786834800000,1789254000000,1792278000000,1795305600000,1797724800000],"start":"2026-01-31T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-19T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Comedy Bar","address":"945 Bloor Street W, Toronto, ON, M6H 1L5","lat":43.66148,"lng":-79.428242},"free":false,"low":23,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each month we're partying HARD and bringing the best sketch comedy this city has to offer, from the hottest up and coming troupes to long time fan favourite troupes and solo acts.\n\nGet ready for a wild night of expecting the unexpected and, of course, sketch comedy. Bring your best party trick and enjoy the vibes. There ain't no party like a S-KETCH PARTY!\n\nYou won’t want to miss this monthly shindig, come party-hardy with us!","categories":["Comedy"],"presenter":null,"image":"IoEFS6qmP2peTL7SwyQW_w","website":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/sketch-party","tickets":null},{"id":"29bf9cd4-9ddf-4ee5-87e2-9f66557669ea","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1779526800000,1780131600000,1780736400000,1781341200000,1781946000000,1782550800000,1783155600000,1783760400000,1784365200000,1784970000000,1785574800000,1786179600000,1786784400000,1787389200000,1787994000000,1788598800000,1789203600000,1789808400000,1790413200000,1791018000000,1791622800000,1792227600000,1792832400000,1793437200000,1794045600000,1794650400000,1795255200000,1795860000000,1796464800000,1797069600000,1797674400000,1798279200000,1798884000000],"start":"2026-05-23T05:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T05:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"St. Lawrence North Market","address":"92 Front St E, Toronto","lat":43.649145,"lng":-79.371526},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visit the Saturday Farmers' Market in the newly redeveloped St. Lawrence Market North building. Discover seasonal produce, baked goods, meats, cheeses, flowers and pantry staples from local vendors all under one roof.","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"a0PsB9WOlmzpz_7ENsYW_A","website":"https://www.stlawrencemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"ca4036eb-5425-4347-b978-ef02e99e99f7","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1779526800000,1780131600000,1780736400000,1781341200000,1781946000000,