resh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"7490ab70-8582-405d-aca1-684ca9fe2421","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"start":"2026-05-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mel Lastman Square","address":"5100 Yonge St, North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.768067488538286,"lng":-79.41329517024496},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"From Farm to Table. We make it, WE bake it, and grow it for you! The perfect place to shop for fresh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"aac51287-1bdc-4431-aa3f-76581a7f773b","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"75f846cc-0470-4c50-a614-b7035bb19901","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"9eff541b-09d0-4200-8ccf-d168ab9d97e5","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"start":"2026-05-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mel Lastman Square","address":"5100 Yonge St, North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.768067488538286,"lng":-79.41329517024496},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"From Farm to Table. We make it, WE bake it, and grow it for you! The perfect place to shop for fresh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"6ef5dcdc-6cc3-4541-8061-57ccd2dd6584","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"start":"2026-05-28T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mel Lastman Square","address":"5100 Yonge St, North York, ON M2N 5V7","lat":43.768067488538286,"lng":-79.41329517024496},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"From Farm to Table. We make it, WE bake it, and grow it for you! The perfect place to shop for fresh fruits, vegetables, honey, maple syrup and flowers. In addition we offer a fine selections of delicious breads, pastries, cheeses and cured meats.\n\nHeld from Mya to October every Thursday,, come and meet our local farmers and vendors who display their best fresh produce and variety of products. Such as rhubarb, strawberries, and asparagus in the early summer to squash and pumpkins in the fall. Most importantly safety measures are in place for a safe shopping experience.\n\nWe look forward to your visit at North York Farmers’ Market.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NJ5eiPqlbTCdw8AkXO9R-Q","website":"https://www.northyorkfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"a580f8d3-549e-4d70-8bb5-fc33a932da0e","name":"North York Farmers' Market","dates":[1779969600000,1780574400000,1781179200000,1781784000000,1782388800000,1782993600000,1783598400000,1784203200000,1784808000000,1785412800000,1786017600000,1786622400000,1787227200000,1787832000000,1788436800000,1789041600000,1789646400000,1790251200000,1790856000000,1791460800000],"s