nformation tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"eb7a31a6-990b-4aa4-bd33-d7e93a1bd3f9","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"4f5e9423-90dc-4f29-953e-4e53427a2b0d","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"8ac79b7d-3816-4b0e-9248-e7aa0e24bd0d","name":"Interpol with support from DIIV","dates":[1790982000000],"start":"2026-10-02T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-02T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Bowl at Sobey Stadium","address":"1 Shoreham Dr, North York, ON, M3N 3A6","lat":43.771640453,"lng":-79.511841342},"free":false,"low":39.5,"high":109.5,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Interpol’s seventh album The Other Side of Make-Believe finds the band exploring new emotional territory while staying true to their signature sound. \n\nAlongside the familiar dark undertones, the record introduces a sense of vulnerability, grace, and even hope, with Paul Banks’ more understated vocals and Daniel Kessler’s expansive guitar work pushing their music into fresh, more introspective territory.\n\nWritten largely in isolation during 2020 and completed in 2021 with producers Flood and Alan Moulder, the album reflects both the uncertainty of the times and a deliberate shift toward resilience and emotional clarity. While themes of distorted reality and modern disillusionment remain, Interpol counterbalances them with a focus on human strength and connection, resulting in a record that feels both reflective and quietly optimistic.","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"JlKIcfgpa1wF4F0Bec2B5w","website":"https://www.ticketmaster.ca/interpol-toronto-ontario-10-02-2026/event/1000649B81805BD2","tickets":"https://www.ticketmaster.ca/interpol-toronto-ontario-10-02-2026/event/1000649B81805BD2"},{"id":"e90a6a2f-c2e1-4f09-9028-794f8db9cad9","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"d1249611-e84f-4fbb-a5d7-05f6445b11a9","name":"The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus by Emma Knight - By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1791327600000],"start":"2026-10-06T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus, by Emma Knight, shortlisted for the 2025 Scotiabank Giller Prize, is a spellbinding debut about friendship, motherhood, first love and the secrets that shape us. Set against the moody backdrop of Edinburgh, the novel follows Pen, a Canadian student unraveling a family mystery while navigating independence and desire. With wit and emotional depth, Knight explores womanhood and the choices that bind us.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readings, discussions, Q&A, book signings and ASL interpretation, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.","categories":["Literary"],"presenter":"City of Toronto","image":"1JKHhOM-wZcXUs7CD2kXfg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4c24b080-834a-499a-8d4f-4dd578c9d279"},{"id":"3254c9cd-98fc-425f-ae04-a9b99ba437bd","name":"Held by Anne Michaels - By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1796774400000],"start":"2026-12-08T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-08T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Held, by 2024 Scotiabank Giller Prize winner Anne Michaels, is a luminous, fragmented novel about love, memory, and the reverberations of war across generations. Beginning on a First World War battlefield, the narrative moves through time and place to explore how desire and grief endure beyond a single lifetime. Michaels – renowned poet and author of Fugitive Pieces—weaves history and intimacy into a work of haunting beauty.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event features readings, discussions, Q&A, book signings and ASL interpretation, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio access.\n","categories":["Literary"],"presenter":"City of Toronto","image":"yFdcXkah7XICEeFv7n5Q3A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/216644f0-d05b-410f-a0d0-be3b766b93a8"},{"id":"6f7d6a6b-92a2-4500-b713-71fc0e679f29","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting there is easy with the free shuttle bus picking up next to Broadview Station or take the TTC's 28 bus from Davisville Station.\n\nThe farmers' market is operated by Evergreen, a national non-profit transforming public spaces in our cities to build a healthier future for people and our planet.","categories":["Environmental","Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"g_7hN7bS9geSUWTPQPVycA","website":"https://www.evergreen.ca/evergreen-brick-work/activities/saturday-farmers-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"7ffa886d-57ea-4b69-8b6c-fb369a5fb398","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting there is easy with the free shuttle bus picking up next to Broadview Station or take the TTC's 28 bus from Davisville Station.\n\nThe farmers' market is operated by Evergreen, a national non-profit transforming public spaces in our cities to build a healthier future for people and our planet.","categories":["Environmental","Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"g_7hN7bS9geSUWTPQPV