ption":"Discover the magic of Underpass Park Farmers' Market—a vibrant gem in Toronto's Corktown and one of the city's most unique farmers market destinations! Surrounded by colorful murals from local artists, this lively outdoor market bursts with farm-fresh fruits and vegetables, mouthwatering baked goods, homemade preserves, and a tempting selection of artisanal treats.\n\nFrom May to October—rain or shine—this pet-friendly hotspot invites you to soak up live music, browse the stalls, and mingle with adorable pups for a truly unforgettable market experience.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"w3Jiy9MEVv3kfA1fQck79w","website":"https://underpassparkmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"c7f30c9d-c871-43f5-892e-3efd6fc84bc8","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1779526800000,1780131600000,1780736400000,1781341200000,1781946000000,1782550800000,1783155600000,1783760400000,1784365200000,1784970000000,1785574800000,1786179600000,1786784400000,1787389200000,1787994000000,1788598800000,1789203600000,1789808400000,1790413200000,1791018000000,1791622800000,1792227600000,1792832400000,1793437200000,1794045600000,1794650400000,1795255200000,1795860000000,1796464800000,1797069600000,1797674400000,1798279200000,1798884000000],"start":"2026-05-23T05:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T05:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"St. Lawrence North Market","address":"92 Front St E, Toronto","lat":43.649145,"lng":-79.371526},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visit the Saturday Farmers' Market in the newly redeveloped St. Lawrence Market North building. Discover seasonal produce, baked goods, meats, cheeses, flowers and pantry staples from local vendors all under one roof.","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"a0PsB9WOlmzpz_7ENsYW_A","website":"https://www.stlawrencemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"4f88a9d6-b381-4344-8f4a-96165b00587f","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"dbe79b8f-3290-4427-9516-b2844dd592a9","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"1997f782-fa81-4ee2-ae1b-a80d24e4ba08","name":"Eglinton Way BIA Farmers' Market","dates":[1780833600000,1781438400000,1782043200000,1782648000000,1783252800000,1783857600000,1784462400000,1785067200000,1785672000000,1786276800000,1786881600000,1787486400000,1788091200000,1788696000000,1789300800000,1789905600000,1790510400000,1791115200000,1791720000000,1792324800000,1792929600000],"start":"2026-06-07T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Green P Parking Lot #47","address":"125 Burnaby Blvd, Toronto","lat":43.70439991,"lng":-79.412600977},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Now in its 9th year, The Eglinton Way BIA Farmers' Market has become a staple Sunday event in Midtown Toronto dedicated to strengthening and promoting the connections between our community and Ontario farms, local artisans and small businesses. With 40+ vendors this season, find everything from fresh meat, eggs and produce, to baked goods, food & drink, household goods, arts, crafts and more! Our market features live music, free kids' activities, and special activations that are perfect for all ages. Follow us on Instagram at @EglintonWay for more information and updates!","categories":["Artisan","Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"uR4r0FHNt-y4Xe6-SE_U-g