y Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"e0226b28-d593-4b7a-baa5-664230f057fd","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"407b3d84-442e-41a5-9bfc-6d30ceb1bec5","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"be3b2092-7afb-4765-814b-34f13bdefede","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"ac492a0e-e0a9-4734-85bf-f4eb8a459a7d","name":"Junction Farmers' Market","dates":[1778936400000,1779541200000,1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000,1793451600000],"start":"2026-05-16T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Baird Park","address":"275 Keele St, Toronto, ON M6P 2K5, Canada","lat":43.663023721805715,"lng":-79.46217817047676},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the lively Junction Farmers Market, where every visit is a celebration of fresh, local, and sustainably produced food! Join a vibrant community supporting passionate growers and producers while discovering delicious finds around every corner.\n\nExperience the joy of healthy, accessible food for everyone in and around the Junction—your next great food adventure starts here!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"1QtxyeTQD-ylYXlIjttO-g","website":"https://junctionmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"e0623ce7-f03c-4bbd-a2d5-f2ab56210b8b","name":"Toronto Sunday Market","dates":[1779634800000,1780239600000,1780844400000,1781449200000,1782054000000,1782658800000,1783263600000,1783868400000,1784473200000,1785078000000,1785682800000,1786287600000,1786892400000,1787497200000,1788102000000,1788706800000,1789311600000,1789916400000,1790521200000,1791126000000,1791730800000,1792335600000,1792940400000,1793548800000,1794153600000,1794758400000,1795363200000,1795968000000,1796572800000,1797177600000,1797782400000],"start":"2026-05-24T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A vibrant weekly market celebrating local creators, delicious food & community\nHandmade Goods • Antiques • Vintage • Family-friendly\n\nSupport local. Shop small. Eat fresh.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"BomI95CaiWtmNfhqDjDNLg","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"0118e7f6-1503-4710-937d-89814b9bad8a","name":"Junction Farmers' Market","dates":[1778936400000,1779541200000,1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000,1793451600000],"start":"2026-05-16T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Baird Park","address":"275 Keele St, Toronto, ON M6P 2K5, Canada","lat":43.663023721805715,"lng":-79.46217817047676},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the lively Junction Farmers Market, where every visit is a celebration of fresh, local, and sustainably produced food! Join a vibrant community supporting passionate growers and producers while discovering delicious finds around every corner.\n\nExperience the joy of healthy, accessible food for everyone in and around the Junction—your next great food adventure starts here!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"1QtxyeTQD-ylYXlIjttO-g","website":"https://junctionmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"fc461e0e-12a0-49a3-8193-430cd2afc3f9","name":"Taylor Memorial Library Talk: Our Urban Forest","dates":[1793818800000],"start":"2026-11-04T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-04T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Taylor Memorial Library","address":"1440 Kingston Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1R3","lat":43.687830698,"lng":-79.271302995},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Join the City of Toronto for an in-library presentation on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto.\n\nWe’ll discuss what makes the urban forest so special and share tools to help you explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities, and leave with greater confidence and a deeper understanding of your City and the natural world around you.","categories":["Environmental","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"ZWXV53k1kqVyHnmPHFOv_g","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a1e4a2491b809c6f1cf550","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a1e4a2491b809c6f1cf550"},{"id":"d1692c7c-b24d-4d78-b602-947aca047558","name":"Sunday Variety Market","dates":[1779544800000,1779631200000,1780149600000,1780236000000,1780754400000,1780840800000,1781359200000,1781445600000,1781964000000,1782050400000,1782568800000,1782655200000,1783173600000,1783260000000,1783778400000,1783864800000,1784383200000,1784469600000,1784988000000,1785074400000,1785592800000,1785679200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793455200000,1793545200000,1794063600000,1794150000000,1794668400000,1794754800000,1795273200000,1795359600000,1795878000000,1795964400000,1796482800000,1796569200000,1797087600000,1797174000000,1797692400000,1797778800000],"start":"2026-05-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"St. Lawrence Market (Big White Tent)","address":"125 The Esplanade, Toronto","lat":43.647946,"lng":-79.371229},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Great finds to be discovered at all price points! Come shop the largest weekly vintage market in Toronto.","description":"Get ready for the ultimate weekend treasure hunt! The Sunday Variety Market is now open every Saturday and Sunday, bringing the city’s biggest and most exciting market experience to life each week. Discover over 75 incredible vendors—dive into vintage fashion from every era, luxury finds, one-of-a-kind handmade goods, unique gifts, antiques, collectibles, sparkling jewelry, and local gems you won’t find anywhere else. Shop vintage like a true Toronto insider under the iconic big white tent and experience the city’s most vibrant small business community in the heart of downtown! \n\nIf you’re looking for weekend plans in Toronto, don't miss this free event St. Lawrence Ma