 Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"af3f30db-bbfe-4be1-acbe-ab1c665b2a01","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"c5eef88b-0373-49f9-a22e-f55d831be31e","name":"Thorncliffe Park Women Community Bazaar","dates":[1778869800000,1779474600000,1780079400000,1780684200000,1781289000000,1781893800000,1782498600000,1783103400000,1783708200000,1784313000000,1784917800000,1785522600000,1786127400000,1786732200000,1787337000000,1787941800000,1788546600000,1789151400000,1789756200000,1790361000000,1790965800000,1791570600000],"start":"2026-05-15T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Burguess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York, ON M4H 1K8","lat":43.703975361240246,"lng":-79.34348238869404},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A grassroots women led organization dedicated to creating and implementing public space enhancement projects in the community of Thorncliffe Park. The community bazaar happens every Friday during from June to October. As vendors at our weekly markets, women from the neighbourhood are able to advance the skills and knowledge they already possess, and are provided with opportunities to gain new ones that can translate into better employment opportunities.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"fO6IaSWH7zDJNLIydPtWHA","website":"https://tpwomenscomm.org/our-community-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"6d6864df-e08b-4f05-9af1-86b32990c382","name":"Scarborough Farmers' Market","dates":[1780428600000,1781033400000,1781638200000,1782243000000,1782847800000,1783452600000,1784057400000,1784662200000,1785267000000,1785871800000,1786476600000,1787081400000,1787686200000,1788291000000,1788895800000,1789500600000,1790105400000,1790710200000,1791315000000],"start":"2026-06-02T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cynthia Lai - Rosebank Park","address":"1051 Progress Ave, Scarborough, ON M1B 5M2","lat":43.79259399732396,"lng":-79.23363880409994},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Our mission then, as it is now, is to bring nutrient-dense, fairly priced, culturally appropriate, fresh fruits, vegetables, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"3174f7c4-53b3-461e-918c-a6b6db3cf90f","name":"Allan Gardens Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1777730400000,1778335200000,1778940000000,1779544800000,1780149600000,1780754400000,1781359200000,1781964000000,1782568800000,1783173600000,1783778400000,1784383200000,1784988000000,1785592800000,1786197600000,1786802400000,1787407200000,1788012000000,1788616800000,1789221600000,1789826400000,1790431200000,1791036000000,1791640800000,1792245600000,1792850400000,1793455200000,1794063600000,1794668400000,1795273200000,1795878000000,1796482800000,1797087600000,1797692400000,1798297200000,1798902000000,1799506800000,1800111600000,1800716400000,1801321200000,1801926000000,1802530800000,1803135600000,1803740400000,1804345200000,1804950000000,1805551200000,1806156000000,1806760800000,1807365600000,1807970400000,1808575200000,1809180000000],"start":"2026-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Children's Conservatory","address":"19 Horticultural Ave, Toronto, ON, M5A 2P2","lat":43.661418998,"lng":-79.37480223},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate local food, community, and sustainable agriculture. Discover fresh produce, artisanal products, and small-scale producers - all while connecting with the people who grow and create them.We invite you to come meet the vendors, discover new favourites, and taste the heart of your community!\n\nThe Allan Gardens Farmers’ Market facilitates a direct exchange between local farmers, food producers, artisan makers, and consumers. Everything sold at the market (50%+1) must be grown, sourced, made, and/or prepared in Toronto and the surrounding  area—ensuring that every purchase supports your neighbourhood economy.\n\nJoin us year- round every Saturday from 10am-2pm, in the beautiful Allan Gardens Children’s Conservatory & Teaching Garden. ","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"1_2B-asoDqdvJSyiKMPiaQ","website":"https://www.friendsofallangardens.ca/saturday-farmers-market","tickets":null},{"id":"c6c5c28d-cb8f-491a-8753-6954d129f347","name":"Allan Gardens Saturday Farmers' Market","dates":[1777730400000,1778335200000,1778940000000,1779544800000,1780149600000,1780754400000,1781359200000,1781964000000,1782568800000,1783173600000,1783778400000,1784383200000,1784988000000,1785592800000,1786197600000,1786802400000,1787407200000,1788012000000,1788616800000,1789221600000,1789826400000,1790431200000,1791036000000,1791640800000,1792245600000,1792850400000,1793455200000,1794063600000,1794668400000,1795273200000,1795878000000,1796482800000,1797087600000,1797692400000,1798297200000,1798902000000,1799506800000,1800111600000,1800716400000,1801321200000,1801926000000,1802530800000,1803135600000,1803740400000,1804345200000,1804950000000,1805551200000,1806156000000,1806760800000,1807365600000,1807970400000,1808575200000,1809180000000],"start":"2026-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Children's Conservatory","address":"19 Horticultural Ave, Toronto, ON, M5A 2P2","lat":43.661418998,"lng":-79.37480223},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate local food, community, and sustainable agriculture. Discover fresh produce, artisanal products, and small-scale producers - all while connecting with the people who grow and create them.We invite you to come meet the vendors, discover new favourites, and taste the heart of your community!\n\nThe Allan Gardens Farmers’ Market facilitates a direct exchange between local farmers, food producers, artisan makers, and consumers. Everything sold at the market (50%+1) must be grown, sourced, made, and/or prepared in Toronto and the surrounding  area—ensuring that every purchase supports your neighbourhood economy.\n\nJoin us year- round every Saturday from 10am-2pm, in the beautiful Allan Gardens Children’s Conservatory & Teaching Garden. ","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"1_2B-asoDqdvJSyiKMPiaQ","website":"https://www.friendsofallangardens.ca/saturday-farmers-market","tickets":null},{"id":"5398f5ff-ce19-47eb-9b63-9d7feb10fb86","name":"Withrow Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000],"start":"2026-05-30T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Withrow Park ","address":"725 Logan Ave, Toronto, ON M4K 3B9","lat":43.67657084103454,"lng":-79.34742988876354},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Just steps from Danforth Avenue in vibrant Greektown, Withrow Park Farmers’ Market bursts to life every season! Since 2006, it’s been the go-to destination for fresh food, lively music, local art, and a joyful sense of community—celebrating the best of Toronto while championing local farmers, producers, and artisans.\n\nFrom June to October, the park transforms into a buzzing hub of delicious discoveries and vibrant connection. We’re passionate about creating an inclusive, sustainable, and community-powered market where every visit is an adventure—and everyone’s welcome!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"L8DDBTjIOMKrxChhtduF6Q","website":"https://withrowmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"d5861690-2a78-4168-bea8-549ceacf5e95","name":"Withrow Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1780146000000,1780750800000,1781355600000,1781960400000,1782565200000,1783170000000,1783774800000,1784379600000,1784984400000,1785589200000,1786194000000,1786798800000,1787403600000,1788008400000,1788613200000,1789218000000,1789822800000,1790427600000,1791032400000,1791637200000,1792242000000,1792846800000],"start":"2026-05-30T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Withrow Park ","address":"725 Logan Ave, Toronto, ON M4K 3B9","lat":43.67657084103454,"lng":-79.34742988876354},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Just steps from Danforth Avenue in vibrant Greektown, Withrow Park Farmers’ Market bursts to life every season! Since 2006, it’s been the go-to destination for fresh food, lively music, local art, and a joyful sense of community—celebrating the best of Toronto while championing local farmers, producers, and artisans.\n\nFrom June to October, the park transforms into a buzzing hub of delicious discoveries and vibrant connection. We’re passionate about creating an inclusive, sustainable, and community-powered market where every visit is an adventure—and everyone’s welcome!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"L8DDBTjIOMKrxChhtduF6Q","website":"https://withrowmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"308b8d81-df17-4914-b23a-66a764c7f753","name":"Market 707","dates":[1779462000000,1779548400000,1779807600000,1779894000000,1779980400000,1780066800000,1780153200000,1780412400000,1780498800000,1780585200000,1780671600000,1780758000000,1781017200000,1781103600000,1781190000000,1781276400000,1781362800000,1781622000000,1781708400000,1781794800000,1781881200000,1781967600000,1782226800000,1782313200000,1782399600000,1782486000000,1782572400000,1782831600000,1782918000000,1783004400000,1783090800000,1783177200000,1783436400000,1783522800000,1783609200000,1783695600000,1783782000000,1784041200000,1784127600000,1784214000000,1784300400000,1784386800000,1784646000000,1784732400000,1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785250800000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785855600000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786460400000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1787065200000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787670000000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788274800000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000],"start":"2026-05-22T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scadding Court Community Centre","address":"707 Dundas St W, Toronto, ON M5T 2W6","lat":43.651713739404556,"lng":-79.40508261942017},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Market 707 is a stretch of sidewalk near Dundas and Bathurst lined with upcycled shipping containers that offer sweet and savoury foods, services, and everything in between. \n\nPresided over by the Scadding Court Community Centre, this impromptu open-air pedestrian mall has one of the most eclectic collection of startup businesses in the city.","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"oa2xxPdB_5ibesOE3pMKmA","website":"https://mkt707.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"30312fd8-f50b-447c-bded-37b5e2154429","name":"Underpass Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1778788800000,1779393600000,1779998400000,1780603200000,1781208000000,1781812800000,1782417600000,1783022400000,1783627200000,1784232000000,1784836800000,1785441600000,1786046400000,1786651200000,1787256000000,1787860800000,1788465600000,1789070400000,1789675200000,1790280000000,1790884800000,1791489600000,1792094400000],"start":"2026-05-14T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Underpass Park","address":"29 Lower River Street, Toronto, ON M5A 1M6","lat":43.65585,"lng":-79.354586},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the magic of Underpass Park Farmers' Market—a vibrant gem in Toronto's Corktown and one of the city's most unique farmers market destinations! Surrounded by colorful murals from local artists, this lively outdoor market bursts with farm-fresh fruits and vegetables, mouthwatering baked goods, homemade preserves, and a tempting selection of artisanal treats.\n\nFrom May to October—rain or shine—this pet-friendly hotspot invites you to soak up live music, browse the stalls, and mingle with adorable pups for a truly unforgettable market experience.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"w3Jiy9MEVv3kfA1fQck79w","website":"https://underpassparkmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"35e1db4e-7e14-401c-9c00-6d28d0395682","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200000,1787598000000,1788202800000,1788807600000,1789412400000,1790017200000,1790622000000,1791226800000,1791831600000,1792436400000,1793041200000],"start":"2026-05-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sorauren Park","address":"50 Wabash Ave, Toronto, ON M6R 1N2, Canada","lat":43.648147722995105,"lng":-79.44310115767041},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This year round farmers' Market operates during the outdoor season, we operate in Sorauren Park which is a beautiful greenspace managed by the City of Toronto and animated by community group, Friends of Sorauren Park. Along with the Farmers’ Market, you’ll find an ice skating rink, dog walking park, community pizza oven, children’s soccer and baseball programmes and even movie nights and an annual pumpkin parade!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"pratsPJvmGxDUcIhkbTofA","website":"https://www.soraurenmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"cdbbcc89-579a-465c-9de8-e3640ffd4c20","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200000,1787598000000,1788202800000,1788807600000,1789412400000,1790017200000,1790622000000,1791226800000,1791831600000,1792436400000,1793041200000],"start":"2026-05-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sorauren Park","address":"50 Wabash Ave, Toronto, ON M6R 1N2, Canada","lat":43.648147722995105,"lng":-79.44310115767041},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This year round farmers' Market operates during the outdoor season, we operate in Sorauren Park which is a beautiful greenspace managed by the City of Toronto and animated by community group, Friends of Sorauren Park. Along with the Farmers’ Market, you’ll find an ice skating rink, dog walking park, community pizza oven, children’s soccer and baseball programmes and even movie nights and an annual pumpkin parade!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"pratsPJvmGxDUcIhkbTofA","website":"https://www.soraurenmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"408e3f2b-38a7-4474-bfe1-410a1e63d2ce","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200000,1787598000000,1788202800000,1788807600000,1789412400000,1790017200000,1790622000000,1791226800000,1791831600000,1792436400000,1793041200000],"start":"2026-05-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sorauren Park","address":"50 Wabash Ave, Toronto, ON M6R 1N2, Canada","lat":43.648147722995105,"lng":-79.44310115767041},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This year round farmers' Market operates during the outdoor season, we operate in Sorauren Park which is a beautiful greenspace managed by the City of Toronto and animated by community group, Friends of Sorauren Park. Along with the Farmers’ Market, you’ll find an ice skating rink, dog walking park, community pizza oven, children’s soccer and baseball programmes and even movie nights and an annual pumpkin parade!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"pratsPJvmGxDUcIhkbTofA","website":"https://www.soraurenmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"52c10bee-d04f-4373-af25-47b50862c188","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"21bc7050-579e-4dcb-b0ef-af70e18d1e7d","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"b6919605-47e1-4b7a-8346-721cf8a76afb","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"fa21dc1c-cb2a-498c-b419-f0ff54f2c080","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00"