driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"e24cd54b-62be-4988-8009-e785fb53e224","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"9649f95a-fcdb-4332-b9c3-b91cc331c1f5","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"8f65e3fd-2f65-438c-bf3b-e210d0195647","name":"Black Creek Farm Stand & Market","dates":[1781805600000,1782410400000,1783015200000,1783620000000,1784224800000,1784829600000,1785434400000,1786039200000,1786644000000,1787248800000,1787853600000,1788458400000,1789063200000,1789668000000,1790272800000,1790877600000,1791482400000,1792087200000,1792692000000,1793296800000],"start":"2026-06-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Black Creek Community Farm","address":"4929 Jane St, North York, ON M3N 2K8","lat":43.774639106068285,"lng":-79.52128184272664},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week during the growing season, we stock our on-site farm stand with freshly harvested produce from our fields. We ensure a weekly selection that highlights peak seasonal crops. Purchasing from our farm stand is a great way to support BCCF and enjoy delicious Toronto-grown produce.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NRVKLaN_ro4wSC8_vXcsRA","website":"https://blackcreekfarm.ca/en/programs-and-activities/farm-stand-markets","tickets":null},{"id":"258c0c27-3eac-4c44-95cc-8732e438c0d1","name":"Dufferin Grove Farmers' Market","dates":[1779390000000,1779994800000,1780599600000,1781204400000,1781809200000,1782414000000,1783018800000,1783623600000,1784228400000,1784833200000,1785438000000,1786042800000,1786647600000,1787252400000,1787857200000,1788462000000,1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000],"start":"2026-05-21T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Dufferin Grove Park","address":"875 Dufferin St, Toronto","lat":43.657042,"lng":-79.433601},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience one of Toronto’s oldest and most vibrant year-round farmers’ markets! The Dufferin Grove Market is bursting with fresh food, passionate local farmers, and a lively sense of community. Shoppers can connect, explore, and savor the beautiful ecosystem—right in the heart of Dufferin Grove Park.\n\nEvery visit brings something new—enjoy live music, free workshops, clothing swaps, creative children’s activities, and even the occasional surprise appearance by the park’s famous squirrels. Don’t miss out on the fun!","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"rvUZNU7wbq8BeE2wpx1azQ","website":"https://www.dufferingrovemarket.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"a5bd7349-a697-4d4a-bd8a-c47dd1bb3511","name":"Dufferin Grove Farmers' Market","dates":[1779390000000,1779994800000,1780599600000,1781204400000,1781809200000,1782414000000,1783018800000,1783623600000,1784228400000,1784833200000,1785438000000,1786042800000,1786647600000,1787252400000,1787857200000,1788462000000,1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000],"start":"2026-05-21T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Dufferin Grove Park","address":"875 Dufferin St, Toronto","lat":43.657042,"lng":-79.433601},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience one of Toronto’s oldest and most vibrant year-round farmers’ markets! The Dufferin Grove Market is bursting with fresh food, passionate local farmers, and a lively sense of community. Shoppers can connect, explore, and savor the beautiful ecosystem—right in the heart of Dufferin Grove Park.\n\nEvery visit brings something new—enjoy live music, free workshops, clothing swaps, creative children’s activities, and even the occasional surprise appearance by the park’s famous squirrels. Don’t miss out on the fun!","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"rvUZNU7wbq8BeE2wpx1azQ","website":"https://www.dufferingrovemarket.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"8d66d3ee-47a7-4d68-aa28-dd7159f7c8ac","