00000,1781119800000,1781724600000,1782329400000,1782934200000,1783539000000,1784143800000,1784748600000,1785353400000,1785958200000,1786563000000,1787167800000,1787772600000,1788377400000,1788982200000,1789587000000,1790191800000,1790796600000,1791401400000],"start":"2026-06-03T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-07T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Robertson Parkette- 1549 Danforth Avenue at Coxwell Avenue ","address":"Robertson Parkette- 1549 Danforth Avenue at Coxwell Avenue ","lat":43.683008,"lng":-79.324328},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy local, farm-fresh Ontario produce, freshly baked loaves, pastries, Grab and Go treats and so much more at the Robertson Parkette\nThe Courtyard Farmers' Markets celebrates our third season in the community🍎  \n\nThank you!  Continued blessings!  \nOne💖!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","Live Performances","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"KhfKbq6xgZXAO1Cqc_Z-Og","website":"https://courtyardfarmersmkt.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"036d0a85-827c-4e9d-b74c-634d4745bb4d","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting there is easy with the free shuttle bus picking up next to Broadview Station or take the TTC's 28 bus from Davisville Station.\n\nThe farmers' market is operated by Evergreen, a national non-profit transforming public spaces in our cities to build a healthier future for people and our planet.","categories":["Environmental","Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"g_7hN7bS9geSUWTPQPVycA","website":"https://www.evergreen.ca/evergreen-brick-work/activities/saturday-farmers-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"8292d1ef-f273-48c6-b292-8ac3ec9dc6fb","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"2fba1233-0d65-412b-a391-c7b74d28f01e","name":"The Leslieville Farmers' Market","dates":[1778418000000,1779022800000,1779627600000,1780232400000,1780837200000,1781442000000,1782046800000,1782651600000,1783256400000,1783861200000,1784466000000,1785070800000,1785675600000,1786280400000,1786885200000,1787490000000,1788094800000,1788699600000,1789304400000,1789909200000,1790514000000,1791118800000,1791723600000,1792328400000,1792933200000],"start":"2026-05-10T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Greenwood Park","address":"150 Greenwood Ave, Toronto","lat":43.669638096,"lng":-79.328165388},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week, the Market brings together local farmers, food producers, artisans, small businesses, live music, and community programming for a lively Sunday gathering in the park.\n\nCome eat, dance, picnic and spend the day in beautiful Greenwood Park while supporting local food systems, small businesses, and community connection in Toronto’s east end! \n\nThe Leslieville Farmers’ Market is a non-profit outdoor farmers’ market held every Sunday in Greenwood Park from May to October. From November to May, the Market moves indoors to the East End Food Hub, with a short winter break in January and February.\n\nSee you Sunday!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"CzJE0RU9YcS__qOfyUvUWA","website":"https://www.leslievillemarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"e9ebd346-e03a-40c2-ac82-7c2a19cafe63","name":"Sunday Variety Market","dates":[1779544800000,1779631200000,1780149600000,1780236000000,1780754400000,1780840800000,1781359200000,1781445600000,1781964000000,1782050400000,1782568800000,1782655200000,1783173600000,1783260000000,1783778400000,1783864800000,1784383200000,1784469600000,1784988000000,1785074400000,1785592800000,1785679200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793455200000,1793545200000,1794063600000,1794150000000,1794668400000,1794754800000,1795273200000,1795359600000,1795878000000,1795964400000,1796482800000,1796569200000,1797087600000,1797174000000,1797692400000,1797778800000],"start":"2026-05-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"St. Lawrence Market (Big White Tent)","address":"125 The Esplanade, Toronto","lat":43.647946,"lng":-79.371229},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Great finds to be discovered at all price points! Come shop the largest weekly vintage market in Toronto.","description":"Get ready for the ultimate weekend treasure hunt! The Sunday Variety Market is now open every Saturday and Sunday, bringing the city’s biggest and most exciting market experience to life each week. Discover over 75 incredible vendors—dive into vintage fashion from every era, luxury finds, one-of-a-kind handmade goods, unique gifts, antiques, collectibles, sparkling jewelry, and local gems you won’t find anywhere else. Shop vintage like a true Toronto insider under the iconic big white tent and experience the city’s most vibrant small business community in the heart of downtown! \n\nIf you’re looking for weekend plans in Toronto, don't miss this free event St. Lawrence Market - Toronto's most historic cultural d