ry era, luxury finds, one-of-a-kind handmade goods, unique gifts, antiques, collectibles, sparkling jewelry, and local gems you won’t find anywhere else. Shop vintage like a true Toronto insider under the iconic big white tent and experience the city’s most vibrant small business community in the heart of downtown! \n\nIf you’re looking for weekend plans in Toronto, don't miss this free event St. Lawrence Market - Toronto's most historic cultural destination.","categories":["Artisan","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"YqzGtnbNKm7C1gKMGjRdVA","website":"https://sundayvariety.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"6b57eb57-d353-4bc4-8e81-d56f7000d56f","name":"Scarborough Farmers' Market","dates":[1780428600000,1781033400000,1781638200000,1782243000000,1782847800000,1783452600000,1784057400000,1784662200000,1785267000000,1785871800000,1786476600000,1787081400000,1787686200000,1788291000000,1788895800000,1789500600000,1790105400000,1790710200000,1791315000000],"start":"2026-06-02T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cynthia Lai - Rosebank Park","address":"1051 Progress Ave, Scarborough, ON M1B 5M2","lat":43.79259399732396,"lng":-79.23363880409994},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Our mission then, as it is now, is to bring nutrient-dense, fairly priced, culturally appropriate, fresh fruits, vegetables, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"1c3a2a8d-29af-43da-970f-5a1f37d0d4e6","name":"Eglinton Way BIA Farmers' Market","dates":[1780833600000,1781438400000,1782043200000,1782648000000,1783252800000,1783857600000,1784462400000,1785067200000,1785672000000,1786276800000,1786881600000,1787486400000,1788091200000,1788696000000,1789300800000,1789905600000,1790510400000,1791115200000,1791720000000,1792324800000,1792929600000],"start":"2026-06-07T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Green P Parking Lot #47","address":"125 Burnaby Blvd, Toronto","lat":43.70439991,"lng":-79.412600977},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Now in its 9th year, The Eglinton Way BIA Farmers' Market has become a staple Sunday event in Midtown Toronto dedicated to strengthening and promoting the connections between our community and Ontario farms, local artisans and small businesses. With 40+ vendors this season, find everything from fresh meat, eggs and produce, to baked goods, food & drink, household goods, arts, crafts and more! Our market features live music, free kids' activities, and special activations that are perfect for all ages. Follow us on Instagram at @EglintonWay for more information and updates!","categories":["Artisan","Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"uR4r0FHNt-y4Xe6-SE_U-g","website":"https://www.theeglintonway.com/farmersmarket","tickets":null},{"id":"762874c3-6466-4288-a888-3574a8b6d319","name":"Eglinton Way BIA Farmers' Market","dates":[1780833600000,1781438400000,1782043200000,1782648000000,1783252800000,1783857600000,1784462400000,1785067200000,1785672000000,1786276800000,1786881600000,1787486400000,1788091200000,1788696000000,1789300800000,1789905600000,1790510400000,17911