0","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A vibrant weekly market celebrating local creators, delicious food & community\nHandmade Goods • Antiques • Vintage • Family-friendly\n\nSupport local. Shop small. Eat fresh.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"BomI95CaiWtmNfhqDjDNLg","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"54bd254a-d511-4e03-9e35-eb86751ee225","name":"Downsview Park Merchants Market","dates":[1779544800000,1779631200000,1780149600000,1780236000000,1780754400000,1780840800000,1781359200000,1781445600000,1781964000000,1782050400000,1782568800000,1782655200000,1783173600000,1783260000000,1783778400000,1783864800000,1784383200000,1784469600000,1784988000000,1785074400000,1785592800000,1785679200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793455200000,1793545200000,1794063600000,1794150000000,1794668400000,1794754800000,1795273200000,1795359600000,1795878000000,1795964400000,1796482800000,1796569200000,1797087600000,1797174000000,1797692400000,1797778800000,1798297200000,1798383600000,1798902000000,1798988400000,1799506800000,1799593200000,1800111600000,1800198000000,1800716400000,1800802800000,1801321200000,1801407600000,1801926000000,1802012400000,1802530800000,1802617200000,1803135600000,1803222000000,1803740400000,1803826800000,1804345200000,1804431600000,1804950000000,1805032800000,1805551200000,1805637600000,1806156000000,1806242400000,1806760800000,1806847200000,1807365600000,1807452000000,1807970400000,1808056800000,1808575200000,1808661600000,1809180000000,1809266400000],"start":"2026-05-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"40 Carl Hall Rd","address":"40 Carl Hall Rd, North York, ON, M3K 2C1","lat":43.7483766822,"lng":-79.4791132214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Downsview Park Merchants Market is one of Toronto’s vibrant weekend destinations, offering a dynamic indoor marketplace experience for shoppers of all ages. Located in North York, the market features a diverse mix of local vendors offering clothing, accessories, home goods, beauty products, electronics, toys, collectibles, gifts, fresh produce, specialty items, and incredible deals. Visitors can also explore the farmers market section featuring fresh fruits, vegetables, and locally sourced goods, alongside an international food court offering a variety of delicious global cuisines and authentic flavours. With a lively, family-friendly atmosphere, the market is a perfect destination for bargain hunters, families, food lovers, and those looking to support local and small businesses. Open every Saturday and Sunday from 10 AM to 5 PM, Downsview Park Merchants Market combines shopping, food, culture, and community into one exciting weekend experience in Toronto.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"HsINX9unS5aRBvcRR5D6QA","website":"https://www.dpmarket.com","tickets":null},{"id":"153215eb-40a5-45f5-a8e7-c4a3f1841978","name":"Threads of Connection and Conversation","dates":[1788444000000,1788530400000,1788616800000,1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000],"start":"2026-09-03T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-01T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall Gallery","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.59766044,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fleeting moments and beauty of urban life captured through visual storytelling inviting viewers to pause, connect and reflect. Anchored in connection, this exhibition preserves the essence of human interwovenness. By Isabel Fryszberg, Janna Robins Walters and Poonam Khanna.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":null,"image":"o43cyz0H12nVokwP81Ppeg","website":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/threads-of-connection-tickets-1991387960998?aff=oddtdtcreator","tickets":null},{"id":"fe409a44-1314-4234-a21c-d370e6efe76d","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting there is easy with the free shuttle bus picking up next to Broadview Station or take the TTC's 28 bus from Davisville Station.\n\nThe farmers' market is operated by Evergreen, a national non-profit transforming public spaces in our cities to build a healthier future for people and our planet.","categories":["Environmental","Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"g_7hN7bS9geSUWTPQPVycA","website":"https://www.evergreen.ca/evergreen-brick-work/activities/saturday-farmers-market/","tickets":null},{"id":"f48bb264-3aff-47f7-9c83-f0292fb5d691","name":"Saturday Farmers' Market at Evergreen Brick Works","dates":[1777723200000,1778328000000,1778932800000,1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000],"start":"2026-05-02T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783,"lng":-79.365628},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Toronto’s largest year-round farmers' market. Shop fresh, seasonal produce, artisanal goods and locally prepared foods from Ontario farmers and small businesses.\n\nGrab a coffee, wander through a vibrant market bursting with peak-season flavours and one-of-a-kind finds, and then enjoy a delicious brunch. Held in an open-air pavilion, the market runs rain or shine. Stick around to enjoy a free guided tour of the historic brick factory, take a stroll around the ponds and nearby nature trails or explore the Children's Garden. Getting ther