 in the beautiful Allan Gardens Children’s Conservatory & Teaching Garden. ","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"1_2B-asoDqdvJSyiKMPiaQ","website":"https://www.friendsofallangardens.ca/saturday-farmers-market","tickets":null},{"id":"b97954c5-dd36-4973-9bb3-2ded25904c3e","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"bc68a8d1-c4fd-4a78-b734-503c84120119","name":"The Stop Farmers' Market @ Wychwood Barns Park","dates":[1779537600000,1780142400000,1780747200000,1781352000000,1781956800000,1782561600000,1783166400000,1783771200000,1784376000000,1784980800000,1785585600000,1786190400000,1786795200000,1787400000000,1788004800000,1788609600000,1789214400000,1789819200000,1790424000000,1791028800000,1791633600000,1792238400000,1792843200000,1793448000000,1794056400000,1794661200000,1795266000000,1795870800000,1796475600000,1797080400000,1797685200000],"start":"2026-05-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-19T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns Park","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring 35+ weekly vendors, the market brings together local farmers, food producers, and neighbours to increase access to healthy food in ways that build community. A program of The Stop Community Food Centre, the market supports both emerging and established small-scale producers while strengthening a resilient local food economy through responsibly grown and produced food. The market is committed to affordability, supporting racialized vendors, and creating welcoming, community-driven public spaces. Reflecting the diverse cultures of the neighbourhood and the broader GTA, the market celebrates the many food traditions that make Toronto vibrant.\n\nCome visit and support our year-round community market operating every Saturday in the Bathurst–St. Clair neighbourhood.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WHwqoysoRgdbIoHAZWiAw","website":"https://www.thestop.org/farmersmarket/","tickets":null},{"id":"c5c3c9a6-95f9-438c-922c-17720e5a7897","name":"Malvern Farmers' Market","dates":[1781121600000,1781726400000,1782331200000,1782936000000,1783540800000,1784145600000,1784750400000,1785355200000,1785960000000,1786564800000,1787169600000,1787774400000,1788379200000,1788984000000,1789588800000,1790193600000,1790798400000,1791403200000,1792008000000],"start":"2026-06-10T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Malvern F","address":"90 Littles Rd, Scarborough, ON M1B 5E2","lat":43.81863198739519,"lng":-79.2054285862019},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fresh, local food at the heart of the neighbourhood Every Wednesday evening from June to October, a weekly space for connection, culture, and community-grown food.\n\nThe market features:\n-Produce grown at Malvern Urban Farm by local farmers\n-Hot meals from community restaurants and caterers\n-Family-friendly activities and information tables\n-Seasonal events and neighbourhood updates\n‍\nThe market is more than a place to shop. It is where stories are shared, flavours are celebrated, and residents reconnect with the land and each other.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Jh5madSLtr7021cfDf95IQ","website":"https://www.mfrc.org/urban-agriculture-and-food-programs","tickets":null},{"id":"42f3b4e9-0994-4a23-a9a1-25d52f8c48cd","name":"Underpass Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1778788800000,1779393600000,1779998400000,1780603200000,1781208000000,1781812800000,1782417600000,1783022400000,1783627200000,1784232000000,1784836800000,1785441600000,1786046400000,1786651200000,1787256000000,1787860800000,1788465600000,1789070400000,1789675200000,1790280000000,1790884800000,1791489600000,1792094400000],"start":"2026-05-14T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Underpass Park","address":"29 Lower River Street, Toronto, ON M5A 1M6","lat":43.65585,"lng":-79.354586},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the magic of Underpass Park Farmers' Market—a vibrant gem in Toronto's Corktown and one of the city's most unique farmers market destinations! Surrounded by colorful murals from local artists, this lively outdoor market bursts with farm-fresh fruits and vegetables, mouthwatering baked goods, homemade preserves, and a tempting selection of artisanal treats.\n\nFrom May to October—rain or shine—this pet-friendly hotspot invites you to soak up live music, browse the stalls, and mingle with adorable pups for a truly unforgettable market experience.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"w3Jiy9MEVv3kfA1fQck79w","website":"https://underpassparkmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"6edb7e32-248d-44e4-a05b-bedb3f9be93d","name":"Underpass Park Farmers' Market","dates":[1778788800000,1779393600000,1779998400000,1780603200000,1781208000000,1781812800000,1782417600000,1783022400000,1783627200000,1784232000000,1784836800000,1785441600000,1786046400000,1786651200000,1787256000000,1787860800000,1788465600000,1789070400000,1789675200000,1790280000000,1790884800000,1791489600000,1792094400000],"start":"2026-05-14T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Underpass Park","address":"29 Lower River Street, Toronto, ON M5A 1M6","lat":43.65585,"lng":-79.354586},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the magic of Underpass Park Farmers' Market—a vibrant gem in Toronto's Corktown and one of the city's most unique farmers market destinations! Surrounded by colorful murals from local artists, this lively outdoor market bursts with farm-fresh fruits and vegetables, mouthwatering baked goods, homemade preserves, and a tempting selection of artisanal treats.\n\nFrom May to October—rain or shine—this pet-friendly hotspot invites you to soak up live music, browse the stalls, and mingle with adorable pups for a truly unforgettable market experience.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"w3Jiy9MEVv3kfA1fQck79w","website":"https://underpassparkmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"3365b1bf-6cec-4fd8-9688-bf3832ca9828","name":"Sorauren Farmers' Market","dates":[1777921200000,1778526000000,1779130800000,1779735600000,1780340400000,1780945200000,1781550000000,1782154800000,1782759600000,1783364400000,1783969200000,1784574000000,1785178800000,1785783600000,1786388400000,1786993200000,1787598000000,1788202800000,1788807600000,1789412400000,1790017200000,1790622000000,1791226800000,1791831600000,1792436400000,1793041200000],"start":"2026-05-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-26T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sorauren Park","address":"50 Wabash Ave, Toronto, ON M6R 1N2, Canada","lat":43.648147722995105,"lng":-79.44310115767041},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This year round farmers' Market operates during the outdoor season, we operate in Sorauren Park which is a beautiful greenspace managed by the City of Toronto and animated by community group, Friends of Sorauren Park. Along with the Farmers’ Market, you’ll find an ice skating rink, dog walking park, community pizza oven, children’s soccer and baseball programmes and even movie nights and an annual pumpkin parade!","categories":["Farmers' Market","Food/Culinary","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"pratsPJvmGxDUcIhkbTofA","website":"https://www.soraurenmarket.com/","tickets":null},{"id":"6ee6422f-57e6-450a-ad34-f4b215889591","name":"Dufferin Grove Farmers' Market","dates":[1779390000000,1779994800000,1780599600000,1781204400000,1781809200000,1782414000000,1783018800000,1783623600000,1784228400000,1784833200000,1785438000000,1786042800000,1786647600000,1787252400000,1787857200000,1788462000000,1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000],"start":"2026-05-21T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Dufferin Grove Park","address":"875 Dufferin St, Toronto","lat":43.657042,"lng":-79.433601},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience one of Toronto’s oldest and most vibrant year-round farmers’ markets! The Dufferin Grove Market is bursting with fresh food, passionate local farmers, and a lively sense of community. Shoppers can connect, explore, and savor the beautiful ecosystem—right in the heart of Dufferin Grove Park.\n\nEvery visit brings something new—enjoy live music, free workshops, clothing swaps, creative children’s activities, and even the occasional surprise appearance by the park’s famous squirrels. Don’t miss out on the fun!","categories":["Farmers' Market"],"presenter":null,"image":"rvUZNU7wbq8BeE2wpx1azQ","website":"https://www.dufferingrovemarket.ca","tickets":null},{"id":"994a34b6-4824-4efd-a49a-b257ea2b5b45","name":"Dufferin Grove Farmers' Market","dates":[1779390000000,1779994800000,1780599600000,1781204400000,1781809200000,1782414000000,1783018800000,1783623600000,1784228400000,1784833200000,1785438000000,1786042800000,1786647600000,1787252400000,1787857200000,1788462000000,1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000],"start":"2026-05-21T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Dufferin Grove Park","address":"875 Dufferin St, Toronto","lat":43.657042,"lng":-79.433601},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience one of Toronto’s oldest and most vibrant year-round farmers’ markets! The Dufferin Grove Market is bursting with fresh food, passionate local farmers, and a lively sense of community. Shoppers can connect, explore, and savor the beautiful ecosystem—right in the heart of Dufferin Grove Park.\n\nEvery visit brings something new—enjoy live music, free workshops, clothing swaps, creative children’s activities, and even the occasional surprise appearance by the park’s famous squirrels. Don’t miss out on the fun!","ca