te":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"70a1ab1b-5257-4c51-88f7-bed2d3900c91","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"669bf0a0-c700-46ba-9642-0ed9928d88c0","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"4186dc35-5317-4ce4-8bb2-3306e10ee32b","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"dcb1d681-902b-46ac-a7d9-8ad94d7d0332","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"7a976857-1346-4625-ac39-cab711ef95b6","name":"Black Creek Farm Stand & Market","dates":[1781805600000,1782410400000,1783015200000,1783620000000,1784224800000,1784829600000,1785434400000,1786039200000,1786644000000,1787248800000,1787853600000,1788458400000,1789063200000,1789668000000,1790272800000,1790877600000,1791482400000,1792087200000,1792692000000,1793296800000],"start":"2026-06-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Black Creek Community Farm","address":"4929 Jane St, North York, ON M3N 2K8","lat":43.774639106068285,"lng":-79.52128184272664},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week during the growing season, we stock our on-site farm stand with freshly harvested produce from our fields. We ensure a weekly selection that highlights peak seasonal crops. Purchasing from our farm stand is a great way to support BCCF and enjoy delicious Toronto-grown produce.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NRVKLaN_ro4wSC8_vXcsRA","website":"https://blackcreekfarm.ca/en/programs-and-activities/farm-stand-markets","tickets":null},{"id":"77dc4c5a-f322-48e2-bf76-c3c6fd9673d3","name":"Black Creek Farm Stand & Market","dates":[1781805600000,1782410400000,1783015200000,1783620000000,1784224800000,1784829600000,1785434400000,1786039200000,1786644000000,1787248800000,1787853600000,1788458400000,1789063200000,1789668000000,1790272800000,1790877600000,1791482400000,1792087200000,1792692000000,1793296800000],"start":"2026-06-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Black Creek Community Farm","address":"4929 Jane St, North York, ON M3N 2K8","lat":43.774639106068285,"lng":-79.52128184272664},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each week during the growing season, we stock our on-site farm stand with freshly harvested produce from our fields. We ensure a weekly selection that highlights peak seasonal crops. Purchasing from our farm stand is a great way to support BCCF and enjoy delicious Toronto-grown produce.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"NRVKLaN_ro4wSC8_vXcsRA","website":"https://blackcreekfarm.ca/en/programs-and-activities/farm-stand-markets","tickets":null},{"id":"767acc39-406a-4fce-b4d5-184f6e1193dd","name":"Scarborough Farmers' Market","dates":[1780428600000,1781033400000,1781638200000,1782243000000,1782847800000,1783452600000,1784057400000,1784662200000,1785267000000,1785871800000,1786476600000,1787081400000,1787686200000,1788291000000,1788895800000,1789500600000,1790105400000,1790710200000,1791315000000],"start":"2026-06-02T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cynthia Lai - Rosebank Park","address":"1051 Progress Ave, Scarborough, ON M1B 5M2","lat":43.79259399732396,"lng":-79.23363880409994},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Our mission then, as it is now, is to bring nutrient-dense, fairly priced, culturally appropriate, fresh fruits, vegetables, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"faaeb5a2-1b87-4503-9bfe-ceef16b658da","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"42ddcd93-b4d5-4f74-ac19-91c4ff45e1a8","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"d21ff999-ed95-4bdc-ad1c-69269b07642d","name":"Scarborough Farmers' Market","dates":[1780428600000,1781033400000,1781638200000,1782243000000,1782847800000,1783452600000,1784057400000,1784662200000,1785267000000,1785871800000,1786476600000,1787081400000,1787686200000,1788291000000,1788895800000,1789500600000,1790105400000,1790710200000,1791315000000],"start":"2026-06-02T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cynthia Lai - Rosebank Park","address":"1051 Progress Ave, Scarborough, ON M1B 5M2","lat":43.79259399732396,"lng":-79.23363880409994},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Our mission then, as it is now, is to bring nutrient-dense, fairly priced, culturally appropriate, fresh fruits, vegetables, and lifestyle products to the people of Scarborough.\n \nOur vendor team consists of family-owned farms, women-led enterprises, and ethno-cultural businesses that represent the true diversity and richness of Toronto, the most multicultural city in the world.\n \nIn keeping with the Toronto Food Strategy, the Scarborough Farmers' Market aims to make fresh local food, and nutrition information accessible to all. \nWe partner with Feeding the City Laboratory at the University of Toronto Scarborough to inform researchers how alternative food distribution is practiced by and for Scarborough community members.","categories":["Farmers' Market","Other"],"presenter":" Red Onion Events & Vision Quest Event Management","image":"opMdrjjDdedtZ9TK-_ML4Q","website":"https://www.scarboroughfarmersmarket.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"e3050230-5e80-49b4-8a9c-65c543a13b6e","name":"Scarborough Farmers' Market","dates":[1780428600000,1781033400000,1781638200000,1782243000000,1782847800000,1783452600000,1784057400000,1784662200000,1785267000000,1785871800000,1786476600000,1787081400000,1787686200000,1788291000000,1788895800000,1789500600000,1790105400000,1790710200000,1791315000000],"start":"2026-06-02T15:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T15:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cynthia Lai - Rosebank Park",