chess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"a21f2731-1b1d-4504-94b2-462cde77dcd6","name":"Pasta Party!","dates":[1788559200000,1793397600000],"start":"2026-09-04T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Le Dolci Culinary School","address":"12 Sousa Mendes St, Toronto, ON, M6P 0A8","lat":43.661026575,"lng":-79.453333936},"free":false,"low":169,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an unforgettable hands-on culinary experience celebrating the art of Italian cooking!\n\nIn this 2-course Italian class, guests will learn how to craft a traditional pasta dish from scratch, paired with a simple, flavourful sauce, and finish the experience by creating a classic tiramisu for dessert.\n\nWhether you are a pasta lover or a dessert enthusiast, this class blends authentic Italian techniques and fresh ingredients, all in a fun, interactive setting.  \n\nPerfect for foodies, date nights or anyone looking to bring a taste of Italy home!","categories":["Food/Culinary","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Le Dolci Culinary School","image":"gu7PLNgQVjzPvgxVRChRzQ","website":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/pasta-party?_pos=1&_psq=Pasta+Parties&_psid=703ad19ca&_ss=e&_v=1.0","tickets":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/pasta-party?_pos=1&_psq=Pasta+Parties&_psid=703ad19ca&_ss=e&_v=1.0"},{"id":"37096cb4-f527-4b85-a31b-8e5be64181b4","name":"GATHER in Toronto Exhibition","dates":[1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785078000000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785682800000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786287600000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1786892400000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787497200000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000],"start":"2026-07-23T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front Street East, 2nd floor","lat":43.649129,"lng":-79.371765},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come learn about ways we move through the world, honouring the land, our stories and each other, celebrating triumphs in our journeys, strengthening fibres in our connectedness. It is within this sacred act of coming together that we find common values, building a unified vision for our future.\n \nListen to local sports origin stories alongside artistic reflections on identity, resilience, and belonging through works that highlight the power of connection across cultures and communities.\n \nThe exhibition features documentaries on Deskaheh, Herb Carnegie, and the St. Christopher House Lacrosse Organization; contemporary art by Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"b5f23706-a5ba-4282-a54c-00fab09a5f27","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tanya Marcuse’s multichannel video Portent presents ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"0098c337-4c67-4a4c-b7f4-a9ba16401b42","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tanya Marcuse’s multichannel video Portent presents ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame re