,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"30ca18f6-f729-4a8e-b84c-6512caed1073","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"563313f1-376f-431c-830d-65fc54b60d75","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"4d156e9f-14be-4ebf-943b-aa1ee450a4b1","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"9c57d614-4071-4a8f-8c6d-0825c2eba6fc","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"569b5e59-2807-4845-8722-1d744d232899","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"f9c44361-0c80-483d-afaa-eda6ed0c0380","name":"Agincourt Library Invasive Plants Talk","dates":[1794855600000],"start":"2026-11-16T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-16T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Agincourt Library","address":"155 Bonis Ave, Scarborough, ON, M1T 3W6","lat":43.785219062,"lng":-79.293413952},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join City of Toronto staff for a presentation on invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. \n\nLearn how to identify these species, understand their impact and effectively manage them. You’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing native habitats. Perfect for gardeners, homeowners and anyone interested in urban ecology. All are welcome. No registration necessary.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"wzuVt8WO1OMBm4VfOFoWsw","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c5555f1e64afd01e64d9b2","tickets":null},{"id":"91ab3771-c55c-437c-9e63-2ffd488ab38d","name":"Toronto Sunday Market","dates":[1770566400000,1771171200000,1771776000000,1772380800000,1772982000000,1773586800000,1774191600000,1774796400000,1775401200000,1776006000000,1776610800000,1777215600000,1777820400000,1778425200000,1779030000000,1779634800000,1780239600000,1780844400000,1781449200000,1782054000000,1782658800000,1783263600000,1783868400000,1784473200000,1785078000000,1785682800000,1786287600000,1786892400000,1787497200000,1788102000000,1788706800000,1789311600000,1789916400000,1790521200000,1791126000000,1791730800000,1792335600000,1792940400000,1793548800000,1794153600000,1794758400000,1795363200000,1795968000000,1796572800000,1797177600000,1797782400000],"start":"2026-02-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating local food, antiques, handmade goods and community.\n\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Consumer Show/Convention"],"presenter":null,"image":"ozk451_PfWrf5ssZGWAwoQ","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/toronto-sunday-market-at-parkdale-hall-tickets-1981191495094"},{"id":"c35b898e-b7fb-45f9-b958-80289964645d","name":"Toronto Cocktail Festival","dates":[1792339200000,1792425600000,1792512000000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000],"start":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bars across Toronto","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":0,"high":190,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto’s biggest celebration of cocktail culture is back and more delicious than ever! Celebrate the art of the cocktail.\n\nWe’ve rounded up the city’s best award-winning bartenders, brand ambassadors and chefs to serve up serious fun and incredible flavours. From industry insiders to casual cocktail lovers, everyone is invited to sip, sample and celebrate Toronto’s world-class cocktail scene.  \n\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","Nightlife"],"presenter":"The Alchemist Magazine","image":"QRMsVbNgsVYLqN2SLnEgdA","website":"https://www.thealchemistmagazine.ca/tcf/","tickets":"https://www.thealchemistmagazine.ca/tcf/"},{"id":"27c49039-30d2-4459-b8d6-5d299058de7f","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"a3d7961b-19e3-4d0f-995e-374d6354b4cc","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,179208