ion","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"ed6bbfcf-274d-4230-9d3d-9f3ef2135097","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"b17e5221-eecc-44a5-8bfb-3dd96994c1c5","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"acb37001-741f-4bd7-905b-655b18e6c4a6","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"ff46d72a-598b-4b9e-971f-fd46f748df2d","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"28aef4b0-a910-4c3e-a99b-580957a4a38a","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,178