ts ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"b55ebd40-fe81-4c22-aebf-b3798957f887","name":"Mixology: Cocktail Class","dates":[1786222800000,1789167600000,1791500400000,1795219200000],"start":"2026-08-08T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-20T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Le Dolci Culinary School","address":"12 Sousa Mendes St, Toronto, ON, M6P 0A8","lat":43.661026575,"lng":-79.453333936},"free":false,"low":139,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come along to our Cocktails Masterclass!\n\nThis is a great beginner class for people 19+ looking to improve their bartending skills! During this 90-minutes class you will get to learn how to mix three different cocktails. \n\nMost of the components for the cocktails will be pre-made by the chef instructor, so you can get right to the fun mixing and tasting part.","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"EmVnfr6izrw6IRMclulJnQ","website":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/mixology-cocktail-class?_pos=1&_psq=*+Mixology+Classes&_psid=99b394d1d&_ss=e&_v=1.0","tickets":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/mixology-cocktail-class?_pos=1&_psq=*+Mixology+Classes&_psid=99b394d1d&_ss=e&_v=1.0"},{"id":"a5abe5a2-a997-4cce-bc56-c2fbcd364d82","name":"Ho, Ho, Holiday Cookie Baking","dates":[1796583600000,1797102000000,1797706800000],"start":"2026-12-06T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-19T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Le Dolci Culinary School","address":"12 Sousa Mendes St, Toronto, ON, M6P 0A8","lat":43.661026575,"lng":-79.453333936},"free":false,"low":149,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for our Holiday Cookie Baking Class!\n\nIn this three-hour, hands-on class, you'll learn how to make three festive holiday cookies: Linzer Cookies, Thumbprint Cookies, and Chocolate Crinkle Cookies. Our talented chefs will guide you through each recipe, sharing tips and techniques along the way.\n\nThe best part? You'll take home the yummy cookies that you will have made!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/ho-ho-holiday-cookie-baking?start=2026-12-01T00:00&select=2026-12-12T14:00","tickets":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/ho-ho-holiday-cookie-baking?start=2026-12-01T00:00&select=2026-12-12T14:00"},{"id":"0141c224-5c24-4f2b-9a97-7fb7e5ce5fbf","name":"Toronto Sunday Market","dates":[1770566400000,1771171200000,1771776000000,1772380800000,1772982000000,1773586800000,1774191600000,1774796400000,1775401200000,1776006000000,1776610800000,1777215600000,1777820400000,1778425200000,1779030000000,1779634800000,1780239600000,1780844400000,1781449200000,1782054000000,1782658800000,1783263600000,1783868400000,1784473200000,1785078000000,1785682800000,1786287600000,1786892400000,1787497200000,1788102000000,1788706800000,1789311600000,1789916400000,1790521200000,1791126000000,1791730800000,1792335600000,1792940400000,1793548800000,1794153600000,1794758400000,1795363200000,1795968000000,1796572800000,1797177600000,1797782400000],"start":"2026-02-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating local food, antiques, handmade goods and community.\n\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Consumer Show/Convention"],"presenter":null,"image":"ozk451_PfWrf5ssZGWAwoQ","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/toronto-sunday-market-at-parkdale-hall-tickets-1981191495094"},{"id":"67e19756-56f4-429e-83ca-06aab63db1f7","name":"Jordan","dates":[1792256400000,1792267200000],"start":"2026-10-17T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Young People's Theatre","address":"165 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5A 3Z4","lat":43.6499984416,"lng":-79.3687420725},"free":false,"low":17,"high":50,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Soar across space and time with Jordan, a young Cree boy who helps Indigenous children with the support of his faithful spirit bear, Maskwa. \n\nWhile his onstage journey is magical, the play is a vibrant tribute to a very real hero: Jordan River Anderson of Norway House Cree Nation, Manitoba.\n\nThe challenges young Jordan faced during his life became the heart of a national movement that led to the creation of Jordan’s Principle — a Canadian legal commitment ensuring equal healthcare for First Nations youth.","categories":["Family/Children","Indigenous","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"kpHDMawXZMf3P_RTEITPlQ","website":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/jordan/","tickets":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/jordan/"},{"id":"8ebe7c2f-2058-4783-83b1-911ba9d2d75d","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,178905600000