 this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"45b45a03-1671-4cbd-93a9-7e8b55b4c3c5","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"7178ffaf-7d64-4e2c-a399-2c64ada824ec","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"ff107422-1fe1-452a-9bf8-0c6ed97c7dc0","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"0d1aa25c-dfbd-43a6-bd55-426ef86f58a6","name":"Benedict Sheehan’s ‘Ukrainian War Requiem’: The National Tour","dates":[1794776400000],"start":"2026-11-15T16:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-15T16:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"St. Paul's Basilica","address":"83 Power St, Toronto, ON, M5A 3A8","lat":43.655592,"lng":-79.362961},"free":false,"low":30,"high":50,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"$45.00 online General Admission; $50 at the door General Admission; $30 for Students 18 and under.","description":"The Axios Men’s Ensemble, in celebration of their historic Juno award, for Classical Album of the Year (Large Ensemble) for the recording of Benedict Sheehan’s Ukrainian War Requiem, have announced a national tour this November.\n\nComposed by two-time Grammy-Nominated Benedict Sheehan, this monumental choral work spans 12 impactful movements that seamlessly blend modern musical styles with ancient chants and traditional Ukrainian motifs. The choral tribute serves as a powerful musical reverence for those affected by the war, offering solace and strength to the living and the grieving, and ultimately providing a solemn space for remembrance and prayer through a skillful and heartfelt tribute to Ukraine and her people.\n\nConducted by Maestro Michael Zaugg, the choir features over 50 performers from Axios Men’s Ensemble, Pro Coro Canada and international soloists. More than music, Ukrainian War Requiem is a journey through grief that reminds us of the enduring grace of the human spirit. ","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"-6JztY8DDStFpcpfeNbGjg","website":"https://www.axiosmensensemble.com/","tickets":"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/friendsofaxiosmenschoirsociety/2202072"},{"id":"024e3380-bc36-4551-8ef3-122597c80f4a","name":"Toronto Sunday Market","dates":[1770566400000,1771171200000,1771776000000,1772380800000,1772982000000,1773586800000,1774191600000,1774796400000,1775401200000,1776006000000,1776610800000,1777215600000,1777820400000,1778425200000,1779030000000,1779634800000,1780239600000,1780844400000,1781449200000,1782054000000,1782658800000,1783263600000,1783868400000,1784473200000,1785078000000,1785682800000,1786287600000,1786892400000,1787497200000,1788102000000,1788706800000,1789311600000,1789916400000,1790521200000,1791126000000,1791730800000,1792335600000,1792940400000,1793548800000,1794153600000,1794758400000,1795363200000,1795968000000,1796572800000,1797177600000,1797782400000],"start":"2026-02-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating local food, antiques, handmade goods and community.\n\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Consumer Show/Convention"],"presenter":null,"image":"ozk451_PfWrf5ssZGWAwoQ","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/toronto-sunday-market-at-parkdale-hall-tickets-1981191495094"},{"id":"ed4f4543-a54b-401c-b41d-1b5e5df855b8","name":"Toronto Sunday Market","dates":[1770566400000,1771171200000,1771776000000,1772380800000,1772982000000,1773586800000,1774191600000,1774796400000,1775401200000,1776006000000,1776610800000,1777215600000,1777820400000,1778425200000,1779030000000,1779634800000,1780239600000,1780844400000,1781449200000,1782054000000,1782658800000,1783263600000,1783868400000,1784473200000,1785078000000,1785682800000,1786287600000,1786892400000,1787497200000,1788102000000,1788706800000,1789311600000,1789916400000,1790521200000,1791126000000,1791730800000,1792335600000,1792940400000,1793548800000,1794153600000,1794758400000,1795363200000,1795968000000,1796572800000,1797177600000,1797782400000],"start":"2026-02-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating local food, antiques, handmade goods and community.\n\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Consumer Show/Convention"],"presenter":null,"image":"ozk451_PfWrf5ssZGWAwoQ","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/toronto-sunday-market-at-parkdale-hall-tickets-1981191495094"},{"id":"9ee10bcb-7928-4ee0-997c-2dd2ca7ae82e","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"7b563c86-8139-4cab-8990-dba2e3ec4034","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,179415