BenTastic and Magic Mel take the stage together for a Christmas celebration full of festive cheer, wonder, and magical surprises!\n\nPacked with laughter, wonder, and plenty of audience participation, this high-energy show blends dazzling illusions, hilarious comedy, and heartwarming holiday spirit.\n\nKids and parents alike will be part of the magic as the show inspires families to discover their own inner sparkle while celebrating the joy of Christmas. Fun for all ages!\n\nPlease note this show requires everyone regardless of age to purchase a ticket. Please be aware the reseller tickets will not be accepted.","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"_-MeSvVzIfRfpr3QdMYeww","website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026"},{"id":"1c93676f-f888-41bb-99b6-b958bf4fcce6","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"f53357a3-f350-4a62-8fd1-792cf0473eb5","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"6a6508d9-baee-4086-8c8b-1415718c6fe1","name":"Rebirth: The Quiet Becoming Installation at Fort York","dates":[1785938400000,1786024800000,1786111200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786543200000,1786629600000,1786716000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787148000000,1787234400000,1787320800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1787752800000,1787839200000,1787925600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788357600000,1788444000000,1788530400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000],"start":"2026-08-05T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864096,"lng":-79.406314887},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bold new outdoor 