ntions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"aced1e7d-6716-44f0-8150-1fd088cf8370","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"4352b604-a5c7-4b70-9350-3e1ed6841fb0","name":"RacquetsUp Expo 2027","dates":[1803056400000,1803135600000,1803222000000],"start":"2027-02-19T12:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-21T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Enercare Centre - Exhibition Grounds","address":"100 Princes' Blvd, Toronto, ON, M6K 3C3","lat":43.63453,"lng":-79.412552},"free":false,"low":32,"high":303,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Group rates are available at info@racquetsupexpo.com","description":"Join the excitement at Canada's first and only dedicated racquet sports expo, designed to unite the community, ignite passion, and foster growth for the sports we love. Whether you're a devoted player, curious newcomer, or industry professional, RacquetsUp Expo 2027 is the essential event of the year!\n\nFor fans and consumers: discover and demo the newest products/gear. See some of your favorite players and leading industry experts. Explore a wide array of racquet sports and the latest training, health, and wellness trends. Receive special offers and expo exclusives.\n\nFor industry professionals: network directly with your target audiences, governing bodies, clubs, influencers, technology providers, and industry leaders. Participate in keynotes, industry panels, and matchmaking events tailored for racquet sports businesses. Introduce new products, services, opportunities on the grandest racquet sports stage.\n\nDon't miss the opportunity to shape the future of racquet sports in Canada!","categories":["Consumer Show/Convention","Seminars/Workshops","Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://racquetsupexpo.com","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/racquetsup-expo-2027-tickets-1978430573102?aff=cityoftoronto"},{"id":"42ea1aa6-efc4-40db-b4ff-ee4ec30812c9","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tanya Marcuse’s multichannel video Portent presents ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"ee505415-77db-4f7b-83b2-599e606d488c","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"73c457b5-7db9-4de6-84ea-39c0736df39f","name":"Vieux Farka Touré and Melat Mengesha","dates":[1791072000000],"start":"2026-10-03T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667901,"lng":-79.396373},"free":false,"low":50,"high":90,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Known worldwide for his electrifying live shows, Vieux Farka Touré’s virtuosic guitar work blends Malian blues, rock, and soul. \n\nOften referred to as “The Hendrix of the Sahara,” Vieux Farka Touré is the son of legendary Malian guitarist Ali Farka Touré, who died in 2006. His live performances are highly energized, and Vieux is known for dazzling crowds with his speed and dexterity on the guitar, as well as his palpable charisma and luminous smile, both of which captivate audiences despite any language barriers. \n\nOpening the show, enjoy winner of Ethiopian Idol, Melat Mengesha.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"4CflToOo9-QWxFuQhYSA9A","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/vieux-farka-toure-449801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts"},{"id":"7330622c-ea90-4907-beae-41b5605edada","name":"Mariza","dates":[1793491200000],"start":"2026-10-31T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667918,"lng":-79.39618},"free":false,"low":70,"high":180,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"International fado superstar Mariza returns to Koerner Hall, bringing her unmistakable voice and magnetic stage presence. \n\nKnown for her soulful voice and the transparency of her lyrics, Mariza has captivated audiences world-wide. No other Portuguese artist since Amália Rodrigues has built an international career with such success, accumulating success after success on the most prestigious world stages, enthusiastic references from the most demanding music critics, and an endless succession of international awards and distinctions. \n\n“Mariza is remaking fado’s ancient sadness into a majestic modern sound.” (Rolling Stone Magazine).\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"RO8dOdbTuNrkVwybbr1aPA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/mariza-426401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/426401"},{"id":"1e31f8a4-b8e1-4cb6-9ea7-04e834e96cc7","name":"The Glenn Gould School Chamber Opera Barber’s A Hand of Bridge and Bernstein’s Trouble in Tahiti","dates":[1794011400000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667904,"lng":-79.396263},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This season’s offering will be a double bill of Samuel Barber’s A Hand of Bridge, a poignant miniature opera that reveals the hidden thoughts of four bridge players during a seemingly ordinary card game, and Leonard Bernstein’s Trouble in Tahiti, a jazz-infused one-act opera depicting a day in the life of a troubled married couple living in 1950s suburbia. \n\nConducted by Jennifer Tung and directed by Mario Pacheco.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"X9oCVnVUJbuDoWmB9o-P2Q","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ggs-chamber-opera-barbers-a-hand-of-bridge-and-bernsteins-trouble-in-tahiti-452601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/452601"},{"id":"203dc0c8-45bf-4547-b31f-aef95d8f2938","name":"Mixology: Cocktail Class","dates":[1786222800000,1789167600000,1791500400000,1795219200000],"start":"2026-08-08T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-20T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Le Dolci Culinary School","address":"12 Sousa Mendes St, Toronto, ON, M6P 0A8","lat":43.661026575,"lng":-79.453333936},"free":false,"low":139,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come along to our Cocktails Masterclass!\n\nThis is a great beginner class for people 19+ looking to improve their bartending skills! During this 90-minutes class you will get to learn how to mix three different cocktails. \n\nMost of the components for the cocktails will be pre-made by the chef instructor, so you can get right to the fun mixing and tasting part.","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"EmVnfr6izrw6IRMclulJnQ","website":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/mixology-cocktail-class?_pos=1&_psq=*+Mixology+Classes&_psid=99b394d1d&_ss=e&_v=1.0","tickets":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/mixology-cocktail-class?_pos=1&_psq=*+Mixology+Classes&_psid=99b394d1d&_ss=e&_v=1.0"},{"id":"60d60a5d-66d7-47e3-bc62-e0e7f6463a6d","name":"Toronto Sunday Market","dates":[1770566400000,1771171200000,1771776000000,1772380800000,1772982000000,1773586800000,1774191600000,1774796400000,1775401200000,1776006000000,1776610800000,1777215600000,1777820400000,1778425200000,1779030000000,1779634800000,1780239600000,1780844400000,1781449200000,1782054000000,1782658800000,1783263600000,1783868400000,1784473200000,1785078000000,1785682800000,1786287600000,1786892400000,1787497200000,1788102000000,1788706800000,1789311600000,1789916400000,1790521200000,1791126000000,1791730800000,1792335600000,1792940400000,1793548800000,1794153600000,1794758400000,1795363200000,1795968000000,1796572800000,1797177600000,1797782400000],"start":"2026-02-08T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-20T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Parkdale Hall","address":"1605 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1A9","lat":43.638869,"lng":-79.444081},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating local food, antiques, handmade goods and community.\n\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Consumer Show/Convention"],"presenter":null,"image":"ozk451_PfWrf5ssZGWAwoQ","website":"https://theparkdalehall.com/new/toronto-sunday-market/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/toronto-sunday-market-at-parkdale-hall-tickets-1981191495094"},{"id":"332bcb78-b93e-4fb9-b0ec-614ab9d6d507","name":"Sketch Party","dates":[1769904000000,1771718400000,1774738800000,1777158000000,1779577200000,1781996400000,1784415600000,1786834800000,1789254000000,1792278000000,1795305600000,1797724800000],"start":"2026-01-31T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-19T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Comedy Bar","address":"945 Bloor Street W, Toronto, ON, M6H 1L5","lat":43.66148,"lng":-79.428242},"free":false,"low":23,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Each month we're partying HARD and bringing the best sketch comedy this city has to offer, from the hottest up and coming troupes to long time fan favourite troupes and solo acts.\n\nGet ready for a wild night of expecting the unexpected and, of course, sketch comedy. Bring your best party trick and enjoy the vibes. There ain't no party like a S-KETCH PARTY!\n\nYou won’t want to miss this monthly shindig, come party-hardy with us!","categories":["Comedy"],"presenter":null,"image":"IoEFS6qmP2peTL7SwyQW_w","website":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/sketch-party","tickets":null},{"id":"b5995b4f-b551-43c5-91d7-aa22da4cef0a","name":"Béla Fleck: My Bluegrass Heart","dates":[1794618000000],"start":"2026-11-13T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-13T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667901,"lng":-79.39622},"free":false,"low":80,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The banjo visionary leads an all‑star ensemble through some new music and classic tunes, blending bluegrass roots with jazz and classical influences.\n\nOver the last four decades, Béla Fleck has made a point of boldly going where no banjo player has gone before, a musical journey that has earned him 19 Grammys in nine different fields, including country, pop, jazz, instrumental, classical, and global music. But his roots are in bluegrass, and that is where he returns with his band of all-star players, My Bluegrass Heart.  ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"RXqI_t-SfR4Uv8wcs-ZuQA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/bela-fleck-my-bluegrass-heart-444601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/444601"},{"id":"6e8a4aab-d761-4302-9909-36f0b51b9eaf","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"e3d43a89-bd24-4edf-8210-2ad262093de2","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"a52dc4bd-7900-41c1-91ce-50c0cac0cd45","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"3c324c60-a87b-4288-8b89-af83f1424d9e","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"c60e836e-dbf2-48b4-b4c6-2c8833ec11dc","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"f4bc0414-b3da-4352-87ea-7c3638fd130a","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"cbcd5cb4-a96c-4299-b6a7-ac1ab8c7d83e","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"8c3273a5-0ac0-4928-a435-c4d8cff893f9","name":"Bruce Liu, piano","dates":[1793404800000],"start":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667933,"lng":-79.396228},"free":false,"low":80,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Described as a pianist with “magician's fingers and soul of integrity” (Le Monde), Canadian Bruce Liu returns to Koerner Hall to perform works by Beethoven, Chopin, Albéniz, and Liszt.\n\nFirst Prize winner of the 18th International Chopin Piano Competition 2021 in Warsaw, Liu has emerged as one of the most compelling pianists of his generation; a musician praised not only for his dazzling technique, but for his curiosity and artistry that combines \"nimble versatility\" (The New York Times) and \"playing of breathtaking beauty\" (BBC Music Magazine). \n\nPlease join us! ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"IMYt8SA5pPTZaJcWkiHwKQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/bruce-liu-piano-426201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/426201"},{"id":"80c13167-3147-46b2-930c-6b345f780e25","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"pre