his fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"48923924-8554-4935-b068-673aa8635986","name":"The Glenn Gould School Spring Opera: Mozart’s Le nozze di Figaro","dates":[1805326200000,1805499000000],"start":"2027-03-17T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-03-19T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":25,"high":60,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Students from The Glenn Gould School’s vocal program present their fully staged annual opera in Koerner Hall, conducted by Judith Yan.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"3zuXFBWgiUYArpr29Yt1fA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/the-glenn-gould-school-spring-opera-430803","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets"},{"id":"3db4af58-22c7-44e2-a351-be90668ec2b9","name":"27th Annual Planet in Focus International Environmental Film Festival","dates":[1792535400000,1792621800000,1792708200000,1792794600000,1792881000000,1792967400000],"start":"2026-10-20T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Paradise Theater","address":"1006c Bloor Street West, Toronto, ON M6H 1M2","lat":43.661115,"lng":-79.430709},"free":false,"low":15,"high":20,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Don’t miss this lineup of groundbreaking documentary films focusing on the planet we share. \n\nThe festival includes Canadian and international films, a free Industry Conference, a free Family Day Program, special guests, panels and filmmaker QnAs. \n\n","categories":["Cultural","Environmental","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"http://planetinfocus.org","tickets":"https://planetinfocus.org/tickets/"},{"id":"6a995525-ec77-445b-b033-a28347098b72","name":"A Very Merry Magic Show","dates":[1797694200000,1797701400000,1797712200000,1797780600000,1797787800000,1797798600000,1797867000000,1797874200000,1797885000000,1797953400000,1797960600000,1797971400000,1798039800000,1798047000000,1798057800000],"start":"2026-12-19T10:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Theatre","address":"76 Wychwood Ave studio 176, Toronto, ON","lat":43.68003,"lng":-79.423396},"free":false,"low":30.49,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This holiday season, BenTastic and Magic Mel take the stage together for a Christmas celebration full of festive cheer, wonder, and magical surprises!\n\nPacked with laughter, wonder, and plenty of audience participation, this high-energy show blends dazzling illusions, hilarious comedy, and heartwarming holiday spirit.\n\nKids and parents alike will be part of the magic as the show inspires families to discover their own inner sparkle while celebrating the joy of Christmas. Fun for all ages!\n\nPlease note this show requires everyone regardless of age to purchase a ticket. Please be aware the reseller tickets will not be accepted.","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"_-MeSvVzIfRfpr3QdMYeww","website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026"},{"id":"000e6d54-c4fb-4196-953e-af602845b5cc","name":"Punch Brothers","dates":[1794960000000],"start":"2026-11-17T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-17T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667895,"lng":-79.396191},"free":false,"low":50,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Punch Brothers, formed by mandolinist Chris Thile in 2006, is known for pushing the boundaries of acoustic music. \n\nIn addition to Thile, the band currently comprises guitarist Chris Eldridge, bassist Paul Kowert, banjoist Noam Pikelny, and violinist Brittany Haas. Punch Brothers has garnered critical acclaim, including a Grammy for Best Folk Album for All Ashore (2018). The Washington Post applauded them for taking “bluegrass to its next evolutionary stage, drawing equal inspiration from the brain and the heart.”.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"THVQ5z91UmuHmK_rCa7xOA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/punch-brothers-441801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/441801"},{"id":"e4e9e8a7-ec38-48e6-a7d0-f10e444d728b","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"a93b8390-4639-4aa2-99cd-efbd9cf408a4","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"492c96f1-82c7-4a6f-b0ed-3fcf4beddcd6","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"72e3782b-b05b-4d32-8676-0aece19fe53a","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,17919900000