 of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"c6019993-ac9f-4fd7-b40e-50776547657e","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"e20f090a-3c9a-4247-abad-7695263d6782","name":"Aga Khan Master Musicians","dates":[1794704400000],"start":"2026-11-14T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-14T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667884,"lng":-79.396297},"free":false,"low":50,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Creating music inspired by their own deep roots in the cultures of the Middle East and Mediterranean Basin, South Asia, Central Asia, and China.\n\nBrought together by the Aga Khan Music Programme to explore how musical innovation can contribute to the revitalization of cultural heritage, the Master Musicians are venerated performers and composer-arrangers who appear on the world’s most prestigious stages while also serving as preeminent teachers, mentors, and curators. Each of these exceptional artists has achieved mastery within a rigorous musical tradition defined by canonical styles, repertoires, pedagogy, and performance techniques. At the same time, they share a belief that tradition can serve as an invaluable compass for an artistic search into new forms of creativity inspired, but not constrained, by the past.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"2BIqtubZh4tvnpjcT1yh4g","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/aga-khan-master-musicians-441401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/441401"},{"id":"646d0195-c107-4b7d-8e36-1abd13adb00a","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"89c60d4b-5e28-4a6a-8d6d-0d79fd6a0caa","name":"GATHER in Toronto Exhibition","dates":[1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785078000000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785682800000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786287600000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1786892400000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787497200000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000],"start":"2026-07-23T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front Street East, 2nd floor","lat":43.649129,"lng":-79.371765},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come learn about ways we move through the world, honouring the land, our stories and each other, celebrating triumphs in our journeys, strengthening fibres in our connectedness. It is within this sacred act of coming together that we find common values, building a unified vision for our future.\n \nListen to local sports origin stories alongside artistic reflections on identity, resilience, and belonging through works that highlight the power of connection across cultures and communities.\n \nThe exhibition features documentaries on Deskaheh, Herb Carnegie, and the St. Christopher House Lacrosse Organization; contemporary art by Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"e2562a6a-dd3b-4da3-ba82-ba139d18330e","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"d2be4677-0692-4a47-b043-9775baeded69","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"68b4ad3f-4de1-404f-b90f-be8bf9a6db71","name":"27th Annual Planet in Focus International Environmental Film Festival","dates":[1792535400000,1792621800000,1792708200000,1792794600000,1792881000000,1792967400000],"start":"2026-10-20T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Paradise Theater","address":"1006c Bloor Street West, Toronto, ON M6H 1M2","lat":43.661115,"lng":-79.430709},"free":false,"low":15,"high":20,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Don’t miss this lineup of groundbreaking documentary films focusing on the planet we share. \n\nThe festival includes Canadian and international films, a free Industry Conference, a free Family Day Program, special guests, panels and filmmaker QnAs. \n\n","categories":["Cultural","Environmental","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"http://planetinfocus.org","tickets":"https://planetinfocus.org/tickets/"},{"id":"f86aff92-42c9-45cc-9fa9-22faa7116ab9","name":"27th Annual Planet in Focus International Environmental Film Festival","dates":[1792535400000,1792621800000,1792708200000,1792794600000,1792881000000,1792967400000],"start":"2026-10-20T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Paradise Theater","address":"1006c Bloor Street West, Toronto, ON M6H 1M2","lat":43.661115,"lng":-79.430709},"free":false,"low":15,"high":20,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Don’t miss this lineup of groundbreaking documentary films focusing on the planet we share. \n\nThe festival includes Canadian and international films, a free Industry Conference, a free Family Day Program, special guests, panels and filmmaker QnAs. \n\n","categories":["Cultural","Environmental","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"http://planetinfocus.org","tickets":"https://planetinfocus.org/tickets/"},{"id":"6af1fd92-a365-43ad-b9cd-7842159c9405","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"9c720500-bb4c-41f3-a66a-daa980c8968d","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"c38719fb-d480-44da-b5d9-ff2a7f2af9f0","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"b50901ba-afe4-43ed-9a80-ef43299507e8","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"0850b6ad-2534-4bd3-a0c1-4e583b4723f4","name":"Laila Biali: Joni Mitchell and the Canadian Songbook Reimagined and Elizabeth Bougerol and Her Band","dates":[1803600000000],"start":"2027-02-25T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-25T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":60,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"2026 Grammy Award nominated vocalist, pianist, songwriter and national radio host Laila Biali’s latest tribute project showcases dynamic covers of our country's musical icons. Expect fresh takes on a range of Canadian artists from across the decades including Leonard Cohen, Neil Young, k.d. lang, Bruce Cockburn, Sarah McLachlan and more, all centred around the heart of this show: prairie royalty, Joni Mitchell.\n\nAfter the concert, enjoy a beverage and more music at the Postlude Performance featuring a local emerging artist in the Leslie and Anna Dan Galleria.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"opqCXI0iZqHqo2ZQlYsG0w","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/laila-biali-joni-mitchell-and-the-canadian-songbook-reimagined-with-elizabeth-bougerol-and-her-band-446801","tickets":"http://rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/446801"},{"id":"8c9be41e-ba00-49b0-85ac-4d5b91661089","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tanya Marcuse’s multichannel video Portent presents ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"2bde5717-47df-49a0-bb5e-96d2443ab02c","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tanya Marcuse’s multichannel video Portent presents ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"243c3184-1735-48a1-924e-b7ceac53b114","name":"Tanya Marcuse: Portent","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tanya Marcuse’s multichannel video Portent presents ominous scenes of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"308d76de-930b-4669-a8cd-c3abceb026c4","name":"Pet First Aid and CPR","dates":[1791118800000],"start":"2026-10-04T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Pack of Paws","address":"105 Jefferson Avenue  Toronto","lat":43.652177,"lng":-79.378967},"free":false,"low":198.36,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Receive hands-on experience with live animals and learn the necessary skills when dealing with first aid emergency situations.\n\nPet parents and professionals alike can benefit greatly from this course. You will feel well-prepared to address any accidents, emergencies, or injuries involving pets in your care.\n\nAdministered by a certified Pet First Aid Instructor, the course is 10-hours long and includes a reference book and a certificate of completion. Dogs are welcome to attend the class.\n\nTopics include: Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR), injury and illness prevention and medication administration.","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"Kr_u0kfmUQ-UccNOEjO3KQ","website":"https://torontodogmoms.com/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/pet-first-aid-cpr-class-tickets-1983976363711?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true#location"},{"id":"d42ea413-4f4d-411d-ae84-ef6d78e26698","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"b2ebb1b0-5c8e-448d-8087-97ce234bf580","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"79c6b0f9-be1a-453d-b7ee-639df2cdb4f4","name":"GATHER in Toronto Exhibition","dates":[1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785078000000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785682800000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786287600000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1786892400000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787497200000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000],"start":"2026-07-23T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front Street East, 2nd floor","lat":43.649129,"lng":-79.371765},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come learn about ways we move through the world, honouring the land, our stories and each other, celebrating triumphs in our journeys, strengthening fibres in our connectedness. It is within this sacred act of coming together that we find common values, building a unified vision for our future.\n \nListen to local sports origin stories alongside artistic reflections on identity, resilience, and belonging through works that highlight the power of connection across cultures and communities.\n \nThe exhibition features documentaries on Deskaheh, Herb Carnegie, and the St. Christopher House Lacrosse Organization; contemporary art by Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"74a07f0d-