es of the natural world: trees swaying in the wind, vapour rising from volcanic fumaroles, icy branches illuminated by flickering light, and other small disturbances that hint at forces beyond our understanding. \n\nThe quiet is deliberate; the frame remains fixed while the environment shifts restlessly within it, evoking a tension between stillness and motion, beauty and unease, the known and unknown.\n\nMarcuse describes her work as an exploration of the kinship between disaster and the sublime, and of the ways the world around us is continually threatened, transformed, and made strange. Portent forms part of her expansive series Book of Miracles (2020-26), inspired by the Augsburger Wunderzeichenbuch, a 16th-century illuminated manuscript depicting natural disasters, supernatural phenomena, celestial spectacles and unexplained oddities.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"MauUIvgc_RtL3xi-f6yStQ","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/tanya-marcuse-portent/","tickets":null},{"id":"bf507b99-c2b9-4ee5-bc3f-785ca7cec406","name":"ARC Ensemble","dates":[1791136800000],"start":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Conservatory of Music","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667875,"lng":-79.396368},"free":false,"low":40,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The ARC Ensemble and students of the Glenn Gould School explore Armenian works composed before the breakup of the Soviet Union and Armenian independence, captivating and evocative music unknown in the West. \n\nIncluded on the program are arrangements of Armenian folksongs for string quartet, a compelling Cello Sonata by Avet Terteryan and seductive piano miniatures by Alexander Spendiarian and Arno Babadjanian.\n\nThe multiple Grammy Award nominated ARC Ensemble comprises the senior faculty of The Royal Conservatory's Glenn Gould School, with special guests drawn from the organization's most accomplished students and alumni. It is among Canada's most distinguished cultural ambassadors with recent appearances in Los Angeles, New York and London’s Wigmore Hall. \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/arc-ensemble-453001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts"},{"id":"b50e0b6f-cacc-4f0a-a810-ea6acf8494a6","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"af6896d3-647e-4498-bfe6-23e8ccd4251e","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966