ll,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"6ec82e3d-211a-447e-846c-02537cb7b228","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"bd7ccf72-73d4-44a1-997b-87e6711a457d","name":"James Ehnes Canada Birthday Tour","dates":[1790985600000],"start":"2026-10-02T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-02T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667903,"lng":-79.396371},"free":false,"low":60,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Recognized as “a violinist in a class of his own”, James Ehnes celebrates his fiftieth birthday with a special international tour. \n\nHis Koerner Hall appearance with pianist Andrew Armstrong features works by Brahms and Bartók, along with a newly commissioned piece by acclaimed Canadian composer Carmen Braden.  \n\nAn Honorary Fellow of The Royal Conservatory, Ehnes has established himself as one of the most sought-after musicians on the international stage. Gifted with a rare combination of stunning virtuosity, serene lyricism, and an unfaltering musicality, he is a favourite guest at the world’s most celebrated concert halls. \n\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"dr08lqpVyfK9XoIFi6FEDw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/james-ehnes-50th-canada-birthday-tour-425801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts"},{"id":"62cab809-8774-42a4-a035-75bee6a6359b","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"bafc8d49-1b19-4922-b39f-7abd0958d785","name":"GATHER in Toronto Exhibition","dates":[1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785078000000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785682800000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786287600000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1786892400000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787497200000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000],"start":"2026-07-23T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front Street East, 2nd floor","lat":43.649129,"lng":-79.371765},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come learn about ways we move through the world, honouring the land, our stories and each other, celebrating triumphs in our journeys, strengthening fibres in our connectedness. It is within this sacred act of coming together that we find common values, building a unified vision for our future.\n \nListen to local sports origin stories alongside artistic reflections on identity, resilience, and belonging through works that highlight the power of connection across cultures and communities.\n \nThe exhibition features documentaries on Deskaheh, Herb Carnegie, and the St. Christopher House Lacrosse Organization; contemporary art by Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"eaff7f62-c22e-49fc-92b0-f851419060c9","name":"GATHER in Toronto Exhibition","dates":[1784818800000,1784905200000,1784991600000,1785078000000,1785337200000,1785423600000,1785510000000,1785596400000,1785682800000,1785942000000,1786028400000,1786114800000,1786201200000,1786287600000,1786546800000,1786633200000,1786719600000,1786806000000,1786892400000,1787151600000,1787238000000,1787324400000,1787410800000,1787497200000,1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,