nd Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"1077fb7c-bd40-42d7-8659-b54bba37c77b","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"4f932022-9dec-45c7-9391-b454ce050e2f","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"cfffabe0-d77e-4e15-a962-4d6dad2e698d","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"0dd47bc2-a236-4af8-b43f-0a254147fc54","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"88726063-7405-456e-a203-6002f528b6f0","name":"People and Places Art Exhibition at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788793200000,1788879600000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000],"start":"2026-09-02T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The York Artists' Guild is a community-based arts group with members from various walks of life. Enjoy their display of art reflecting various styles, techniques and tastes themed around the idea of gathering, people and places. View the art and meet some of the artists during the exhibit launch Saturday September 5th, 1-3pm. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":"York Artists' Guild","image":"6lo6jiuT3LdsPXXLZw6ndg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"6334a556-0881-42fb-85fe-7d02f3bd39d2","name":"Pumpkin Pie Class","dates":[1789927200000,1791136800000,1791655200000],"start":"2026-09-20T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Le Dolci Culinary School","address":"12 Sousa Mendes St, Toronto, ON, M6P 0A8","lat":43.661026575,"lng":-79.453333936},"free":false,"low":139,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a cozy baking class where you'll master the art of making the perfect pumpkin pie from scratch.\n\nLearn how to prepare a flaky, buttery crust and create a rich, spiced pumpkin filling that brings comfort and tradition to the holiday table. Whether you're a beginner or a seasoned baker, this hands-on class will leave you with the skills and recipe to impress your family and friends this fall. \n\nCome for the pie, stay for the warm autumn vibes! At the end of class you will have a beautifully decorated pie, just in time for Thanksgiving!","categories":["Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":"qV2CylWTk126RNadYGTdQg","website":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/pies-pumpkin-pie-class?_pos=1&_psq=Pumpkin+Pie+Class&_psid=0cf28c33d&_ss=e&_v=1.0&variant=50587778744536","tickets":"https://www.ledolci.com/products/pies-pumpkin-pie-class?_pos=1&_psq=Pumpkin+Pie+Class&_psid=0cf28c33d&_ss=e&_v=1.0&variant=50587778744536"},{"id":"91c88596-0750-4711-b878-1584e3b364e0","name":"Heaven","dates":[1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791050400000,1791072000000],"start":"2026-09-29T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Theatre Centre","address":"1115 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6J 1J1","lat":43.643099215,"lng":-79.423282309},"free":false,"low":18,"high":42,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Virtuosic dancer and award-winning choreographer Sasha Ivanochko revisits one of her most ground-breaking works this fall.\n\nThe gasp of breath, the startling slap of flesh on flesh, the stamp of foot to floor these are the sounds of vulnerability and power that score Heaven, performed naked and without music. \n\nRooted in the idea of heaven as a site of union, the choreography invites audiences into an intimate encounter with the body, its limits, its desires, and its need for connection, offering a viewing experience that is direct, unmediated and deeply human. \n\nHeaven features performers Jessie Garon, Scott McCabe, and Sully Malaeb Proulx, with lighting design by James Proudfoot. Do not miss this chance to see a rare performance of an incredible  Canadian dance piece.\n","categories":["Dance","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"mKigBTLtwuEQp19b6xsRkA","website":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/","tickets":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/"},{"id":"9475ae59-f16c-4244-967c-1719e2a9b9af","name":"Heaven","dates":[1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791050400000,1791072000000],"start":"2026-09-29T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Theatre Centre","address":"1115 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6J 1J1","lat":43.643099215,"lng":-79.423282309},"free":false,"low":18,"high":42,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Virtuosic dancer and award-winning choreographer Sasha Ivanochko revisits one of her most ground-breaking works this fall.\n\nThe gasp of breath, the startling slap of flesh on flesh, the stamp of foot to floor these are the sounds of vulnerability and power that score Heaven, performed naked and without music. \n\nRooted in the idea of heaven as a site of union, the choreography invites audiences into an intimate encounter with the body, its limits, its desires, and its need for connection, offering a viewing experience that is direct, unmediated and deeply human. \n\nHeaven features performers Jessie Garon, Scott McCabe, and Sully Malaeb Proulx, with lighting design by James Proudfoot. Do not miss this chance to see a rare performance of an incredible  Canadian dance piece.\n","categories":["Dance","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"mKigBTLtwuEQp19b6xsRkA","website":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/","tickets":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/"},{"id":"c711a520-1d4e-4584-8c4d-cd36eafaa8df","name":"Heaven","dates":[1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791050400000,1791072000000],"start":"2026-09-29T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Theatre Centre","address":"1115 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6J 1J1","lat":43.643099215,"lng":-79.423282309},"free":false,"low":18,"high":42,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Virtuosic dancer and award-winning choreographer Sasha Ivanochko revisits one of her most ground-breaking works this fall.\n\nThe gasp of breath, the startling slap of flesh on flesh, the stamp of foot to floor these are the sounds of vulnerability and power that score Heaven, performed naked and without music. \n\nRooted in the idea of heaven as a site of union, the choreography invites audiences into an intimate encounter with the body, its limits, its desires, and its need for connection, offering a viewing experience that is direct, unmediated and deeply human. \n\nHeaven features performers Jessie Garon, Scott McCabe, and Sully Malaeb Proulx, with lighting design by James Proudfoot. Do not miss this chance to see a rare performance of an incredible  Canadian dance piece.\n","categories":["Dance","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"mKigBTLtwuEQp19b6xsRkA","website":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/","tickets":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/"},{"id":"7ba7c4c0-6b5d-4e8d-a259-b6c7aa829af2","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"429e5e5f-8938-41d9-9bbf-196e8b49cb67","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"0fbad0aa-f3e8-479d-a289-d3d42712c6b2","name":"Ten Years of Community: A Week of Expert Masterclasses","dates":[1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000],"start":"2026-09-29T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-01T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Global Startups","address":"325 Front St West","lat":43.6512,"lng":-79.379504},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Global Startups celebrates 10 years with a week of expert-led masterclasses during Toronto Tech Week, September 29 to October 1 at 325 Front St W. Sessions cover AI and business automation, Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM, compliance and audit readiness, SR&ED tax credits in the age of AI, foreign exchange risk management, multicultural marketing, cross-cultural leadership, property management finance, employee benefits and insurtech, brand strategy for founders, and climate tech education investment. Each session is delivered by a vetted community member to a curated audience of founders, operators, and business leaders. Attendance is free and registration is by approval. The week closes with a community gathering for all alumni and members.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://luma.com/globalstartups","tickets":"https://luma.com/globalstartups"},{"id":"2e302496-cace-4c48-964b-931e800a67bd","name":"A Very Merry Magic Show","dates":[1797694200000,1797701400000,1797712200000,1797780600000,1797787800000,1797798600000,1797867000000,1797874200000,1797885000000,1797953400000,1797960600000,1797971400000,1798039800000,1798047000000,1798057800000],"start":"2026-12-19T10:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Theatre","address":"76 Wychwood Ave studio 176, Toronto, ON","lat":43.68003,"lng":-79.423396},"free":false,"low":30.49,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This holiday season, BenTastic and Magic Mel take the stage together for a Christmas celebration full of festive cheer, wonder, and magical surprises!\n\nPacked with laughter, wonder, and plenty of audience participation, this high-energy show blends dazzling illusions, hilarious comedy, and heartwarming holiday spirit.\n\nKids and parents alike will be part of the magic as the show inspires families to discover their own inner sparkle while celebrating the joy of Christmas. Fun for all ages!\n\nPlease note this show requires everyone regardless of age to purchase a ticket. Please be aware the reseller tickets will not be accepted.","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"_-MeSvVzIfRfpr3QdMYeww","website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026"},{"id":"824fcd70-26d5-456f-a020-5fa2c9a566f2","name":"A Very Merry Magic Show","dates":[1797694200000,1797701400000,1797712200000,1797780600000,1797787800000,1797798600000,1797867000000,1797874200000,1797885000000,1797953400000,1797960600000,1797971400000,1798039800000,1798047000000,1798057800000],"start":"2026-12-19T10:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Theatre","address":"76 Wychwood Ave studio 176, Toronto, ON","lat":43.68003,"lng":-79.423396},"free":false,"low":30.49,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This holiday season, BenTastic and Magic Mel take the stage together for a Christmas celebration full of festive cheer, wonder, and magical surprises!\n\nPacked with laughter, wonder, and plenty of audience participation, this high-energy show blends dazzling illusions, hilarious comedy, and heartwarming holiday spirit.\n\nKids and parents alike will be part of the magic as the show inspires families to discover their own inner sparkle while celebrating the joy of Christmas. Fun for all ages!\n\nPlease note this show requires everyone regardless of age to purchase a ticket. Please be aware the reseller tickets will not be accepted.","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"_-MeSvVzIfRfpr3QdMYeww","website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026"},{"id":"967007db-95f5-4a6b-bb89-46bd79dfbec1","name":"A Very Merry Magic Show","dates":[1797694200000,1797701400000,1797712200000,1797780600000,1797787800000,1797798600000,1797867000000,1797874200000,1797885000000,1797953400000,1797960600000,1797971400000,1798039800000,1798047000000,1798057800000],"start":"2026-12-19T10:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T15:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Theatre","address":"76 Wychwood Ave studio 176, Toronto, ON","lat":43.68003,"lng":-79.423396},"free":false,"low":30.49,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This holiday season, BenTastic and Magic Mel take the stage together for a Christmas celebration full of festive cheer, wonder, and magical surprises!\n\nPacked with laughter, wonder, and plenty of audience participation, this high-energy show blends dazzling illusions, hilarious comedy, and heartwarming holiday spirit.\n\nKids and parents alike will be part of the magic as the show inspires families to discover their own inner sparkle while celebrating the joy of Christmas. Fun for all ages!\n\nPlease note this show requires everyone regardless of age to purchase a ticket. Please be aware the reseller tickets will not be accepted.","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"_-MeSvVzIfRfpr3QdMYeww","website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/a-very-merry-magic-show-2026"},{"id":"72dbcc3c-49a8-42fb-9f33-ad5fdbd43223","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminate