n our connectedness. It is within this sacred act of coming together that we find common values, building a unified vision for our future.\n \nListen to local sports origin stories alongside artistic reflections on identity, resilience, and belonging through works that highlight the power of connection across cultures and communities.\n \nThe exhibition features documentaries on Deskaheh, Herb Carnegie, and the St. Christopher House Lacrosse Organization; contemporary art by Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"d51b4bd7-dba3-40b3-beed-3321ffa44e53","name":"Pasta Party!","dates":[1788559200000,1793397600000],"start":"2026-09-04T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Le Dolci Culinary School","address":"12 Sousa Mendes St, Toronto, ON, M6P 0A8","lat":43.661026575,"lng":-79.453333936},"free":false,"low":169,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an unforgettable hands-on culinary experience celebrating the art of Italian cooking!\n\nIn this 2-course Italian class, guests will learn how to craft a traditional pasta dish from scratch, paired with a simple, flavourful sauce, and finish the experience by creating a classic tiramisu for dessert.\n\nWhether you are a pasta lover or a dessert enthusiast, this class blends authentic Italian techniques and fresh ingredients, all in a fun, interactive setting.  \n\nPerfect for foodies, date nights or anyone looking to bring a taste of Italy home!","categories":["Food/Culinary","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Le Dolci Culinary School","image":"gu7PLNgQVjzPvgxVRChRzQ","website":"https://www.