the land, our stories and each other, celebrating triumphs in our journeys, strengthening fibres in our connectedness. It is within this sacred act of coming together that we find common values, building a unified vision for our future.\n \nListen to local sports origin stories alongside artistic reflections on identity, resilience, and belonging through works that highlight the power of connection across cultures and communities.\n \nThe exhibition features documentaries on Deskaheh, Herb Carnegie, and the St. Christopher House Lacrosse Organization; contemporary art by Marina Dempster, Maria Hupfield, Safoura Zahedi, Ben Spears, Pedro Zepeda, Milo Osceola, Daniel Henhawk, and David Barnett; as well as new acquisitions alongside historic items from the City of Toronto Art and Artifact Collection.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"-m6p-aI3Br63z-qiiUz5dg","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"451714f4-b1a9-4d15-8b5c-45d292fad290","name":"BMO Student Life Expo 2026","dates":[1794762000000],"start":"2026-11-15T12:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-15T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"222 Bremner Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3L9","lat":43.642632,"lng":-79.384647},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n$10.00 for parents and guardians.","description":"Mark your calendars, your future starts here!\n\nPlanning for after high school? Whether you're considering university, college, skilled trades, apprenticeships, travel or jumping straight into the workforce, join us in exploring what's next.\n\nMeet face-to-face with representatives from universities and colleges, skilled trades and apprenticeship programs, career and employment organizations, scholarship, financial aid providers and much more!\n\nDon't miss out on this exciting opportunity to enrich your student experience. \n\n","categories":["Consumer Show/Convention","Othe