ow grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"6e233425-d88c-48d7-877e-9ce698c0e7a0","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"ae523874-05d0-408a-93ef-c947ee1036d9","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"d32349eb-6fd9-446d-a598-58759af18754","name":"Garrick Ohlsson, piano","dates":[1794168000000],"start":"2026-11-08T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-08T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667943,"lng":-79.396248},"free":false,"low":75,"high":135,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"“By almost any measure, Ohlsson is one of the great American pianists.” (The Washington Post).\n\nA towering figure among the world’s greatest pianists, Garrick Ohlsson is renowned for his “incredible technique with razor-sharp accuracy” (Seattle Times). The first American to win the International Chopin Piano Competition, he continues to captivate audiences with performances of remarkable depth and authority. \n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"1rUAQWFC1o6bY34FIedKtA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/garrick-ohlsson-piano-426801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/426801"},{"id":"42eefa59-0853-4179-8be6-7d307578036f","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"74b8f59d-53a8-4d78-8c9f-f582ee3dce79","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"3d66866a-2129-4774-a1e6-ade382fc2c37","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"2aa2fd53-1b3c-4234-aa45-2f62bb1f8850","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"1b621b4d-2b1f-4ec2-9730-195803732026","name":"Heaven","dates":[1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791050400000,1791072000000],"start":"2026-09-29T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Theatre Centre","address":"1115 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6J 1J1","lat":43.643099215,"lng":-79.423282309},"free":false,"low":18,"high":42,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Virtuosic dancer and award-winning choreographer Sasha Ivanochko revisits one of her most ground-breaking works this fall.\n\nThe gasp of breath, the startling slap of flesh on flesh, the stamp of foot to floor these are the sounds of vulnerability and power that score Heaven, performed naked and without music. \n\nRooted in the idea of heaven as a site of union, the choreography invites audiences into an intimate encounter with the body, its limits, its desires, and its need for connection, offering a viewing experience that is direct, unmediated and deeply human. \n\nHeaven features performers Jessie Garon, Scott McCabe, and Sully Malaeb Proulx, with lighting design by James Proudfoot. Do not miss this chance to see a rare performance of an incredible  Canadian dance piece.\n","categories":["Dance","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"mKigBTLtwuEQp19b6xsRkA","website":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/","tickets":"https://theatrecentre.org/event/heaven-legacy-collective/"},{"id":"9ce60015-d6ae-4e07-a972-95c0b41d92d1","name":"Jean-Guihen Queyras, cello, with Alexandre Tharaud, piano","dates":[1794013200000],"start":"2026-11-06T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-06T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.66793,"lng":-79.396253},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The celebrated French-Canadian cellist and French pianist reunite for an afternoon of refined artistry, performing works by Brahms, Debussy, Schubert, and others.\n\nJean-Guihen Queyras learnt his interpretative approach from none other than Pierre Boulez, with whom his artistic partnership spanned many years. A flawless technique and a clear, decisive sound shapes his approach to every performance and his absolute commitment to the music itself. \n\nIn a career spanning 25 years, Alexandre Tharaud has become a unique figure in the classical music world and a key exponent of French pianism. His extraordinary repertoire ranges from Couperin, Bach, and Scarlatti, through Mozart, Beethoven, Schubert, Chopin, Brahms, and Rachmaninov, to the major 20th century French composers. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"W9rQbhpEVIlYsWhU2S_HHA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/jean-guihen-queyras-cello-with-alexandre-tharaud-piano-427001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/427001"},{"id":"b9a4fff5-4de0-411f-9e0f-9520dbfa63b9","name":"Take it Slow: Lichens of Toronto Webinar","dates":[1791993600000],"start":"2026-10-14T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"On-line Event","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a webinar on some of Toronto’s most complex and enigmatic organisms: lichens. We’ll learn about basic lichen biology, including structure and various growth forms, their roles and relationships, and how and where to find them. We’ll also cover some of the common lichens found in and around Toronto and some handy tools and resources for exploring.","categories":["Environmental","Virtual/Online Event"],"presenter":null,"image":"8yNqOhXrsnYFO1wWGzAalA","website":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/7249762a-b982-4962-bb9b-8653b83c2363@f0bc8ec6-9ed8-4d0c-9189-411ad949cc65","tickets":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/7249762a-b982-4962-bb9b-8653b83c2363@f0bc8ec6-9ed8-4d0c-9189-411ad949cc65"},{"id":"4c541515-9f5f-4df4-8d72-802a5a934d7c","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"2e2a3e97-64fb-4b12-9dd7-ebe3ae05a329","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"72bb6789-9bdf-4390-84f2-297d8db8049b","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"9016fdde-0cdf-435c-bbe1-afa29220df1b","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"edbd4044-2641-414e-a05c-fe0789f09ef6","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","ven