"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"c7b5ca37-7ea9-487a-a1a7-3f36125bd063","name":"Ten Years of Community: A Week of Expert Masterclasses","dates":[1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000],"start":"2026-09-29T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-01T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Global Startups","address":"325 Front St West","lat":43.6512,"lng":-79.379504},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Global Startups celebrates 10 years with a week of expert-led masterclasses during Toronto Tech Week, September 29 to October 1 at 325 Front St W. Sessions cover AI and business automation, Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM, compliance and audit readiness, SR&ED tax credits in the age of AI, foreign exchange risk management, multicultural marketing, cross-cultural leadership, property management finance, employee benefits and insurtech, brand strategy for founders, and climate tech education investment. Each session is delivered by a vetted community member to a curated audience of founders, operators, and business leaders. Attendance is free and registration is by approval. The week closes with a community gathering for all alumni and members.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://luma.com/globalstartups","tickets":"https://luma.com/globalstartups"},{"id":"a2d71295-6790-4645-8fa0-714e556d3b70","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"10a531a6-4b83-46eb-aeb2-416b6615eae1","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"92f798e3-6c03-4580-9d34-0f6fa990ff86","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"6c48f8d6-d691-4cb4-9822-0cdd8d685a45","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"922d36cb-dec1-4f1a-ad75-bd3b04cb9206","name":"Trick or Trees Planting Event: Masseygrove Park","dates":[1792850400000],"start":"2026-10-24T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Masseygrove Park","address":"80 Kendleton Dr, Etobicoke, ON M9V 1V5","lat":43.735458,"lng":-79.586894},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Join us for a Halloween planting event at Masseygrove Park! Enhance our urban tree canopy by planting native trees and shrubs. Costumes are encouraged.\n\nEvent site conditions vary. Contact us for more information including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"ofBUtEyIZ0UeWwsSFZsYLQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"c67c6f81-b470-424c-a7cd-be92f10419d6","name":"Elm Park Tree Planting Event","dates":[1793718000000],"start":"2026-11-03T10:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-03T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Elm Park","address":"230 Gosford Blvd, North York, ON M3N 1V5","lat":43.769497,"lng":-79.527135},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Nurture nature by planting native trees and shrubs at Elm Park.\n\nEvent site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"5FBRsi59GZKd0vmn4kCGiw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"210d7178-dc4f-4429-9c23-7137cc36fbb2","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"150bf10c-4406-4dc2-ab91-c54e9d4c008b","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200