Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"876ea10b-b57c-40da-a348-123feafe1533","name":"Roby Lakatos and Medusa Quartet with Turkwaz","dates":[1796256000000],"start":"2026-12-02T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-02T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.66792,"lng":-79.396238},"free":false,"low":55,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Hungarian violinist Roby Lakatos dazzles with fiery Roma‑inspired virtuosity. \n\nMedusa and Turkwaz, a powerhouse octet of string players, percussionists and vocalists open the night.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"g23l4FVwhHUD3Cm9LGw1zw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/roby-lakatos-447601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/447601"},{"id":"d8bcc45d-42c7-4f38-80c3-7e4bab222747","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"41a192f4-951f-4bae-9ae8-4059afdcd834","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"6351e9b6-08fc-4946-8255-b1509b8124a1","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"b006ad4f-bf47-42ad-8953-6a39c09062c2","name":"Bravo Beethoven and Homeland","dates":[1791070200000],"start":"2026-10-03T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity- St. Paul's Centre","address":"427 Bloor St. West, Toronto, M5S 1X7","lat":43.759292,"lng":-79.407796},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a night that's equal parts celebration and discovery.\n\nWe welcome internationally acclaimed pianist Sheng Cai for an evening anchored by two Beethoven favourites and the world premiere of Vahram Sargsyan's Ergir (Homeland), a deeply personal journey through ancestral melodies by a Jules Léger Prize-winning composer. Joyful and nostalgic, Homeland is rooted in ancestral memory, and hearing it for the very first time will create beautiful new memories.\n\nThe program opens with Beethoven's Piano Concerto No. 2, bright and full of personality, closes as Maestro Nurhan Arman leads the orchestra in Beethoven's \"Harp\" String Quartet in a lush orchestral version.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Sinfonia Toronto","image":"k10144fRhtZ-rlbJqjF1WA","website":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/bravo-beethoven","tickets":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/bravo-beethoven"},{"id":"3f71909e-d1b1-433b-8444-9bf1d6708e93","name":"Sleuth","dates":[1792193400000,1792260000000,1792279800000,1792346400000,1792539000000,1792594800000,1792625400000,1792711800000,1792864800000,1792884600000,1792951200000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793286000000,1793316600000,1793403000000,1793469600000,1793489400000,1793559600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":52,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFees and taxes included. Three play packages save 15 per cent.","description":"A love letter to the classic crime thriller, Anthony Shaffer’s Sleuth is packed with razor-sharp dialogue and psychological games that will keep you guessing until the very end. When a celebrated mystery writer invites his wife’s lover to his secluded English country estate, what begins as a seemingly civilized encounter quickly spirals into a dangerous contest of wit and manipulation. But who is really in control, and who is playing whom?\n\nDirected by Peter Fernandes, this gripping production stars Patrick Galligan as Andrew Wyke and Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"cbd1faf2-50c4-42e2-9e6a-2a97a2429994","name":"Sleuth","dates":[1792193400000,1792260000000,1792279800000,1792346400000,1792539000000,1792594800000,1792625400000,1792711800000,1792864800000,1792884600000,1792951200000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793286000000,1793316600000,1793403000000,1793469600000,1793489400000,1793559600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":52,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFees and taxes included. Three play packages save 15 per cent.","description":"A love letter to the classic crime thriller, Anthony Shaffer’s Sleuth is packed with razor-sharp dialogue and psychological games that will keep you guessing until the very end. When a celebrated mystery writer invites his wife’s lover to his secluded English country estate, what begins as a seemingly civilized encounter quickly spirals into a dangerous contest of wit and manipulation. But who is really in control, and who is playing whom?\n\nDirected by Peter Fernandes, this gripping production stars Patrick Galligan as Andrew Wyke and Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"f7ec9e51-c3fe-47f6-94a0-709a9193c5f0","name":"Sleuth","dates":[1792193400000,1792260000000,1792279800000,1792346400000,1792539000000,1792594800000,1792625400000,1792711800000,1792864800000,1792884600000,1792951200000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793286000000,1793316600000,1793403000000,1793469600000,1793489400000,1793559600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":52,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFees and taxes included. Three play packages save 15 per cent.","description":"A love letter to the classic crime thriller, Anthony Shaffer’s Sleuth is packed with razor-sharp dialogue and psychological games that will keep you guessing until the very end. When a celebrated mystery writer invites his wife’s lover to his secluded English country estate, what begins as a seemingly civilized encounter quickly spirals into a dangerous contest of wit and manipulation. But who is really in control, and who is playing whom?\n\nDirected by Peter Fernandes, this gripping production stars Patrick Galligan as Andrew Wyke and Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"734c3e4c-826a-467d-81c5-5bb20c72c824","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"46135674-a2c5-45b9-9775-20dd6f4db45c","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"1e5cb2f9-fb63-43ee-8a75-86912ab52f75","name":"Pineway Park Tree Planting Event","dates":[1791986400000],"start":"2026-10-14T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Pineway Park","address":"110 Pineway Blvd, North York, ON M2H 1C2","lat":43.796124,"lng":-79.375891},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Enhance our urban tree canopy by planting native trees and shrubs at Pineway Park.\n\nPlease note there are no washroom facilities on site. Event site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"OulBdyfjecdAMILc68ecog","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"54c5da28-fdab-49e0-9f6b-f4a1996b487d","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"0987177a-c7f8-4a18-8343-05e51f67e5c2","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"0b0bfd62-af76-4e5b-97f4-7d10b4689c09","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"8f613ed6-5492-4301-a47f-a5a3b5271bf7","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"07182afa-3b72-48e0-bad4-0439e2c660e3","name":"Celebrating Steve Reich at 90","dates":[1791329400000],"start":"2026-10-06T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856,"lng":-79.396059},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us in a major celebration of the iconic composer, performed by some of the world’s greatest interpreters of his music. \n\nThe concert includes the North American premiere performance of Reich’s “In All Your Ways,” a new work co-commissioned by Soundstreams and leading music organisations from around the world. Also tune into “Music for 18 Musicians,” considered one of Reich’s most iconic works and a hybrid version of the legendary work “Clapping Music” that features Reich himself performing the ostinato part, on film, with Russell Hartenberger performing the other part live in the auditorium. \n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"IwWkW0soLipsLJkoYA5yKQ","website":"https://soundstreams.ca/events/celebrating-steve-reich-at-90/","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/soundstreams-presents-steve-reich-at-90-455401"},{"id":"c22c18f1-6378-4a03-b311-7ea207bc3a78","name":"Pablo Ferrández","dates":[1791502200000],"start":"2026-10-08T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON","lat":43.647496,"lng":-79.375145},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Subscribe and save up to 40%","description":"One of the most compelling artists on today’s international stage, Pablo Ferrández has quickly established himself as a major voice in classical music.\n\nNamed after his great Spanish predecessor Pablo Casals and hailed by some as “the next Yo-Yo Ma”, the Tchaikovsky Prize-winning artist opens our season with his Canadian solo recital debut. \n\nCelebrating the 150th anniversary of Casals, the program honours the legendary artist whose artistry reshaped the cello’s voice, featuring solo works by J.S. Bach, Benjamin Britten and Gaspar Cassadó.\n\n“A cellist of magnetic presence and extraordinary lyricism.” - Gramophone.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Music Toronto","image":"UTCNeyWdc9k7CzaYz7MsPw","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/pablo-ferrandez","tickets":"https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event/100064FC217FE3D7"},{"id":"ac17dfc5-c8cc-4449-abe2-9d91a782442a","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"71cea894-be58-48e2-8bec-4280cb76b840","name":"The Rugby Rematch Tour","dates":[1792191600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"BMO Field","address":"170 Princes' Blvd, Toronto, ON, M6K 3C3","lat":43.633275,"lng":-79.418573},"free":false,"low":58.82,"high":87.8,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nGroup tickets available.","description":"Rugby Canada is bringing a major international showdown to Toronto this fall and it’s kind of a big deal. \n\nCanada's Women's Rugby Team, world-ranked No. 3, will make their long-awaited debut at BMO Field hosting world No. 1 England in a high-stakes rematch of the 2025 Women’s Rugby World Cup final.  \n\nThe game is part of the Rugby Rematch Tour, a two-city series that gives Canadian fans a rare chance to see some of the best players in the world compete on home turf.  \n\nWhether you’re a die-hard rugby fan, a general sports lover, big on women’s sports, or just looking for something new to check out in the city, this event promises something for everyone. \n\nGet your tickets now and help Rugby Canada set a new North-American attendance record for a women's rugby match.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":"Canadian Tire Corporation","image":"X2Nv2J4GqoEbUTi-15wkdA","website":"https://rugbyrematchtour.ca","tickets":"https://www.ticketmaster.ca/rugby-canada-wxv-toronto-v-england-toronto-ontario-10-16-2026/event/100064AC9E459BCC"},{"id":"990b6b0b-4425-4d89-83c6-43f89c1a4889","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"a74ef055-7291-4848-b168-b97bac47c64c","name":"John Beasley’s Unlimited Miles: Miles Davis at 100","dates":[1794099600000],"start":"2026-11-07T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-07T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667902,"lng":-79.396305},"free":false,"low":50,"high":125,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Under the direction of Grammy Award-winning pianist, composer, and arranger John Beasley, star‑studded musicians Marcus Strickland on saxophone, Sean Jones on trumpet, Ben Williams on bass, and Terreon Gully on drums delve into the visionary spirit and boundless creativity of Miles Davis.  \n\nA musical shapeshifter with deep jazz roots, Beasley performed with Miles Davis and Freddie Hubbard in his twenties and has since collaborated with Dianne Reeves, Christian McBride, Chaka Khan, A.R. Rahman, Chucho Valdés, and Steely Dan, among others. \n\n“Beasley, the one-time keyboardist for Freddie Hubbard and Miles Davis, reflects a variety of generational influences, incorporating the emphatic chordal clusters of Herbie Hancock, the rhythmic quirkiness of Monk and the lush intelligence of Art Tatum into a highly refined personal voice.” (Los Angeles Times).\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"ctkQtaqWhPINbCU9zdNJgQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/john-beasleys-unlimited-miles-miles-davis-at-100-426601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/426601"},{"id":"3655150a-b67b-4e96-aaab-2888f64a26d4","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7Zt