 bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"de676c4a-e1f8-4625-b06f-765a8cd3e1bc","name":"Dance of Oak Leaves","dates":[1791066600000],"start":"2026-10-03T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Burdock Music Hall","address":"1184 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M6H 1N2","lat":43.659416,"lng":-79.437781},"free":false,"low":22.45,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Plus HST.","description":"The celebrated Toronto-based Kurdish kamāncha player, composer and singer Shahriyār Jamshidi returns Toronto to reverberate the sounds of Kurdish musical heritage.\n\nHighlighting the Kurdish mountain themes which spread from West Asia through Central Asia in his kamāncha performance while singing the unforgettable tunes with new arrangements from all four parts of Kurdistan, including performing his compositions. \n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"vV7aYAzxkfHt3b9bEBiilQ","website":"https://shahriyarjamshidi.com/event/an-autumn-eventide-with-kurdish-kamancha-burdock-music-hall/","tickets":"https://www.showpass.com/dance-of-oak-leaves/"},{"id":"8c9cb237-24b9-42f4-a279-84c6f7a35ef0","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"01d5b901-a77e-4d0a-9c1d-b868f548c42b","name":"Royal Conservatory Orchestra with conductor Tania Miller with Anna Yin, violin","dates":[1795827600000],"start":"2026-11-27T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-27T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667891,"lng":-79.396304},"free":false,"low":25,"high":60,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Canadian conductor Tania Miller has distinguished herself as a dynamic interpreter, musician, and innovator. \n\nArtistic Director of the Brott Music Festival in Canada and the Artistic Director and Conductor of the National Academy Orchestra of Canada and of Brott Opera, Maestra Miller recently debuted with the National Symphony of Mexico and has upcoming concerts with the Xalapa Symphony of Mexico, the Janáček Philharmonic in Ostrava, Czech Republic and Madison Symphony.   ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"PxC654gMhDYbcyavjSD-sQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/royal-conservatory-orchestra-with-conductor-tania","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/432001"},{"id":"3541712c-dd65-4e4c-80bc-834282b102e2","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"29ea0264-180c-4cf5-b2d8-be00fd7c2690","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"64bbb762-e180-4fbf-a89b-264c0d77ce43","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800