Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"e66c0a57-0549-489d-908b-090a9519933a","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"4c4c0bc9-b683-48ff-9910-c72305410d0d","name":"Toronto Comedy All Stars","dates":[1785632400000,1786847400000,1788057000000,1788575400000,1789261200000,1790476200000,1790994600000,1792890000000,1794022200000,1794103200000,1796441400000,1798938000000],"start":"2026-08-01T21:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-02T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557,"lng":-79.379778},"free":false,"low":22,"high":25,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Catch the hottest standups from Toronto’s world class comedy scene!\n\nFeaturing comedians seen on Prime, Netflix Is A Joke Fest, Just For Laughs, CBC, Crave, Hulu and more. \n\nDiscover the next wave of comedy stars at the iconic Second City stage, famous for launching legends like Catherine O'Hara, Eugene Levy, Mike Myers & many more!\n\nOver the past decade this show has sold out at prestigious venues like the National Arts Centre in Ottawa, Yuk Yuk’s Comedy Club in Toronto and the Gas Station Arts Centre in Winnipeg. \n\nThis show is rated M for Mature. Viewer discretion advised.","categories":["Comedy","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Second City","image":"HFuSoAQdzxyCxb_O9N3j4A","website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/toronto-comedy-all-stars-tor","tickets":"https://linktr.ee/torontocomedyallstars"},{"id":"5ad8a2d6-4017-4299-ac8b-8c9e22ea2e53","name":"Country Night featuring The Jim Cuddy Family Band","dates":[1792263600000],"start":"2026-10-17T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Variety Village","address":"3701 Danforth Ave, Scarborough, ON, M1N 2G2","lat":43.698594,"lng":-79.257226},"free":false,"low":100,"high":250,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Get ready for an unforgettable concert experience!\n\nLed by Canadian musician and Blue Rodeo co-founder Jim Cuddy, alongside his sons, Devin Cuddy and Sam Polley, The Jim Cuddy Family Band will bring an incredible evening of live music and unforgettable performances to Variety Village.\n\nOpening the show, cheer on Cheatin’ Hearts as they bring their high-energy line dancing experience.\n\nKnown across Toronto for creating fun, welcoming dance experiences, their energetic instructors will have everyone moving, whether you’re a seasoned dancer or trying line dancing for the very first time. Grab your boots, bring your best moves, and get ready to dance the night away!","categories":["Charity/Cause","Dance","Live Performances"],"presenter":"DeClute Real Estate","image":"Qq2bOBspsYJvVtO3Gkcw_Q","website":"https://country-night.raiselysite.com/","tickets":"https://country-night.raiselysite.com/"},{"id":"5b5322f7-d2f5-4f0b-918e-9c415bad3ac0","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"ea2277d6-b86a-4481-96aa-c7ecaedfdf09","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"6c67a6e5-42b0-401a-8c92-85942a1fa72b","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"15a36f52-4725-498e-a2ae-add691e5d10e","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"9034f48f-7063-4258-8a46-7d237254fb71","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"2920ba1b-063a-4672-93e1-33def15364bc","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793