0,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"bd266aac-d726-4e20-8625-d93e00f1574b","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"b53acbe9-b55b-49b7-b445-17781d0bd017","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"7bf6e0b8-1d1d-401c-b096-c32b3b81b034","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"ad368bd9-e32d-43dd-aca5-a8b4dd0a4da1","name":"Madison Chow: Overflow","dates":[1788966000000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789315200000,178