00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The water has a body, and so do I. A body as old as time itself, one that has ebbed and flowed for longer than I can comprehend. \n\nWithin the tradition of photography, we have often constrained bodies of water and other natural elements to romantic fragments within their time. We halt them within the photographic moment, failing to recognize water for its ephemeral and animate nature, one that requires our dedication and time to understand.\n\nOverflow seeks to recognize picture as privilege by inviting water to be a collaborator in the photographic process. By using a camera-less medium, the traditional colonial gaze of the lens is removed from the creation of the image, allowing the water to take a leading role in its own imaging. To create these images, I met the water at the shoreline, often in the quiet of morning, and arranged a composition that included nearby flora, natural objects from along the shore, or my own body.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","History"],"presenter":null,"image":"dIbhRBySswwZ6Cbw9goudg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/madison-chow-overflow/","tickets":null},{"id":"6e7c558c-c29a-4ac8-8c21-9c872b354e54","name":"Indigenous Beading Workshop: Flat Stitch Ojibway Flower","dates":[1791644400000],"start":"2026-10-10T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bata Shoe Museum","address":"327 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W7","lat":43.667232212,"lng":-79.400148381},"free":false,"low":65,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a day of creativity, connection, and cultural learning in this hands-on Indigenous beading workshop led by Natalie Ortiz. Participants will learn how to create beautiful Beaded Flat Stitch Ojibway Flowers while exploring the rich traditions and teachings behind this intricate art form.\n\nGuided step-by-step by Natalie, guests will be introduced to foundational beading techniques and design practices rooted in Indigenous traditions. Whether you are completely new to beading or looking to deepen your skills, this welcoming workshop offers an opportunity to slow down, learn through making, and create a meaningful handmade piece to take home.\n\nRecommended for participants ages 16 and up.","categories":["Indigenous","Museum","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":"dgrHIaDmJxGHXxfJXdLEjg","website":"https://www.batashoemuseum.ca","tickets":"https://www.batashoemuseum.ca"},{"id":"0ea84220-6d27-4dea-999d-f1587dc1eb85","name":"Black History Planting Event: Cedarvale Park","dates":[1791036000000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedarvale Park","address":"57 Strathearn Rd, Toronto, ON M6C 1R5","lat":43.692607,"lng":-79.428461},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Join us for a special Black History planting event at Cedarvale Park. Plant native trees and shrubs to enhance the urban canopy and learn about Black History and nature with scholar, writer and activist Jacqueline L. Scott. Additional registration for the tour is required. Please email us at greentoronto@toronto.ca. \n\nEvent site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.\n","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"-Er20u6oUZ_IOTpdAamfUQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"1512de95-5c09-4dc9-a16a-c42dbe90b72c","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"f28197db-5168-4413-8e08-0e6081ef6225","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"67a59c65-ca0f-4337-a1e7-b033c8e760cd","name":"Nuit Blanche at 401 Richmond","dates":[1791068400000,1791154800000],"start":"2026-10-03T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"401 Richmond Street West","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Throughout Toronto’s all-night celebration of contemporary art, 401 will be teeming with dynamic and interactive exhibitions, installations and performances. \n\nTwo floors of creative exploration offer a unique experience highlighting a diversity of cultural practice and showcasing the iconic address that continues to transform Toronto’s cultural landscape.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"tOyXWXnZgnVpRiTLhq-WCg","website":"https://401richmond.com/event/nuit-blanche-2026/","tickets":null},{"id":"5adddedb-88d1-4513-b097-d705d0192967","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"3ff41f44-52be-4951-bd7d-1f15026470ae","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"17be7620-12d4-4a0e-a065-6204102a94a3","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"4b3d4d08-29cf-4f7b-9a6c-4ece91d48445","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"f04ac9e6-4333-48bc-b108-2c28269c51d4","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,178696800000