8d986615daf5","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","dates":[1789565400000,1789738200000,1790170200000,1790343000000,1790775000000,1790947800000,1791379800000,1791552600000,1791984600000,1792157400000],"start":"2026-09-16T09:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T09:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"i2SMsQnvkRtaYNfLbdOTrw","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-cedarridge/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-cedarridge/"},{"id":"83e7fb2f-bbd5-4e7e-870b-b91b300eb0cb","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","dates":[1789565400000,1789738200000,1790170200000,1790343000000,1790775000000,1790947800000,1791379800000,1791552600000,1791984600000,1792157400000],"start":"2026-09-16T09:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T09:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"i2SMsQnvkRtaYNfLbdOTrw","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-cedarridge/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-cedarridge/"},{"id":"d3de2d4e-bcec-402c-95a4-9dc2849308d7","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at East Scarborough Storefront","dates":[1789578000000,1789750800000,1790182800000,1790355600000,1790787600000,1790960400000,1791392400000,1791565200000,1791997200000,1792170000000],"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"F4gQpCvBNPCjggJ5mJPA0g","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/"},{"id":"3bee3b05-78bb-4d22-9c55-fbfb4580b285","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at East Scarborough Storefront","dates":[1789578000000,1789750800000,1790182800000,1790355600000,1790787600000,1790960400000,1791392400000,1791565200000,1791997200000,1792170000000],"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"F4gQpCvBNPCjggJ5mJPA0g","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/"},{"id":"c8211c0a-ab01-4cd0-9177-1e4026047e51","name":"Paddleboarding at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789223400000,1789828200000,1790433000000,1791037800000],"start":"2026-09-12T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Please register using the correct link below:\nSat September 12 Paddleboarding\n10:30 am, 12:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999636049252\nSat September 19 Paddleboarding\n10:30 am, 12:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999638061270\nSat September 26 Paddleboarding\n10:30 am, 12:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999638111420\n\n","description":"Get out on the water and experience Biidaasige Park from a whole new perspective! Join Don’t Mess with the Don for a fun and refreshing paddleboarding adventure along Toronto’s stunning new waterfront park. Whether you’re a first-timer or an experienced paddler, this is a great way to connect with nature, enjoy the river, and take in the park’s unique landscapes from the water. All equipment is provided, including a paddleboard, paddle, and personal flotation device (PFD). \n\nParticipants will have up to 1.5 hours to explore at their own pace. Please wear weather-appropriate clothing and water shoes, and bring water to stay hydrated. Recommended for ages 12+. \n\nCome discover the beauty of Biidaasige Park, build confidence on the water, and enjoy an unforgettable summer morning outdoors!","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"L4b1C942bMoMQdF9ic2Ofw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1998641932823"},{"id":"c7db6575-bead-489b-a5aa-f42f095c35db","name":"Stewart Goodyear with the New Orford String Quartet","dates":[1797192000000],"start":"2026-12-13T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.66787,"lng":-79.39627},"free":false,"low":60,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"\"One of the best pianists of his generation\" (Philadelphia Inquirer), the RCM alumnus and Artist-in-Residence Stewart Goodyear performs Ravel’s shimmering Piano Trio, Brahms’s richly expressive Piano Quintet along with his own quintet piece with the New Orford String Quartet. \n\nProclaimed \"a phenomenon\" by the Los Angeles Times, Goodyear is an accomplished concert pianist, improviser, and composer. \n\nHe has performed with and has been commissioned by, many of the major orchestras and chamber music organizations around the world. His recent commissions include an orchestral work for the Chineke! Orchestra, his Piano Quintet for the Penderecki String Quartet and a piano work for the Honens Piano Competition.  \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/stewart-goodyear-with-the-new-orford-string-quartet-428802","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/428802"},{"id":"2f4dc501-8792-4372-b0df-163b187ea957","name":"Ontology Exhibition","dates":[1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000],"start":"2026-09-26T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"In this solo exhibition, Zhan Zhang creates hypothetical paper-based life forms and biotic communities to explore the delicate interplay between visibility, memory and cultural identity. The title “Ontology” refers to the study of being – examining what types of entities exist, how they can be grouped and how they relate to one another.\n\nExistence is not static; it is intertwined with absence, memory and what has not yet dissipated. Zhang is fascinated by creating things people were never meant to see – or were never meant to exist. These organic, hollow forms are neither specimens nor memorials, but attempts to embody a “presence through absence.”\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"VeVMw9xjXdYqOr7ZtaLj4w","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"d1648a09-a773-4e3a-b3d7-2f8e41939c5c","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"23daa48c-26ac-412a-8e93-29e670c52a5a","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"114d38af-5d4b-4e26-90f5-56940be0f7af","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"12edc2ac-d931-45c8-aaf1-ee78bd959015","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"878e8dac-ac38-4857-bef7-853ec9b464a0","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"baa3557b-8024-42f8-aad4-1001efdf9277","name":"Ravi Coltrane: The John Coltrane Centennial with Ewen Farncombe and Friends","dates":[1796518800000],"start":"2026-12-05T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-05T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667878,"lng":-79.396302},"free":false,"low":50,"high":135,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The visionary saxophonist honours his father’s legacy. \n\nRavi Coltrane is a critically acclaimed Grammy Award-nominated saxophonist, bandleader and composer. Over the course of a twenty year career, Mr. Coltrane has worked as a sideman to many, recorded noteworthy albums for himself and others and founded a prominent independent record label, RKM. \n\nEwen Farncombe on piano, Jesse Ryan on saxophone, Norbert Botos on drums and Jon Meyer on bass, open the evening with a Miles Davis set. Farncombe is a Juno Award nominated pianist and composer who has earned a reputation as a highly skilled musician. They will reimagine tunes from Miles’ Kind of Blue along with other works by the master. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"txL8g-5wplGW9XJoAz1YWg","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ravi-coltrane-the-john-coltrane-centennial-426002","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/426002"},{"id":"18d1a421-c752-4328-ad97-d77aa0346a02","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"3621a483-013d-42fb-b4b3-c87d6d51271e","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"efed7b93-40de-4441-98a9-2abf4ff17129","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"d6b9df3f-a5ce-456e-bc74-998d8f5a4644","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"5d81442f-02bd-47be-a8ef-1672a1584589","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most eleme