 Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"2a62f3e2-a5fb-4692-b44c-e98a59ee8f51","name":"Royal Conservatory Orchestra with Conductor Laura Jackson and Shyler Macaggi on Viola","dates":[1791590400000],"start":"2026-10-09T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-09T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667895,"lng":-79.396272},"free":false,"low":25,"high":60,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Known for her dynamic presence on the podium and her “splendid and confident” (San Francisco Classical Voice) conducting, Laura Jackson leads the Royal Conservatory Orchestra in a powerful season-opening program. \n\nPlease join us! This concert is preceded by a short performance by talented students of The Royal Conservatory. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"DOxA3T0CEbNpz85XcxhOgw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/royal-conservatory-orchestra-with-conductor-laura","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts"},{"id":"f122ab6d-343d-481e-8253-e8c18c956797","name":"Sleuth","dates":[1792193400000,1792260000000,1792279800000,1792346400000,1792539000000,1792594800000,1792625400000,1792711800000,1792864800000,1792884600000,1792951200000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793286000000,1793316600000,1793403000000,1793469600000,1793489400000,1793559600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":52,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFees and taxes included. Three play packages save 15 per cent.","description":"A love letter to the classic crime thriller, Anthony Shaffer’s Sleuth is packed with razor-sharp dialogue and psychological games that will keep you guessing until the very end. When a celebrated mystery writer invites his wife’s lover to his secluded English country estate, what begins as a seemingly civilized encounter quickly spirals into a dangerous contest of wit and manipulation. But who is really in control, and who is playing whom?\n\nDirected by Peter Fernandes, this gripping production stars Patrick Galligan as Andrew Wyke and Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"3bb6c73b-1a0a-4c51-b10f-79b86e100449","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"4885bc88-6b1e-4f29-a208-984194577d9e","name":"Sleuth","dates":[1792193400000,1792260000000,1792279800000,1792346400000,1792539000000,1792594800000,1792625400000,1792711800000,1792864800000,1792884600000,1792951200000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793286000000,1793316600000,1793403000000,1793469600000,1793489400000,1793559600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":52,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFees and taxes included. Three play packages save 15 per cent.","description":"A love letter to the classic crime thriller, Anthony Shaffer’s Sleuth is packed with razor-sharp dialogue and psychological games that will keep you guessing until the very end. When a celebrated mystery writer invites his wife’s lover to his secluded English country estate, what begins as a seemingly civilized encounter quickly spirals into a dangerous contest of wit and manipulation. But who is really in control, and who is playing whom?\n\nDirected by Peter Fernandes, this gripping production stars Patrick Galligan as Andrew Wyke and Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"df324f6e-a3a0-4b48-b572-99480713e792","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"cd102902-f0d6-4b9f-ab97-9948900cdc51","name":"Robi Botos and Friends","dates":[1796947200000],"start":"2026-12-10T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-10T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667938,"lng":-79.39616},"free":false,"low":50,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The protégé of Canadian jazz legend Oscar Peterson and RCM’s Jazz Artist in Residence returns with his mesmerizing blend of bebop, modern jazz and eastern European sounds.\n\nA three-time Juno Award-winning musician, composer and educator, Robi Botos has been hailed as one of the most diverse multi-instrumentalists of this generation. \n\nDrawing on inspiration from his Hungarian roots, his invariably expanding taste in music, or the experiences that shaped his life, Robi’s incomparable creativity and seemingly limitless technical ability have kept audiences returning to his performances with an eagerness for more than 25 years.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"AKfxgMeN9WlDortbeRX9iA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/robi-botos-and-friends-454201","tickets":"http://rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/454201"},{"id":"312b56e8-ff32-401d-8139-ce8ae45a64d4","name":"The Robert W. and G. Ann Corcoran Concerto Competition Finals","dates":[1800489600000],"start":"2027-01-20T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-20T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667899,"lng":-79.396257},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Students of The Glenn Gould School compete for the opportunity to perform a concerto with the Royal Conservatory Orchestra during the 2027 - 28 concert season.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/the-robert-w-and-g-ann-corcoran-concerto-competition-finals-452001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/452001"},{"id":"08b95fb1-1c1a-40e6-a576-78178d401ebf","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"1b3356d6-6120-44f9-b26f-be54c4c09c46","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,17