ne Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"564b7ede-87ea-4a5e-8971-8d42c97cba5f","name":"A Fine Balance","dates":[1787700600000,1787787000000,1787873400000,1787959800000,1788046200000,1788132600000,1788219000000,1788305400000,1788391800000,1788478200000,1788564600000,1788651000000,1788737400000,1788823800000,1788910200000,1788996600000,1789083000000,1789169400000,1789255800000,1789342200000,1789428600000,1789515000000,1789601400000,1789687800000,1789774200000,1789860600000,1789947000000,1790033400000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790465400000,1790551800000,1790638200000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791070200000,1791156600000,1791243000000,1791329400000,1791415800000,1791502200000,1791588600000,1791675000000,1791761400000],"start":"2026-08-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rohinton Mistry’s beloved novel exploring resilience and injustice during India’s 1975 emergency comes to life in a new stage adaptation.\n\nIn a cramped Bombay apartment turned illegal garment factory, four unlikely companions are thrown together. As the political crisis deepens and the country reels under authoritarian crackdown, this fragile household becomes a refuge and an unexpected bond begins to take hold.\n\nAs devastating as it is humane, A Fine Balance, adapted by Anosh Irani, Governor General’s Literary Award finalist and recipient of the Writers’ Trust Engel Findley Award, vividly brings Mistry's powerful story to the stage.\n\nAccolades for the novel include the Giller Prize, 1995, Los Angeles Times Book Prize for Fiction, 1996, Oprah’s Book Club, November 2001, Commonwealth Writers’ Prize, 1996 and Booker Prize Shortlisted Finalist, 1996.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"nYaJaPii2CPhcIO2l_b2ZQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/a-fine-balance","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1076"},{"id":"46806ab8-cba6-4bf7-898f-80ffe240ba78","name":"So Now You Know: Personal Stories in Motion","dates":[1791054000000],"start":"2026-10-03T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Harbourfront Centre","address":"235 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63923186,"lng":-79.383105327},"free":false,"low":50,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Includes taxes and fees.","description":"A poignant dance and theatre performance of shared personal stories on love, childhood, family and more.\n\nSo Now You Know is a community engagement performance that combines storytelling and movement to create a show that is hilarious, poignant and uplifting. Artistic director Janet Roston and storytelling coach Ryan Bergmann work alongside members from the Toronto community to develop their personal stories of discovery and shape movement unique to each of them. \n\nThis is an afternoon about (and for) Toronto!","categories":["Dance","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"ZgqnY9bk-YEK58JgCWl_lg","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/so-now-you-know/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1284357?performanceId=11846598"},{"id":"1b331a9f-d577-46ba-8ed1-5dd0186702cf","name":"Daniil Trifonov, piano","dates":[1795377600000],"start":"2026-11-22T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667927,"lng":-79.396209},"free":false,"low":135,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Grammy Award–winning pianist Daniil Trifonov returns to perform a vibrant program of works by Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Ginastera and his own works.\n\nCombining consummate technique with rare sensitivity and depth, Trifonov’s performances are a perpetual source of awe. Named Gramophone’s 2016 Artist of the Year and Musical America’s 2019 Artist of the Year, he was made a Chevalier de l’Ordre des Arts et des Lettres by the French government in 2021.\n\n“Without question the most astounding young pianist of our age.” (The London Times).\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"rS11tb5WViha0rhJ1MBHKg","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/daniil-trifonov-piano-427002","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/427002"},{"id":"e6812d24-5bfc-4e4e-b3af-c93b51a15af9","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"2ca2bd47-03f7-4e44-a5ab-48bc871ba756","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"f5ed32b0-427d-4a2a-b4b1-b7852a7ef0e9","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"0e4a8a2a-7ea7-4879-a560-26b687dcbb67","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"cad4119d-275c-4ac3-a925-8a34ef004026","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"ae074d77-5d65-49c5-8e2e-b7172c42b385","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"7c527c00-5ee2-45bf-b419-d10861bab7dd","name":"Richard Avedon: Immortal: Portraits of Aging","dates":[1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789398000000,1789484400000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790002800000,1790089200000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790607600000,1790694000000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791212400000,1791298800000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791817200000,1791903600000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792422000000,1792508400000,1792594800000,1792681200000,1792767600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793026800000,1793113200000,1793199600000,1793286000000,1793372400000,1793458800000,1793548800000,1793635200000,1793721600000,1793808000000,1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794240000000,1794326400000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1794844800000,1794931200000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795449600000,1795536000000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796054400000,1796140800000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000],"start":"2026-09-09T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For nearly half a century, celebrated American photographer Richard Avedon confronted one of portraiture’s enduring taboos: aging. \n\nFrom his earliest years at Harper’s Bazaar, Avedon broke with the conventions of idealized celebrity portraiture, revealing the marks of time on his subjects’ faces with unsparing clarity. \n\nBringing together nearly 100 portraits made between the early 1950s and 2004, the exhibition features artists, writers, musicians and cultural icons including Toni Morrison, Gabriel García Márquez, Duke Ellington, Ronald Reagan, the Duke and Duchess of Windsor, Patti Smith, Truman Capote and the Dalai Lama. \n\nImmortal also includes a restaging of Avedon’s seminal 1974 Museum of Modern Art exhibition Jacob Israel Avedon, which chronicled his father’s final years in nine extraordinary portraits. Taken as a whole, the photographs reveal a lesser-known dimension of Avedon’s practice and offer an unprecedented exploration of aging through his distinctive vision.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/richard-avedon-immortal/","tickets":null},{"id":"c8537f56-6cab-45a4-8b90-2f139918affb","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"d4bfef65-ca73-450e-90fd-221a43e5ea04","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"83318d12-3db8-4c02-a3ef-d3b4dd4fed7b","name":"Wine in the Wilderness","dates":[1789860600000,1789927200000,1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790787600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-19T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":45,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Harlem, 1964. As riots unfold outside, painter Bill Jameson is inside his apartment putting the final touches on a portrait series about Black womanhood. \n\nWhen Tommy is brought in to model, her presence begins to reveal the quiet hierarchies shaping the evening. As drinks are poured and conversation loosens, the group is forced to reckon with how easy it is to repeat the very judgments they hope to rise above.\n\nBy turns funny, intimate, and piercingly intelligent, Wine in the Wilderness is a landmark work. Directed by Jordan Laffrenier, whose searing production of Slave Play was a highlight of last season, this revival brings fresh urgency and emotional precision to Alice Childress’ razor-sharp portrait of seeing and being seen.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Msm8pfduFCPyvnJiCNBpMQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/wine-in-the-wilderness","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9689"},{"id":"810365e9-cdf9-4846-8acd-c03a101d1817","name":"A Christmas Carol","dates":[1794528000000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794789000000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795393800000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795998600000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796603400000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797208200000,1797381000000,1797467400000,1797553800000,1797640200000,1797726600000,1797813000000,1797985800000,1798072200000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":50,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dickens’s timeless holiday story of transformation, kindness and human connection.\n\nThis fresh adaptation by Tim Carroll brings Charles Dickens’s world to life through inventive puppetry, towering ghosts that fill the stage, traditional carols and audience participation with spirited sing-alongs. Interactive performers mingle throughout the theatre, while beautifully detailed period costumes and sets create an atmospheric Victorian Christmas.\n\nMore than 175 years after Dickens first published A Christmas Carol, audiences still recognize themselves in Ebenezer Scrooge: someone who discovers that it’s never too late in life to choose kindness and human connection. For centuries, this iconic story has endured because its themes are still relevant today: What really matters to us? And can people truly change?\n","categories":["Literary","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LEdIigpmjGIgT9QepzspLw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/a-christmas-carol/","tickets":"https://ci.ovationtix.com/36999/production/1283036"},{"id":"a858d668-d323-43a0-85e1-b41e72f15449","name":"Dance Collection DANSE Hall of Fame","dates":[1794171600000],"start":"2026-11-08T16:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-08T16:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Palais Royale Ballroom","address":"1601 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6K 3C1","lat":43.636713,"lng":-79.447178},"free":false,"low":225,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Dance artist tickets, at a reduced price point, will be released closer to the event date. If you are a working Canadian dance professional, you can submit to be included on the waiting list at michael@dcd.ca. Numbers are limited. Submitting your name is not a guarantee you will be offered at ticket.","description":"Join us in celebrating DANSE's 40th Anniversary year as we introduce this year's Hall of Fame inductees! \n\nThis celebration will bring together artists, cultural leaders, donors, sponsors, and audiences from across Canada for an evening of inductions, live performances, community gathering, and delicious appetizers and beverages.","categories":["Dance"],"presenter":null,"image":"A4oGNmx55gYisB83Iwl2Pg","website":"https://halloffame.dcd.ca","tickets":"https://www.eventbee.com/v/2026halloffame#/tickets"},{"id":"aad14343-6645-4907-b7e3-06e0316d2243","name":"The Glenn Gould School: Barber’s A Hand of Bridge and Bernstein’s Trouble in Tahiti","dates":[1794097800000],"start":"2026-11-07T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-07T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This season’s offering will be a double bill feature. Enjoy Samuel Barber’s A Hand of Bridge, a poignant miniature opera that reveals the hidden thoughts of four bridge players during a seemingly ordinary card game. \n\nAs well, listen to Leonard Bernstein’s Trouble in Tahiti, a jazz-infused one-act opera depicting a day in the life of a troubled married couple living in 1950s suburbia. \n\nConducted by Jennifer Tung and directed by Mario Pacheco.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"G-TT5mlKuyWnx74Oc5s_JQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ggs-chamber-opera-barbers-a-hand-of-bridge-and-bernsteins-trouble-in-tahiti-452801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/452801"},{"id":"41ffe10d-70e8-4aee-b8a1-46a738cefd4e","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"396722d3-b264-40b6-bbf5-58f41954d621","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"3efcaeda-9299-4329-8450-f290697374cb","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"b42597f1-7181-4f15-b5d5-663803eb9d8c","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"30e42045-6398-46dd-8a6f-82b88851d7e0","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"b90031e7-40ea-4f93-9eaf-b1e87974bfb9","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"d9c89c87-c76a-4284-bb5a-10a635730cac","name":"Ravine Days Stewarding with Toronto Nature Stewards Highland Creek Park 11-Oct-2026","dates":[1791730800000],"start":"2026-10-11T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Highland Creek Park ","address":"428 Livingston Rd N, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1M4","lat":43.7559834431,"lng":-79.2033254851},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"As part of City of Toronto Ravine Days, the Toronto Nature Stewards Highland Creek team will be adding short talks (~5-10 minutes) - about the beauty, biodiversity and cultural significance of our ravines - to our scheduled nature stewarding. The topic for this event will be early settlers and a changing Highland Creek.\n\nRoll up your sleeves, take part in ecological restoration by removing invasive plants and learn something new about Highland Creek Park!\n\nNote: this is one of a series of 4 opportunities to participate in Ravine Days Stewarding at Highland Creek Park. The full series takes place on the following dates: 27-Sep-2026 (Creation of Highland Creek Ravine), 30-Sep-2026 (Indigenous Peoples and Highland Creek), 11-Oct-2026 (Early Settlers and a Changing Highland Creek), 18-Oct-2026 (Invasive Plants in Highland Creek Ravine).","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"vDcf3gCcb5IOKcHNwPRTuA","website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/ravine-days-stewarding-with-toronto-nature-stewards-highland-creek-park-tickets-2000526904825?aff=oddtdtcreator","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/ravine-days-stewarding-with-toronto-nature-stewards-highland-creek-park-tickets-2000526904825?aff=oddtdtcreator"},{"id":"c294dc4e-5472-4c7b-8b0c-be69bf0a55a0","name":"Pineway Park Tree Planting Event","dates":[1791986400000],"start":"2026-10-14T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Pineway Park","address":"110 Pineway Blvd, North York, ON M2H 1C2","lat":43.796124,"lng":-79.375891},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Enhance our urban tree canopy by planting native trees and shrubs at Pineway Park.\n\nPlease note there are no washroom facilities on site. Event site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"OulBdyfjecdAMILc68ecog","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"e43b8a3c-c5da-4c95-816b-857e5c550989","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"9e47e8a6-22a1-44a8-9eec-fb9b7c079e9e","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"6eae7741-242c-40ec-9899-357d501bbd0d","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"4053591a-ae94-4782-a844-69f42d4bc833","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"8c024094-1a36-4bb2-a678-28e58b69c21e","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"bc389311-5b36-433e-85d7-cf2790232f12","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"61325a75-f6eb-46dc-ad43-00d88e596480","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,17889624