e connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"7ef13cae-ca8c-4ab8-95a6-b2c93a4af0b5","name":"Music Toronto - Karen Ouzounian and Lembit Beecher's MAYRIG/MOTHER","dates":[1808078400000],"start":"2027-04-18T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-18T16:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nSubscribe and Save up to 40%","description":"Cellist Karen Ouzounian, acclaimed for her work with the Silkroad Ensemble and the Aizuri Quartet, joins composer-pianist Lembit Beecher to close the season’s MUSE series with Mayrig, an immersive multimedia program centered on the human voice. \n\nVoices of Ouzounian’s mother and grandmother weave through Armenian music from Anatolia, songs of Lebanon, and the music of Charles Aznavour, alongside new works exploring memory, heritage, and resilience across generations.\n\nThe program spans centuries and cultures, opening and closing with Marin Marais’s Les Voix Humaines. Traditional Armenian songs and early Anatolian recordings appear alongside arrangements of music by Charles Aznavour and Ashot Satyan. Original works by Lembit Beecher are joined by contemporary voices including Layale Chaker, Nathalie Joachim, Niloufar Nourbakhsh, and Karen Ouzounian, interwoven with recorded voices from Ouzounian’s family.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"efwP9WZZRluCc8MFYeu1ow","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/karen-ouzounian-lembit-beecher","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/karen-ouzounian-lembit-beecher"},{"id":"91dafa31-dc04-4bb2-aaef-7f3210aef3a4","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"77cec43f-e58f-4016-b76c-ea53d6521c3f","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"48dc92fb-5892-4840-99ac-b66db105c0af","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"77decd10-7972-4cb8-bee7-c705fb7d77eb","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"d6e01554-752f-48c1-95f2-c6f24bb0f819","name":"Raised by Women","dates":[1806190200000,1806256800000,1806449400000,1806535800000,1806622200000,1806708600000,1806775200000,1806795000000,1806861600000,1807054200000,1807117200000,1807140600000,1807227000000,1807313400000,1807380000000,1807399800000,1807466400000],"start":"2027-03-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-11T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Métis playwright and performer Keith Barker in an intimate, stand-up-inspired solo show that’s as funny as it is searching. With sharp wit and big heart, Keith traces his upbringing by formidable women in Northern Ontario and the complicated legacy of a father who was largely absent but never insignificant.\n\nMoving seamlessly between laughter and reflection, this deeply personal performance finds grace in the mess, proving the funniest stories are often the most true.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage ","image":"PpRZw7S1GaDYkY1vKfSEQg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/raised-by-women","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9700"},{"id":"9068887c-ea4f-4fc6-9712-eda26b309fb1","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"5fe7a39d-2250-4e83-