ption-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"b2e2189b-60a2-48ef-9a31-90b29bd80b5d","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"4bf1afda-9c44-4080-be2c-e0109c65e389","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"bae2f88f-7066-4d9c-8dbb-6403566b61ce","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"f5c3b2b3-24f2-4c2c-b13f-fd27b45cba6e","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"1934d337-1575-45de-809f-986db7445288","name":"Youth Entrepreneurship Program","dates":[1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"fff2b82f-2bc5-47e4-bbf3-143a63f8e13d","name":"The Rainbow Fish Musical","dates":[1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000],"start":"2026-09-19T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Theatre","address":"76 Wychwood Ave studio 176, Toronto, ON","lat":43.680031,"lng":-79.423389},"free":false,"low":30.49,"high":35.49,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nReseller tickets will not be accepted.\n\nPhoto-op with the cast after the show included with every purchase. ","description":"When Rainbow Fish refuses to share their vibrant, shimmering scales, the whole ocean seems to turn against the vain creature. Unhappy that no one adores them anymore, the Rainbow Fish seeks out the wise Octopus, who helps the fish learn that it's far better to be admired for being kind than for being beautiful. \n\nJoin us for this kids-friendly musical performance and immerse yourself in the ocean!\n\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/rainbow-fish-musical-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/rainbow-fish-musical-2026"},{"id":"06a37dc3-4ab5-44fc-88c2-5d4780aad797","name":"Michael Massie | now and then Curatorial Tour with Alysa Procida","dates":[1800478800000],"start":"2027-01-20T16:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-20T16:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the ideas behind this exhibit in a special curator-led tour with exhibition guest curator Alysa Procida. Through an engaging, in-depth discussion, Alysa will explore the exhibition’s curatorial vision and the creative evolution of Michael Massie’s remarkable practice.\n\nSpanning the breadth of Massie’s career, the exhibit brings together an extraordinary collection of works, including his celebrated teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a striking new series of large-scale sculptural installations. This tour offers a unique opportunity to gain deeper insight into the stories, themes, and artistic vision that shape one of the exhibition’s most compelling contemporary voices.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"1n01NQ-zp3Ba9SWUdFBnlQ","website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/michael-massie-now-and-then-curatorial-tour-with-alysa-procida-tickets-1997994860412?aff=ebdsoporgprofile","tickets":null},{"id":"987ff96f-c99c-4ed5-b8fd-404900d0c4c9","name":"Youth Entrepreneurship Program","dates":[1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"2cd7b0ce-4857-4036-a7ac-9b90838c5fa1","name":"Youth Entrepreneurship Program","dates":[1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"e979dbf6-c485-47c5-b113-1fc982dc08b7","name":"Youth Entrepreneurship Program","dates":[1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"d33e2f4e-f1a0-4bac-805b-96a8e713457f","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"87b6e57c-1155-40c8-a513-d613102f739c","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"4d856312-7602-4cc4-a449-aa43527c9424","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"ae7c024d-04c5-46a7-881c-1d0f8a6a9b79","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"3aa62d68-c3ba-4010-9a22-1c6e413aeeb8","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"5d92d4b6-7801-4b24-b4b3-29eb20ebf8d4","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"927c63b1-7135-42ea-8e50-c2b7a056ebac","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"7ef69256-3106-4214-a65d-e979f4e49f15","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"60755c71-14d1-4825-befe-49946019858d","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"8f848134-e720-4815-8941-ca61c343821b","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"05f73e45-16af-40cc-92a4-fdaf8ce0958a","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"52d6bb88-38a1-498a-84fc-6dd547818622","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"9cd70182-a26f-4afe-bbe7-e7058efdd283","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"679b2dd5-0434-45a6-bdff-95bc49611c53","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"5ef70d56-a201-4258-ad29-767571de625f","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"8ee3f7a1-c93c-4093-9c3e-fc7a1ce9e097","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"7d672a61-7dea-4dfe-8926-dcecdf3f122f","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"d17c2df8-4014-4faf-b328-1b98d4c0b8ae","name":"Music Toronto - New Orford String Quartet","dates":[1809646200000],"start":"2027-05-06T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-06T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nSubscribe and Save up to 40%","description":"Well known to Toronto chamber music audiences, the New Orford String Quartet brings its celebrated artistry to Music Toronto in a program of brilliance, energy and spiritual depth. \n\nJoseph Haydn’s sparkling Op. 76 No. 5 opens the evening, followed by Kelly-Marie Murphy’s gripping Dark Energy. The program culminates in the transcendent beauty of Ludwig van Beethoven’s A minor Quartet, Op. 132, part of Music Toronto’s exploration of beloved Beethoven masterpieces during the 2027 anniversary year.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"7wuvYLBJBi1ugT-3JBemUw","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/new-orford-string-quartet","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/new-orford-string-quartet"},{"id":"f2f9c185-c519-4aa6-a836-b787d0623a25","name":"Lassonde Art Trail: Art + Nature Tour","dates":[1789228800000,1789833600000,1790438400000,1791043200000,1791648000000,1792252800000,1792857600000,1793462400000,1794070800000,1794675600000],"start":"2026-09-12T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-14T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join LAT every Saturday at 12 pm or 2 pm for a drop-in Art + Nature tour led by a LAT Art Guide. These walking tours invite participants to explore the artworks along the Lassonde Art Trail while discovering the rich history, ecology, and ongoing transformation of Biidaasige Park.\n\n12 pm - Art + Nature Tour (30 minutes, slow paced)\n2 pm - Art + Nature Tour (1 hour)\nMeet in front of Old Fire Hall 30. All tours are drop-in and free to attend. Please be aware that the trees in the park system are not yet mature, so there is little shade. We recommend dressing according to the weather. Tours are subject to cancellation in the event of adverse weather. Please see Lassonde Art Trail website for further details.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Xy_GPUCC1IStLKdFhFwxCg","website":"https://lassondearttrail.org/art-trail/","tickets":null},{"id":"300a1278-0473-43bb-b566-2728724ee149","name":"Music in the Tavern at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1790895600000,1793923200000,1796342400000],"start":"2026-10-01T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-03T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"The ticket included stew and bread. ","description":"Experience an evening of traditional folk music, historic food, and community in the nearly 200-year-old tavern. Enjoy refreshments from the historic bar and a traditional stew served by the hearth. Gather with friends and community to enjoy music, food, and history.\n\nBread and stew are included with every ticket purchased. \nDrinks are for sale at the event. \n\nTickets are not refundable or transferable. ","categories":["Food/Culinary","Museum","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"9dOP0v02KGJnOe0YD--GeQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/8b34e779-518a-4f76-973d-7e99b7d515ca"},{"id":"21dd935c-4abc-408c-8906-c14653191998","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"d552f2d0-9721-49f1-9eb5-6dde79dc5b48","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"d6875d84-b699-45ce-b5cf-322af7ccc84e","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"90480b05-ae3f-4e6f-b40d-2a5b5cd60751","name":"Bertrand Chamayou, Piano","dates":[1801422000000,1801425600000],"start":"2027-01-31T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-31T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":50,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us for an unforgettable evening with Bertrand Chamayou, one of today’s most strikingly brilliant pianists, as he performs a program celebrating the Romantic and French repertoires!\n\nChamayou has been recognised for his revelatory performances, at once powerfully virtuosic, imaginative and breathtakingly beautiful. A leading interpreter of French music, his vast repertoire includes major bodies of work such as the complete piano works of Ravel, Liszt’s Etudes and Années de Pèlerinage, and Messiaen's Vingt regards sur l'Enfant Jésus. He performs regularly with fellow musicians including cellist Sol Gabetta and is creating a Messiaen project with soprano-conductor Barbara Hannigan, with whom he performed in Koerner Hall in 2024. \n\nThis concert is preceded by a short performance by talented students of The Royal Conservatory. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"H8mRp1LEsdKmUcCdCRHHPw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/bertrand-chamayou-piano-429601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/429601"},{"id":"bb54dda9-8ffd-4f0e-af0e-d876210244b2","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"7de5aba8-ce10-49e3-96af-b415f4c11547","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,179267