, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"ac3e944d-9743-4d7c-bddb-1bed43b6a0c1","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"2b1b6944-8184-4888-b465-aba2e154bd72","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"bb9f88d1-0f8d-4095-a520-ca6ca418a119","name":"Music in the Tavern at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1790895600000,1793923200000,1796342400000],"start":"2026-10-01T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-03T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"The ticket included stew and bread. ","description":"Experience an evening of traditional folk music, historic food, and community in the nearly 200-year-old tavern. Enjoy refreshments from the historic bar and a traditional stew served by the hearth. Gather with friends and community to enjoy music, food, and history.\n\nBread and stew are included with every ticket purchased. \nDrinks are for sale at the event. \n\nTickets are not refundable or transferable. ","categories":["Food/Culinary","Museum","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"9dOP0v02KGJnOe0YD--GeQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/8b34e779-518a-4f76-973d-7e99b7d515ca"},{"id":"f44a3637-bd8f-482d-8cce-240d918343c5","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"780c5a4f-56d7-4dcb-8808-f3ca294f80cc","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"336f4ced-bc5a-43a4-9538-d0184da0148b","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"1f8f647d-54fb-4221-91d8-848de6d673d7","name":"Sir Stephen Hough, piano","dates":[1800820800000],"start":"2027-01-24T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-24T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":65,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"One of the most distinctive artists of his generation, Sir Stephen Hough performs works by Schubert, Brahms and Beethoven, along with his own arrangement of the suite from Mary Poppins. \n\nNamed by The Economist as one of Twenty Living Polymaths, Hough was the first classical performer to be awarded a MacArthur Fellowship (2001). He was awarded Northwestern University’s 2008 Jean Gimbel Lane Prize in Piano, won the Royal Philharmonic Society Instrumentalist Award in 2010. In 2014 he was made a Commander of the Order of the British Empire (CBE) and was knighted in the Queen’s Birthday Honours in 2022. \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"Xn2GeRv5ESdMjnldlaN8fw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/sir-stephen-hough-piano-429401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/429401"},{"id":"e919a59e-0f45-4141-88bc-aae217dee3af","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"d4106640-5515-4224-8460-f89f46c67558","name":"Ratatouille in Concert","dates":[1803772800000],"start":"2027-02-27T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-27T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Roy Thomson Hall","address":"60 Simcoe St, Toronto, ON, M5J 2H5","lat":43.646699,"lng":-79.386451},"free":false,"low":64.7,"high":188.8,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIncluding HST and fees.","description":"Savour Disney and Pixar’s Ratatouille on the big screen!\n\nOrchestra music will be performed live in sync to the picture, original dialogue and sound effects! \n\nConducted by Sarah Hicks, the FILMharmonique Orchestra will prepare Oscar- and GRAMMY-winner Michael Giacchino’s delectable score for one night only!","categories":["Family/Children","Film","Music"],"presenter":"Disney Concerts","image":"GpAWZnBQnD3E_MZ92M5bQQ","website":"https://roythomsonhall.mhrth.com/tickets/ratatouille-in-concert/","tickets":"https://roythomsonhall.mhrth.com/tickets/ratatouille-in-concert/"},{"id":"8cbd7b13-747e-4bb8-ba47-e5e53683621e","name":"Royal Conservatory Orchestra with conductor Earl Lee","dates":[1801875600000],"start":"2027-02-05T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-05T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":25,"high":60,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nPrelude Recital starts at 6:45p.m. \nPlease click on the picture to access the ticket selection page. ","description":"We welcome you to join us for this special performance. Winner of the 2022 Sir Georg Solti Conducting Award, Korean-Canadian conductor Earl Lee has emerged as one of the most compelling and versatile artists of his generation. Alyssa Bartholomew, soprano and winner of the 2026 Robert W. and G. Ann Corcoran Concerto Competition, will also perform.\n\n Ear has led many of North America’s foremost orchestras, including the New York Philharmonic, Boston Symphony Orchestra, San Francisco Symphony, Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra, Toronto Symphony Orchestra and Atlanta Symphony Orchestra. In August 2025, Lee stepped in on short notice to replace Zubin Mehta in the Boston Symphony Orchestra’s performance of Beethoven’s Symphony No. 9 at Tanglewood, where The Boston Globe praised his interpretation as “an unhurried, momentous ritual … the finale nothing short of spectacular.” \n\nThis concert is preceded by a short performance by talented students of The Royal Conservatory. Please join us! ","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"2-_oOdAWnrkIzJlBVi5lOQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/royal-conservatory-orchestra-with-conductor-ea-2","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/431401"},{"id":"3892c810-1981-4170-9603-1ab8deadfca8","name":"Cookie Decorating: Halloween at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793462400000,1793469600000],"start":"2026-10-31T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":false,"low":10,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, enjoy a fun, family-friendly cookie decorating class where history meets creativity. Historic recipe cookies and decorating supplies are provided. Just bring your imagination and your sweet tooth. No previous experience needed. Cookies contain gluten, dairy and eggs.\n\nA ticket-holding adult must accompany children 16 years of age and younger.","categories":["Family/Children","Food/Culinary","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"g6nKGGP1E3l19cC5kc92_A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/toronto/activity/search?onlineSiteId=0&activity_keyword=Halloween%20Cookie%20Decorating%20at%20Montgomery%27s%20Inn&viewMode=list"},{"id":"3fd04b8f-50e4-44e1-8721-4817c82f8e83","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,178904