l,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"41f66aee-cecd-4973-8223-3af75a7cc42c","name":"The Rainbow Fish Musical","dates":[1789826400000,1789912800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1792245600000,1792332000000],"start":"2026-09-19T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Theatre","address":"76 Wychwood Ave studio 176, Toronto, ON","lat":43.680031,"lng":-79.423389},"free":false,"low":30.49,"high":35.49,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nReseller tickets will not be accepted.\n\nPhoto-op with the cast after the show included with every purchase. ","description":"When Rainbow Fish refuses to share their vibrant, shimmering scales, the whole ocean seems to turn against the vain creature. Unhappy that no one adores them anymore, the Rainbow Fish seeks out the wise Octopus, who helps the fish learn that it's far better to be admired for being kind than for being beautiful. \n\nJoin us for this kids-friendly musical performance and immerse yourself in the ocean!\n\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/rainbow-fish-musical-2026","tickets":"https://tickets.ticketwise.com/event/rainbow-fish-musical-2026"},{"id":"160bc32c-0fb9-4e61-ae7f-4f62464354f7","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"48072100-1215-4c55-8b81-5df7b7d0fe10","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"d8c340b0-db41-49c7-8a13-f410d9760238","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZha