0000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000],"start":"2026-10-03T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIn addition to the cost of museum admission ticket.","description":"Discover the haunted history of the Museum as you walk through the very halls where ghosts are said to roam.  \n\nUncover eerie tales, hear ghostly whispers, and explore hidden corners where shadows play tricks on the mind. Don't miss this unique opportunity to explore the supernatural side of art, culture and nature.  ","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"v01BsJ3lGOfA9VI9Eep9fg","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours"},{"id":"64eb6174-6af9-4a11-a836-95e1ac248205","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"a160fe00-a0e9-4772-a70f-01b242d1ef7c","name":"Brews and Bites: Fall Festival at Todmorden Mills","dates":[1791039600000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361228,"lng":-79.36033401},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Connect with one of Toronto’s earliest brewery sites, enjoy local craft beverages and food, find out more about the site’s brewing history, join the historic house tours and engage with local organizations to share stories about food, brewing and communities. This outdoor celebration brings people together through the love of brewing, community and food. Join friends and family and celebrate the stories that connect everyone. ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"n8dZXohFORlN8WznvC9IaQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"b1181bca-1929-4578-85ed-d1d6273f653b","name":"Haunted ROM Tour","dates":[1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000],"start":"2026-10-03T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIn addition to the cost of museum admission ticket.","description":"Discover the haunted history of the Museum as you walk through the very halls where ghosts are said to roam.  \n\nUncover eerie tales, hear ghostly whispers, and explore hidden corners where shadows play tricks on the mind. Don't miss this unique opportunity to explore the supernatural side of art, culture and nature.  ","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"v01BsJ3lGOfA9VI9Eep9fg","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature