6800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"470789a9-f00f-4cfa-971c-a7c04f48530b","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"1bda19e8-4b0d-411a-a1e5-6e14b6ed26ed","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadi