 acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"05c92271-5c23-46a4-ae32-1f1c733bdc74","name":"2026 Hockey Hall of Fame Induction Celebration","dates":[1794063600000,1794150000000,1794263400000],"start":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-09T17:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Hockey Hall of Fame ","address":"Brookfield Place, 30 Yonge Street, Toronto ON, M5E 1X8","lat":43.647006,"lng":-79.377245},"free":false,"low":295,"high":625,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join the Hockey Hall of Fame as we welcome hockey’s newest legends, Class of 2026 Inductees: Patrice Bergeron, Brian Burke, Cindy Curley, Carey Price, Pekka Rinne and Keith Tkachuk.\n\nThis is your chance to say, \"I was there\". Experience an unforgettable weekend with special events and fan experiences, including the Legends Photo Op, QnA Fan Forum and the annual Hockey Hall of Fame Game.\n\nThe celebration culminates with the prestigious Induction Gala, an extraordinary evening featuring red carpet arrivals, hockey legends, gourmet hospitality, a premier silent auction and the live induction of the Class of 2026.\n\n","categories":["Celebrations","Charity/Cause","Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"jv2np708BWDdUpeAAnj7yw","website":"https://www.hhof.com/induction/induction2026/inductiontickets.html","tickets":"https://www.hhof.com/induction/induction2026/inductiontickets.html"},{"id":"c759abcd-14c0-4fa9-a646-6a67f09bc0f7","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"96ff78d2-8330-4245-92aa-24b25cfd7383","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"0e5013aa-a46a-4b28-864a-dfa8cd40a5ab","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"8a7c7e0a-1d3e-4789-8005-146b7ef386b1","na