about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"0ccb3020-8350-438c-9b61-39b28985df2a","name":"Sex in the '80s","dates":[1800145800000,1800212400000,1800405000000,1800491400000,1800577800000,1800664200000,1800750600000,1800817200000,1801009800000,1801096200000,1801182600000,1801269000000,1801355400000,1801422000000,1801614600000,1801701000000,1801787400000,1801873800000,1801960200000,1802026800000],"start":"2027-01-16T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":35,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Old history. New rules.\n\nThey haven’t seen each other since the 1980s. Now two accomplished architects are reunited in a glass-walled Toronto office tower on the eve of a high-stakes competition. Both intend to keep things strictly professional. That proves harder than expected.\n\nAs a long-buried chapter of their shared history resurfaces, a polite reunion turns into a pointed, funny sparring match about memory, ambition, and how much the rules have changed. Meanwhile, their twentysomething colleagues look on and aren’t shy about weighing in.\n\nSmart, topical, and wickedly witty, this is a workplace comedy about generational change and the risky business of revisiting the past.","categories":["Comedy","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"Fcu46jHUFdGt1qpYFrx14A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s","tickets":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/sex-in-the-80s"},{"id":"1e47c4fd-0410-4480-bc3e-c39ec8d81ae6","name":"Grand Soft Day","dates":[1808577000000,1808591400000,1808672400000,1808679600000,1809181800000,1809196200000,1809268200000,1809282600000],"start":"2027-04-24T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Young People's Theatre","address":"165 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5A 3Z4","lat":43.6499984416,"lng":-79.3687420725},"free":false,"low":27,"high":33,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Splash in puddles, wind whipping your hair and the satisfying crunch of frost underfoot. Now that sounds like a perfect day for play! \n\nThis charming production invites children to step into the wilderness and experience the joy of adapting to whatever the sky brings.\n\nThe story is mostly non-verbal, unfolding through live music, physical storytelling, and a sprinkle of English, Irish, and Italian words. Co-created by the award-winning teams of Branar (Ireland) and NIE (UK/Norway), this sensory-filled performance shows that mustering the bravery to face the unexpected is what makes every day an adventure.\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"WMRwMsEXupzeYf4mjPBcCg","website":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/","tickets":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/"},{"id":"c4875433-4ffa-4ab1-8991-f1f3d225c9ae","name":"Grand Soft Day","dates":[1808577000000,1808591400000,1808672400000,1808679600000,1809181800000,1809196200000,1809268200000,1809282600000],"start":"2027-04-24T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Young People's Theatre","address":"165 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5A 3Z4","lat":43.6499984416,"lng":-79.3687420725},"free":false,"low":27,"high":33,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Splash in puddles, wind whipping your hair and the satisfying crunch of frost underfoot. Now that sounds like a perfect day for play! \n\nThis charming production invites children to step into the wilderness and experience the joy of adapting to whatever the sky brings.\n\nThe story is mostly non-verbal, unfolding through live music, physical storytelling, and a sprinkle of English, Irish, and Italian words. Co-created by the award-winning teams of Branar (Ireland) and NIE (UK/Norway), this sensory-filled performance shows that mustering the bravery to face the unexpected is what makes every day an adventure.\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"WMRwMsEXupzeYf4mjPBcCg","website":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/","tickets":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/"},{"id":"02eece74-1cb7-444e-aba2-74f047f82ac2","name":"Duende International Flamenco Festival: Flamenco and the World","dates":[1795042800000,1795136400000,1795222800000,1795309200000,1795395600000],"start":"2026-11-18T18:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Aga Khan Museum","address":"77 Wynford Dr, North York, ON M3C 1K1","lat":43.725278,"lng":-79.332045},"free":false,"low":45,"high":150,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate flamenco’s global transformation!\n\nExperience the vibrant evolution of flamenco, from its regional roots in Andalusia to a dynamic global art form shaped by cross-cultural exchange. \n\nThis year’s lineup spans both traditional flamenco from Andalusia and innovative collaborations at the crossroads of qawwali and Persian muqam, tracing the art form’s evolution from its regional roots to a global practice.","categories":["Dance","Live Performances","Museum"],"presenter":"Aga Khan Museum","image":"qp_RMmWPShlY0lOpIswCKQ","website":"https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/duende-2026/?utm_source=city+of+toronto&utm_medium=event+listing&utm_campaign=duende+26","tickets":"https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/duende-2026/?utm_source=city+of+toronto&utm_medium=event+listing&utm_campaign=duende+26"},{"id":"939ad598-9e25-481c-a6f0-c97f2b0977cc","name":"The Adventures of Indie Santiago: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt","dates":[1792346400000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-10-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n\n\nTicket admission is priced per person and includes Royal Ontario Museum admission, an on-site host and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a $15 discount. Children aged 12 and under can participate in the hunt for free, although museum admission must still be purchased directly from the ROM.","description":"Please join us for an exciting new Mystery Scavenger Hunt!\n\nFamous adventuring heiress Indie Santiago was visiting an archaeological dig in the Accona Desert when she mysteriously disappeared - along with a recently unearthed artifact! \n\nThere has been a mysterious murder and the museum's collections hold the key. As you gather clues, you'll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where and with what. Will your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We highly recommend every player bring a fully charged phone with the Goosechase app downloaded, as the hunt is delivered through the app; this allows each player to view the hunt material and be able to submit text, photo and video submissions as part of enjoying the full experience. See you soon!","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"kfsu4wZQlTpwqqYhFr8ZwQ","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"85daa852-3285-4e3f-a4a8-4a1a88ab91b0","name":"Grand Soft Day","dates":[1808577000000,1808591400000,1808672400000,1808679600000,1809181800000,1809196200000,1809268200000,1809282600000],"start":"2027-04-24T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Young People's Theatre","address":"165 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5A 3Z4","lat":43.6499984416,"lng":-79.3687420725},"free":false,"low":27,"high":33,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Splash in puddles, wind whipping your hair and the satisfying crunch of frost underfoot. Now that sounds like a perfect day for play! \n\nThis charming production invites children to step into the wilderness and experience the joy of adapting to whatever the sky brings.\n\nThe story is mostly non-verbal, unfolding through live music, physical storytelling, and a sprinkle of English, Irish, and Italian words. Co-created by the award-winning teams of Branar (Ireland) and NIE (UK/Norway), this sensory-filled performance shows that mustering the bravery to face the unexpected is what makes every day an adventure.\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"WMRwMsEXupzeYf4mjPBcCg","website":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/","tickets":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/"},{"id":"bfca488e-8e1b-43c7-809f-0c6d128493d5","name":"Grand Soft Day","dates":[1808577000000,1808591400000,1808672400000,1808679600000,1809181800000,1809196200000,1809268200000,1809282600000],"start":"2027-04-24T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Young People's Theatre","address":"165 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5A 3Z4","lat":43.6499984416,"lng":-79.3687420725},"free":false,"low":27,"high":33,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Splash in puddles, wind whipping your hair and the satisfying crunch of frost underfoot. Now that sounds like a perfect day for play! \n\nThis charming production invites children to step into the wilderness and experience the joy of adapting to whatever the sky brings.\n\nThe story is mostly non-verbal, unfolding through live music, physical storytelling, and a sprinkle of English, Irish, and Italian words. Co-created by the award-winning teams of Branar (Ireland) and NIE (UK/Norway), this sensory-filled performance shows that mustering the bravery to face the unexpected is what makes every day an adventure.\n","categories":["Family/Children","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"WMRwMsEXupzeYf4mjPBcCg","website":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/","tickets":"https://www.youngpeoplestheatre.org/shows-tickets/grand-soft-day/"},{"id":"0c24f8c9-2cd6-4270-9949-88e7773ec131","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of 