magining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"6839d76b-cb03-42ae-bc09-bde91def7f0f","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"66bf2d9a-588d-41e5-83ab-f56aa31b3647","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"02314bb1-46b5-47f3-9c9d-039ce812c3f0","name":"Jim Cuddy Orchestrated","dates":[1802480400000],"start":"2027-02-12T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-12T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":75,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The multi-Juno Award winner and Canadian legend returns to Koerner Hall with new orchestral arrangements of his hits.\n\nJim Cuddy has written many of the songs that have become indelible in the soundtrack of Canadian lives. As a solo artist and as one half of the creative core of Blue Rodeo, he has helped define the sound of Canadian music for more than four decades. Since Blue Rodeo’s formation in 1984, their music has resonated across generations, earning both critical acclaim and a devoted national audience.\n\nAfter the concert, keep the party going with an exclusive post-show DJ set!\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"pIKmBUKLpUgPgjVTfqqLgw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/jim-cuddy-453801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/453801"},{"id":"c5cd76dd-79ba-4d8b-8056-e285d8a022ea","name":"Une Vie d’Amour","dates":[1802566800000],"start":"2027-02-13T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-13T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":75,"high":130,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come celebrate Valentine’s Day and let yourself be swept away by the magic of love!\n\nThis stunning tribute to the most beautiful love songs from the French music repertoire features powerful voices from the Patrimoine Musical Francophone shows.The exceptional concert takes audiences on a journey through timeless melodies that have captured hearts across generations featuring songs by Édith Piaf, Jacques Brel, Charles Aznavour and Gilbert Bécaud.\n\nAccompanied by world class musicians, enjoy a heartfelt homage to French 20th century masterpieces.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/une-vie-damour-449601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/449601"},{"id":"22c05354-97ef-4dac-b6e5-6ac22ccd7386","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"0533a08e-0b27-464f-9c95-f2a256fbff07","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing