cal performances by Maurice Gordon and friends, celebrating the music of Harry Belafonte and Jimmy Cliff. Also tune into Foster Motel, as they bring their brand of outlaw indie folk and roots rock.\n\nBoth acts are playing special sets featuring multiple surprise guests each!  \n\nBid in a silent auction with art from incredible East End artists including Al Runt, Carolina Reis, Heidi Burkhardt, Kat Palmer, Lisa Herrera, Ashley Snook, Hannah Burkhardt, Susan Fothergill and Susan Horley.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"coq1FrXMmVhmlcNSF_XUfA","website":"https://www.canadahelps.org/en/charities/applegrove-community-complex/events/east-end-music-fest-2026/","tickets":"https://www.canadahelps.org/en/charities/applegrove-community-complex/events/east-end-music-fest-2026/"},{"id":"105239d5-fe06-457a-bba9-e237d0a2078b","name":"Late Night at the Bata Shoe Museum","dates":[1789160400000,1791579600000,1794607200000,1797026400000],"start":"2026-09-11T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-11T17:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bata Shoe Museum","address":"327 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W7","lat":43.667232212,"lng":-79.400148381},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy our new late night hours with special craft programming new each week plus access to all current exhibitions!\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"766d4Dy_JwfFqJGk_5CsrA","website":"https://batashoemuseum.ca/","tickets":"https://batashoemuseum.ca/"},{"id":"f521e205-752c-4921-b0d6-d237cfd227b0","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"739a9719-6bef-4be7-ac1d-eebb63e16498","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"87f16ec1-5f0d-40fa-a665-895db54a429b","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"864177e1-a58b-4a90-ba24-8d25284b5d28","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":nu