, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"3f2545e0-ff4c-43ec-9df2-2fc771b4b94c","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"2b42ef6d-3996-435c-88be-63c39f81bbce","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"bb588f99-c137-4536-8dfa-402ac4647265","name":"A Love Affair with the Unknown by Gillian Deacon – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1822777200000],"start":"2027-10-05T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-10-05T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nA Love Affair with the Unknown is a personal memoir examining how we navigate uncertainty, loss and transformation. Drawing on her experiences with illness, healing and life-changing challenges, Gillian Deacon, veteran journalist and television/radio host, explores what it means to live with vulnerability while remaining open to possibility, connection and growth. She will discuss lessons learned through periods of upheaval and how embracing the unknown can lead to greater resilience, creativity and meaning.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"xOF2hcT4Mkqe17tolrymsg","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4e9e6d8b-6a3f-472f-92ec-964c81318da1"},{"id":"71f5c41a-2f2b-45d9-ad7f-cc668e2a4b87","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"10b2a09b-c21d-4435-8351-266a5881d009","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"5542d3e5-857a-40e8-87ba-fb6361971411","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"6a13f386-d440-40d6-b434-8c476f25d7b0","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"b4c69938-2409-4704-8424-00ceb535a17c","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"9eeb7067-7976-464f-ba2d-a24154b24da4","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"a96f15ab-086c-48fa-b2ab-faf8d7890d80","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"9a67fed3-2a29-44fa-99d4-556453ea2c56","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"75d95eb3-0e46-4be0-b7c0-db7d8a20a39e","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"e4fbe1a5-0b55-4806-9baf-cd5846a687bc","name":"2026 Hockey Hall of Fame Induction Celebration","dates":[1794063600000,1794150000000,1794263400000],"start":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-09T17:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Hockey Hall of Fame ","address":"Brookfield Place, 30 Yonge Street, Toronto ON, M5E 1X8","lat":43.647006,"lng":-79.377245},"free":false,"low":295,"high":625,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join the Hockey Hall of Fame as we welcome hockey’s newest legends, Class of 2026 Inductees: Patrice Bergeron, Brian Burke, Cindy Curley, Carey Price, Pekka Rinne and Keith Tkachuk.\n\nThis is your chance to say, \"I was there\". Experience an unforgettable weekend with special events and fan experiences, including the Legends Photo Op, QnA Fan Forum and the annual Hockey Hall of Fame Game.\n\nThe celebration culminates with the prestigious Induction Gala, an extraordinary evening featuring red carpet arrivals, hockey legends, gourmet hospitality, a premier silent auction and the live induction of the Class of 2026.\n\n","categories":["Celebrations","Charity/Cause","Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"jv2np708BWDdUpeAAnj7yw","website":"https://www.hhof.com/induction/induction2026/inductiontickets.html","tickets":"https://www.hhof.com/induction/induction2026/inductiontickets.html"},{"id":"091bbd82-2a76-471c-a165-67012c420a33","name":"Rachel Fenlon, soprano and piano","dates":[1800748800000],"start":"2027-01-23T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-23T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667876,"lng":-79.396203},"free":false,"low":21,"high":50,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Canadian classical singer and pianist Rachel Fenlon presents deeply personal interpretations of song, performing simultaneously as vocalist and pianist in an intimate presentation.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"Wqp3mSaIbYjgC5NF4rvsqQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/rachel-fenlon-soprano-and-piano-450001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/450001"},{"id":"b4a64b73-34c1-43f3-9bdf-eb2707d53918","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"c2d028b2-95e6-4fb2-8028-dadedd492d91","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"6af9bb83-c688-45a5-9143-64c2e1d016c9","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"4bd81aa6-d578-480d-85c4-e666cc2b41b0","name":"Salif Keïta","dates":[1809734400000],"start":"2027-05-07T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-07T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an unforgettable evening celebrating the extraordinary music and legacy of one of Africa’s most iconic voices.\n\nKnown as “The Golden Voice of Africa,” the Malian superstar delivers an unforgettable evening of Afro-pop elegance and emotional depth. For 55 years, Salif Keïta has stood as the undisputed pioneer of Afro-pop, reshaping the global soundscape with his fearless innovation. His legendary career is defined by a remarkable, soaring voice and a lifelong commitment to genre-defying collaborations. Today, with 20 acclaimed albums, five Grammy nominations and timeless global anthems like \"Yamore\" and \"Madan,\" Keïta’s monumental legacy in music history remains unmatched.\n\nAfter the concert, enjoy a beverage and more music at the Postlude Performance featuring a local emerging artist in the Leslie & Anna Dan Galleria. We look forward to welcoming you to experience this extraordinary performance and celebrate African music.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Nightlife"],"presenter":"Batuki Music","image":"YAWc0oqJUErxQbwo6riTdQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/salif-keita-448001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/salif-keita-448001"},{"id":"64cb294b-83c3-4e77-98df-9da87a0d5b68","name":"By the Lake Book Club – 6-Event Package (2027)","dates":[1801612800000],"start":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":120,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall and Toronto Book Awards, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nJoin leading Canadian authors as they dive into conversation about their latest books with Humber Polytechnic alumni at Assembly Hall. The 2027 lineup features the 2026 Toronto Book Award Winner, Nadja Lubiw-Hazard, Ashraf Zaghal, Tyler Pennock, Gillian Deacon and Carrianne Leung.\n\nThe signature series features six Tuesday-night events, between February and December. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation.\n\n2026 Toronto Book Award Winner - February 2, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nNadja Lubiw-Hazard - March 9, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nAshraf Zaghal  - April 13, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nTyler Pennock - September 14, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nGillian Deacon - October 5, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nCarrianne Leung - December 7, 2027 at 7 p.m.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#multipacks/4fbe5173-7528-46e3-8d0c-5c7f321f0e9d"},{"id":"3c2e4257-8283-4569-ad6d-e999021fbd27","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"377aadf8-e439-4924-867b-2975e9c7eb8a","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"43f19dc1-ac63-4a66-a518-6e13ce085d0a","name":"Kronos Quartet","dates":[1804204800000,1804294800000],"start":"2027-03-04T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-03-05T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":60,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The groundbreaking string quartet returns with their fresh new lineup, continuing a legacy of innovation that has transformed the contemporary music landscape.\n\nFor nearly 50 years, San Francisco’s Kronos Quartet: David Harrington (violin), Gabriela Díaz (violin), Hank Dutt (viola) and Ayane Kozasa (cello, have reimagined what the string quartet experience can be. \n\nOne of the most celebrated and influential groups of our era, Kronos has given thousands of concerts worldwide, released more than 70 recordings, and collaborated with many of the world’s most accomplished composers and performers across many genres. Kronos has received more than 40 awards, including three Grammys and the Polar Music, Avery Fisher, and Edison Klassiek Oeuvre Prizes.\n\nPlease join us! Kronos will also be performing with the talented students from the Glenn Gould School. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"lPCTDe5cMJqbbBPHL2-Utw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/kronos-quartet-431201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/431201"},{"id":"554ba174-9c19-44d1-a369-a2728128d8e5","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"e000715a-4636-4864-8df7-623f5f2d67f6","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793