exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"55f7279f-23a0-45d1-982b-2833fe80e320","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"83eca156-2fa8-49bd-81b1-7edc1d922cc2","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"2a88d707-580f-48fa-bc89-20264fb1c289","name":"Linocut Workshop: André Perugia Themed Tote Bag","dates":[1795476600000],"start":"2026-11-23T18:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-23T18:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bata Shoe Museum","address":"327 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W7","lat":43.667232212,"lng":-79.400148381},"free":false,"low":50,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nCost inclusive all materials and access to all current exhibitions.","description":"Inspired by our current exhibition, André Perugia: A Design Legend Unveiled, step into the bold and imaginative world of André Perugia.\n\nIn this hands-on linocut workshop inspired by the visionary footwear designer’s sculptural and avant-garde creations. Participants will learn the fundamentals of linocut carving and printmaking while designing a one-of-a-kind tote bag influenced by Perugia’s iconic shapes, surreal details, and daring sense of style. Perfect for beginners and seasoned creatives alike, this workshop offers a chance to explore the intersection of fashion, art, and craftsmanship through print.\n\nRecommended for participants ages 16 and up.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":"C5HVYT1IK1J2jn3K2Ek18A","website":"https://batashoemuseum.ca/event/linocut-workshop-perugia-tote/","tickets":"https://batashoemuseum.ca/event/linocut-workshop-perugia-tote/"},{"id":"6e6e6dca-5bbb-464c-abd5-c9a142509b3e","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"857eb29c-86a6-46fd-94e0-c6f90813c3ae","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog intera