oss the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"a09f531a-463d-4814-8b30-702c5ee64f3e","name":"Black History Planting Event: Cedarvale Park","dates":[1791036000000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedarvale Park","address":"57 Strathearn Rd, Toronto, ON M6C 1R5","lat":43.692607,"lng":-79.428461},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Join us for a special Black History planting event at Cedarvale Park. Plant native trees and shrubs to enhance the urban canopy and learn about Black History and nature with scholar, writer and activist Jacqueline L. Scott. Additional registration for the tour is required. Please email us at greentoronto@toronto.ca. \n\nEvent site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.\n","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"-Er20u6oUZ_IOTpdAamfUQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"bccad804-af12-4139-ad5a-1d88d9c48bbb","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"5bcef127-faf7-4db4-92cd-257c3cfdb269","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"d91db05f-cfa7-44fe-b713-ea6c1cdf2ac7","name":"SHADE by Jordan Shaw at Budapest Park","dates":[1787716800000,1787803200000,1787889600000,1787976000000,1788062400000,1788148800000,1788235200000,1788321600000,1788408000000,1788494400000,1788580800000,1788667200000,1788753600000,1788840000000,1788926400000,1789012800000,1789099200000,1789185600000,1789272000000,1789358400000,1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000],"start":"2026-08-26T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Budapest Park","address":"1575 Lake Shore Blvd W, Toronto, ON, M6R 1B5","lat":43.636828816,"lng":-79.446436254},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At first, Shade appears as a series of aluminum lattice structures: geometric, quiet, casting patterns across the grass. Spend a few minutes observing and something shifts — the shadows have moved. As you move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"f3a67b6c-a448-4e64-8df8-d373d24276fb","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"bf96ff8f-3db5-4a7a-ab0f-677d876c2f47","name":"Creditors: Canadian Premiere","dates":[1807313400000,1807399800000,1807466400000,1807659000000,1807745400000,1807831800000,1807918200000,1808004600000,1808071200000,1808263800000,1808350200000,1808436600000,1808523000000,1808609400000,1808676000000,1808868600000,1808955000000,1809041400000,1809127800000,1809214200000,1809280800000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-02T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":170,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every desire has a cost.\n\nAt a secluded seaside hotel, a young artist and his magnetic wife find their marriage unsettled by the arrival of a charismatic stranger. What begins as friendly conversation turns into something sharper: a slow, surgical dismantling of certainty, confidence, and love.\n\nIn this razor-edged reimagining of Strindberg’s classic, Artistic Director Brendan Healy and an all-star cast transform a classic battle of the sexes into a thrilling psychological chamber piece about ego, desire, and the stories we tell about ourselves. Seductive, unsettling, and darkly funny, Creditors asks: who owns the narrative and who pays the price?","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"UYkm0kYQcwn7lFj5t8EA3A","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/creditors","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9702"},{"id":"4b7c92e0-a3d8-4eb6-b746-2e6f7363a645","name":"Donovan Woods","dates":[1809216000000],"start":"2027-05-01T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Royal Conservatory of Music","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":55,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Known for his candid, emotionally resonant songwriting, Donovan Woods blends folk, country, and pop.\n\nIn 2026, he is back with brand new music with his new EP, Squander Your Gifts. The five track EP is a collection of songs dedicated to his friend and writing partner, Abe Stoklasa, who passed away in November 2023. A reflection into loss, love, and living, the singer once again finds a way to paint a picture and make a deeply personal experience resonate with fans.\n\nDonovan Woods continues to solidify his place as one of North America’s most compelling songwriters; unflinchingly honest, an artist who isn’t afraid to bare his soul.\n\nAfter the concert, enjoy a beverage and more music at the Postlude Performance featuring a local emerging artist  in the Leslie & Anna Dan Galleria.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"ypTL3HcJKTDI9LDVocbbWg","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/donovan-woods-445001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/445001"},{"id":"7a78c48d-2e4d-4d65-bfec-66e4e1def1aa","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,17924112000