ll,"costNotes":"\nTickets available November 4, 2026.","description":"Solo and chamber works are performed by young artists on the cusp of major careers, who are enrolled in The Rebanks Family Fellowship and International Performance Residency Program at The Glenn Gould School.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"GLn4N339UYQqP0iripwBcw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/rebanks-family-fellowship-concert-450401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/450401"},{"id":"55de57e1-848f-434c-b05d-53d60fb6916a","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"b4954ea8-ac59-4f24-b791-55fb4d81a958","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"adf640a0-bd44-4720-81d1-9f026799a7cd","name":"Kronos Quartet","dates":[1804204800000,1804294800000],"start":"2027-03-04T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-03-05T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":60,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The groundbreaking string quartet returns with their fresh new lineup, continuing a legacy of innovation that has transformed the contemporary music landscape.\n\nFor nearly 50 years, San Francisco’s Kronos Quartet: David Harrington (violin), Gabriela Díaz (violin), Hank Dutt (viola) and Ayane Kozasa (cello, have reimagined what the string quartet experience can be. \n\nOne of the most celebrated and influential groups of our era, Kronos has given thousands of concerts worldwide, released more than 70 recordings, and collaborated with many of the world’s most accomplished composers and performers across many genres. Kronos has received more than 40 awards, including three Grammys and the Polar Music, Avery Fisher, and Edison Klassiek Oeuvre Prizes.\n\nPlease join us! Kronos will also be performing with the talented students from the Glenn Gould School. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"lPCTDe5cMJqbbBPHL2-Utw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/kronos-quartet-431201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/431201"},{"id":"cf545e02-1cb8-46a6-8e15-8811f3aa3630","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"ab6a8751-8b2e-4e6b-99ff-bc132e00b926","name":"The Stories We Carry: A Conversation with Bernice Carnegie","dates":[1791054000000],"start":"2026-10-03T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front St E, Toronto,","lat":43.649145,"lng":-79.371526},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Visit Market Gallery for an engaging conversation with Bernice Carnegie, an internationally recognized speaker, storyteller, and author whose work brings together stories of inclusion, compassion, leadership, and community. \n\nThe daughter of hockey legend Herb Carnegie, Bernice carries forward her family’s legacy by sharing stories rooted in lived experience, resilience, and belonging.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"st33BWwA46U1aU99GizFPA","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f7c26c9c-84af-4bfb-870b-a495f8fd7593"},{"id":"c972a945-586a-404b-bd0f-3931b30662fd","name":"Newcomer Planting Event: Sweeney Park","dates":[1791468000000],"start":"2026-10-08T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Sweeney Park","address":"110 Sweeney Dr, North York, ON M4A","lat":43.735816,"lng":-79.316203},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIndividuals and small groups do not need to register. We require groups of five or more to register in advance to ensure we have enough materials and tools at each event. Email us to register.","description":"Join us at Sweeney Park for a special newcomer planting event. We will be enhancing our tree canopy by planting native trees and shrubs.\n\nEvent site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"6UK-WezmMaxp70l-MracuA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/get-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"4a077cdd-8dbc-4632-90df-87ec3795fdd8","name":"Lillian H. Smith Library Tree Tour","dates":[1791482400000],"start":"2026-10-08T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Lillian H. Smith Library","address":"239 College St, Toronto, ON, M5T 1R5","lat":43.657917812,"lng":-79.398382385},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Lillian H. Smith branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of trees. Join the City of Toronto to explore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n\nThis is a free event, with registration required. Registration will open September 2.\n\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.","categories":["Environmental","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"XqsBNFCxYQq25Yg1hpMaSw","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a74d6f13f18b57d5233dd69","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a74d6f13f18b57d5233dd69"},{"id":"15ff18ff-0b53-461e-8064-1fe4c46b2916","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"9bc89e40-8e55-47d6-81f6-445736cc8d6b","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"caad1cd6-069f-4025-b4b1-901d551efb03","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,179518