G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"c0daa80d-e623-48e4-a2b0-5a8a1888f00e","name":"Flemingdon Park Library Talk: Our Urban Forest","dates":[1795017600000],"start":"2026-11-18T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-18T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Flemingdon Park Library","address":"29 St Dennis Dr, North York, ON, M3C 3J3","lat":43.717940678,"lng":-79.331687362},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Join the City of Toronto for an in-library presentation on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto.\n\nWe’ll talk about what makes the urban forest so special, and share tools to explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities, and leave with emboldened confidence and understanding of your City and the natural world that surrounds you.\n\nNo registration required; drop-in until room is at full capacity.","categories":["Environmental","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"qKTeaHBLN2tLqIXbYGn-Nw","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8e1c354995480655ec7358","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8e1c354995480655ec7358"},{"id":"74ffcfd3-9185-47d9-9584-d7668a4db490","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,179276