ibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"bad3cd21-5412-4c6b-ba97-3b2ebfe242ea","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"adff81be-2517-4d77-9987-d75e8e7bb701","name":"Tomorrow’s Memories: Gibson House 175 (Nuit Blanche Toronto)","dates":[1791068400000,1791154800000],"start":"2026-10-03T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Gibson House","address":"5172 Yonge St, North York, ON, M2N 5P6","lat":43.769686148,"lng":-79.414666941},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience an immersive outdoor nighttime installation celebrating 175 years of Gibson House Museum. See a transformed historic landscape featuring youth-created crocheted flora and fauna, archival photographs, embroidery-inspired artwork, light, sound and storytelling. \n\nCreated by the City in partnership with Toronto History Museums Youth Volunteers, the installation reflects on themes of memory, land and community, inviting visitors to discover how 175 years of history continue to shape the future of North York.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"ixatwmGnJ-6w6teIRf1QlQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/gibson-house-museum/","tickets":null},{"id":"7dcbb28b-8dbe-48fd-9301-c4111d0977ad","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1