scription":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"ee38074c-5760-4319-a984-be3092db3fec","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"655803d8-b50f-4e82-bdc8-9d443b4172ed","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"a52b625f-af5d-4fb8-bce7-ddc834a57f9a","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"b756a2fa-c4ac-419c-b213-a203f7a65905","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"cbb76d66-52ff-4ec4-bbf9-23b19b28de8e","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"533d2174-d15b-4e2e-9517-d5dd25a7507e","name":"Johannes Moser, cello, with Marc-André Hamelin, piano","dates":[1803776400000],"start":"2027-02-27T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-27T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":60,"high":120,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Cellist Johannes Moser joins pianist Marc-André Hamelin to perform an all-Beethoven program that showcases the profound partnership between cello and piano in the composer’s groundbreaking works.\n\nHailed by Gramophone magazine as “one of the finest among the astonishing gallery of young virtuoso cellists\", German-Canadian cellist Johannes Moser has performed with Emanuel Ax, Joshua Bell, Jonathan Biss, James Ehnes, Vadim Gluzman, Leonidas Kavakos, Midori, Menahem Pressler and Marc-André Hamelin. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"H8Bysx0lT63aTpH2xuahVw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/johannes-moser-cello-with-marc-andre-hamelin-piano-430201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/430201"},{"id":"d5e74214-a210-4c56-b089-a9ed0707432e","name":"This is Us: Art Exhibition","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Leslie Grove Gallery","address":"1158 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M4M 1L2","lat":43.662683087,"lng":-79.33369142},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Living and working within blocks of one another, our diverse artists bring different backgrounds, experiences, and ways of seeing the world. \n\nTogether, our varied work creates a sense of cohesion and harmony that reflects the community we share. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":"North Toronto Group of Artists","image":null,"website":"https://www.artistsnetwork.ca/patrons-calendar.","tickets":null},{"id":"19c93908-5b2e-4969-8960-c9e9fe97b033","name":"This is Us: Art Exhibition","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Leslie Grove Gallery","address":"1158 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M4M 1L2","lat":43.662683087,"lng":-79.33369142},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Living and working within blocks of one another, our diverse artists bring different backgrounds, experiences, and ways of seeing the world. \n\nTogether, our varied work creates a sense of cohesion and harmony that reflects the community we share. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":"North Toronto Group of Artists","image":null,"website":"https://www.artistsnetwork.ca/patrons-calendar.","tickets":null},{"id":"797cf987-0899-4526-8dc3-35cb324948a6","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,179