u move around the structures, perspectives change. What becomes clear is that the work has two authors — you and the sun. The sun continues its arc regardless, changing the work's shadows and presence throughout the day. Shade is analog interactivity in its most elemental form — a reminder that we move through a world that is constantly changing, independent of us. We bring our presence, our attention, our memory and the world brings everything else.\n\nJordan Shaw is a Toronto-based artist and creative technologist whose practice explores data as material, he works across sculpture, installation, light and textile. His public artworks have been installed at Ontario Place, the City of Pickering and municipalities across Canada. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"B4ojJZhax41imauSMd6vvg","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"83679594-98ca-4053-a48b-37079d60ae75","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"d5de3a16-c9ed-41ff-bc34-90f3372f19d8","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792