anstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"8fad9376-85b1-41ac-a2f1-06e0169f9401","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"4205e754-b9aa-4159-a9ba-c37610e10ca5","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"477cef7f-cedb-47e0-97ca-a63d0b01b571","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"d24aa5c9-8df3-44b7-b08b-519343f2cc52","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witn