:"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"e6fe0b07-7d03-47f1-a860-e9dc21a9e944","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"67e9b4ac-513b-47a8-a92b-49523c0195ff","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"5ec5704b-9842-4340-b7d3-99cb29e49e0e","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"b5a0cb1d-8261-4ef1-b4b5-67b6b633d794","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"92de9bd9-2747-40d9-8cde-6184938dcedc","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"4693caa5-4c59-4cb6-9f79-1747fb70f94c","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"37e5b9b4-d231-4f61-825d-54c1dd6991ce","name":"In Broken Light Exhibition at Spadina Museum","dates":[1787756400000,1787842800000,1787929200000,1788015600000,1788102000000,1788361200000,1788447600000,1788534000000,1788620400000,1788706800000,1788966000000,1789052400000,1789138800000,1789225200000,1789311600000,1789570800000,1789657200000,1789743600000,1789830000000,1789916400000,1790175600000,1790262000000,1790348400000,1790434800000,1790521200000,1790780400000,1790866800000,1790953200000,1791039600000,1791126000000,1791385200000,1791471600000,1791558000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1791990000000,1792076400000,1792162800000,1792249200000,1792335600000],"start":"2026-08-26T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Visit the reception desk to register. Tickets are first-come first-serve and subject to capacity.","description":"See a contemporary art exhibition of five sculptural interventions located throughout the historic Spadina Museum, created by artist Ry Van Der Hout and curated by Adrien Sun Hall. Working with photography, stained glass, mirrors, and acts of rupture and repair, Van Der Hout reveals the emotional residue held within objects, architecture and stories. Cracks and fractures become apertures through which forgotten stories emerge, the artworks functioning as contemporary reliquaries for lives remembered and overlooked.\n\nMoving between deep histories, the present day and an imagined future, this exhibition traces connections across time, where fragments persist, reflections multiply, and the boundaries between past, present and future remain open.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"caTKB0eJSOICT9G9ZdiXWw","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":null},{"id":"92ca42d8-6cc2-489b-ab42-223d02ef1e9a","name":"Winter Wings: Songbirds in Toronto Winter Webinar","dates":[1796317200000],"start":"2026-12-03T12:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"On-line Event","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an introduction to winter birding in Toronto. We'll explore a few of the fascinating birds that call the city home in winter, learn how birds adapt to winter conditions, listen to some common calls and highlight some of the best places to spot birds across Toronto. Whether you're brand new to birding or looking for a reason to get outside in frigid winter weather, you'll leave inspired to connect with nature safely and respectfully.","categories":["Environmental","Virtual/Online Event"],"presenter":null,"image":"yXvgF_GOs5uPt5ghC1hKcg","website":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/a6d0a87b-6c42-4f32-bd2e-557b8cae2db1@f0bc8ec6-9ed8-4d0c-9189-411ad949cc65","tickets":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/a6d0a87b-6c42-4f32-bd2e-557b8cae2db1@f0bc8ec6-9ed8-4d0c-9189-411ad949cc65"},{"id":"e72713a7-19ff-41b8-8bba-81da2679c543","name":"The Phil and Eli Taylor Performance Academy Showcase Concert","dates":[1795296600000],"start":"2026-11-21T16:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-21T16:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":" 273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667961,"lng":-79.396163},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTickets available starting from 10 a.m. on Friday, November 13, 2026.","description":"Enjoy a concert by the leading young classical musicians in Canada. Hear the stars of tomorrow!  \n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"0s1DeSo3ufaqZQikP6fHzw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/taylor-academy-showcase-concert-450801-1","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/450801"},{"id":"a877d98d-8d4d-4e75-8f05-b75805c2fc08","name":"KUNÉ","dates":[1803171600000],"start":"2027-02-20T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-20T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":40,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Founded at the Royal Conversatory of Music to honour the sesquicentennial, Canada’s global orchestra celebrates its 10th anniversary.\n\nKUNÉ, Canada’s Global Orchestra, was intended as a one-night-only showcase to celebrate Canada’s cultural diversity and pluralism. Now, 10 years and two albums later, the ensemble seeks to communicate in ways that words, politicians, and spiritual leaders cannot, and help to find a common language through music. The musicians hail from all corners of the globe (Peru, Burkina Faso, Cuba, Ukraine, and beyond) and play instruments as diverse as they are, from the tar of Iran to the bouzouki of Greece to the clarinet of Türkiye.\n\nAfter the concert, enjoy a beverage and more music at the Postlude Performance featuring a local emerging artist.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"8LVfmWgnwgvGnFSGIbrKhA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/kune-445201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/445201"},{"id":"6bc1d888-e0ea-4a77-abd1-2abbb01abbce","name":"A Beethoven Celebration with John O’Conor","dates":[1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Irish pianist John O’Conor celebrates his 80th birthday with Beethoven, joined by Glenn Gould School students and a special duet piano performance with James Anagnoson, Dean Emeritus of the GGS and Piano Department Chair.\n\n\"A pianist of unbounding sensitivity\" (Gramophone), O'Conor is renowned globally for his masterly playing over the last 50 years. A Steinway Artist, he is Chair of the Piano Division at Shenandoah University in Virginia, Professor of Piano at The Glenn Gould School, Distinguished Visiting Artist at the TU Dublin Conservatoire of Music and Visiting Professor at Showa University in Japan.\n\nAnagnoson is one of Canada's best-known pianists and pedagogues. He has been on the piano faculty of the Glenn Gould School since its formation in 1987 and has also taught at the University of Toronto and the University of Western Ontario.\n\nPresented in honour of Canada-Ireland 180.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuq1nhSOjxbaTkZi9UhIEQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/john-oconor-80th-birthday-celebration-448801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/448801"},{"id":"77ad510b-ebf6-4fef-9d65-efacf3811949","name":"Youth Entrepreneurship Program","dates":[1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"155cb089-9fa2-4be0-a4d9-5f69ed52a38f","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"d81b8331-5e23-404b-a002-3c95d5431d46","name":"Salon du Chocolat et de la Pâtisserie","dates":[1795183200000,1795269600000,1795356000000],"start":"2026-11-20T09:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Congress Centre","address":"650 Dixon Rd, Etobicoke, ON M9W 1J1","lat":43.648684,"lng":-79.38446},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come visit a legendary global network active in 14 world capitals from Paris to Tokyo!\n\nPerfect for all sweet tooths and chocolate lovers.","categories":["Family/Children","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://torontosalonduchocolat.com/","tickets":"https://app.eventnroll.com/en/tickets/buy-tickets/2073/12112"},{"id":"0945940d-49bb-40d0-82b4-64b966a8d8f6","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"129662cf-be22-4561-bb62-f9cdf6568a08","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"c7456d49-b67a-446a-be43-1c8f0f034687","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Fall Flavours: Walking Food Tour","dates":[1789659000000,1790263800000,1790868600000,1791473400000,1792078200000,1792683000000,1793287800000,1793896200000,1794501000000,1795105800000,1795710600000],"start":"2026-09-17T11:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T11:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting point: Fusettes","address":"407 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1S9","lat":43.659499524,"lng":-79.382002835},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fall Flavours is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"04f3ee90-c50c-4802-b368-a18ae4a44309","name":"Sappho Say What?","dates":[1791417600000],"start":"2026-10-07T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-07T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Comedy Bar","address":"945 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M6H 1L5","lat":43.661342,"lng":-79.427859},"free":false,"low":23,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Serving up an All-Lesbian-Lineup stand-up show! \n\nDon't miss this super-sapphic-ultra-modern-girl night of fabulous comedy! Lez be friends with a lineup of Toronto’s best comics! Pull up in your Subaru for a night of fantastic fun!\n\nWe’ve got comedy award winners and comedians seen on OutTV, JFL, CBC, SiriusXM, TikTok and more!\n\nFeaturing Tamara Appleton, Anasimone, Winnie Jiang and Spencer Glassman. With headliner, Canadian Screen Award Award winner, from CBC Comedy, Debaters and Pop Cultured, Elvira Kurt.\n\nCome join the funny!","categories":["Comedy","2SLGBTQ+","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"4wUN_hl_sKHpsJkzJj5e6g","website":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/sappho-say-what","tickets":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/sappho-say-what"},{"id":"b4a447a7-54c0-4113-b81e-7953321377a7","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"fe140106-a15b-448f-b008-9fa66c8eec8b","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"1b6cbb82-436b-4810-af0c-f65735402d7a","name":"Sleuth","dates":[1792193400000,1792260000000,1792279800000,1792346400000,1792539000000,1792594800000,1792625400000,1792711800000,1792864800000,1792884600000,1792951200000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793286000000,1793316600000,1793403000000,1793469600000,1793489400000,1793559600000],"start":"2026-10-16T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Fleck at Harbourfront Centre Theatre","address":"231 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON, M5J 2G8","lat":43.63867054,"lng":-79.382157854},"free":false,"low":52,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFees and taxes included. Three play packages save 15 per cent.","description":"A love letter to the classic crime thriller, Anthony Shaffer’s Sleuth is packed with razor-sharp dialogue and psychological games that will keep you guessing until the very end. When a celebrated mystery writer invites his wife’s lover to his secluded English country estate, what begins as a seemingly civilized encounter quickly spirals into a dangerous contest of wit and manipulation. But who is really in control, and who is playing whom?\n\nDirected by Peter Fernandes, this gripping production stars Patrick Galligan as Andrew Wyke and Sepehr Reybod as Milo Tindle, delivering a riveting battle of intellects in one of the most acclaimed suspense plays ever written.\n\nWhether you’re a lifelong fan of whodunits or discovering Sleuth for the first time, don’t miss this rare opportunity to experience a Shaw Festival production that honours the enduring legacy of classic suspense theatre.\n\nPart of the Shaw Festival at Harbourfront Centre.","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Shaw Festival","image":"VCsZhz3MQf0Gdy5fVOulKw","website":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/","tickets":"https://harbourfrontcentre.com/event/sleuth/"},{"id":"79ea06bd-f391-4f0d-9eb9-219c723c92cf","name":"Molly Steels: I Am/Was/Always","dates":[1793199600000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000],"start":"2026-10-28T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-05T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Image Centre","address":"33 Gould St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1E9","lat":43.657662387,"lng":-79.379262289},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The philosopher Diana Prokofyeva considers a photograph to be a phenomenon that exists as a way to avoid death by copying a moment and suspending it within time - a way to be between two worlds:, the living and the dead. She suggests that a photograph gives confidence of existence, a way to state, “Here I am and was, and always shall have been.”.\n\nView this evolving series that looks to photography as a method of conceptualizing grief and mortality. Using family archives from the past century and conceptual imagery, I locate myself within a chain of human experience. I look to the women who came before me, observing the proof of their existence with reverence and the knowledge that I will one day add to this catalogue. Through this series I aim to overshadow existential fear with curiosity.\n\nEphemeral aspects of nature are woven into this work as both an unrelenting force and a source of comfort. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"oUxX7buKjY1V2s_fjb6MLg","website":"https://theimagecentre.ca/exhibition/molly-steels-iamwasalways/","tickets":null},{"id":"36e3bae1-33a0-4385-924b-86bd4157a9a4","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"9c3d37f4-5c5c-4733-a4e9-53468f959ddf","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"dc61c44b-a6d0-445e-88e0-14eac96d429a","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"624a62e4-b971-4e9e-a57a-370db926ebc8","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"1ed829d0-21e9-4429-84ca-32c47e66fa15","name":"Exhibition: \"Returning to Ourselves and Michael Massie: now and then\"","dates":[1788987600000,1789056000000,1789142400000,1789228800000,1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000],"start":"2026-09-09T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-30T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Onsite Gallery","address":"199 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 0H4","lat":43.649477,"lng":-79.388341},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Please join us at the 'Returning to Ourselves - Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird: A Retrospective of Art and Design by Cree Métis Siblings'. Curated by Lisa Deanne Smith.\n\nThis exhibit presents over 40 years of transformative work by Rebecca Baird and Kenny Alvin Baird. The exhibition spans sculpture, painting and traditional material practices, alongside interior design and more.\n\n'Michael Massie: now and then' brings together works from across his career, including a large collection of teapots, previously unexhibited pieces and a new body of large-scale sculptural installations, to celebrate the enduring importance of joy, experimentation and humour in his work. Guest-curated by Alysa Procida and enjoy our Special Projects Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/michael-massie-now-and-then","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/opening-reception-returning-to-ourselves-michael-massie-now-and-then-tickets-1997059101532?aff=ebdsoporgprofile"},{"id":"045d54f5-29b0-430a-a8f1-9d4239723bc5","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"ea542065-87aa-4c5d-87e8-7271f8f5b855","name":"Measure for Measure","dates":[1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-09-15T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Crow's Theatre","address":"345 Carlaw Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2T1","lat":43.66515638,"lng":-79.341549283},"free":false,"low":30,"high":95,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Shakespeare’s tale of justice vs. morality, live on air.\n\nReturning after its acclaimed limited run is House + Body’s bold reimagining of Shakespeare’s Measure for Measure, setting this urgent story of justice and morality inside a chaotic modern sound studio.\n\nWhen Isabella’s brother is sentenced to death, she embarks on a journey to save his life but is forced to confront a system where authority wavers and moral certainty erodes. Watch as five actors juggle twenty roles live on air, racing through a high-stakes broadcast as offstage antics spiral as wildly as the drama that unfolds.\n\nFast, sharp, and darkly funny, this Measure for Measure asks who holds power and who pays the price.\n\n \n\nAccolades for Measure For Measure:\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (Toronto Star)\n\n• Top 10 Productions of 2025 (NEXT Magazine)","categories":["Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"LF03SE79WOXcy11ZNBC9IQ","website":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/measure-for-measure-2026","tickets":"https://www.crowstheatre.com/shows-events/calendar?shows=1077"},{"id":"59cd0d1e-5903-4a38-ac6f-fa00101a4a6f","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"62848f33-7e57-41c9-a108-53f0c2145484","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"a8b6d631-7eea-4710-9b8d-afee4a874cf0","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"6037b2f6-d2a6-4c4b-ba0f-43cb6a4e15f9","name":"The Adventures of Indie Santiago: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt","dates":[1792346400000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-10-18T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n\n\nTicket admission is priced per person and includes Royal Ontario Museum admission, an on-site host and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a $15 discount. Children aged 12 and under can participate in the hunt for free, although museum admission must still be purchased directly from the ROM.","description":"Please join us for an exciting new Mystery Scavenger Hunt!\n\nFamous adventuring heiress Indie Santiago was visiting an archaeological dig in the Accona Desert when she mysteriously disappeared - along with a recently unearthed artifact! \n\nThere has been a mysterious murder and the museum's collections hold the key. As you gather clues, you'll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where and with what. Will your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We highly recommend every player bring a fully charged phone with the Goosechase app downloaded, as the hunt is delivered through the app; this allows each player to view the hunt material and be able to submit text, photo and video submissions as part of enjoying the full experience. See you soon!","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"kfsu4wZQlTpwqqYhFr8ZwQ","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"407426e3-665b-4d74-9728-04ae905439a9","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"0fc0113d-d0a5-44f7-809c-bba1e2092373","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"