ll,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"c839a44e-a86c-4961-8864-3cb41ced9006","name":"Ethennonnhawahstihnen' Library Tree Tour","dates":[1791385200000],"start":"2026-10-07T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-07T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Ethennonnhawahstihnen' Library","address":"100 Ethennonnhawahstihnen' Lane, North York, ON, M2K 0G5","lat":43.768717995,"lng":-79.375804929},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Ethennonnhawahstihnen’ branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of trees. Join the City to explore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n\nThis is a free program.\n\nRegistration is required and will open one month before the event.\n\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. ","categories":["Environmental","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"QqhJhze2D8PB2fxUyXy8OQ","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6cc7a274e3b8b75db66fdd","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6cc7a274e3b8b75db66fdd"},{"id":"b50c103a-9054-4e75-a3fc-06fd00625f83","name":"Academy Chamber Orchestra","dates":[1797724800000,1809039600000],"start":"2026-12-19T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-04-29T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.66787,"lng":-79.39619},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n\nFree tickets available starting from 10 a.m. on Friday, December 11, 2026 and 10 a.m. on Thursday, April 22, 2027.","description":"String students from The Phil and Eli Taylor Performance Academy for Young Artists come together as the Academy Chamber Orchestra to perform a special concert.\n\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"yYyYfSDaLmmxLgwu2gGx-Q","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts"},{"id":"34e52b6c-f723-4970-bc47-1af9aae9b21e","name":"The Glenn Gould School Chamber Competition Finals","dates":[1806534000000],"start":"2027-03-31T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-03-31T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Tickets available starting from 10 a.m. on Wednesday March 24, 2027.","description":"Hear the talented ensembles of The Glenn Gould School compete!\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"Kbj9IAqiqUUamzT4J8ER5w","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ggs-chamber-competition-finals-454401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/454401"},{"id":"188d3532-6837-4868-a600-955299fb5044","name":"The Glenn Gould School Piano Showcase","dates":[1809214200000],"start":"2027-05-01T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The extraordinary pianists of The Ihnatowycz Piano Program take centre stage.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"IzNl7_8JjmA0UvlI4HvkiQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ggs-piano-showcase-452201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/452201"},{"id":"672fdad0-d738-4783-bdf1-54dd31b43de6","name":"Yesterday. Today. Forever.","dates":[1785758400000,1785844800000,1785931200000,1786017600000,1786104000000,1786190400000,1786276800000,1786363200000,1786449600000,1786536000000,1786622400000,1786708800000,1786795200000,1786881600000,1786968000000,1787054400000,1787140800000,1787227200000,1787313600000,1787400000000,1787486400000,1787572800000,1787659200000,1787745600000,1787832000000,1787918400000,1788004800000,1788091200000,1788177600000,1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788609600000,1788696000000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789214400000,1789300800000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789819200000,1789905600000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790424000000,1790510400000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791028800000,1791115200000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791633600000,1791720000000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792238400000,1792324800000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792843200000,1792929600000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793448000000,1793538000000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794056400000,1794142800000,1794229200000],"start":"2026-08-03T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-09T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mount Pleasant Cemetery","address":"375 Mount Pleasant Road","lat":43.712625,"lng":-79.357673},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Walk through a series of artistic and interpretive installations across ten cemetery sites and several funeral centres.\n\nAcross the participating sites, visitors will encounter a constellation of experiences, including interpretive panels, meditative spaces, soundscapes, experimental film, symbolic thresholds, and opportunities to leave a message of their own.\n\nCemeteries bring generations into conversation. They hold names, trees, monuments, rituals, and traces of lives that still shape the world around us. The project invites visitors to reflect on how grief, memory, nature, design and community shape the places we inherit and the futures we share.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Mount Pleasant Group","image":"nid4j8jkM4_7uRp7j1JIyQ","website":"https://mpg200.ca/installations","tickets":null},{"id":"a44a567f-b019-463a-b4ce-48188c2de96b","name":"Schmaltz and Pepper","dates":[1803240000000],"start":"2027-02-21T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-21T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":40,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"2026 Grammy Award winner Drew Jurecka is joined by violinist Rebekah Wolkstein, Juno Award-winning pianist Jeremy Ledbetter and Toronto Symphony Orchestra clarinetist Eric Abramovitz in a virtuosic night of high-energy klezmer, jazz and cabaret.\n\nThis ensemble is redefining the traditional boundaries of Yiddish music, blending classical mastery with innovative compositions and soulful arrangements. A mere six months after Abramovitz and Wolkstein came up with the idea to form a band, they had a full show of original music and inventive arrangements. Their debut performance was a live to air broadcast with a studio audience at Zoomer Hall in Toronto for Classical 96.3FM in May 2024.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"febWCBJX8U7VL3CjVpr4Gw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/schmaltz-and-pepper-448201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/448201"},{"id":"44e9b738-acc1-4797-9680-5e98e0ff0485","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"36baca62-bf9f-44d8-9658-fcc2e4704175","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"972137f6-4e73-4147-845d-ee2a53ccbf59","name":"Seven Heavens Away by Ashraf Zaghal – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1807657200000],"start":"2027-04-13T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-13T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":28,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nSeven Heavens Away is a coming-of-age novel set in Jerusalem, following a Palestinian teenager grappling with grief, identity and belonging after a close friend's death amid escalating violence. Navigating family, friendship and a complicated bond with a Jewish girl, he confronts hard questions about loss, hope and the future. Ashraf Zaghal will reflect on the novel's creative process, writing about memory and displacement, and how his characters illuminate identity, community and resilience.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"ejg68c81vEna8sUvd0oLXw","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/1f02cd39-1e2b-420f-b5e9-ec0bb3f0bab4"},{"id":"494cbe48-842e-4c90-ae15-e81d8a2f68c5","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"079e1c19-3a45-4447-949d-dbcf2d562220","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"004244bd-1c13-41d7-9b91-a6d817e12368","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"7a025112-6d1e-4abf-8432-160e0e0977df","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"63842814-2bbe-4ab2-98c2-36f213f6d3ad","name":"To a Flame","dates":[1790119800000,1790206200000,1790292600000,1790379000000,1790445600000,1790465400000,1790532000000,1790724600000,1790811000000,1790897400000,1790983800000,1791050400000,1791070200000,1791136800000],"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674248952,"lng":-79.387972597},"free":false,"low":15,"high":65,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be entranced by an explosive theatrical feast of image and language that pulls the audience deep into a Victorian Gothic Horror. \n\nThree confined women await the conclusion of their stories in the ancestral home of the man they call Father. Secrets burn to be revealed, aches of the past refuse to be suppressed, and the very house itself vibrates with desire for revenge. \n\nThis groundbreaking new work by Governor General Award-winning playwright Erin Shields and directed by Josette Bushell-Mingo intertwines American Sign Language and English with vibrant movement and live music into a haunting, multi-sensory performance that brings Deaf and hearing audiences into a shared theatrical experience through its bilingual artistic design. The ensemble cast features Deaf performer and cultural leader Dawn Jani Birley, with Nickeshia Garrick and Juliana Monk, accompanied by cellist Beth Silver. ","categories":["Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"yZg0SMTeDvFbyWzuteU1Lg","website":"https://www.nightwoodtheatre.net/to-a-flame/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002l5vx2AA"},{"id":"cd7a5323-777d-4efc-b44a-dca0c3e206ab","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"629a48c0-1a96-4860-a49e-cc40b8791b17","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"1696d2dc-70ac-42e0-b31a-5ddd37c42d4f","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"a9e706b2-5006-4e21-a27e-db5717ca73ee","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"7556ef05-8215-4bc9-b2ae-8040513a3480","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr15