lores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"86f1d389-2772-4ac4-bec5-b18a3eda7d44","name":"A Midsummer Night's Dream","dates":[1792711800000,1792798200000],"start":"2026-10-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-23T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"P.C. Ho Theatre at the Chinese Cultural Centre of the Greater Toronto","address":"5183 Sheppard Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1B 5Z5","lat":43.794675633,"lng":-79.233487478},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for William Shakespeare’s classic comedy, A Midsummer Night's Dream, with a Canadian twist, accompanied by Mendelssohn’s famous score. \n\nThis show brings out the magic of Northern Canada’s woodland and tundra landscapes and creatures of the forest. The ballet is a tale of love and, often misguided, magic set in motion by the mischievous trickster Puck. \n\nThis family-friendly short ballet will captivate audiences of all ages and will warm the hearts of young and old alike!","categories":["Dance","Family/Children","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"3SuOcCybKLxf9aCDbInfeg","website":"https://www.jorgendance.ca/events/list/?tribe-bar-search=midsummer+toronto","tickets":"https://jorgendance.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1695836051?aff=jorgendance"},{"id":"a77879fd-bbc0-4d2d-9446-8c9efdee36b3","name":"The Second City Toronto: Mainstage Comedy 92nd Revue","dates":[1787097600000,1787184000000,1787270400000,1787356800000,1787443200000,1787529600000,1787616000000,1787702400000,1787788800000,1787875200000,1787961600000,1788048000000,1788134400000,1788220800000,1788307200000,1788393600000,1788480000000,1788566400000,1788652800000,1788739200000,1788825600000,1788912000000,1788998400000,1789084800000,1789171200000,1789257600000,1789344000000,1789430400000,1789516800000,1789603200000,1789689600000,1789776000000,1789862400000,1789948800000,1790035200000,1790121600000,1790208000000,1790294400000,1790380800000,1790467200000,1790553600000,1790640000000,1790726400000,1790812800000,1790899200000,1790985600000,1791072000000,1791158400000],"start":"2026-08-18T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Second City Toronto","address":"110 Harbour St, Toronto, ON, M5J 0B7","lat":43.641557456,"lng":-79.379778422},"free":false,"low":39,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"For over 65 years, Second City has delighted audiences around the world with brilliant songs, hilarious sketches, and iconic characters. \n\nIn our time-honoured tradition, you are invited to become part of our creative process…audiences have the chance to influence brand new material being developed in real time. Come be part of the laughter!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Comedy","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor","tickets":"https://www.secondcity.com/shows/toronto/the-second-city-mainstage-92nd-revue-tor"},{"id":"96e7c141-ff69-454d-8022-355540efc427","name":"Riverdale Library Tree Tour","dates":[1791237600000],"start":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Library","address":"370 Broadview Ave, Toronto, ON, M4K 2M8","lat":43.6658148319,"lng":-79.3531801849},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Riverdale branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of trees. Join City of Toronto staff to explore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. \n\nThe tour will start and end at the Riverdale Branch and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens, hats, sunscreen, water, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.","categories":["Environmental","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"6JNCQVu_ynWbpUrq7WEKmg","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a495489541102b7fa8a674a","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a495489541102b7fa8a674a"},{"id":"3a5a2e22-0c2d-4adb-82b6-5c93e0fc2c68","name":"Riverdale Library Tree Tour","dates":[1791237600000],"start":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-05T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Library","address":"370 Broadview Ave, Toronto, ON, M4K 2M8","lat":43.6658148319,"lng":-79.3531801849},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Riverdale branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of trees. Join City of Toronto staff to explore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. \n\nThe tour will start and end at the Riverdale Branch and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens, hats, sunscreen, water, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.","categories":["Environmental","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"6JNCQVu_ynWbpUrq7WEKmg","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a495489541102b7fa8a674a","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a495489541102b7fa8a674a"},{"id":"13b9fa59-10ba-4a3a-bab5-02fa8ff3b7e3","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"l