 and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"91ec2572-d1e4-4b07-8497-5de081ceaaef","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"b9943ced-d6e9-4362-ba1e-f3974a1d24da","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"1709cfc9-044f-4092-b0db-983291cad3db","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"93aee778-ab52-47de-b661-f37ae056587b","name":"Endgame","dates":[1795046400000,1795222800000,1795289400000,1795309200000,1795375800000,1795568400000,1795654800000,1795741200000,1795827600000,1795894200000,1795914000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Corleck","address":"3 Eireann Quay, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R7","lat":43.634381646,"lng":-79.396724873},"free":false,"low":60,"high":100,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Samuel Beckett’s Endgame is the tragicomic tale of a man living with his parents and his servant in a world beyond time and place. With nowhere to go and not much to do, they spend their days telling stories and contemplating the absurdity of life.\n\nDirected by Druid’s Tony Award-winning Artistic Director Garry Hynes, the first woman to win the Tony for Best Director (Martin McDonagh’s The Beauty Queen of Leenane), Endgame stars Druid Ensemble members Aaron Monaghan, Rory Nolan and Tony Award-winner Marie Mullen, with Bosco Hogan.\n\nEndgame follows Druid’s award-winning 2016 production of Beckett’s Waiting for Godot, which toured the world for three years, wowing audiences and critics alike. \n\n\"It’s awfully good to be in their company… the fine, funny artists of Garry Hynes’s venerable Druid troupe\" – The New York Times Critic's Pick.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4twV4j3NTLNmn8ev9r6CqA","website":"https://www.canadairelandfoundation.com/cif_event/endgame/","tickets":"https://buytickets.at/canadairelandfoundation1/2282229"},{"id":"073cf3a1-dd82-495a-8e00-c559f98fda3d","name":"Skin by Tyler Pennock – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1820962800000],"start":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nSkin is a genre-blending poetry collection rooted in Treaty 8 territory, exploring memory, place, identity and belonging through a Two-Spirit Indigenous perspective. Through lyrical reflections on family, community, grief and land, Tyler Pennock examines how history and personal experience shape our understanding of ourselves and our connections to others. Pennock will share the collection's motivation, the intersections of poetry and storytelling and how home, identity and resilience emerge throughout these poems.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.\n\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"BV9gr9Ar8R4PmzfiD0oGQA","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/6696e062-c866-4f03-9aaf-483973d5e1c6"},{"id":"664a2c91-32c6-484d-8fbf-f992c449a691","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"4dbd95f9-df82-470b-97a5-654a00ca7543","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106