ers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"3bc28cd7-2904-4030-b847-e92ddcb9b2f7","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"54862e9d-ea19-4e28-8c2b-649ace91de9c","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"6654d1fa-56f7-4b59-89eb-7980c9f182f5","name":"Dancing Blossoms Installation","dates":[1787922000000,1788008400000,1788094800000,1788181200000,1788267600000,1788354000000,1788440400000,1788526800000,1788613200000,1788699600000,1788786000000,1788872400000,1788958800000,1789045200000,1789131600000,1789218000000,1789304400000,1789390800000,1789477200000,1789563600000,1789650000000,1789736400000,1789822800000,1789909200000,1789995600000,1790082000000,1790168400000,1790254800000,1790341200000,1790427600000,1790514000000,1790600400000,1790686800000,1790773200000,1790859600000,1790946000000,1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000],"start":"2026-08-28T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Delight in Paula Hartmann's Dancing Blossoms, a kinetic installation composed of dozens of delicate paper mobiles suspended in air, evoking the quiet poetry of spring trees swaying in the wind. Crafted from featherlight paper and fine wire, each mobile captures a fleeting moment of bloom, movement, and renewal.\n\nAbout the Artist\nPaula Hartmann is a Canadian visual artist whose joyful, kinetic sculptures transform humble materials into poetic, suspended worlds. Based in Toronto and originally from Germany, she draws on cultural traditions, folk aesthetics, and contemporary design to create works that explore impermanence, transformation, and belonging. Often incorporating paper, wire, and natural elements, her mobiles and installations invite viewers into moments of play, presence, and quiet wonder. Her installations have been featured in major public art events, including Toronto’s Nuit\nBlanche, the Burlington Waterfront Sculpture Trail, and City of Craft Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"6w2zOg_MReBeep-DtTCBng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"f298a407-cdcf-464b-8797-fb785fef7ded","name":"The Gitchi Manitou Manidoo Onitariio- Life in Toronto Drawing The Ravine","dates":[1791133200000],"start":"2026-10-04T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"John Mckenzie House ","address":"34 Parkview Ave, North York, ON M2N 3Y2","lat":43.771605,"lng":-79.411383},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come join us for an in-person event where creativity flows and nature inspires! Concept: Drawing the Ravine is a guided \"en plein air\" outdoor sketching and painting activation that invites Torontonians to slow down, observe, and connect with the ecological and cultural significance of our ravine system. The program blends art, stewardship, and public education, aligning directly with the City’s Ravine Strategy goals of awareness, access, and care.\nWhy this activation matters: Toronto’s ravines are one of the city’s most defining landscapes, yet many residents experience them only as trails rather than places of reflection, creativity, and learning. This activation transforms a ravine space into a gentle, low‑impact outdoor studio where participants can explore:\n\t• the textures and forms of native species and animals, draw your Toronto animal spirit\n\t• the movement of water and light and trees, draw your plants and trees\n\t• the layered history of the Don watershed\n\t• the role of ravine","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental","Run/Walk"],"presenter":"S'MAD ( Sustainable market art + design)","image":"qi7Vf88GYZtflA4wbErREg","website":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/drawing-the-ravine-tickets-1999193236788?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/drawing-the-ravine-tickets-1999193236788?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"d3fc41e9-9e30-4f2e-ab52-1c633267beb6","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"363708b3-c81b-4ad2-abb8-088044f5bb3c","name":"A Translucent City: Collective Memories of the Future","dates":[1788789600000,1788876000000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789394400000,1789480800000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789999200000,1790085600000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790604000000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791208800000,1791295200000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791813600000,1791900000000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792418400000,1792504800000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000,1793631600000,1793718000000,1793804400000,1793890800000,1793977200000,1794063600000,1794236400000,1794322800000,1794409200000,1794495600000,1794582000000,1794668400000,1794841200000,1794927600000,1795014000000,1795100400000,1795186800000,1795273200000,1795446000000,1795532400000,1795618800000,1795705200000,1795791600000,1795878000000,1796050800000,1796137200000,1796223600000,1796310000000,1796396400000,1796482800000,1796655600000,1796742000000,1796828400000,1796914800000,1797001200000,1797087600000,1797260400000,1797346800000,1797433200000,1797519600000,1797606000000,1797692400000,1797865200000,1797951600000,1798038000000,1798124400000,1798210800000,1798297200000,1798470000000,1798556400000,1798642800000,1798729200000],"start":"2026-09-07T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-31T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Urbanspace Gallery","address":"401 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 3A8","lat":43.647755,"lng":-79.394748},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"What do cities remember? How do our stories, relationships and experiences shape the places we call home?\n\nDrawing on community conversations, storytelling, a Sharing Circle and arts-based research, this evolving exhibition, featuring illuminated textile maps, documentary film and opportunities for public participation, explores how people connect to place and imagine urban futures. \n\nVisitors are invited to return throughout the exhibition, contribute to a growing textile installation and experience how the work changes over time.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Film"],"presenter":null,"image":"NgegXWP7YyX5G3PIBLwp2g","website":"https://www.urbanspacegallery.ca/event/a-translucent-city-collective-memories-of-the-future/","tickets":null},{"id":"e6b87bf8-efa3-42e8-ab9b-f33e4571875a","name":"Riverside Halloween Fest","dates":[1792940400000],"start":"2026-10-25T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Joel Weeks Park","address":"10 Thompson St, Toronto","lat":43.659092324,"lng":-79.352713196},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Get your costumes ready for our spook-tacular annual event!\n\nEnjoy pumpkin decorating, treats, DJ tunes, face painting and more! There’s also free fun for your dogs, including a dog costume contest with judging and prizes, treats and more fun. \n\nSee event website for more details and event perks and promos.","categories":["Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":"Riverside BIA","image":"ueYBVOI0YtanjhrylsQV-A","website":"https://riverside-to.com/halloween-fest/","tickets":"https://riverside-to.com/halloween-fest/"},{"id":"f9bf0fda-2b90-4b8b-9c54-3bbe713cec5c","name":"2026 Hockey Hall of Fame Induction Celebration","dates":[1794063600000,1794150000000,1794263400000],"start":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-09T17:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Hockey Hall of Fame ","address":"Brookfield Place, 30 Yonge Street, Toronto ON, M5E 1X8","lat":43.647006,"lng":-79.377245},"free":false,"low":295,"high":625,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join the Hockey Hall of Fame as we welcome hockey’s newest legends, Class of 2026 Inductees: Patrice Bergeron, Brian Burke, Cindy Curley, Carey Price, Pekka Rinne and Keith Tkachuk.\n\nThis is your chance to say, \"I was there\". Experience an unforgettable weekend with special events and fan experiences, including the Legends Photo Op, QnA Fan Forum and the annual Hockey Hall of Fame Game.\n\nThe celebration culminates with the prestigious Induction Gala, an extraordinary evening featuring red carpet arrivals, hockey legends, gourmet hospitality, a premier silent auction and the live induction of the Class of 2026.\n\n","categories":["Celebrations","Charity/Cause","Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"jv2np708BWDdUpeAAnj7yw","website":"https://www.hhof.com/induction/induction2026/inductiontickets.html","tickets":"https://www.hhof.com/induction/induction2026/inductiontickets.html"},{"id":"0812589f-b0ec-4883-a34b-d66aefce6859","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"b936838f-2172-47cc-97fb-9598719a26c6","name":"Nuit Talk: UFO with Brandon Vickerd","dates":[1791077400000],"start":"2026-10-03T21:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T21:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Queen Street Road Closure","address":"130 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M5H 2N5","lat":43.651985008,"lng":-79.384957167},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Brandon Vickerd’s artworks straddle the line between high and low culture, acting as a catalyst for critical thought. Hear Brandon speak about his UFO crash site public art sculpture and the inspirations behind it.  \n\nThe Nuit Talks program includes pop-up artist talks scheduled throughout the night, connecting attendees directly to the artists and deepening their understanding and appreciation of art. Many artists are also in attendance at their projects and able to speak to the public about their work.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"AVLmzU-NPmJspvYMGfB8Xg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/","tickets":null},{"id":"d1c0fae4-7db9-4753-95b6-7d5ade8bc78d","name":"This is Us: Art Exhibition","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Leslie Grove Gallery","address":"1158 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M4M 1L2","lat":43.662683087,"lng":-79.33369142},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Living and working within blocks of one another, our diverse artists bring different backgrounds, experiences, and ways of seeing the world. \n\nTogether, our varied work creates a sense of cohesion and harmony that reflects the community we share. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":"North Toronto Group of Artists","image":null,"website":"https://www.artistsnetwork.ca/patrons-calendar.","tickets":null},{"id":"229545ff-d2d5-4ffa-af30-bb22895b634b","name":"This is Us: Art Exhibition","dates":[1789574400000,1789