is Us: Art Exhibition","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Leslie Grove Gallery","address":"1158 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M4M 1L2","lat":43.662683087,"lng":-79.33369142},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Living and working within blocks of one another, our diverse artists bring different backgrounds, experiences, and ways of seeing the world. \n\nTogether, our varied work creates a sense of cohesion and harmony that reflects the community we share. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":"North Toronto Group of Artists","image":null,"website":"https://www.artistsnetwork.ca/patrons-calendar.","tickets":null},{"id":"edb8cd3d-d9a3-42b4-9cfe-7d74cd7f235c","name":"This is Us: Art Exhibition","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Leslie Grove Gallery","address":"1158 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M4M 1L2","lat":43.662683087,"lng":-79.33369142},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Living and working within blocks of one another, our diverse artists bring different backgrounds, experiences, and ways of seeing the world. \n\nTogether, our varied work creates a sense of cohesion and harmony that reflects the community we share. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan"],"presenter":"North Toronto Group of Artists","image":null,"website":"https://www.artistsnetwork.ca/patrons-calendar.","tickets":null},{"id":"7ebc56cf-e80b-440b-bfee-5189e6ffa5d2","name":"Meow Meow: Feline Festive","dates":[1797123600000],"start":"2026-12-12T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-12T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667878,"lng":-79.396243},"free":false,"low":50,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Rekindle the true spirit of the holidays with the fabulous Meow Meow!  \n\nThe international cabaret sensation brings her singular blend of comedy, glamour, and vocal brilliance for a holiday performance like no other. Featuring a band of superb musicians, and music ranging from jazzy vintage showbiz to original and contemporary classics, this is going to be a night to remember.  \n\nDuring this unforgettably steamy evening, prepare to be hypnotized, inspired, and slightly terrified as “the chanteuse brilliantly embodies a new kind of performance art” (The New Yorker). ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"D4Em1f7wSDCnh43NdgfhNg","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/meow-meow-feline-festive-428601","tickets":"http://rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/428601"},{"id":"378f0480-0496-4083-aa03-673ada05a287","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"33e102c1-b078-43fa-b925-7fc4acfbc8fd","name":"Cookie Decorating: Halloween at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793462400000,1793469600000],"start":"2026-10-31T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":false,"low":10,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, enjoy a fun, family-friendly cookie decorating class where history meets creativity. Historic recipe cookies and decorating supplies are provided. Just bring your imagination and your sweet tooth. No previous experience needed. Cookies contain gluten, dairy and eggs.\n\nA ticket-holding adult must accompany children 16 years of age and younger.","categories":["Family/Children","Food/Culinary","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"g6nKGGP1E3l19cC5kc92_A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/toronto/activity/search?onlineSiteId=0&activity_keyword=Halloween%20Cookie%20Decorating%20at%20Montgomery%27s%20Inn&viewMode=list"},{"id":"62e2253a-9788-438e-a346-84ac65e53144","name":"Youth Entrepreneurship Program","dates":[1789066800000,1789671600000,1790276400000,1790881200000,1791486000000,1792090800000,1792695600000,1793300400000,1793908800000,1794513600000],"start":"2026-09-10T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-12T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heritage Skills Development Centre","address":"2387 Eglinton Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1K 2M5","lat":43.731392727,"lng":-79.268830069},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Do you have an idea, a passion, or the drive to build or grow your own business? \n\nThe Scarborough Youth Entrepreneurship Project is offering a 10-week in-person training program designed to help you turn your ideas into reality. In this training, you will gain hands-on skills in business development, financial literacy, leadership, and decision-making while connecting with mentors, funding opportunities, and a strong network of entrepreneurs. \n\n\n","categories":["Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"O7jOq6D42lNBBHU9VVcazQ","website":"https://forms.gle/KVzdgApj11XiCWUEA","tickets":null},{"id":"e01637bd-3316-4877-b16f-8c77fa384d8e","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"f0c90695-bdf1-4b44-bd46-6e50b6286384","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"2f21a84b-4261-426e-9e18-0f12596a2475","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"5aa97717-f091-49de-8b45-06fd13f47a3a","name":"Goodnight Desdemona (Good Morning Juliet)","dates":[1794011400000,1794097800000,1794164400000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794682800000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795024800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795287600000,1795307400000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-06T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A joyful comedy that flips the script on Shakespeare's most infamous heroines.\n\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of her landmark play, acclaimed novelist and playwright Ann-Marie MacDonald steps into the spotlight as Constance Ledbelly, the overlooked academic who tumbles headlong into Shakespeare’s worlds and discovers that the heroines (and even Constance herself) may be capable of far more than anyone imagined.\n\nAt once wildly funny and moving, this Canadian classic unleashes Desdemona and Juliet as fierce forces of their own destiny and reminds us that sometimes the bravest act is claiming your own story.","categories":["History","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"_IifGvvMLdKvkwvqxvxGOA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/goodnight-desdemona-good-morning-juliet","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9691"},{"id":"3130c0d1-5c6a-4cc0-8e0a-bb59d0ee6066","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"c98d71f8-5418-41df-8e1c-36cbda7529ef","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"bdc95e10-402a-473b-860a-f9b39e401580","name":"Rogers v. Rogers","dates":[1794184200000,1794357000000,1794443400000,1794529800000,1794616200000,1794702600000,1794769200000,1794961800000,1795048200000,1795134600000,1795221000000,1795307400000,1795374000000,1795566600000,1795653000000,1795739400000,1795825800000,1795912200000,1795978800000,1796171400000,1796257800000,1796344200000,1796430600000,1796517000000,1796583600000,1796776200000,1796862600000,1796949000000,1797035400000,1797121800000,1797188400000],"start":"2026-11-08T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-13T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Berkeley Street Theatre","address":"26 Berkeley St, Toronto, ON, M5A 2W3","lat":43.650577241,"lng":-79.36426063},"free":false,"low":70,"high":140,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The hit show returns to a new venue, same buzz!\n\nBased on Rogers v. Rogers: The Battle for Control of Canada’s Telecom Empire by Alexandra Posadzki.\n\nTelecom tycoon Ted Rogers built an empire turning Canada’s airwaves into cash. Now his son Edward, long dismissed by his father, is fighting for control of the family business. Meanwhile, shrewd public servant Matthew Boswell is determined to derail Rogers’ billion-dollar takeover of Shaw Communications.\n\nFrom award-winning playwright Michael Healey (The Master Plan, The Drawer Boy) and starring Tom Rooney (Fifteen Dogs, Uncle Vanya) comes a story of outsized ambition, personal grudges, and corporate power.\n\nInspired by one of the most dramatic boardroom showdowns in Canadian history, this riveting new drama examines the price of pushing back, the unraveling bonds of kin, and the legacy that money can and cannot buy.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Theatre"],"presenter":"Canadian Stage","image":"aPOiZbQ-WiDkmCKRq1MWMg","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/rogers-v.-rogers","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/9693/9823"},{"id":"c5865b3d-c8ca-48c5-9d91-e42f31812a1d","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"4869d2f3-b398-4ffe-95ab-f5703427897b","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"31447b95-0869-4943-b790-ab1b1026ec5c","name":"Intrigue at the Museum: A Mystery Scavenger Hunt at ROM","dates":[1788631200000,1789927200000,1791050400000,1793469600000,1794769200000,1795892400000,1797793200000,1799521200000,1800817200000],"start":"2026-09-05T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-24T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795,"lng":-79.394212},"free":false,"low":47.5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTicket price includes   per person and include admission to the Royal Ontario Museum, your on-site host, and access to our scavenger hunt app. Tickets must be purchased in advance. If you have a ROM Membership, please call us for a discount code.For questions about the hunt, tickets or location, please contact Urban Capers Scavenger Hunts at the email below.","description":"\nPlease join us! Back by popular demand, our classic murder mystery scavenger hunt returns (formerly called Murder at the ROM).\n\nThere has been a mysterious murder, and the museum's collections hold the key.  As you gather clues, you’ll begin to piece together a tale of greed, lust, pride, and revenge. Working in teams, sleuths travel through the museum's galleries solving whodunnit, where, and with what. \n\nWill your team solve the mystery before the clock runs out?\n\nNote: We encourage all players (or as many as possible) to bring a fully charged phone with our scavenger hunt app downloaded for submitting answers and creative team photos and videos during the adventure. Please arrive 10 minutes early to sign in, use coat check and the facilities. Your hosts will greet you and provide an orientation before the two-hour game begins, ending with a conclusion, shout-outs and a winning team! See you soon! ","categories":["History","Museum","Trivia"],"presenter":null,"image":"CWJ_i7JR_cd-aiuSgw1m8A","website":"https://www.bookeo.com/urbancapers","tickets":"https://bookeo.com/urbancapers"},{"id":"b01116b2-1aad-4ab8-b2ff-f549da7aa3c0","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cinderella","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9695"},{"id":"c5214230-2e7a-4ff6-8bf4-d231ba1e128e","name":"Cinderella","dates":[1796515200000,1796576400000,1796774400000,1796860800000,1796947200000,1797033600000,1797112800000,1797181200000,1797379200000,1797465600000,1797552000000,1797638400000,1797717600000,1797786000000,1797984000000,1798070400000,1798156800000,1798243200000,1798322400000,1798390800000,1798588800000,1798675200000,1798761600000,1798848000000,1798927200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-12-05T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Winter Garden Theatre","address":"189 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1M4","lat":43.653065074,"lng":-79.3792038148},"free":false,"low":49,"high":169,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The classic story, turned on its heel.\n\nThink you’ve outgrown the panto? Think again.\n\nOur new take on Cinderella delivers all the glitter and spectacle of the beloved tradition with a clever, contemporary edge. Packed with infectious pop anthems, sly humour, and spectacular stagecraft, this is a holiday outing designed as much for grown-ups as it is for kids.\n\nWhether you’re reliving the tradition or discovering it for the first time, this is holiday theatre with wit, style, and a knowing wink.","categories":["Comedy","Family/Children","Live Performances","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"7WK7Gk8ZaBFodp61LlcVkA","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/ci