in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"2e506fea-912b-44ff-b335-a0ec4232b58b","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"355008e1-a002-49bc-86c4-85817e948eaf","name":"Tales of the Damned: Immersive Theatre Experience","dates":[1792020600000,1792193400000,1792279200000,1792366200000,1792539000000,1792625400000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1792971000000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793403000000,1793498400000,1793579400000],"start":"2026-10-14T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Campbell House Museum","address":"160 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M5H 3H3","lat":43.651058,"lng":-79.387322},"free":false,"low":42.15,"high":54.99,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bone-chilling Halloween tradition!\n\nFrom the creators of the immersive sensations “Tales of the Grotesque” (2023, 2024) and the landmark production of “Tales of the Damned” (2025) comes the revival of Toronto’s favourite gothic horror anthology. \n\nWith fresh characters, familiar tales, and its twisted brand of terror, this site-specific theatrical experience brings literature’s most depraved characters to life and death. \n\nAfter a lady of the night is murdered, a mad doctor strikes a pact with the Devil to raise her from the dead. But all hell breaks loose when he comes face-to-face with her killer at a masquerade. Descend into madness with Victor Frankenstein, Henry Jekyll, and Dorian Gray to discover the results of playing God, and the monstrous repercussions when the Devil comes to collect. \n\nStep into the story as you move through the candlelit Campbell House mansion to confront history's most iconic villains. Ages 14 and up, minors must be accompanied by an adult.","categories":["Live Performances","Museum","Theatre","Halloween"],"presenter":"Campbell House Museum","image":"vywbbYFbH0ca7m8NLmLaow","website":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1","tickets":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1"},{"id":"4cdedf2a-6f54-455d-9c13-e4ba20d8919f","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"b19ae869-2e84-497a-b502-b4d2a6c587d4","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"2236dc07-8e5b-4715-a002-a41391d6ecd6","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,