es","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"8f5def35-de16-479b-8083-8652451565b8","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"d9c9eabc-8b83-4a87-a068-477f2c524fef","name":"The Descent of Orpheus","dates":[1792711800000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1792953000000],"start":"2026-10-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"TELUS Centre for Performance and Learning at Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":85,"high":250,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy our season premiere with Canada’s first fully-staged production of M.A. Charpentier’s The Descent of Orpheus. \n\nFounding Co-Artistic Directors Marshall Pynkoski, C.M. and Jeannette Lajeunesse Zingg, C.M. direct and choreograph this fresh, contemporary, and emotionally-driven staging of Charpentier’s masterpiece, grounded in the concept of period performance. \n\nThe production is the earliest known French operatic take on the Orpheus myth from Ovid's Metamorphoses. Celebrated American tenor Daniel McGrew is making his Canadian debut with Opera Atelier as Orpheus opposite French-Canadian soprano Mireille Asselin as Eurydice. ","categories":["Dance","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Opera Atelier","image":"5Kjgp2yeVCQPw_sKJnSawg","website":"https://www.operaatelier.com/shows/the-descent-of-orpheus/","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts?tps_activeFacetTab=Concerts%20Presented%20By%20Others&fq=eventpresenter%7C%7COpera+Atelier"},{"id":"4c1437a7-0dc5-4ea0-91f8-42d2e2c4495a","name":"Tenfold: 10 year anniversary exhibition","dates":[1791496800000,1791576000000,1791651600000],"start":"2026-10-08T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Remote Gallery","address":"568 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 1Y9","lat":43.647051565,"lng":-79.401506964},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"We celebrate ten years of artistic practice, collaboration, and community. \n\nTo mark this milestone, artists from the studios were invited to bring their work together in a collective exhibition. \n\nThe title \"Tenfold\" speaks both to this ten-year journey and to the many ways creativity expands when developed collectively. \n\nWhile each artist explores distinct questions through their own techniques and visual language, Tenfold highlights the dialogues, affinities, and contrasts that emerge between their practices. \nIndividual voices remain visible, while their hared experiences reveal the rich sense of exchange fostered within the Akin studio community.\n\nParticipating artists include Anne Kobayashi, Barbara Bailey, Bernadette Peets, Bettina Westwood, Carrie Fisher, Eli Moser, Hamid Mohammadi, Loren Kaplan, Mark Buck, Miles Ingrassia, MP Guillot, Robert Simoni, Shayla Bond, Tatjana Reithofer and Veronica Zaretski.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Celebrations"],"presenter":"Akin Dupont Studios","image":null,"website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/tenfold-akin-duponts-10-year-anniversary-exhibition-tickets-2001630172729","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/tenfold-akin-duponts-10-year-anniversary-exhibition-tickets-2001630172729"},{"id":"9389aaa8-97a7-4b38-a24e-698add07db3e","name":"ROM After Dark","dates":[1793403000000,1793489400000],"start":"2026-10-30T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":40,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The wait is over...welcome back to the best Halloween Party in the city!\n\nAs night falls, the Museum transforms with eerie décor for an unforgettable evening of live music, DJ sets and non-stop dancing. \n\nCome dressed in your best Halloween look or simply ready to celebrate. The night will be packed with high-energy entertainment and so many spooky surprises.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Nightlife","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"cpcsg5qxLMVvl-Lh-JcmOA","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/events/rom-after-dark-all-hallows-eve?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=rad","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/events/rom-after-dark-all-hallows-eve?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=rad"},{"id":"266a3052-1164-49e2-91c0-c819c1b7ea79","name":"Rebirth: The Quiet Becoming Installation at Fort York","dates":[1785938400000,1786024800000,1786111200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786543200000,1786629600000,1786716000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787148000000,1787234400000,1787320800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1787752800000,1787839200000,1787925600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788357600000,1788444000000,1788530400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000],"start":"2026-08-05T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864096,"lng":-79.406314887},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bold new outdoor installation on the Gardiner Expressway beside Fort York Visitor Centre. Created by artists Delali Cofie and Yuma Dean Hester, it reimagines the site’s layered histories through contemporary art. An accompanying exhibition inside the Visitor Centre deepens the experience, inviting visitors to encounter the Fort as a living cultural landscape shaped by reflection, dialogue and collaboration.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"_QHlUAQMVyNc88AaSDfQ8A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":null},{"id":"85b83070-71db-47a9-88d1-dd901379e697","name":"Rebirth: The Quiet Becoming Installation at Fort York","dates":[1785938400000,1786024800000,1786111200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786543200000,1786629600000,1786716000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787148000000,1787234400000,1787320800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1787752800000,1787839200000,1787925600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788357600000,1788444000000,1788530400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792