"venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"defe4d84-8cca-4896-a984-e4c1552fc909","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"b330169b-6d57-4d9f-b496-d6e8762e5858","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"2af248d8-2dda-4ff8-823d-a280fef94ded","name":"Chalkfarm Park - 11 a.m. to 1 p.m.","dates":[1791126000000],"start":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"ChalkfarmPark","address":"2230 Jane St, North York","lat":43.72380267,"lng":-79.509800109},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Try something new, get moving and connect through sport, Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels.\n\nWith a variety of sports equipment on board, vibrant vans tour neighbourhoods, transforming parks and outdoor spaces into pop-up sport hubs, bringing energy and excitement directly to communities around the city. Proudly powered in partnership with Nike, Play Mobile is committed to the future of youth sport, creating more equitable and inclusive access to play – with a focus on encouraging girls to participate and stay involved in sport.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"JY5NZWRAS6Lt1TXJKw_GWw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=35%20Raven%20Rd&lat=43.713345&lng=-79.50442&zoom=17","tickets":null},{"id":"4e4feac6-368a-4237-91f0-9f1739192a8b","name":"North Kipling Community Centre - 2:30 to 4:30 p.m.","dates":[1791138600000],"start":"2026-10-04T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"North Kipling CC","address":"2 Rowntree Rd, Etobicoke, ON, M9V 5C7","lat":43.752091902,"lng":-79.584471986},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Try something new, get moving and connect through sport, Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels.\n\nWith a variety of sports equipment on board, vibrant vans tour neighbourhoods, transforming parks and outdoor spaces into pop-up sport hubs, bringing energy and excitement directly to communities around the city. Proudly powered in partnership with Nike, Play Mobile is committed to the future of youth sport, creating more equitable and inclusive access to play – with a focus on encouraging girls to participate and stay involved in sport.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"JY5NZWRAS6Lt1TXJKw_GWw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=36%20Prince%20Charles%20Dr&lat=43.722727&lng=-79.435676&zoom=11","tickets":null},{"id":"11b7649b-603c-4ce1-b318-38573aebe4d8","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"b39b5b63-4b04-400a-91cc-61bb341e0360","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"df6847e3-568d-4c02-841b-0676c3a597be","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"b2894e4f-b2dc-44f4-8bfd-aec2d40ddb4b","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"7876757a-c3b8-4f73-b680-1a1e75401969","name":"Shab-e She’r (Poetry Night) CXXV","dates":[1792537200000],"start":"2026-10-20T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-20T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Tranzac","address":"292 Brunswick Ave, Toronto, ON, M5S 2M7","lat":43.665226,"lng":-79.407554},"free":false,"low":10,"high":20,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nCash at the door, there is an ATM machine at the venue. ","description":"Canada’s most diverse and brave poetry reading and open mic series.\n\nFeatured poets include Christine Miskonoodinkwe-Smith and Sacha Archer, with an open mic opporutnity in any language.","categories":["Indigenous","Literary"],"presenter":null,"image":"s5gNEiDwMkV4AQTkYO2hpQ","website":"https://www.facebook.com/share/19TmNuhhox/","tickets":null},{"id":"56256242-15d2-498c-bd36-248eb0e0fdf5","name":"Art Guild of Scarborough's Juried Fall Art Show and Sale","dates":[1794063600000,1794150000000],"start":"2026-11-07T10:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-08T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Centennial Recreation Centre: Scarborough","address":"1967 Ellesmere Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1H 2W5","lat":43.774594,"lng":-79.237411},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nRefreshments included.","description":"Featuring over 400 original, juried works of art by member artists, many of whom will be in attendance. \n\nWorks include watercolour, pastel, oil, acrylic, ink, sculpture and mixed media. \n\nThe Art Guild of Scarborough is a non-profit organization. Since 1962, it has brought together artists to promote and celebrate the creation of original art. Members range in experience from novice to professional. The Art Guild of Scarborough holds weekly member meetings featuring both demonstrations by notable artists and hands-on art activities.  ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"_rtt0R_qDYfVA3ssRZJBMg","website":"http://theartguildofscarborough.com/upcoming-shows","tickets":null},{"id":"44b1fa1f-54ed-4488-9618-6f66332ac047","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"d16283d9-22c9-4609-af63-a81c4354b024","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"1128b597-ef82-4115-a356-624e01baa7b1","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"86995536-eded-4db9-951d-651aac2a9101","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"c7f91476-601b-45d2-a84a-cd36faea97ba","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"d6342673-efb0-4009-b144-218dee734aa4","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"6ee9970d-77aa-4d9e-b97d-945eab3d3622","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"