tricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"61776fc4-cda7-4705-ac4e-bd84a8ff94f1","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"58443118-9fc7-4113-bf01-974976758735","name":"Mozart and Dvorak Flowering Moon","dates":[1809214200000],"start":"2027-05-01T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-01T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity- St. Paul's Centre","address":"427 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1X7","lat":43.66603939,"lng":-79.405707818},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"We close out our 28th season with an evening that honours both musical tradition and the natural world and one world premiere unlike anything else this season.\n\nPianist Heghine Rapyan, praised by BBC Music Magazine as \"excellent\" and a \"sensational discovery,\" performs Mozart's Piano Concerto No. 9, \"Jeunehomme\" one of the composer's most beloved and daring works. The evening opens with the world premiere of Waawaaskone-giizis (Flowering Moon) by Anishinaabe composer Barbara Assiginaak, 13 musical vignettes depicting 13 flowers of the Flowering Moon, honouring Mother Earth and the ecosystems that sustain us. \n\nMaestro Nurhan Arman closes with his own orchestral arrangement of Dvorak's glorious Chamber Symphony Op. 77a, folk-inspired, rich, and full of joy.\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Sinfonia Toronto","image":"aXaZU9FkBhz9c7BlN27K4w","website":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/mozart-dvorak","tickets":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/mozart-dvorak"},{"id":"9d25ad2b-dd91-4a7c-ab03-d1dcf45f6e3e","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"fcf4252f-0c21-4860-b56b-dcb12db997cb","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,179229600