":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy fall-themed fun at Scarborough Museum throughout October weekends. Sip a warm drink from the museum kitchen and savour a treat prepared on the historic stove. Spark creativity with family-friendly paper crafts, a scavenger hunt, and seasonal activities designed for all ages.\n\nAll ages. Drop-In. FREE. All are welcome. ","categories":["Family/Children","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"BA9dThVY5VHcVGOcWEUaCw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/scarborough-museum/","tickets":null},{"id":"34dc7013-d6ab-4864-9df4-eccdb5d9e9fc","name":"Fall Flavours &  Crafts at Scarborough Museum","dates":[1791039600000,1791126000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793458800000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scarborough Museum","address":"1007 Brimley Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1P 3E8","lat":43.757624474,"lng":-79.254809969},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy fall-themed fun at Scarborough Museum throughout October weekends. Sip a warm drink from the museum kitchen and savour a treat prepared on the historic stove. Spark creativity with family-friendly paper crafts, a scavenger hunt, and seasonal activities designed for all ages.\n\nAll ages. Drop-In. FREE. All are welcome. ","categories":["Family/Children","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"BA9dThVY5VHcVGOcWEUaCw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/scarborough-museum/","tickets":null},{"id":"24e16185-5ae1-40b2-8716-baf7b8fad34f","name":"R.V. Burgess Park - 2:30 to 4:30 p.m.","dates":[1791657000000],"start":"2026-10-10T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"RV Burgess Park","address":"46 Thorncliffe Park Dr, East York","lat":43.702786643,"lng":-79.342761794},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels, no registration or reservations are required to participate. The new soccer Play Mobile is dedicated to the world’s most popular game. All ages are invited to learn and celebrate soccer in a fun, supportive environment with no experience required.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"D-JBEvzzMMBRxdflGESP0g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=929%20Kennedy%20Rd&lat=43.742518&lng=-79.269905&zoom=11","tickets":null},{"id":"0915f132-587c-41f2-b5a2-8866ed1a415e","name":"Howl-O-Ween Unleashed 2026","dates":[1792947600000],"start":"2026-10-25T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Festival Terrace at Downsview Park","address":"70 Canuck Ave, North York, ON, M3K 2C5","lat":43.744269913,"lng":-79.48436452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Drop by for spook-tacular, fun-filled day. \n\nEnjoy a fang-tastic vendor market, where you can find a variety of products and services for your furbabies! Show off your furry friends and their costumes for some treats before hitting the dog park. Trick or (dog) treat!\n\nCome visit the Downsview Park tent and show us your costumes and make sure to strike a pose with your pup at our various photo booth stations!\n\nCheck out the vendor market powered by Toronto Dog Moms and take home some dog treats and other accessories (while supplies last).\n\nWho can resist the eerie-istable, cuteness overload of this pawsitively exciting event? No one!\n","categories":["Family/Children","Other","Halloween"],"presenter":"Downsview Park","image":null,"website":"https://downsviewpark.ca/events/howl-o-ween-unleashed-2026","tickets":"https://downsviewpark.ca/events/howl-o-ween-unleashed-2026"},{"id":"dfa7fa12-7f6d-40af-96fd-32c60cda9270","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"2631385c-e909-4933-9a6d-1777312285b6","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"8fea1730-b27b-4ccb-86b7-bb09e11f5792","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791