innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"9909da2d-55ed-455a-8af5-fa92a7f791c9","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Recommended for ages 12 and up. Youth 12-16 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAll ticket sales are non-refundable. Tickets are transferable.","description":"Join us for a chilling tour at Colborne Lodge in High Park. Visit the gravesite of John and Jemima Howard. Delve deeply into ideas about death and the afterlife from the 1800s and hear true tales of paranormal activities. Decide for yourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"a95877f0-02a9-40e5-94b1-474251239f0a","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"