Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"52c4f9b3-b5b4-4ef3-9fe0-d5311a8dc2e0","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"e75a798d-996e-440d-955f-87e3b6196ac1","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"6a211e5a-ff33-4388-b72e-eb2486aff3da","name":"When Toronto Gathered: Election‑Night Rituals & Civic Culture","dates":[1792702800000],"start":"2026-10-22T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-22T17:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mackenzie House Museum 82 Bond Street","address":"82 Bond St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1X2","lat":43.655694,"lng":-79.37831},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"At Mackenzie House Museum, home of Toronto's first mayor, historian Jamie Bradburn presents a lively look at Toronto election history. In the early 20th century, election nights turned into impromptu street parties, giving  Torontonians a reason to gather. Guests are invited to print their own historic poster on the 1840s printing press and grab a bucket of popcorn 