98131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"d05b3311-264b-4ff7-97d9-c9a7574f7c5a","name":"Gay AF Comedy","dates":[1790987400000],"start":"2026-10-02T20:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-02T20:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Comedy Bar","address":"945 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M6H 1L5","lat":43.661342,"lng":-79.427859},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A celebration of Toronto's LGBTQ+ comedic talent.\n\nToronto's favourite Queer comedy fix is serving big laughs with a lineup of Canada’s top LGBTQ comedians, so be prepared for a fabulous night of Queer comedy that’s straight up hilarious!\n\nFeaturing Mickey Dykeman, Steve Degay, Luke Witt, Daphney Joseph and Bren D'Souza. Hosted by Robert Watson.\n\nGrab your friends (with consent) and come join the funny!\n","categories":["Comedy","2SLGBTQ+","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"xdITAlExKtW2fg68gbgGOA","website":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/gay-af-JFL","tickets":"https://comedybar.ca/shows/gay-af-JFL"},{"id":"38f0af78-3940-4ec4-ae17-a9898e0ff34e","name":"Rihab Chaieb, mezzo-soprano, with Ammiel Bushakevitz, piano","dates":[1794772800000],"start":"2026-11-15T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-15T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667907,"lng":-79.396185},"free":false,"low":55,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tunisian-Canadian mezzo-soprano Rihab Chaieb and Israeli pianist Ammiel Bushakevitz blend French repertoire with Tunisian lullabies.\n\nChaieb’s voice has been praised for possessing a “a dark, velvety sheen, rich but never overindulgent” (Stage and Cinema). A former member of the Metropolitan Opera’s Lindemann Young Artist Program, Chaieb has quickly become one of the most compelling voices of her generation appearing regularly at the Canadian Opera Company, the Metropolitan Opera, and throughout Europe. \n\nAmmiel Bushakevitz began playing the piano at the age of four. As a song accompanist, soloist, and chamber musician, he has performed on six continents, including at Carnegie Hall in New York, Wigmore Hall in London, the Philharmonie de Paris, the Konzerthaus in Berlin, the Concertgebouw in Amsterdam and the Shanghai Concert Hall.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"2u1Ivtw6buwq8gyKOC6xxA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/rihab-chaieb-mezzo-soprano-with-ammiel-bushakevitz-piano-430601","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/430601"},{"id":"c2d5ce53-7f95-4275-9baa-7ba988e011c5","name":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit","dates":[1790791200000,1790877600000,1790949600000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front Street West, Toronto, ON M5V 2W6","lat":43.64392037329108,"lng":-79.38668733673923},"free":false,"low":275,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Local Delegate – All 4 Days: CA$275.00 (With discount code CA$137.50), Local Delegate – Day 3 Only: CA$140.00 (with code CA$70.00), Local Delegate – Day 4 Only: CA$200.00 (with discount code CA$100.00), Student Admission (Valid Student ID Required): CA$70.00 Marketplace Vendor: CA$250.00 (with discount code CA$125.00), They can use the discount code 2026FOA they can enjoy 50% off expires Sep 12.","description":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit is a four-day hybrid conference, taking place virtually on September 30 - October 1, 2026, and in person on October 2-3, 2026 at the Metro Toronto Convention Centre in Toronto, Ontario. The Summit brings together entrepreneurs, startups, investors, business leaders, and ecosystem partners from Canada and Africa. It features expert panels, workshops, startup pitches, networking, business matchmaking, and a career fair, creating opportunities for investment, partnerships, entrepreneurship, and Canada - Africa economic collaboration.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Friends of Africa Coalition","image":"XOz0W9bL3jJbnbVI5aIgTg","website":"https://friendsofafrica.ca/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/16th-african-economic-summit-friends-of-africa-2026-tickets-1803110374669?discount=2026FOA"},{"id":"8737ee20-a7e2-4858-9686-b49af3b58b2f","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,179