6000000],"start":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Coronation Park","address":"3700 Eglinton Ave W, York","lat":43.6856847365,"lng":-79.4980823137},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Try something new, get moving and connect through sport, Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels.\n\nWith a variety of sports equipment on board, vibrant vans tour neighbourhoods, transforming parks and outdoor spaces into pop-up sport hubs, bringing energy and excitement directly to communities around the city. Proudly powered in partnership with Nike, Play Mobile is committed to the future of youth sport, creating more equitable and inclusive access to play – with a focus on encouraging girls to participate and stay involved in sport.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"JY5NZWRAS6Lt1TXJKw_GWw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=44%20Tobermory%20Dr&lat=43.762598&lng=-79.512091&zoom=17","tickets":null},{"id":"c8717c53-3111-4ebb-9691-7cbed5d3ba88","name":"Jimmie Simpson Park - 11 a.m. to 1 p.m.","dates":[1791126000000],"start":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Jimmie Simpson Park","address":"872 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6J 1G3","lat":43.645387844,"lng":-79.414393382},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels, no registration or reservations are required to participate. The new soccer Play Mobile is dedicated to the world’s most popular game. All ages are invited to learn and celebrate soccer in a fun, supportive environment with no experience required.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"D-JBEvzzMMBRxdflGESP0g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=2000%20MCNICOLL%20AVE&lat=43.812658&lng=-79.305013&zoom=11","tickets":null},{"id":"8c3bc275-9123-4f5d-aedc-1c847f3b6350","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"4906f339-283e-4f05-93cd-69d551dde409","name":"A Love Affair with the Unknown by Gillian Deacon – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1822777200000],"start":"2027-10-05T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-10-05T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nA Love Affair with the Unknown is a personal memoir examining how we navigate uncertainty, loss and transformation. Drawing on her experiences with illness, healing and life-changing challenges, Gillian Deacon, veteran journalist and television/radio host, explores what it means to live with vulnerability while remaining open to possibility, connection and growth. She will discuss lessons learned through periods of upheaval and how embracing the unknown can lead to greater resilience, creativity and meaning.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"xOF2hcT4Mkqe17tolrymsg","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4e9e6d8b-6a3f-472f-92ec-964c81318da1"},{"id":"f2457175-115b-4c16-8f21-b9938f87d4c8","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by w