rt Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"95e6a0aa-fd97-4ded-8bdc-64205ebb511b","name":"Queen East Eats Fall Food Tours","dates":[1791046800000,1794679200000,1796493600000,1797098400000],"start":"2026-10-03T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-12T13:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Restaurants/Cafes/Bars in Riverside and Leslieville","address":"657 Queen St E, Toronto","lat":43.658232745,"lng":-79.351745596},"free":false,"low":10,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTickets are available for purchase about two weeks before the tour. ","description":"Celebrate fall and support small businesses.\n\nGet ready to visit six pre-selected local food and drink establishments in Riverside and Leslieville, while learning about the story behind the businesses with your expert guide.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Tour"],"presenter":"Riverside BIA","image":"D9twy0ORnOjZy3lFBl4ztA","website":"https://QueenEastEatsFoodTours.eventbrite.ca","tickets":"https://QueenEastEatsFoodTours.eventbrite.ca"},{"id":"d2783bc2-3fc5-4458-99fe-274c1a05c19b","name":"Nuit Blanche 2026","dates":[1791068400000,1791154800000],"start":"2026-10-03T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Various","address":"","lat":43.655115,"lng":-79.388237},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join in a free all-night celebration of contemporary art that transforms Toronto’s public spaces into unexpected landscapes and animates cultural sites throughout the city.\n\nThis year’s theme, Tomorrow’s Memories, invites you to look back to the artists, curators, communities and places that defined Nuit Blanche and its twenty-year history.\n\nNuit Blanche is Toronto’s annual all-night celebration of contemporary art, produced by the City of Toronto in collaboration with Toronto’s arts community. Its locations, theme, curation and artists change from year to year, with a selection of projects extended after the event. Since 2006, this award-winning event has featured almost 1,800 art installations by approximately 6,350 artists and has generated over $550 million in economic impact for Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"D9unQ_dL2JAu1TGQVkODBg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/","tickets":null},{"id":"2fc0629f-8959-4847-9c4f-93240ad99276","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"174c441e-f1f4-46ed-826e-c9f26fb650c6","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"a1d0b3f2-ef69-4982-9bff-851cf2c24ec9","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dat