g author of Prophecy: Prediction, Power, and the Fight for the Future, from Ancient Oracles to AI, and Associate Professor of Philosophy at the University of Oxford. \n\nHer keynote will examine predictive AI and the future of politics in Canada and will be followed by a conversation with renowned journalist and Samara Centre board member Lisa LaFlamme.","categories":["Charity/Cause","Talks"],"presenter":"Samara Centre for Democracy","image":"fNsm6Qmya238AXVFdyLLbQ","website":"https://www.samaracentre.ca/events/in-defence-of-democracy-2026-carissa-veliz-with-lisa-laflamme","tickets":"https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event/100064FFDE176919"},{"id":"95682d92-af2c-4ecd-a399-05a2b8544a52","name":"Seven Heavens Away by Ashraf Zaghal – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1807657200000],"start":"2027-04-13T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-13T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":28,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nSeven Heavens Away is a coming-of-age novel set in Jerusalem, following a Palestinian teenager grappling with grief, identity and belonging after a close friend's death amid escalating violence. Navigating family, friendship and a complicated bond with a Jewish girl, he confronts hard questions about loss, hope and the future. Ashraf Zaghal will reflect on the novel's creative process, writing about memory and displacement, and how his characters illuminate identity, community and resilience.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"ejg68c81vEna8sUvd0oLXw","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/1f02cd39-1e2b-420f-b5e9-ec0bb3f0bab4"},{"id":"336cbffe-cbe4-4517-813d-2113e76220bb","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"c467dcc9-eba9-4f70-90b0-76cd8d6bb49f","name":"“Dakiimi / To have land“ by Amber Quail","dates":[1790445600000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791295200000],"start":"2026-09-26T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Hub","address":"1326 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON, M4L 1Z1","lat":43.671781866,"lng":-79.32550473},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Iconography in Western culture has been a central theme in Amber’s visual arts practice. Familiar household archetypes, reimagined through an Indigenous lens, invite viewers to consider alternate truths beyond those presented by the dominant culture.\n\nAn off-reserve member of Alderville First Nation, Amber’s practice is based in Tkaronto and South Algonquin. In Dakiimi / To Have Land, the iconic board game Monopoly serves as both an anchor and a catalyst for reflection on land theft and greed. Through vibrant beadwork, mixed-media works, and paintings, Amber explores land, ownership, power and the enduring impacts of colonialism.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Indigenous"],"presenter":"Riverdale Hub Gallery","image":null,"website":"https://riverdalehub.ca/dakiimi-to-have-land-an-exhibition-by-amber-smith-quail/","tickets":"https://riverdalehub.ca/gallery-event-registration/"},{"id":"936a2c4a-6424-4bab-848e-15e8d0ca984b","name":"“Dakiimi / To have land“ by Amber Quail","dates":[1790445600000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791295200000],"start":"2026-09-26T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Hub","address":"1326 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON, M4L 1Z1","lat":43.671781866,"lng":-79.32550473},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Iconography in Western culture has been a central theme in Amber’s visual arts practice. Familiar household archetypes, reimagined through an Indigenous lens, invite viewers to consider alternate truths beyond those presented by the dominant culture.\n\nAn off-reserve member of Alderville First Nation, Amber’s practice is based in Tkaronto and South Algonquin. In Dakiimi / To Have Land, the iconic board game Monopoly serves as both an anchor and a catalyst for reflection on land theft and greed. Through vibrant beadwork, mixed-media works, and paintings, Amber explores land, ownership, power and the enduring impacts of colonialism.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Indigenous"],"presenter":"Riverdale Hub Gallery","image":null,"website":"https://riverdalehub.ca/dakiimi-to-have-land-an-exhibition-by-amber-smith-quail/","tickets":"https://riverdalehub.ca/gallery-event-registration/"},{"id":"300fe920-a05f-472e-b83c-a9702ace862b","name":"(Sold Out) In Broken Light Artist/Curator Guided Tours at Spadina Museum","dates":[1789682400000,1789851600000,1791057600000,1792101600000],"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679047,"lng":-79.408181},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Limited tickets now sold out","description":"Join artist Ry Van Der Hout and curator Adrien Sun Hall for a special guided tour of the contemporary art exhibition, In Broken Light. Hear from the artist or the curator their own perspectives on the five glass sculptures spanning the four levels of Spadina Museum. \n\nDiscussion includes themes of rupture, repair and how the art speak to the layered history at Spadina Museum.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Y0xDdT14ZflLoRl1dLbL0g","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d3f62fdc-e7d9-4b86-bc72-6cfd0934e234"},{"id":"c2090707-2f17-4117-b619-2bb38feddcf3","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"9bcee260-42ff-48f2-85a2-2e7571946307","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,