26400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"40468aeb-7346-44de-90e1-8074ba578a05","name":"Rebellion Talks: The Rebels' Island Stronghold","dates":[1797102000000],"start":"2026-12-12T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-12T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361228,"lng":-79.36033401},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Learn about the violent aftermath of the Rebellion of 1837. The revolutionaries didn't give up easily. Even after Mackenzie's army was crushed at the Battle of Montgomery's Tavern, the rebels kept fighting. They rallied new supporters as they seized control of an island in the Niagara River, declared it to be the independent Republic of Canada, and launched what became known as the Patriot War. It's a story of bloody battles, revolutionary spies, pirate admirals, and two competing visions for the future of the continent. \n\nFrom October 2026 to April 2027, historian Adam Bunch brings Toronto’s history to life in a series of talks exploring the Upper Canada Rebellion and its lasting impact on the city. From spies and taverns to political reform, rural rebels and the Patriot War, each talk reveals a different story connected to the museum where it takes place.","categories":["History","Museum","Talks"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"lFQ2_yqKrapNAFPmtaErMg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/todmorden-mills/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/737c342d-4dcd-4103-a9b7-5e13d2b40d53"},{"id":"7aecfb0d-dede-48bc-91b8-c6b12680c8de","name":"The Life of a Creature by Nadja Lubiw-Hazard – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1804636800000],"start":"2027-03-09T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-03-09T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":28,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nThrough interconnected stories, The Life of a Creature explores human-animal bonds. Nadja Lubiw-Hazard examines trauma, grief, healing and connection through characters including a veterinarian, a grieving mother and a woman reflecting on Chernobyl's feral dogs, revealing how all living beings are linked. She'll discuss the collection's themes, her approach to writing these bonds and how loss, resilience and transformation shape the stories.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnic alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"y6UlxWQBrC8Mq4YueQCtaQ","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/8e6d46bc-02a0-4756-9f61-5e366042241f"},{"id":"c5000787-60db-4dc8-8aea-efbaf3931480","name":"Piece by Piece: Celebration at East Scarborough Storefront","dates":[1792774800000],"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-23T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes to celebrate the unveiling of a new community mosaic mural created through Piece by Piece, a 10-week program that brought together 15 seniors to learn mosaic art and collaboratively design a mural inspired by the theme of gardens and nature.\n\nCreated through hands-on learning and creative collaboration, the finished artwork will be permanently installed at East Scarborough Storefront. This special gathering recognizes the creativity, dedication, and achievements of the participants while celebrating the completion of the project\n\nThe event is open to all. Brief remarks will take place shortly after the event begins, and light refreshments will be provided. No RSVP is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Celebrations","Family/Children"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"rJM7nh409Jm710FMwogAGA","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"f36bd4d8-c293-4ba1-8109-96abb35fb288","name":"Haunted ROM Tour","dates":[1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000],"start":"2026-10-03T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIn addition to the cost of museum admission ticket.","description":"Discover the haunted history of the Museum as you walk through the very halls where ghosts are said to roam.  \n\nUncover eerie tales, hear ghostly whispers, and explore hidden corners where shadows play tricks on the mind. Don't miss this unique opportunity to explore the supernatural side of art, culture and nature.  ","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"v01BsJ3lGOfA9VI9Eep9fg","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours"},{"id":"a4634175-fa99-4548-a038-08f5eb64a325","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"4ccf28cf-baf3-4193-a423-0243e727c320","name":"Toronto International Festival of Authors 2026","dates":[1793212200000,1793298600000,1793385000000,1793455200000,1793547000000],"start":"2026-10-28T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T10:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Victoria University at the University of Toronto","address":"91 Charles St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1K5","lat":43.666951,"lng":-79.392113},"free":false,"low":15,"high":159,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n5-Day, 2-Day, and Single Day Passes available. Masterclasses require separate registration. Box office also available on site during Festival hours.","description":"Welcome to Canada’s largest and longest-running literary festival.! \n\nThis fall, TIFA 2026 brings the world’s most compelling writers into conversation with one another and with you. Join us for over 100 events with some of the world’s most beloved authors.\n\nFrom author conversations to electric readings and intimate masterclasses, the Festival is where stories cross borders, ideas find each other, and readers discover that literature is very much alive. \n\nThis year’s guestlist includes Barbara Kingsolver, Dave Eggers, Marie Ndiaye, Ann-Marie MacDonald, Andrew Sean Greer, Patrick deWitt, David Szalay, Vivek Shraya, Canisia Lubrin and Téa Mutonji.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"xo8dfCMetGe-UyXKAAVoiA","website":"https://festivalofauthors.ca/festival/?utm_source=eventlisting&utm_medium=eventlisting&utm_campaign=fallfestival","tickets":"https://festivalofauthors.ca/festival/?utm_source=eventlisting&utm_medium=eventlisting&utm_campaign=fallfestival"},{"id":"ed1f1c75-1ed8-4805-99ee-86bf64cefee4","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"e9b6e9ad-9885-412d-a6c1-e0f71ef3511c","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"d36699fe-f70a-4fef-992c-65a1d616050f","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,17