al sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"a40482ee-bae3-479b-bc3c-c0b62e1876ff","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"7fa323dd-f531-4be4-bf7e-fc244c44a66a","name":"Folk(Lore) on the Block: Artist Talk & Community Celebration","dates":[1791129600000],"start":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Boys and Girls Club of East Scarborough","address":"100 Galloway Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1W7","lat":43.757428446,"lng":-79.193338505},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join in celebrating local Kingston-Galloway/Orton Park stories, artists, their artwork, and the community! Youth Community Animators heard from KGO organizations, businesses and community members to inform their pieces. At this artist talk, the Youth Community Animators will share what they learned, created and reflected on after speaking to local KGO community members about their stories. Their art tells stories of where they began and where they want to go. See all of the beautiful art pieces they've created! Refreshments will be provided.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Talks"],"presenter":"Kimberly Lopez and the Ginhawa Collective","image":"cs8WNm00IDAud4KE2PTZbw","website":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/folklore-on-the-block-final-artist-talk-tickets-2002248243395","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/folklore-on-the-block-final-artist-talk-tickets-2002248243395"},{"id":"8dc7c7da-5102-4b43-a3e8-40ebac7912ed","name":"Tales of the Damned: Immersive Theatre Experience","dates":[1792020600000,1792193400000,1792279200000,1792366200000,1792539000000,1792625400000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1792971000000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793403000000,1793498400000,1793579400000],"start":"2026-10-14T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Campbell House Museum","address":"160 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M5H 3H3","lat":43.651058,"lng":-79.387322},"free":false,"low":42.15,"high":54.99,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bone-chilling Halloween tradition!\n\nFrom the creators of the immersive sensations “Tales of the Grotesque” (2023, 2024) and the landmark production of “Tales of the Damned” (2025) comes the revival of Toronto’s favourite gothic horror anthology. \n\nWith fresh characters, familiar tales, and its twisted brand of terror, this site-specific theatrical experience brings literature’s most depraved characters to life and death. \n\nAfter a lady of the night is murdered, a mad doctor strikes a pact with the Devil to raise her from the dead. But all hell breaks loose when he comes face-to-face with her killer at a masquerade. Descend into madness with Victor Frankenstein, Henry Jekyll, and Dorian Gray to discover the results of playing God, and the monstrous repercussions when the Devil comes to collect. \n\nStep into the story as you move through the candlelit Campbell House mansion to confront history's most iconic villains. Ages 14 and up, minors must be accompanied by an adult.","categories":["Live Performances","Museum","Theatre","Halloween"],"presenter":"Campbell House Museum","image":"vywbbYFbH0ca7m8NLmLaow","website":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1","tickets":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1"},{"id":"7dcf448a-e4d8-4815-954d-debe00258d7a","name":"Royal Conservatory Orchestra with conductor James Conlon and Mira Kardan, cello","dates":[1806451200000],"start":"2027-03-30T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-03-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":25,"high":60,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"James Conlon is a rare figure whose work has defined and enriched the classical music traditions of the US and Europe for over 50 years. \n\nSince his New York Philharmonic debut in 1974, he has led virtually every major American and European symphony orchestra and has conducted at most of the world’s most prestigious opera houses. Conlon has been Music Director of the Los Angeles Opera for 20 years, where he has led more operas (over 500 performances of more than 70 works), more than any other conductor in the company’s 40-year history. \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"yXicLxt0OuaFTOsdm8FVzw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/royal-conservatory-orchestra-with-conductor-james-conlon","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/431601"},{"id":"06beb8d6-be14-4bc3-96e2-b4f5d8e2c620","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,