le directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"8ebc2a53-b19c-4c8f-8306-4be3790a795e","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"e15a1194-4546-42bd-998c-b167aa031bd5","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"636e33aa-9e84-4dc6-8806-5bda4aab0e3b","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"f43e0141-9816-48c4-be96-8c099b2e2cff","name":"Violins Unbound","dates":[1793665800000],"start":"2026-11-02T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-02T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Hugh's Room","address":"296 Broadview Ave, Toronto, ON, M4M 2G7","lat":43.663844723,"lng":-79.352266217},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Few instruments can match the violin’s extraordinary combination of brilliance, agility and expressive power. \n\nThis Encounters event will showcase all that the violin can offer, featuring violinists Judith Fliedl, visiting from Austria on a Canadian tour and Toronto-based violinist Roan Ma, performing a world premiere for violin duet by André Ristic, commissioned by Soundstreams. \n\nThe program will also include works by John Beckwith, Chris Paul Harman, Parisa Sabet, and Ana Sokolović. \n\nA discussion and audience QnA with Fliedl and Ma will follow the performance.  \n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"4C6NAOI_jOx_8HM2TKDqVQ","website":"https://soundstreams.ca/events/td-encounters-violins-unbound-2/","tickets":"https://soundstreams.ca/events/td-encounters-violins-unbound-2/"},{"id":"58248264-fc2b-48f9-a040-7a4cdab5cbad","name":"VIEWS: KGO Made Mural Unveiling","dates":[1792864800000],"start":"2026-10-24T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Heron Park Community Recreation Centre","address":"292 Manse Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1E 3V4","lat":43.768855609,"lng":-79.176938353},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"VIEWS: KGO Made is a youth-led community arts initiative engaging youth from the Kingston-Galloway/Orton Park (KGO) community in the creation of a collaborative mural at Heron Park Community Centre. The mural project builds on themes, stories, and perspectives identified through previous community consultation and engagement, translating the voices and experiences of KGO residents into a meaningful visual artwork.\n\nJoin the youth artists as they celebrate their hard work and creativity while giving back to and representing one of Scarborough’s most vibrant and important neighbourhoods\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Celebrations","Family/Children"],"presenter":null,"image":"wSD8qeh5z4NqYHgXh_X26g","website":"https://www.nextgenerationarts.ca/events","tickets":null},{"id":"98e627e0-883b-4d78-b2a6-060a6033256e","name":"Art Toronto 2026","dates":[1793304000000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000],"start":"2026-10-29T16:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 2W6","lat":43.644049656,"lng":-79.386720757},"free":false,"low":25,"high":440,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Canada’s leading international fair for modern and contemporary art will bring together 105 galleries, organizations and cultural institutions from across Canada, the United States, Latin America and Europe.\n\nEnjoy thousands of works by emerging and established artists across painting, sculpture, photography, textiles, installation and new media.\n\nHighlights include the return of Arte Sur, featuring 11 galleries from Mexico, Central America and South America, as well as solo presentations dedicated to individual artists and new programming for emerging collectors. \n\nNearly one-third of participating galleries will present work by Indigenous artists. \n\nVisitors can also take part in curator-led tours, Platform Talks and educational programming designed to make collecting more accessible.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"yjzdEkBXJtQkDio5WDHxpQ","website":"https://arttoronto.ca/home/","tickets":"https://arttoronto.ca/home/tickets/?gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=22937691808&gbraid=0AAAABAIViEuF591mb7ytL22VlsqQ59F77&gclid=CjwKCAjwq8PVBhAKEiwA2i3SHfXK2uu4R_jwkDAZLzJTTvotY6tTc5gybgEiTsGq5YvEuZT1MkbmOhoC1hYQAvD_BwE"},{"id":"da3615de-284e-4c48-a85a-2e12433d5245","name":"Nuit Talk: Ever Sick with SJ Okemow","dates":[1791084600000],"start":"2026-10-03T23:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T23:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity Square Labyrinth","address":"24 Trinity Sq, Toronto","lat":43.654216306,"lng":-79.381840514},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"SJ Okemow creates a space for all abilities to dance and heal their bodies and souls inspire. Hear SJ speak about her creative process in developing this new media animation installation. \n\nThe Nuit Talks program includes pop-up artist talks scheduled throughout the night, connecting attendees directly to the artists and deepening their understanding and appreciation of art. Many artists are also in attendance at their projects and able to speak to the public about their work.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"Q11dE4QGiOjvQeEfXx6s2A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/","tickets":null},{"id":"92d4bfdd-2d97-4523-bbfa-432e1885f7f0","name":"Tenfold: 10 year anniversary exhibition","dates":[1791496800000,1791576000000,1791651600000],"start":"2026-10-08T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Remote Gallery","address":"568 Richmond St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 1Y9","lat":43.647051565,"lng":-79.401506964},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"We celebrate ten years of artistic practice, collaboration, and community. \n\nTo mark this milestone, artists from the studios were invited to bring their work together in a collective exhibition. \n\nThe title \"Tenfold\" speaks both to this ten-year journey and to the many ways creativity expands when developed collectively. \n\nWhile each artist explores distinct questions through their own techniques and visual language, Tenfold highlights the dialogues, affinities, and contrasts that emerge between their practices. \nIndividual voices remain visible, while their hared experiences reveal the rich sense of exchange fostered within the Akin studio community.\n\nParticipating artists include Anne Kobayashi, Barbara Bailey, Bernadette Peets, Bettina Westwood, Carrie Fisher, Eli Moser, Hamid Mohammadi, Loren Kaplan, Mark Buck, Miles Ingrassia, MP Guillot, Robert Simoni, Shayla Bond, Tatjana Reithofer and Veronica Zaretski.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Celebrations"],"presenter":"Akin Dupont Studios","image":null,"website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/tenfold-akin-duponts-10-year-anniversary-exhibition-tickets-2001630172729","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/tenfold-akin-duponts-10-year-anniversary-exhibition-tickets-2001630172729"},{"id":"d121a397-405b-4a8b-afcf-53d2f5ae6a30","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"22c56aa1-5e27-417d-832f-09f2a18ba06f","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"9e4cf431-7e3e-4d46-b2d7-6b2886c06c2c","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800