tive impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"1dd8c14b-9039-45c0-a0e2-1f077d71f295","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"ef6b9c67-10b1-420c-b3b7-fe4d867134d6","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"9c7a1328-baad-435a-bddd-e41d1138ee0e","name":"From Earth to Brick: A Hands-On Rammed Earth Workshop (SOLD OUT)","dates":[1791048600000],"start":"2026-10-03T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T13:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curious about sustainable building materials? Or just want to get your hands dirty?  \n \nOn October 3, join Waterfront Toronto, Arcana Materials Co and Aerecura Sustainable Builders for a hands-on, family-friendly workshop exploring rammed earth, a low-carbon building method that compresses layers of natural materials such as soil, sand, recycled bricks and clay to create strong, long-lasting structures.\n \nDuring the workshop, participants will learn the basics of rammed earth construction while crafting their own brick. Whether you're interested in sustainability, architecture, or learning a new technique for small scale DIY seating and landscape projects, or simply trying something new, this workshop offers a fun introduction to an innovative and sustainable building technique.\n \nAfter each of the workshops, participants are invited to join a free guided tour of Kara Hamilton's artwork, Delicate Matter  (for the birds), located along the eastern section of the Lassonde Art Trail. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"oc0tIiYGhH6uSGKFyKSDMw","website":"https://www.waterfrontoronto.ca/events/earth-brick-hands-rammed-earth-workshop-october-3-2026","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/from-earth-to-brick-a-hands-on-rammed-earth-workshop-tickets-2000982311960?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"a9b84d91-23d3-4e47-9d91-a44b04616426","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"b35856de-5bab-45df-a060-931f2e0398a8","name":"Mozart's Spring Calla Lilies","dates":[1807313400000],"start":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-09T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity- St. Paul's Centre","address":"427 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1X7","lat":43.66603939,"lng":-79.405707818},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate spring in the most musical way possible two stellar soloists, five gorgeous works, and an evening that moves from Bach to Mozart with plenty of drama and beauty along the way.\n\nOboist Caitlin Broms-Jacobs, praised for her \"gorgeous singing tone\" and principal oboist of the Manitoba Chamber Orchestra, opens with Bach's Concerto for Oboe in D Minor and Mozetich's Calla Lilies, a luminous meditation on fleeting beauty. Violinist Tina Sievers, winner of the 2025 Sinfonia Toronto Concerto Competition and a soloist who has performed with the Toronto Symphony Orchestra, brings Schubert's carefree Rondo in A Major and the dazzling fireworks of Sarasate's Zigeunerweisen (Gypsy Airs). \n\nThe evening closes with Maestro Nurhan Arman's own orchestral arrangement of Mozart's cheerful \"Spring\" String Quartet.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Sinfonia Toronto","image":"1CMwhcYoe-syvBamCzj2bw","website":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/mozarts-spring","tickets":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/mozarts-spring"},{"id":"6394d78a-fcd1-4570-9357-23d1af271d21","name":"Coffee City: Canada's Coffee Culture Festival","dates":[1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000],"start":"2026-10-16T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Design Exchange","address":"234 Bay St., Toronto, ON M5K 1B2","lat":43.647828,"lng":-79.380055},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A whole city of coffee. Free to explore.\n\nStep into Coffee City, a coffee capital built just for one weekend, filling three floors of Design Exchange. You're not just visiting. You're a citizen here.\n\nWander through where coffee actually lives: cozy home setups, real café counters, even an outdoor coffee corner. Grab a cup. Take photos at the city's landmarks. And right at the city's center: watch Canada's best baristas battle it out live at the Canadian National Latte Art Championship, which will choose the champion to represent Canada on the world stage, running all three days, right in front of you.\n\nEnjoy hands-on experiences (each ticketed separately) like latte art, coffee bean samples, mix-your-own-drink and more!\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/canadas-coffee-culture-festival-coffee-city-tickets-2001243381827","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/canadas-coffee-culture-festival-coffee-city-tickets-2001243381827"},{"id":"317017bb-ff0f-4f6e-927b-c39d9323d5a3","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Recommended for ages 12 and up. Youth 12-16 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAll ticket sales are non-refundable. Tickets are transferable.","description":"Join us for a chilling tour at Colborne Lodge in High Park. Visit the gravesite of John and Jemima Howard. Delve deeply into ideas about death and the afterlife from the 1800s and hear true tales of paranormal activities. Decide for yourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"208248c6-f5fa-4bce-ab8a-3861c2a188b6","name":"Cigar Club: 10-Year Anniversary","dates":[1794099600000],"start":"2026-11-07T20:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-07T20:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Horseshoe Tavern","address":"370 Queen St W, Toronto, ON M5V 2A2","lat":43.64919,"lng":-79.395326},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto music veterans join the Cigar Club as they hit the stage to celebrate this milestone!\n\nFeaturing Fortunate Losers and The Young Scones. \n\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"lYcE4mIt7uqG6t5vTX-TBg","website":"https://www.tixr.com/groups/horseshoetavern/events/cigar-club-10-year-anniversary-207130","tickets":"https://www.tixr.com/groups/horseshoetavern/events/cigar-club-10-year-anniversary-207130"},{"id":"28af1faa-7909-4b9b-a7e7-0bc32efe4df3","name":"Rebirth: The Quiet Becoming Installation at Fort York","dates":[1785938400000,1786024800000,1786111200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786543200000,1786629600000,1786716000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787148000000,1787234400000,1787320800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1787752800000,1787839200000,1787925600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788357600000,1788444000000,1788530400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000],"start":"2026-08-05T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864096,"lng":-79.406314887},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bold new outdoor installation on the Gardiner Expressway beside Fort York Visitor Centre. Created by artists Delali Cofie and Yuma Dean Hester, it reimagines the site’s layered histories through contemporary art. An accompanying exhibition inside the Visitor Centre deepens the experience, inviting visitors to encounter the Fort as a living cultural landscape shaped by reflection, dialogue and collaboration.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"_QHlUAQMVyNc88AaSDfQ8A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":null},{"id":"69b5d611-c307-4667-9d5a-a2354a405516","name":"Roots & Belonging: Black History Nature Walk & Museum Experience","dates":[1791655200000],"start":"2026-10-10T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640348,"lng":-79.459963},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience 19th-century history and Black Canadian storytelling on an immersive guided tour of High Park. Tour Colborne Lodge, re-examine local history, engage with nature and participate in meaningful storytelling led by Black Canadian Hikers. Connect with fellow community members in an inclusive, welcoming space for Black communities, museum visitors and allies.\n\nSpots are limited for this event. Please arrive early to ensure your place. First come, first served.","categories":["Museum","Talks","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"hyVnji1a8cTtv_EuD3gHNA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":null},{"id":"f188e325-500f-48e5-b56e-0cf50f500136","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on yo