d inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"4c12f4fa-667b-4699-8b26-5c9e9b8e2315","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"7f1855c3-8b4a-4b1f-bdab-d48f0085c790","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at East Scarborough Storefront","dates":[1789578000000,1789750800000,1790182800000,1790355600000,1790787600000,1790960400000,1791392400000,1791565200000,1791997200000,1792170000000],"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"F4gQpCvBNPCjggJ5mJPA0g","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/"},{"id":"de92cf86-8b36-4793-8882-cbd156115f80","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"914b707d-4376-437a-96b6-026ea2ae4ee2","name":"Pablo Ziegler Quintet with Roberta Gambarini: Blues Porteño","dates":[1803844800000],"start":"2027-02-28T15:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T15:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":50,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Astor Piazzolla’s Grammy Award‑winning pianist and his quintet are joined by the gifted Italian jazz vocalist for a unique collaboration.\n\nFor decades, Buenos Aires-born pianist, composer, and arranger Pablo Ziegler has been one of the most important figures in Argentine new tango, the vibrant musical hybrid of classic tango, American jazz, and European art music. \n\nThree-time Grammy Award nominated vocalist Roberta Gambarini burst on the world’s jazz scene in 1998, when she became one of the runners-up in the Thelonious Monk Jazz Vocal Competition.\n\nAfter the concert, enjoy a beverage and more music at the Postlude Performance featuring a local emerging artist in the Leslie and Anna Dan Galleria. \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"c8DIw5w1uzMd_MQZcaXoAQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/pablo-ziegler-quintet-with-roberta-gambarini-blues-porteno-447401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/447401"},{"id":"75d4e85e-faf8-4f6e-8b8b-2bccfd6587be","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"f398d11b-30e9-4098-a3b3-638bcc8b7cf3","name":"Flapper?! I Hardly Know Her Drag Brunch","dates":[1791129600000],"start":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"The Alpine","address":"2872 Dundas St W, Toronto, ON, M6P 1Y8","lat":43.665533679,"lng":-79.465249569},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Get into the swing of things! \n\nWe’re stepping back a hundred-ish years for a little glitz, glamour, debauchery, and all that jazz. Dust off your pearls and come party with the girls for a Drag brunch like no other.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"5vT6-VeH7wBcsAD_UVNoCg","website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999958710340","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999958710340"},{"id":"1c435401-707e-4213-9141-7ebbe3644bfe","name":"Summer Explorations","dates":[1790528400000,1791133200000],"start":"2026-09-27T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Camera Club ","address":"587 Mount Pleasant Rd, Toronto, ON, M4S 2M5","lat":43.703764696,"lng":-79.387999462},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover fresh perspectives in an exhibition showcasing the creative journeys our members pursued over the past summer. \n\nThrough new equipment, innovative processing methods, and experimental techniques, each photographer has found new ways to expand their artistic practice.\n\nTogether, these works celebrate curiosity, creative growth and the power of photography to inspire others to explore their own vision.\n\n ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"04S_1UdIpiKwlxIFQNyxJg","website":"https://torontocameraclub.com/program/powell-gallery","tickets":null},{"id":"a14c0b83-c837-4aef-8e2d-abfc732ed1df","name":"Lantern Tours at Montgomery's Inn: Beyond Mourning","dates":[1792879200000,1792886400000,1792965600000,1792972800000,1793311200000,1793318400000,1793397600000,1793404800000],"start":"2026-10-24T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, uncover eerie tales about the past inhabitants of the Inn and the Old Town of Islington. Journey from the dimly lit historic house to the Islington burial ground, learn about Victorian death practices, and hear new stories connecting to Toronto’s past. \n\nContent warning: Topics include illness, death and related subjects.\nRecommended for ages 14 and up. Anyone under 17 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"OGMQ_a1JowZ9TDZayyn_6Q","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aae32edb-e8f5-4760-b053-81cb44cc2186"},{"id":"b5ed8d80-ddfc-4248-82a9-b1ebd5b0c990","name":"Lantern Tours at Montgomery's Inn: Beyond Mourning","dates":[1792879200000,1792886400000,1792965600000,1792972800000,1793311200000,1793318400000,1793397600000,1793404800000],"start":"2026-10-24T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, uncover eerie tales about the past inhabitants of the Inn and the Old Town of Islington. Journey from the dimly lit historic house to the Islington burial ground, learn about Victorian death practices, and hear new stories connecting to Toronto’s past. \n\nContent warning: Topics include illness, death and related subjects.\nRecommended for ages 14 and up. Anyone under 17 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"OGMQ_a1JowZ9TDZayyn_6Q","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aae32edb-e8f5-4760-b053-81cb44cc2186"},{"id":"bfbb3fb7-0333-4354-9479-c4cefdea734b","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"258cdea6-b3df-45ee-b974-df7d882a5e7d","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"ab5238db-040f-46a7-959f-ff5b51f947b1","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"5e6e3bce-437b-4809-babc-763a5bb0804d","name":"Places That Stayed: Celebratory Event","dates":[1792098000000],"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit launch at East Scarborough Storefront (ESS). Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the outdoor exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces in Kingston-Galloway/Orton Park (KGO) that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Stroll along the community garden fence and explore the photographs, which offer a youth perspective on the KGO community. Join the celebration at ESS for refreshments before a short photo walk through the Highland Creek Ravine. The exhibit will remain on display outdoors until November 30.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Celebrations"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"KrwTX3fL8PE2q51l8930NQ","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"42e0f7b8-dd9d-42a4-af03-6c8096373b7e","name":"Lantern Tours at Montgomery's Inn: Beyond Mourning","dates":[1792879200000,1792886400000,1792965600000,1792972800000,1793311200000,1793318400000,1793397600000,1793404800000],"start":"2026-10-24T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, uncover eerie tales about the past inhabitants of the Inn and the Old Town of Islington. Journey from the dimly lit historic house to the Islington burial ground, learn about Victorian death practices, and hear new stories connecting to Toronto’s past. \n\nContent warning: Topics include illness, death and related subjects.\nRecommended for ages 14 and up. Anyone under 17 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"OGMQ_a1JowZ9TDZayyn_6Q","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aae32edb-e8f5-4760-b053-81cb44cc2186"},{"id":"37acef64-0f88-4a46-877b-0f8c07ce1529","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980