n under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"5a2c90de-1780-46bd-8f05-6097ef7dbd72","name":"Autumn Nature Tour at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1792245600000],"start":"2026-10-17T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Charles Bruce-Thompson and Lynn Short of the Toronto Field Naturalists for a guided walk through Biidaasige Park.\n\nLearn about the history of the area and the creation of the new river mouth and park. There will be opportunities to observe visiting wildlife – including migratory birds – that have been attracted to this new natural area on the waterfront of Toronto.\n\nMeeting spot: Old Fire Hall 30 Community Recreation Centre, 51 Commissioners St.\n\nBe prepared:\n\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather.\nComfortable, close-toed shoes are highly recommended.\nBring a water bottle and snacks, if needed.","categories":["Environmental","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"J2YQ-VZsyLx5GrUkK6YHuw","website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/autumn-nature-tour-at-biidaasige-park-tickets-2002150570252","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/autumn-nature-tour-at-biidaasige-park-tickets-2002150570252"},{"id":"14801226-e51f-44d8-b173-a7894da5fdcf","name":"A Haunting on the Hill? Halloween at Spadina","dates":[1792794600000,1792881000000,1793399400000],"start":"2026-10-23T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":false,"low":30,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Calling all brave detectives! The Austin family have fled their Spadina mansion in the dead of the night due to the unexplained and uncanny disturbances that have been taking place in their ancestral home after nightfall.  Investigate this bizarre case: are these the makings of a disgruntled staff? A scorned stranger? Innocent pranks of witty neighbours? Or perhaps, the very phenomenon we fear when things go bump in the night... Follow the clues, solve the riddles, and help to decipher this most curious case.\n\nDisclaimer: This event is designed around a fictional scenario of real-life people. Event includes a talk by Ann McDougall, author of A Ghost In the Room. Topics include paranormal, occult, and death. The activities will involve puzzle-solving, unscrambling, some strong scents, light effects. The museum will be in low-light conditions and require guests to navigate through narrow pathways. For ages 13+.","categories":["History","Museum","Talks","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"gUDKLMZPNIIrnLM377mJuQ","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/44a643b9-ae16-4669-ba0f-1d54db9c62be"},{"id":"ffe48d33-356a-4474-a81c-1dbcfc9f1848","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"d0fc925c-8c76-44d4-8136-cdf0bf66d99e","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,179925