 been taking place in their ancestral home after nightfall.  Investigate this bizarre case: are these the makings of a disgruntled staff? A scorned stranger? Innocent pranks of witty neighbours? Or perhaps, the very phenomenon we fear when things go bump in the night... Follow the clues, solve the riddles, and help to decipher this most curious case.\n\nDisclaimer: This event is designed around a fictional scenario of real-life people. Event includes a talk by Ann McDougall, author of A Ghost In the Room. Topics include paranormal, occult, and death. The activities will involve puzzle-solving, unscrambling, some strong scents, light effects. The museum will be in low-light conditions and require guests to navigate through narrow pathways. For ages 13+.","categories":["History","Museum","Talks","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"gUDKLMZPNIIrnLM377mJuQ","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/44a643b9-ae16-4669-ba0f-1d54db9c62be"},{"id":"e1ded991-2f72-4be6-99d8-d7cbf1f02451","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"c33078a2-7304-4f84-953d-3fb7f8dc19ce","name":"Coffee City: Canada's Coffee Culture Festival","dates":[1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000],"start":"2026-10-16T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Design Exchange","address":"234 Bay St., Toronto, ON M5K 1B2","lat":43.647828,"lng":-79.380055},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A whole city of coffee. Free to explore.\n\nStep into Coffee City, a coffee capital built just for one weekend, filling three floors of Design Exchange. You're not just visiting. You're a citizen here.\n\nWander through where coffee actually lives: cozy home setups, real café counters, even an outdoor coffee corner. Grab a cup. Take photos at the city's landmarks. And right at the city's center: watch Canada's best baristas battle it out live at the Canadian National Latte Art Championship, which will choose the champion to represent Canada on the world stage, running all three days, right in front of you.\n\nEnjoy hands-on experiences (each ticketed separately) like latte art, coffee bean samples, mix-your-own-drink and more!\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/canadas-coffee-culture-festival-coffee-city-tickets-2001243381827","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/canadas-coffee-culture-festival-coffee-city-tickets-2001243381827"},{"id":"3b6f63e7-4e79-4785-985f-9cd7896dd459","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"926236d3-1f84-4a70-a17e-3973eef9aee9","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"ad065dd9-5622-4813-b974-54b17bb19b0f","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"5c59605c-1759-41e9-8448-7dbc8ad33f43","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"9867a013-8d47-4915-a06c-897ef59a6cb7","name":"Summer Explorations","dates":[1790528400000,1791133200000],"start":"2026-09-27T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Camera Club ","address":"587 Mount Pleasant Rd, Toronto, ON, M4S 2M5","lat":43.703764696,"lng":-79.387999462},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover fresh perspectives in an exhibition showcasing the creative journeys our members pursued over the past summer. \n\nThrough new equipment, innovative processing methods, and experimental techniques, each photographer has found new ways to expand their artistic practice.\n\nTogether, these works celebrate curiosity, creative growth and the power of photography to inspire others to explore their own vision.\n\n ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"04S_1UdIpiKwlxIFQNyxJg","website":"https://torontocameraclub.com/program/powell-gallery","tickets":null},{"id":"3c747489-21b7-41e2-b342-206f2ec93e6e","name":"QueerForestClub hikes the Ravine (With Z from Queer Ecology)","dates":[1792249200000],"start":"2026-10-17T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Nordheimer Ravine","address":"","lat":43.683618,"lng":-79.414913},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations are always welcome on our zeffy!","description":"QueerForestClub will be hiking the ravine and exploring the city together. This event will have two parts. First, we will be led on a walk while Z from QueerEcology teaches us about how Queer much of our environment is. Then, they will introduce the collaborative zine project they have been working on. In the second part of the event, participants will get the chance to create art and discuss the power of zine-making and storytelling.","categories":["Environmental","2SLGBTQ+","Run/Walk"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":null,"tickets":"https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/qfc-34-oct-17-nordheimer-ravine"},{"id":"217e4f96-d07f-42cc-bc97-6288b1906672","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritag