llDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"280226ee-08c9-4a30-b627-4450dbece4cb","name":"Coffee City: Canada's Coffee Culture Festival","dates":[1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000],"start":"2026-10-16T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Design Exchange","address":"234 Bay St., Toronto, ON M5K 1B2","lat":43.647828,"lng":-79.380055},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A whole city of coffee. Free to explore.\n\nStep into Coffee City, a coffee capital built just for one weekend, filling three floors of Design Exchange. You're not just visiting. You're a citizen here.\n\nWander through where coffee actually lives: cozy home setups, real café counters, even an outdoor coffee corner. Grab a cup. Take photos at the city's landmarks. And right at the city's center: watch Canada's best baristas battle it out live at the Canadian National Latte Art Championship, which will choose the champion to represent Canada on the world stage, running all three days, right in front of you.\n\nEnjoy hands-on experiences (each ticketed separately) like latte art, coffee bean samples, mix-your-own-drink and more!\n","categories":["Cultural","Food/Culinary"],"presenter":null