is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"fce1d066-ba82-42ce-941a-a03bec70b851","name":"Yuja Wang, piano","dates":[1806865200000,1806883200000],"start":"2027-04-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":85,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Pianist Yuja Wang is widely recognised as one of the most important artists of her generation, hailed for her supreme musicianship, insightful interpretations, and charismatic stage presence.\n\nHer work has been honoured with many accolades and prizes, including a Grammy Award (Best Classical Instrumental Solo) for her 2023 album The American Project. She makes her sixth appearance in Koerner Hall.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"wMY-ke7ciZLDiB7eJfx5SQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/"},{"id":"f3e6817a-fa4b-4981-8447-bea1aa421119","name":"The Glenn Gould School New Music Ensemble: Path of Uneven Stones A Celebration of Linda Catlin Smith","dates":[1807657200000],"start":"2027-04-13T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-13T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Temerty Theatre","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Free tickets available starting from 10 a.m. on Tuesday April 6, 2027.\n","description":"Curated by Brian Current, this concert celebrates Linda Catlin Smith’s milestone birthday with luminous works performed by Glenn Gould School students.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/ggs-new-music-ensemble-path-of-uneven-stones-453201","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/453201"},{"id":"8713cbfd-f2eb-45b0-ae10-33a3fba8426f","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","dates":[1789565400000,1789738200000,1790170200000,1790343000000,1790775000000,1790947800000,1791379800000,1791552600000,1791984600000,1792157400000],"start":"2026-09-16T09:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T09:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":[