iers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"c92a5c6a-f186-4549-a43f-4eef6bdf0f9b","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"48cd8e2a-7c86-47ed-aff4-d92206855dc1","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"e2b5006d-33b7-459e-9db9-ec637eb2980a","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"66a8e16d-9843-42b4-8360-d6edb949ef06","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"1da263bf-cd23-40df-aea3-9a8ae234d5fc","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"1e233a68-dffe-4ec3-85c3-b60b69f53a19","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"8aefc590-0695-4ccc-9801-e7a7fba3567c","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"b208acd3-4ae1-452f-ba90-6d914e376075","name":"Mayumi Seiler, violin, Min‑Jeong Koh, viola and Daniel Hamin Go, cello","dates":[1799607600000],"start":"2027-01-10T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-10T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667878,"lng":-79.3962},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrated RCM faculty members and a rising star alumnus unite for an exquisite trio recital of works by Beethoven, Ernő Dohnányi and a new commission by Vancouver-based Stefan Hintersteininger.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"-WyzV0tXUvrSanr2vBiytA","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/mayumi-seiler-violin-min-jeong-koh-violin-and-daniel-hamin-go-cello-449001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/449001"},{"id":"6dfc1487-d2b7-42b1-871e-ad902cb65549","name":"“Dakiimi / To have land“ by Amber Quail","dates":[1790445600000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791295200000],"start":"2026-09-26T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Hub","address":"1326 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON, M4L 1Z1","lat":43.671781866,"lng":-79.32550473},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Iconography in Western culture has been a central theme in Amber’s visual arts practice. Familiar household archetypes, reimagined through an Indigenous lens, invite viewers to consider alternate truths beyond those presented by the dominant culture.\n\nAn off-reserve member of Alderville First Nation, Amber’s practice is based in Tkaronto and South Algonquin. In Dakiimi / To Have Land, the iconic board game Monopoly serves as both an anchor and a catalyst for reflection on land theft and greed. Through vibrant beadwork, mixed-media works, and paintings, Amber explores land, ownership, power and the enduring impacts of colonialism.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Indigenous"],"presenter":"Riverdale Hub Gallery","image":null,"website":"https://riverdalehub.ca/dakiimi-to-have-land-an-exhibition-by-amber-smith-quail/","tickets":"https://riverdalehub.ca/gallery-event-registration/"},{"id":"12d69066-5335-469d-9fa0-21e7ca65a7a8","name":"“Dakiimi / To have land“ by Amber Quail","dates":[1790445600000,1790690400000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791295200000],"start":"2026-09-26T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-06T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Hub","address":"1326 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON, M4L 1Z1","lat":43.671781866,"lng":-79.32550473},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Iconography in Western culture has been a central theme in Amber’s visual arts practice. Familiar household archetypes, reimagined through an Indigenous lens, invite viewers to consider alternate truths beyond those presented by the dominant culture.\n\nAn off-reserve member of Alderville First Nation, Amber’s practice is based in Tkaronto and South Algonquin. In Dakiimi / To Have Land, the iconic board game Monopoly serves as both an anchor and a catalyst for reflection on land theft and greed. Through vibrant beadwork, mixed-media works, and paintings, Amber explores land, ownership, power and the enduring impacts of colonialism.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Indigenous"],"presenter":"Riverdale Hub Gallery","image":null,"website":"https://riverdalehub.ca/dakiimi-to-have-land-an-exhibition-by-amber-smith-quail/","tickets":"https://riverdalehub.ca/gallery-event-registration/"},{"id":"89d9eb13-09e8-4bd4-a5c9-6316dbf532df","name":"By the Lake Book Club – 3-Event Package (2027)","dates":[1820962800000],"start":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":55,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nEnjoy the final three By the Lake Book Club events of 2027 for just $55. Join Humber Polytechnic alumni as they dive into conversation with leading Canadian authors. This package features Tyler Pennock, Gillian Deacon and Carrianne Leung. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. \n\nThe signature series features six Tuesday-night events, between February and December. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation.\n\nTyler Pennock - September 14, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nGillian Deacon - October 5, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nCarrianne Leung - December 7, 2027 at 7 p.m.\n\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#multipacks/f89d2f6f-5509-40a1-b58c-a5d199cbe683"},{"id":"6215af2c-f8ff-470b-ab18-0ce7b811e155","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"b0b91687-1fb4-4d4d-8d6c-918fde368204","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"54a0bcc8-bcdf-43f7-85ae-1b7869a196c5","name":"Tales of the Damned: Immersive Theatre Experience","dates":[1792020600000,1792193400000,1792279200000,1792366200000,1792539000000,1792625400000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1792971000000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793403000000,1793498400000,1793579400000],"start":"2026-10-14T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Campbell House Museum","address":"160 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M5H 3H3","lat":43.651058,"lng":-79.387322},"free":false,"low":42.15,"high":54.99,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bone-chilling Halloween tradition!\n\nFrom the creators of the immersive sensations “Tales of the Grotesque” (2023, 2024) and the landmark production of “Tales of the Damned” (2025) comes the revival of Toronto’s favourite gothic horror anthology. \n\nWith fresh characters, familiar tales, and its twisted brand of terror, this site-specific theatrical experience brings literature’s most depraved characters to life and death. \n\nAfter a lady of the night is murdered, a mad doctor strikes a pact with the Devil to raise her from the dead. But all hell breaks loose when he comes face-to-face with her killer at a masquerade. Descend into madness with Victor Frankenstein, Henry Jekyll, and Dorian Gray to discover the results of playing God, and the monstrous repercussions when the Devil comes to collect. \n\nStep into the story as you move through the candlelit Campbell House mansion to confront history's most iconic villains. Ages 14 and up, minors must be accompanied by an adult.","categories":["Live Performances","Museum","Theatre","Halloween"],"presenter":"Campbell House Museum","image":"vywbbYFbH0ca7m8NLmLaow","website":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1","tickets":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1"},{"id":"354f9032-e926-4970-acae-929fb23dd513","name":"Tales of the Damned: Immersive Theatre Experience","dates":[1792020600000,1792193400000,1792279200000,1792366200000,1792539000000,1792625400000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1792971000000,1793143800000,1793230200000,1793403000000,1793498400000,1793579400000],"start":"2026-10-14T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Campbell House Museum","address":"160 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M5H 3H3","lat":43.651058,"lng":-79.387322},"free":false,"low":42.15,"high":54.99,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bone-chilling Halloween tradition!\n\nFrom the creators of the immersive sensations “Tales of the Grotesque” (2023, 2024) and the landmark production of “Tales of the Damned” (2025) comes the revival of Toronto’s favourite gothic horror anthology. \n\nWith fresh characters, familiar tales, and its twisted brand of terror, this site-specific theatrical experience brings literature’s most depraved characters to life and death. \n\nAfter a lady of the night is murdered, a mad doctor strikes a pact with the Devil to raise her from the dead. But all hell breaks loose when he comes face-to-face with her killer at a masquerade. Descend into madness with Victor Frankenstein, Henry Jekyll, and Dorian Gray to discover the results of playing God, and the monstrous repercussions when the Devil comes to collect. \n\nStep into the story as you move through the candlelit Campbell House mansion to confront history's most iconic villains. Ages 14 and up, minors must be accompanied by an adult.","categories":["Live Performances","Museum","Theatre","Halloween"],"presenter":"Campbell House Museum","image":"vywbbYFbH0ca7m8NLmLaow","website":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1","tickets":"https://www.whitemillstheatreco.com/upcoming-events-1"},{"id":"37da3214-191e-445e-a489-d03fbd307d7d","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000