e":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"i2SMsQnvkRtaYNfLbdOTrw","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-cedarridge/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-cedarridge/"},{"id":"e2cb21c0-e136-4750-99b9-2354dcb4edde","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"d4459462-8fb6-4e9a-92f1-b09210551cd5","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"538698ba-a600-47de-a31c-56a3ec06f6d2","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"2eeebbd0-ee34-4486-b010-9ac581736f8d","name":"Crothers Woods Trail Stewardship Event","dates":[1792332000000],"start":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Crothers Woods","address":"200 Pottery Rd, East York","lat":43.68933986,"lng":-79.362775138},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nThis event is not suitable for small children or large groups. All attendees must register. Email us to register.","description":"Help steward, repair and improve the natural surface trails at Crothers Woods. \n\nPlease note, there are no washroom facilities on site. Event site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"51pUu7Wc878qRW2n7r34-g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/ge\\t-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"f1cdea5f-2a98-4ff0-bc8e-b82f231ffddf","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"014cd60b-b0ce-4742-af1f-3b1e13f6e84b","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"c19caa5f-4f6f-4c5b-b8a4-20c6656b5b28","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"0f0d95eb-71b6-483f-8151-c550e333bac0","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at East Scarborough Storefront","dates":[1789578000000,1789750800000,1790182800000,1790355600000,1790787600000,1790960400000,1791392400000,1791565200000,1791997200000,1792170000000],"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"F4gQpCvBNPCjggJ5mJPA0g","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/"},{"id":"b4dd012a-74d7-4bb8-925b-2ced3e1dc2f6","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"9bf13e52-c1b2-4494-a1d9-ee5b66fd2932","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"827af6e9-fae1-4e7e-970b-48d173bbce1e","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000