ices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"599a9102-fd2c-4aab-bad1-03e69436a8b7","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"a67daa04-012c-4bb4-914e-30ebbd6f0ab2","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"eb7784e6-34bd-4b79-9fe9-dfdaa2b59ff7","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"6f07372d-94a7-4b20-b59d-3e07fb426c60","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,17