00,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"e52bc275-3d87-4ddd-972b-1fa9c77b75e4","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"3044ea2e-3d54-4129-9a80-0d625b7418f2","name":"Lantern Tours at Montgomery's Inn: Beyond Mourning","dates":[1792879200000,1792886400000,1792965600000,1792972800000,1793311200000,1793318400000,1793397600000,1793404800000],"start":"2026-10-24T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, uncover eerie tales about the past inhabitants of the Inn and the Old Town of Islington. Journey from the dimly lit historic house to the Islington burial ground, learn about Victorian death practices, and hear new stories connecting to Toronto’s past. \n\nContent warning: Topics include illness, death and related subjects.\nRecommended for ages 14 and up. Anyone under 17 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"OGMQ_a1JowZ9TDZayyn_6Q","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aae32edb-e8f5-4760-b053-81cb44cc2186"},{"id":"ad91838b-8435-418e-b33a-44d32420d6bc","name":"Glen Long Park - 11 a.m. to 1 p.m.","dates":[1791039600000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Glen Long Park","address":"35 Glen Long Ave, North York, ON, M6B 2M1","lat":43.708778236,"lng":-79.455865001},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Try something new, get moving and connect through sport, Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels.\n\nWith a variety of sports equipment on board, vibrant vans tour neighbourhoods, transforming parks and outdoor spaces into pop-up sport hubs, bringing energy and excitement directly to communities around the city. Proudly powered in partnership with Nike, Play Mobile is committed to the future of youth sport, creating more equitable and inclusive access to play – with a focus on encouraging girls to participate and stay involved in sport.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"JY5NZWRAS6Lt1TXJKw_GWw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=140%20Stilecroft%20Dr&lat=43.746886&lng=-79.498855&zoom=17","tickets":null},{"id":"6352cdf2-7955-4a9b-bc2a-f1fe9f607ed5","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website