00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"94d6141a-9749-451a-8605-e0fa3511b9dc","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"8257f073-fcd8-42aa-b638-27fdd3ac9db8","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"4e5ee5ee-6bc9-44cc-944e-0686914c6c8c","name":"COC Free Concert Series at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1791399600000],"start":"2026-10-07T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-07T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy music in the garden at the Inn. Celebrate the 20th anniversary of the Canadian Opera Company (COC) Free Concert Series with world-class pop-up performances in partnership with the Toronto History Museums. The Out in the City series features music from Hasti Ensemble – a cross-cultural music group dedicated to exploring the artistic dialogue between Persian and Indian classical music. Gathering music from both traditions, the ensemble creates performances that celebrate the rich rhythmic, melodic, and improvisational heritage of these musical cultures. Pick up a treat from the market and stay for the music. \n\nLimited seating available. ","categories":["Live Performances","Museum","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"TktwqlUq31bod_88DJyNXQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"01dc0ad6-2b68-44d6-90c7-bb968b434a19","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"08cd58d9-2f78-47cb-925a-823621c49f6e","name":"Queen East Eats Fall Food Tours","dates":[1791046800000,1794679200000,1796493600000,1797098400000],"start":"2026-10-03T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-12T13:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Restaurants/Cafes/Bars in Riverside and Leslieville","address":"657 Queen St E, Toronto","lat":43.658232745,"lng":-79.351745596},"free":false,"low":10,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTickets are available for purchase about two weeks before the tour. ","description":"Celebrate fall and support small businesses.\n\nGet ready to visit six pre-selected local food and drink establishments in Riverside and Leslieville, while learning about the story behind the businesses with your expert guide.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Tour"],"presenter":"Riverside BIA","image":"D9twy0ORnOjZy3lFBl4ztA","website":"https://QueenEastEatsFoodTours.eventbrite.ca","tickets":"https://QueenEastEatsFoodTours.eventbrite.ca"},{"id":"983de2f1-2a92-4b5a-9b32-90f76d1f9954","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"61fac51a-b14c-41fc-83a2-667e440ab6ea","name":"MULTIfest Interactive Art festival","dates":[1790888400000,1790974800000,1791061200000,1791147600000,1791234000000,1791320400000,1791406800000,1791493200000],"start":"2026-10-01T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Stackt Market","address":"28 Bathurst St, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R4","lat":43.640948,"lng":-79.402169},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto’s new festival of interactive and digital art, returns to STACKT Market!\n\nWe're bringing together interactive art installations, audiovisual performances and beginner-friendly workshops, alongside artist talks, family programming and community events.\n\nExplore immersive digital artworks, interact with responsive installations, experience live audiovisual performances, and get hands-on with creative technology through workshops in electronic music making, projection mapping and more.\n\nTogether with Nuit Blanche, enjoy an afternoon Show and Tell and immersive round table, followed by an Immersive Happy Hour with DJs, live visuals and interactive art.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"KoSi1GfJkywyaekelu014A","website":"https://multi-fest.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"318079d6-7026-479f-aca6-1aa47d38ce78","name":"ICONIC: The Big Fun Party","dates":[1792794600000,1792881000000],"start":"2026-10-23T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Daniels Spectrum","address":"585 Dundas St E, Toronto, ON M5A 2B7","lat":43.6601,"lng":-79.360417},"free":false,"low":250,"high":400,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The city’s newest, hottest event is back! \n\nGet ready to sparkle and slay at our unforgettable evening of divas and dancing featuring fierce, show-stopping performances by legendary talent followed by a spectacular dance party.\n\nBut remember, ICONIC is not just a party, it is a movement with every beat and step supporting equitable and essential 2SLGBTQIA+ health care programs at Sherbourne Health.\n\nJoin the movement and be ICONIC!\n\n","categories":["Charity/Cause","2SLGBTQ+","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"2Hh5U4lww_FRbJ_696jjfQ","website":"https://iconicparty.ca","tickets":"https://iconicparty.ca"},{"id":"a0566b56-00e4-45c1-88f9-ec04a9bb39d8","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W