nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"75f60122-a361-447d-8b66-d252283a7952","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"fb8d6777-c4cf-4e29-9013-8e07b2f83370","name":"Kids Vote Weekend","dates":[1791640800000,1791727200000],"start":"2026-10-10T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Advance voting places","address":"","lat":43.760711,"lng":-79.615173},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Calling all Toronto kids, vote for Toronto’s Tree of the Year! \n\nTrees fill our vibrant parks, forests and green spaces. The City plants up to 120,000 trees a year that help clean the air, provide shade, support wildlife and more. Help us vote for one of the five candidates this year! \n\nKids Vote Weekend encourages young people who are under the age of 18 to learn about elections and start their journey to becoming a lifelong voter. \n\nThe winning tree will be announced after the October 26 municipal election.","categories":["Family/Children"],"presenter":null,"image":"BJZAL5xwkrtUUm5iRuZ2vw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/city-government/elections/kids-vote-weekend/","tickets":null},{"id":"534df691-304f-42d4-b1cc-ccd6a61c7ea8","name":"Kids Vote Weekend","dates":[1791640800000,1791727200000],"start":"2026-10-10T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-11T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Advance voting places","address":"","lat":43.760711,"lng":-79.615173},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Calling all Toronto kids, vote for Toronto’s Tree of the Year! \n\nTrees fill our vibrant parks, forests and green spaces. The City plants up to 120,000 trees a year that help clean the air, provide shade, support wildlife and more. Help us vote for one of the five candidates this year! \n\nKids Vote Weekend encourages young people who are under the age of 18 to learn about elections and start their journey to becoming a lifelong voter. \n\nThe winning tree will be announced after the October 26 municipal election.","categories":["Family/Children"],"presenter":null,"image":"BJZAL5xwkrtUUm5iRuZ2vw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/city-government/elections/kids-vote-weekend/","tickets":null},{"id":"4deffa9f-ce47-41f7-9f7d-e99be2f935da","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"2bf48ca8-b367-4203-9a75-6321219b3834","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"e2a177ca-692c-4bb3-bb35-956d057a60ce","name":"Kevin Chen and Illia Ovcharenko, duo piano with the Amadeus Choir and The Glenn Gould School","dates":[1805655600000],"start":"2027-03-21T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-03-21T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":50,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Two extraordinary young pianists join forces for a rare performance of Beethoven’s monumental Symphony No. 9 arranged for two pianos, a vocal quartet from The Glenn Gould School and a choir. \n\nPlease join us! \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"9XZChR4xc8KWFhIRUtop3w","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/kevin-chen-and-illia-ovcharenko-430002","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/430002"},{"id":"4a66b745-ad56-461b-9edd-7b1fb14145ca","name":"Rebanks Family Fellowship Concert","dates":[1794441600000,1807138800000],"start":"2026-11-11T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-04-07T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Mazzoleni Concert Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1W2","lat":43.667901,"lng":-79.396334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nTickets available November 4, 2026.","description":"Solo and chamber works are performed by young artists on the cusp of major careers, who are enrolled in The Rebanks Family Fellowship and International Performance Residency Program at The Glenn Gould School.\n\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"GLn4N339UYQqP0iripwBcw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/rebanks-family-fellowship-concert-450401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/450401"},{"id":"5f4d43eb-404b-463e-b41a-f54265263b90","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728