time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"3ebfd1ff-f105-478d-a7a6-49ba190616e9","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"3050685b-302e-4c60-ba84-b67527bc99e7","name":"Music Toronto - Escher String Quartet","dates":[1806017400000],"start":"2027-03-25T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2027-03-25T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nSubscribe and Save up to 40%","description":"Escher String Quartet makes its Music Toronto debut with a program that moves from Classical brilliance to late-Romantic intensity. \n\nJoseph Haydn’s sparkling Op. 76 No. 1 opens the evening, followed by the lush cinematic voice of Erich Wolfgang Korngold’s rarely heard Third Quartet, before the profound lyricism and drama of Johannes Brahms’s A minor Quartet. Formed in 2005, the Escher is named for the Dutch graphic artist M.C. Escher, inspired by his method of interplay between individual components working together to form a whole.\n\nIn partnership with Music Toronto, the quartet will be in residence at the University of Toronto Faculty of Music, culminating in a Pre-Concert performance alongside student chamber musicians.\n\n“Elegant, incisive and full of character.” — The New York Times","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"bH2dUJGtIkQY7TB7J5IsNA","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/escher-string-quartet","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/escher-string-quartet"},{"id":"129bcb8e-e8bc-43e8-9c7f-34f821bcdfdd","name":"Rebellion Talks: The Strange & Tragic Tale of Robert Baldwin","dates":[1795737600000],"start":"2026-11-26T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-26T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679046946,"lng":-79.408181452},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Listen to the story of Robert Baldwin, one of the strangest and most pivotal figures in Canadian history. Not everyone who demanded change believed in violence. One of the leading champions of Canadian democracy refused to take up arms and join the rebels. Baldwin's summer home was located where the museum is today. Investigate the role Baldwin played in trying to find a peaceful solution to the rebellion crisis, how he eventually accomplished what Mackenzie never did, and the bizarre twist to his tragic love story.\n\nFrom October 2026 to April 2027, historian Adam Bunch brings Toronto’s history to life in a series of talks exploring the Upper Canada Rebellion and its lasting impact on the city. From spies and taverns to political reform, rural rebels and the Patriot War, each talk reveals a different story connected to the museum where it takes place.","categories":["History","Museum","Talks"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"yOS4dXjLhyIxrD4HODyuGg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/spadina-museum/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/14a799b6-fc79-416d-9feb-1c61e08e758a"},{"id":"1bee4864-5fda-4f11-8caa-7536d87bc08b","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"b1520cb7-06fd-4979-bf3d-67b897582e2d","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"f586144a-106d-43f1-9d4b-7030499b6c52","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"6f8d2f94-af96-4949-af25-dd37f9015f86","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Fall Flavours: Walking Food Tour","dates":[1789659000000,1790263800000,1790868600000,1791473400000,1792078200000,1792683000000,1793287800000,1793896200000,1794501000000,1795105800000,1795710600000],"start":"2026-09-17T11:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T11:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting point: Fusettes","address":"407 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1S9","lat":43.659499524,"lng":-79.382002835},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fall Flavours is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"18a36add-0e5b-48c4-b574-7ed7656edd04","name":"Lantern Tours at Fort York: After Dark","dates":[1792711800000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1793316600000,1793403000000],"start":"2026-10-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"100 Garrison Rd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.638491,"lng":-79.40518},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Hear chilling and eerie tales on a lantern tour of Fort York and its historic surroundings. Learn about a haunted lighthouse and the bloody Battle of York. Explore the military burial ground. Tour the creepy shadows and 200-year-old buildings of Fort York at night and learn of the fort’s history and its many paranormal mysteries.","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"G-eno19UG31sj5aKkgxxQg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/09cc8903-6509-4ac3-9964-74a070bbb946"},{"id":"ba260e4a-fe4b-40e6-90b6-c8310a3a0830","name":"ROM After Dark","dates":[1793403000000,1793489400000],"start":"2026-10-30T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":40,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The wait is over...welcome back to the best Halloween Party in the city!\n\nAs night falls, the Museum transforms with eerie décor for an unforgettable evening of live music, DJ sets and non-stop dancing. \n\nCome dressed in your best Halloween look or simply ready to celebrate. The night will be packed with high-energy entertainment and so many spooky surprises.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Nightlife","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"cpcsg5qxLMVvl-Lh-JcmOA","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/events/rom-after-dark-all-hallows-eve?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=rad","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/events/rom-after-dark-all-hallows-eve?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=rad"},{"id":"fa413d07-9dce-4bd3-b708-8e144f46b972","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"e565f1a2-80ea-422a-85d4-da265906e32a","name":"New Bad Ideas Live: An Evening of New Ideas, New Music and New Stories","dates":[1792969200000],"start":"2026-10-25T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Great Hall","address":"1087 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6J 1H3","lat":43.643349,"lng":-79.422058},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":", $30.00 (Arts Workers)","description":"After a sold-out 2025 concert and encore matinee, New Bad Ideas Live returns! \n\nPremiering four newly commissioned works by celebrated Canadian Music Theatre creators alongside highlights from Bad Hats’ ever-growing canon of musicals and songs from our acclaimed New Bad Ideas program, New Bad Ideas Live is an annual invitation for audiences to see what’s going on behind the scenes at Bad Hats while getting a sneak peek at some of Canada’s most exciting new musicals in development.\n\nNew Bad Ideas Live once again invites audiences into the first sparks of creation. Bad Hats Artistic Director Fiona Sauder and Artistic Managing Director Matt Pilipiak have curated a dynamic evening of new music and storytelling, performed by a knockout ensemble of Canadian talent. ","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"4G01d2yQ08XzNuTrAlKEOw","website":"https://badhatstheatre.com/new-bad-ideas-live-","tickets":"https://badhatstheatre.com/tickets"},{"id":"fde2b523-af35-4dc7-8587-62bcdbb1e51b","name":"Come Play Werewolf at the Yonge Eglinton Centre","dates":[1792706400000],"start":"2026-10-22T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-22T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Yonge Eglinton Centre","address":"2300 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4P 1E4","lat":43.707157575,"lng":-79.399083527},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come join us for a fun game of Werewolf! Whether you’re a seasoned player or completely new, everyone is welcome to test their intuition, sharpen their critical thinking, and enjoy some friendly deception and debate.\n\nWerewolf is a social deduction game where players work together to identify the hidden werewolves before they are eliminated. Each session runs about 3 to 4 hours, with 3 to 5 games depending on group size.\n\nThe goal is simple, bring people together, explore different spaces around Toronto, and create an affordable way to meet others and enjoy good company. ","categories":["Public Square","Trivia","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"ATHyjdHsbWwwzjw6QapCXw","website":"https://www.sites.google.com/view/wwto","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1997612803670?aff=oddtdtcreator"},{"id":"2d13950d-e93a-4d78-9a3f-b7ecbaf61a14","name":"Steeles Library Tree Tour","dates":[1792173600000],"start":"2026-10-16T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T14:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Steeles Library","address":"375 Bamburgh Crcl, Scarborough, ON, M1W 3Y1","lat":43.815681245,"lng":-79.322382371},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The Steeles branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of trees. Join the City of Toronto to explore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n\nThe tour will start and end at the Steeles Branch side entrance and will be guided by City of Toronto staff. There may be uneven, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens, hats, sunscreen, water, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.\n\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver. Registration is required.\n\n","categories":["Environmental","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"-x4VeRICU-WrF7Mbxdvq3g","website":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a972cec1c197d11325c7611","tickets":"https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a972cec1c197d11325c7611"},{"id":"68856aa6-a542-4c59-a3cb-d193293ea9a5","name":"Piece by Piece: Celebration at Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","dates":[1792764000000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.757430206,"lng":-79.207131759},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a celebration marking the completion of Piece by Piece, a mosaic art project that brought together 15 seniors for 10 weeks of creative learning and collaboration.\n\nInspired by the theme of gardens and nature, participants designed and created unique mosaic stepping stones that have been permanently installed as a community mural on the grounds of Cedar Ridge Creative Centre. This special gathering celebrates the creativity, dedication, and achievements of the participants while unveiling the completed artwork.\n\nThe event is open to all. Brief remarks will take place shortly after the event begins, and light refreshments will be provided. No RSVP is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Celebrations","Family/Children"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"otp2C0iqc5ZxPwGUmmHoqg","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"4891e5fa-c97f-4378-8765-2913173de49c","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"3411ca04-6b27-45f8-bf56-bc5b787f7383","name":"Nuit Talk: Museum of Lost Things with Rhonda Weppler and Trevor Mahovsky","dates":[1791086400000],"start":"2026-10-04T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Old City Hall, Room 155","address":"60 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M5H 2M3","lat":43.652350814,"lng":-79.381863479},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The artists are present. Rhonda Weppler and Trevor Mahovsky share their journeys in creating Museum of Lost Things through hands-on workshops across North America. Chat with Rhonda and Trevor directly and ask them about their artistic process. \n\nNuit Talks program includes pop-up artist talks scheduled throughout the night, connecting attendees directly to the artists and deepening their understanding and appreciation of art. Meet many artists at their projects and speak to them about their work.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"097P3WZwLRDQeRdVabLYIA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/","tickets":null},{"id":"aa9a70bb-a1d6-4c0d-b26c-a9293e60a7fb","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"a56eec11-c100-4b63-ae95-50dd2d63b3bd","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"959e3687-b2c0-4379-be3b-f269b8ab8024","name":"Historic Holiday Gingerbread Workshop at Fort York","dates":[1797696000000,1797706800000,1797782400000,1797793200000,1798041600000,1798052400000,1798128000000,1798138800000,1798387200000,1798398000000,1798646400000,1798657200000,1798732800000,1798743600000,1798905600000,1798916400000,1798992000000,1799002800000],"start":"2026-12-19T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-03T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site ","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864,"lng":-79.406315},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience the warmth of the holiday season through a hands-on baking workshop in the historic Officers' Mess Kitchen.  Children and teens aged 8 to 14 can prepare an historic recipe using traditional methods including creaming butter, pounding sugar, grating spices, sifting flour, rolling and cutting dough.  \n\nWhile the gingerbread bakes, participants can enjoy a festive scavenger hunt in the Fort and return back to the kitchen to sample their freshly baked gingerbread biscuits and take home the historic recipe to recreate in their own kitchens.  ","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Museum","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"OOkRdDMZf1TJSEdlmkqvKg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f778e3cc-f1b6-403a-baa6-4c8276e34a34"},{"id":"b1d7c48e-765d-49a8-bebd-964931a8c715","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"71a42061-1dee-42a0-b4a6-a8d9646eef52","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000