at direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"0a38ed22-1e6e-45fc-9cfe-fc239736eb1c","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"85331701-9cd8-4e9c-bb2f-63e47eb24053","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"7fdbf929-a3ef-4060-9b26-9d27556755c0","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"e5373477-e2b6-4464-8c53-a56bdd16f9ae","name":"Toronto Coin Expo: Canada's Coin Show","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Reference Library ","address":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 2G8","lat":43.671878938,"lng":-79.386669972},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nKids 16 and under attend for free. Tickets can be purchased at the door for cash only.","description":"Join us at the Toronto Coin Expo, Canada’s premier coin and banknote show and auction, located in downtown Toronto. \n\nFeaturing over 50 internationally renowned coin and banknote dealers, representing Canada, United States, and the World of collectable currencies. \n\nThis is the place to buy, sell, and appraise your coins, banknotes, tokens, medals, militaria, gold and silver.\n\nYou are sure to find a one-of-a-kind coin or banknote treasures!\n","categories":["Consumer Show/Convention","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":"9vLYmoiOaoAhcURPQGx8iQ","website":"https://www.torontocoinexpo.ca","tickets":"https://tickets-ca.evvnt.com/events/toronto-coin-expo-canadas-coin-show-10-23-2026"},{"id":"97c7882d-6d57-4eb7-9c50-3580ea539141","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Fall Flavours: Walking Food Tour","dates":[1789659000000,1790263800000,1790868600000,1791473400000,1792078200000,1792683000000,1793287800000,1793896200000,1794501000000,1795105800000,1795710600000],"start":"2026-09-17T11:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T11:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting point: Fusettes","address":"407 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1S9","lat":43.659499524,"lng":-79.382002835},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fall Flavours is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"ac7a745d-c6b9-4b0b-b1c0-a170446074aa","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Fall Flavours: Walking Food Tour","dates":[1789659000000,1790263800000,1790868600000,1791473400000,1792078200000,1792683000000,1793287800000,1793896200000,1794501000000,1795105800000,1795710600000],"start":"2026-09-17T11:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T11:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting point: Fusettes","address":"407 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1S9","lat":43.659499524,"lng":-79.382002835},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fall Flavours is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"1750f664-8591-4315-ade8-95c00d335b05","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Fall Flavours: Walking Food Tour","dates":[1789659000000,1790263800000,1790868600000,1791473400000,1792078200000,1792683000000,1793287800000,1793896200000,1794501000000,1795105800000,1795710600000],"start":"2026-09-17T11:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T11:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting point: Fusettes","address":"407 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1S9","lat":43.659499524,"lng":-79.382002835},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fall Flavours is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"a97240be-2204-450c-8a78-8efa54242f7f","name":"Always In Fashion","dates":[1789574400000,1789660800000,1789747200000,1789833600000,1789920000000,1790179200000,1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000],"start":"2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-01-03T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"5751b04b-60d7-4090-a820-55d9972a5b78","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"8180c0e4-1d1e-4118-b740-f251498398f7","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"f26fee04-78bb-4580-b644-028a1671ba8e","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"a40f30dc-ab99-420c-b435-a42357f07260","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"498f92ce-50bd-442d-a053-2a1d255c6ee6","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,179078760000