":"0fa00b4e-28e7-4d30-94c2-044d6e2cd0b1","name":"By the Lake Book Club – 6-Event Package (2027)","dates":[1801612800000],"start":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":120,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall and Toronto Book Awards, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nJoin leading Canadian authors as they dive into conversation about their latest books with Humber Polytechnic alumni at Assembly Hall. The 2027 lineup features the 2026 Toronto Book Award Winner, Nadja Lubiw-Hazard, Ashraf Zaghal, Tyler Pennock, Gillian Deacon and Carrianne Leung.\n\nThe signature series features six Tuesday-night events, between February and December. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation.\n\n2026 Toronto Book Award Winner - February 2, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nNadja Lubiw-Hazard - March 9, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nAshraf Zaghal  - April 13, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nTyler Pennock - September 14, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nGillian Deacon - October 5, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nCarrianne Leung - December 7, 2027 at 7 p.m.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#multipacks/4fbe5173-7528-46e3-8d0c-5c7f321f0e9d"},{"id":"07ef508f-d57f-4bc0-80b1-6e73bce98b12","name":"(Sold Out) In Broken Light Artist/Curator Guided Tours at Spadina Museum","dates":[1789682400000,1789851600000,1791057600000,1792101600000],"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679047,"lng":-79.408181},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Limited tickets now sold out","description":"Join artist Ry Van Der Hout and curator Adrien Sun Hall for a special guided tour of the contemporary art exhibition, In Broken Light. Hear from the artist or the curator their own perspectives on the five glass sculptures spanning the four levels of Spadina Museum. \n\nDiscussion includes themes of rupture, repair and how the art speak to the layered history at Spadina Museum.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Y0xDdT14ZflLoRl1dLbL0g","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d3f62fdc-e7d9-4b86-bc72-6cfd0934e234"},{"id":"a11058c4-19a1-4dc1-a003-ca040063d206","name":"(Sold Out) In Broken Light Artist/Curator Guided Tours at Spadina Museum","dates":[1789682400000,1789851600000,1791057600000,1792101600000],"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679047,"lng":-79.408181},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Limited tickets now sold out","description":"Join artist Ry Van Der Hout and curator Adrien Sun Hall for a special guided tour of the contemporary art exhibition, In Broken Light. Hear from the artist or the curator their own perspectives on the five glass sculptures spanning the four levels of Spadina Museum. \n\nDiscussion includes themes of rupture, repair and how the art speak to the layered history at Spadina Museum.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Y0xDdT14ZflLoRl1dLbL0g","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d3f62fdc-e7d9-4b86-bc72-6cfd0934e234"},{"id":"3e0ef0b4-4846-4556-a8f2-14d1131cd0a2","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,17905