,"tickets":null},{"id":"3a51ec84-166c-46a2-b5b8-31540efd68ca","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"c50b14dc-9a44-426d-ab5c-f1a4b583a0ae","name":"Music Toronto - What Makes It Great with Rob Kapilow and Meagan Milatz","dates":[1800219600000],"start":"2027-01-17T16:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-01-17T16:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nSubscribe and Save up to 40%","description":"Master communicator Rob Kapilow and brilliant Canadian pianist Meagan Milatz explore Beethoven’s electrifying Appassionata Sonata, revealing how the composer transforms simple musical ideas through bold and imaginative variations. \n\nPart of our Sunday afternoon MUSE (Music Unveiled, Stories, Explorations) series, this illuminating event readies listeners for Danny Driver’s performance of Beethoven’s monumental Diabelli Variations in March 2027.\n\n“Kapilow is the ideal guide—erudite, engaging, and endlessly illuminating.” — The New York Times","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"NRR0uJAiWtna-Be2Y0HYXA","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/wmig-beethoven-appassionata","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/wmig-beethoven-appassionata"},{"id":"4731df9f-49d3-4b00-b8aa-bd3218e7a234","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"49e60ae9-6934-414d-a729-1f929622eb00","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"6d6e20d9-7701-4a83-bae3-aabd97673336","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"24820210-4547-4999-92c4-647258238ba9","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"b4a79f37-37ef-451e-8a33-00d303b5be64","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"24b0beca-2bbe-496a-8994-53733c2afea4","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"facca2be-09c5-4b92-b20a-555e91d67446","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"bc21dff2-c737-4804-9dff-0324282919d7","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"fc817c9a-c94c-4a2d-8bf8-ec09200051c9","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Fall Flavours: Walking Food Tour","dates":[1789659000000,1790263800000,1790868600000,1791473400000,1792078200000,1792683000000,1793287800000,1793896200000,1794501000000,1795105800000,1795710600000],"start":"2026-09-17T11:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-26T11:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting point: Fusettes","address":"407 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M5B 1S9","lat":43.659499524,"lng":-79.382002835},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Fall Flavours is a seasonal one-hour food tour designed especially for people who work in and around the neighbourhood. \n\nDiscover the flavours of the season while visiting local restaurants, cafés and food spots, with tasting-sized bites and stories from the streets of Downtown Yonge. \n\nIt’s a quick, delicious way to make your lunch hour feel like a little adventure! Find some new local favourites along the way.\n\nOne hour. Multiple food stops. A taste of the season and of the city!  Come hungry and discover somewhere new.","categories":["Food/Culinary","Run/Walk","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"fcdcc455-3241-479a-8db8-295462381cd9","name":"Retra