 day of entrepreneurship, innovation, and meaningful connections! As part of the Expo, the Innovation & Growth Pitch Competition will showcase Ontario-based tech-enabled startups pitching their ventures to investors, industry leaders, and innovation partners. Attendees will have opportunities to hear from emerging founders, connect with investors and funding organizations, explore commercialization and applied research opportunities, and participate in networking activities designed to spark new connections and collaboration. Whether you’re a founder, investor, industry leader, researcher, or part of the innovation ecosystem, join us to discover new ideas and explore opportunities to grow and collaborate.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Humber Polytechnic","image":null,"website":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/research-unplugged-2026-tickets-1995515141506?keep_tld=true","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/research-unplugged-2026-tickets-1995515141506?keep_tld=true"},{"id":"2ae7aa88-bd4d-43b2-bcbe-d9b3cd89c035","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"15b5ef19-fc87-4a87-a147-66de9da86ab6","name":"Public Pier","dates":[1789768800000,1789837200000,1790373600000,1790442000000,1790978400000,1791046800000],"start":"2026-09-18T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Marina Quay West","address":"539 Queens Quay West, Toronto","lat":43.636696,"lng":-79.394687},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Public Pier is turning Marina Quay West into a day-to-night cultural destination right in Toronto's Waterfront - featuring music, dance, food, public art and immersive nighttime projections\n\nEnjoy day-to-night experiences on the waterfront including food and drink from The Super Yummy Market, local DJs including CYRO Sounds, Introspkt and Nabz, free beginner-friendly dance workshops, and public art including SILO Nights, where each evening the Canada Malting Silos will be illuminated with immersive artworks by local and international artists.\n\n\n ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Food/Culinary","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"c6PLTik8EeSto-SlLgqhKw","website":"https://publicpier.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"484159f6-8f96-4cb0-ab8d-ff56efef9e44","name":"Public Pier","dates":[1789768800000,1789837200000,1790373600000,1790442000000,1790978400000,1791046800000],"start":"2026-09-18T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Marina Quay West","address":"539 Queens Quay West, Toronto","lat":43.636696,"lng":-79.394687},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Public Pier is turning Marina Quay West into a day-to-night cultural destination right in Toronto's Waterfront - featuring music, dance, food, public art and immersive nighttime projections\n\nEnjoy day-to-night experiences on the waterfront including food and drink from The Super Yummy Market, local DJs including CYRO Sounds, Introspkt and Nabz, free beginner-friendly dance workshops, and public art including SILO Nights, where each evening the Canada Malting Silos will be illuminated with immersive artworks by local and international artists.\n\n\n ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Food/Culinary","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"c6PLTik8EeSto-SlLgqhKw","website":"https://publicpier.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"ced49601-3c64-43ba-b699-807609a77d6f","name":"WHAT MAKES IT GREAT?® - MENDELSSOHN","dates":[1794776400000],"start":"2026-11-15T16:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-15T16:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nPlease view our website for subscription-based pricing and save up to 40% on tickets. ","description":"Featuring Jonathan Crow, violin; Annalee Patipatanakoon, violin; Sharon Wei, viola; Roman Borys, cello; and the Dior String Quartet.\n\nIn \"What Makes It Great?\", composer, commentator, and author Rob Kapilow unlocks great music with insight, humour, and live musical examples. \n\nExplore the brilliance of Mendelssohn’s Octet as Kapilow reveals the invention and youthful genius behind one of chamber music’s most exhilarating works. His presentation is followed by a complete performance and audience Q&A.\n\nPart of our Sunday afternoon MUSE (Music Unveiled, Stories, Explorations) series.\n","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Talks"],"presenter":"Music Toronto","image":"wzGoWIo3ELq4pzQ3IQ0OuA","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/wmig-mendelssohn-octet","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/wmig-mendelssohn-octet"},{"id":"ca4e1a44-518f-49f2-b886-f2bf313c4d9b","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"244356d4-a23b-4de6-9d59-f454d58708e7","name":"Canvas Chronicles","dates":[1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000],"start":"2026-09-23T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T08:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Every brushstroke tells a story in the Federation of Canadian Artists Toronto exhibit. This collection captures the artist’s thoughts, emotions, and moments in time, weaving technical skill and personality into complex visual narratives. The adventurous members invite you to engage with their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"e0d4e96f-bd71-43d8-8cac-a1598b9444e7","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"2d72fbf9-9a0f-4172-8d82-6109e3fad48b","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"68707f47-126a-43bb-b6ad-ca649dac29e8","name":"Yulianna Avdeeva, piano","dates":[1808679600000],"start":"2027-04-25T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-25T15:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":50,"high":110,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A pianist of fiery temperament and virtuosity, Yulianna Avdeeva is the Gold Medalist of the 2010 International Chopin Piano Competition, which launched her to international fame for “consistently [leading] the field in terms of sheer passion and musicianship, not to mention technical security,” and for her “spontaneous and volatile” performances “full of depth and colour” (The Telegraph). \n\nA favorite artist in Europe, Yulianna has recurring concert engagements at the Warsaw Philharmonic, Rudolfinum in Prague, Pierre Boulez Saal in Berlin, Vienna Konzerthaus, and Elbphilharmonie in Hamburg. She recently performed recital debuts at the Salzburg and Gstaad festivals and at the Concertgebouw in Amsterdam.\n\nPlease join us! ","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"T0zf2ZQ1KlApekWqV8fr3Q","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/yulianna-avdeeva-430001","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/430001"},{"id":"596b0534-90c7-43cb-9fb8-a274b15e6fbe","name":"Ménestrel","dates":[1796322600000],"start":"2026-12-03T13:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-12-03T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Walter Hall, University of Toronto","address":"80 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C5","lat":43.666495,"lng":-79.394538},"free":false,"low":0,"high":55,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nFree for students and accompanying caregivers. \nJoin us for the Tuning Your Mind pre-concert presentation at 12:15 p.m., free for all ticket holders.","description":"Celebrate the magic of midwinter with Yuletide: A Ceremony of Midwinter, an enchanting mix of ancient repertoire and traditional folk songs, brought to life through the sounds of lute, recorder and the female voice.\n\nFeaturing Janelle Lucyk, soprano; Kerry Bursey, lute; and Vincent Lauzer, recorder, this atmospheric performance invites audiences to experience the music, traditions and spirit of the midwinter season.\n\nJoin us for this special celebration and experience the music and traditions of the midwinter season together.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"KYfdVIFRaoemHSUqKfjP_g","website":"https://www.wmct.on.ca","tickets":"https://www.wmct.on.ca"},{"id":"d94f85e0-84bf-4d92-b3d5-ff53a8a09478","name":"Art on a Tuesday: Dinner, Drinks & Live Entertainment","dates":[1792794600000],"start":"2026-10-23T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-23T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Half Note 416","address":"3357 Kingston Road, Scarborough, ON M1M 1R3","lat":43.733877,"lng":-79.222605},"free":false,"low":35,"high":50,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nCouples and group packages are available. ","description":"After a break, Toronto’s intimate multidisciplinary showcase is back with a fresh look and a new lineup. \n\nExperience one curated night featuring live R&B, stand-up comedy, magic, mentalism, spoken word, violin, visual art and featured creatives. \n\nListen to club favourites with reggae, soca, afrobeats and hip-hop. \n\nDiscover local talent, meet new people and experience entertainment that keeps the night moving. \n\nWhether you have joined us in the past or are discovering us for the first time, come experience the return. \n\nIt’s not a concert. It’s not the club. It’s an intimate, curated night of art, entertainment and connection, designed to keep the dopamine flowing.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://artonatuesday.ca","tickets":"https://artonatuesday.ca/"},{"id":"36120a98-86c9-4c31-92ab-89208ed6fe60","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"802bd725-ff2c-4f4b-9333-732570bde2f9","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, O