s of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"8e6216b2-cf8c-44c0-b92a-abbba24ea258","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"6a0114fa-cedc-470a-8fd0-65fb3eb2617e","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"1f61f96d-8318-4d8f-9cf5-4b03d2dfac7b","name":"Seeing Sound Exhibit (A Synesthetic Experience) by Pauline Douady","dates":[1789822800000,1789993800000,1790080200000,1790166600000,1790253000000,1790339400000,1790425800000,1790598600000,1790685000000,1790771400000,1790857800000,1790944200000,1791030600000,1791203400000,1791289800000,1791376200000,1791462600000,1791549000000,1791635400000,1791808200000,1791894600000,1791981000000,1792067400000,1792153800000,1792240200000],"start":"2026-09-19T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T08:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Alliance Française Toronto","address":"24 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2S7","lat":43.668767,"lng":-79.40519},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"French Synesthete artist Pauline Douady transforms sounds, voices, and atmospheres into visual art: drawings, prints, and paintings. \n\nThe exhibition is enriched with audio content accessible accessible directly on your phone via QR codes, creating a space for pause and inner reflection. \n\nFor the full immersive experience, don't forget your headphones!","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"W3jrGDlvLLzVpEEUh4WDlw","website":"https://www.alliance-francaise.ca/en/art/cultural-season/308-seeing-sound-a-synesthetic-experience-by-pauline-douady","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/voir-les-sons-seeing-sound-by-pauline-douady-tickets-1992241897144?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true"},{"id":"76d499d6-35e6-4de8-9116-04420023b37f","name":"Harp Hues Beneath the Sea of Time","dates":[1804206600000],"start":"2027-03-04T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-03-04T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Trinity- St. Paul's Centre","address":"427 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1X7","lat":43.66603939,"lng":-79.405707818},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Featuring one of the most evocative instruments in the orchestra and a world premiere written for the evening's soloist.\n\nHarpist Teresa Suen-Campbell, whose recent album with Sinfonia Toronto was praised as \"a splendid presentation\" by Textura and celebrated for its \"warmth, clarity and emotional depth\" by Harp Column, takes centre stage for the world premiere of Alice Ping Yee Ho's Beneath the Sea of Time, a harp concerto commissioned by Sinfonia Toronto that uses the sea as a metaphor for memory, loss, and renewal. \n\nPianist Theadora Koski joins the orchestra for Mozart's beloved Piano Concerto No. 23, intimate, lyrical, and graceful before the evening closes with Maestro Nurhan Arman's own orchestral arrangement of Dvorak's glorious \"American\" String Quartet, one of the most joyful works in the chamber repertoire.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Sinfonia Toronto","image":"sy98QEdnUs_slQZerlPAcw","website":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/harp-hues","tickets":"https://www.sinfoniatoronto.com/2026-2027-season/harp-hues"},{"id":"ac60e2db-6272-4365-9a0d-48be5cdb96a0","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"e6c6ed9e-2e4c-40b5-ab70-aeb47ac24a60","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790