ith their inspired works—art that stirs imagination, reveals process, and celebrates the stories behind each creation.\n\nReception: September 27, 2–4 p.m.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"4-Cfo3Q5_lOCyFEhvqYtpQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/","tickets":null},{"id":"0324d9cd-f506-46ae-b69e-e0c7566021f7","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"5ba6b417-bffb-4eda-bea1-880fa7919030","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"b33ced2b-d8e5-4048-b86c-1a1d18f2be3a","name":"MULTIfest Interactive Art festival","dates":[1790888400000,1790974800000,1791061200000,1791147600000,1791234000000,1791320400000,1791406800000,1791493200000],"start":"2026-10-01T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Stackt Market","address":"28 Bathurst St, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R4","lat":43.640948,"lng":-79.402169},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto’s new festival of interactive and digital art, returns to STACKT Market!\n\nWe're bringing together interactive art installations, audiovisual performances and beginner-friendly workshops, alongside artist talks, family programming and community events.\n\nExplore immersive digital artworks, interact with responsive installations, experience live audiovisual performances, and get hands-on with creative technology through workshops in electronic music making, projection mapping and more.\n\nTogether with Nuit Blanche, enjoy an afternoon Show and Tell and immersive round table, followed by an Immersive Happy Hour with DJs, live visuals and interactive art.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"KoSi1GfJkywyaekelu014A","website":"https://multi-fest.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"3e3e1c50-7024-4cc2-99c6-22b34a94aefb","name":"MULTIfest Interactive Art festival","dates":[1790888400000,1790974800000,1791061200000,1791147600000,1791234000000,1791320400000,1791406800000,1791493200000],"start":"2026-10-01T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-08T17:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Stackt Market","address":"28 Bathurst St, Toronto, ON, M5V 0R4","lat":43.640948,"lng":-79.402169},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Toronto’s new festival of interactive and digital art, returns to STACKT Market!\n\nWe're bringing together interactive art installations, audiovisual performances and beginner-friendly workshops, alongside artist talks, family programming and community events.\n\nExplore immersive digital artworks, interact with responsive installations, experience live audiovisual performances, and get hands-on with creative technology through workshops in electronic music making, projection mapping and more.\n\nTogether with Nuit Blanche, enjoy an afternoon Show and Tell and immersive round table, followed by an Immersive Happy Hour with DJs, live visuals and interactive art.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"KoSi1GfJkywyaekelu014A","website":"https://multi-fest.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"b8177a16-5e47-4622-b171-efb37ea47ce2","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"1b6ba7ba-9e44-4876-96a7-4e83cd24a4bb","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"876a0aa2-93a8-4516-89da-1220c5458a66","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"bd7ffd7f-dc67-4532-ac49-b93e54d690db","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"d2020f98-204c-4ed7-96a4-13669742ea1c","name":"Yuja Wang, piano","dates":[1806865200000,1806883200000],"start":"2027-04-04T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-04T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":85,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Pianist Yuja Wang is widely recognised as one of the most important artists of her generation, hailed for her supreme musicianship, insightful interpretations, and charismatic stage presence.\n\nHer work has been honoured with many accolades and prizes, including a Grammy Award (Best Classical Instrumental Solo) for her 2023 album The American Project. She makes her sixth appearance in Koerner Hall.","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"wMY-ke7ciZLDiB7eJfx5SQ","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/"},{"id":"3d58c8f2-09c2-455e-9cba-3976d3b83634","name":"Haunted ROM Tour","dates":[1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000],"start":"2026-10-03T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIn addition to the cost of museum admission ticket.","description":"Discover the haunted history of the Museum as you walk through the very halls where ghosts are said to roam.  \n\nUncover eerie tales, hear ghostly whispers, and explore hidden corners where shadows play tricks on the mind. Don't miss this unique opportunity to explore the supernatural side of art, culture and nature.  ","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"v01BsJ3lGOfA9VI9Eep9fg","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=hunt