hats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours"},{"id":"e190138c-efe7-4e98-92ab-2915b869f6e8","name":"Cabaret","dates":[1802565000000,1802631600000,1802824200000,1802910600000,1802997000000,1803083400000,1803169800000,1803236400000,1803429000000,1803515400000,1803601800000,1803688200000,1803774600000,1803841200000],"start":"2027-02-13T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Bluma Appel Theatre","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":50,"high":160,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Dancing at the edge of history.\n\nFew musicals feel as essential to revisit or as urgent to re-examine as Cabaret.\n\nSet in Berlin as the shadows of extremism lengthen, Cabaret invites us into a world of music, seduction and dangerous denial. Beneath its unforgettable songs lies one of musical theatre’s most incisive examinations of how societies unravel. Not overnight, but slowly, and in plain sight.\n\nWith a bold new vision by director Kimberley Rampersad, this production invites Toronto audiences to experience Cabaret not as a relic of the past, but as a work of thrilling theatrical intelligence and modern relevance.","categories":["2SLGBTQ+","Theatre"],"presenter":null,"image":"pkCZpzaPmYrcpwzY7m72jQ","website":"https://www.canadianstage.com/shows-events/season/cabaret","tickets":"https://my.canadianstage.com/overview/9713"},{"id":"b62650c6-690c-4aae-89df-4d50f8854608","name":"More Than a Game: Stories and Legacy of Lacrosse","dates":[1794078000000],"start":"2026-11-07T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-07T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front St E, Toronto, Second floor","lat":43.649145,"lng":-79.371526},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Toronto History Museums’ Chief Curator, Tara Chadwick, in conversation with Lance Winn, Sports Broadcaster and Vice-President of the Arena Lacrosse League, and lacrosse players and supporters as they reflect on the legacy and significance of lacrosse programming. The conversation will highlight the role of lacrosse in supporting youth engagement and building community, connection, and opportunity.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"FVfD2_YwPTP4dJ3PqQ211A","website":null,"tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aba36095-ae39-42f3-8dcc-6172e692a71b"},{"id":"a9178ffd-6864-46a2-8cf4-241924e0c990","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"4e82d5c8-2bc9-4918-b2e4-56562d58787a","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"b8b3e773-4deb-44de-b612-50fcde6ec48a","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"58d5968a-5a18-4f3f-9a1d-edf530a8f2ae","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"ff6da3ae-8b5b-4c90-a2cd-fe0ca8e782a7","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"8a04eaaa-6d20-4676-89b1-7ac9b1f9de22","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"cc2b66a3-a837-4a80-a4fb-efa20a4b46ce","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.d