and Design\n\nJoin the recipient of the 2026 Toronto Book Award for a special discussion celebrating this year's winning book. Recognizing literary excellence and a strong connection to Toronto, the award honours works that contribute to the city's rich cultural and literary landscape. This event offers an opportunity to hear from the award-winning author about their work, creative process and the stories that inspire them. Winning author to be announced November 15.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnic alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book signing and American Sign Language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aa781327-e16b-4746-85a8-0d42659b267c"},{"id":"108d4d35-51ff-4283-b2d3-8ea3276e35c7","name":"Phantom Live","dates":[1792954800000,1792971000000],"start":"2026-10-25T15:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Eglinton Grand","address":"400 Eglinton Ave W, Toronto, ON, M5N 1A2","lat":43.70439955,"lng":-79.410511225},"free":false,"low":25,"high":49,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the opulent Eglinton Grand for an unforgettable show this Halloween season. \n\nLon Chaney’s 1925 horror film The Phantom of the Opera gets a thrilling new soundtrack by Juno Award-winning composer and jazz bassist Andrew Downing, performed live by the Amadeus Choir with the composer and his all-star band. \n\nBlending a choral textures, jazz improv, and classic cinema, you won’t want to miss this elegant night out! \n","categories":["Film","Live Performances","Music","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"aOyYJ7DkcnZ91Ptb--iAdg","website":"https://amadeuschoir.com/phantom-live/","tickets":"https://amadeuschoir.com/phantom-live/"},{"id":"18ccdd27-28d8-4365-828c-59e5dba8222a","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"ee369c59-0776-43e2-b398-84d5c0532fe6","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"4a4e8bf9-5b83-4a8d-8807-180925df34d1","name":"Dog Days: Canadian Opera Premiere","dates":[1795048200000,1795134600000,1795294800000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674249,"lng":-79.387973},"free":false,"low":70,"high":105,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A contemporary opera that combines classical vocals with dark ambient noise and amplified electric guitars. \n\nSet during a fictional wartime blackout, the story follows a rural working-class family attempting to survive amidst military collapse and severe food shortages. The psychological drama explores human resilience, desperation, and moral breakdown when social structures disintegrate.\n\nCritically acclaimed by The New York Times, this breakthrough work from the writing team of composer David T. Little (Soldier Songs, JFK) and Canadian librettist Royce Vavrek (Angel’s Bone, Listen, Quiet) put them on the map. They have since gone on, both together and in collaboration with others, to revolutionize opera in North America.","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Theatre"],"presenter":"Tapestry Opera and Against the Grain Theatre","image":"r3Bej54LjTXdeoVxlHVQ8g","website":"https://tapestryopera.com/performances/dog-days/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002p2Zh2AI"},{"id":"1ac5ba47-e772-404f-9ca8-98399fe5266b","name":"Dog Days: Canadian Opera Premiere","dates":[1795048200000,1795134600000,1795294800000,1795374000000],"start":"2026-11-18T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-22T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Nancy and Ed Jackman Performance Centre","address":"877 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 3M2","lat":43.674249,"lng":-79.387973},"free":false,"low":70,"high":105,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A contemporary opera that combines classical vocals with dark ambient noise and amplified electric guitars. \n\nSet during a fictional wartime blackout, the story follows a rural working-class family attempting to survive amidst military collapse and severe food shortages. The psychological drama explores human resilience, desperation, and moral breakdown when social structures disintegrate.\n\nCritically acclaimed by The New York Times, this breakthrough work from the writing team of composer David T. Little (Soldier Songs, JFK) and Canadian librettist Royce Vavrek (Angel’s Bone, Listen, Quiet) put them on the map. They have since gone on, both together and in collaboration with others, to revolutionize opera in North America.","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Theatre"],"presenter":"Tapestry Opera and Against the Grain Theatre","image":"r3Bej54LjTXdeoVxlHVQ8g","website":"https://tapestryopera.com/performances/dog-days/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002p2Zh2AI"},{"id":"703240fb-62ac-414e-882a-02cf3c0b4460","name":"Voice and the Violin: Joshua Bell, violin and Larisa Martínez, soprano","dates":[1808866800000],"start":"2027-04-27T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-04-27T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":80,"high":175,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Superstar violinist Joshua Bell and acclaimed soprano Larisa Martínez perform their celebrated program of romantic arias and modern classics. \n\nBorn from the duo’s love of making music together in their home, the program explores repertoire from classical art song and opera to musical theatre and selections by Puerto Rican and Spanish composers. \n","categories":["Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"gOj0xlDfABvGxMV1ZGN3hw","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/joshua-bell-violin-and-larisa-martinez-soprano-with-peter-duggan-piano-429801","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/429801"},{"id":"74e4dab6-f6ab-420c-807b-022d4d5cf11e","name":"Himari, violin, with Chelsea Wang, piano","dates":[1809820800000],"start":"2027-05-08T20:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-05-08T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":20,"high":115,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The once-in-a-generation Japanese prodigy plays Schubert’s “Grand Duo” and other works at her Koerner Hall debut with pianist Chelsea Wang.\n\nPraised by The New York Times as an “excellent young pianist,” Chelsea Wang has appeared as a soloist and chamber musician throughout North America, Europe and Asia, in venues including Carnegie Hall, Kimmel Center’s Perelman Hall, Konzerthaus Berlin, Taipei National Concert Hall and more. She has had the honour of playing for many notable musicians and chamber groups, including Sir András Schiff, Richard Goode, Jonathan Biss, Miriam Fried, Leonidas Kavakos and Emerson Quartet, among others. Last season she played with violinist Ray Chen in Koerner Hall. \n\n\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"sk-NpCQGaSVISfFklAlh2Q","website":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concert/himari-violin-and-chelsea-wang-piano-428401","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/tickets/seats/428401"},{"id":"d60eb2a0-0b08-4487-b65c-972bb749a203","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"07a90964-27e9-4a47-9521-0484ba57db46","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"b48ec3b9-e7e5-4cc2-8cf0-9c96735cac5e","name":"Ravine walk at Raymore","dates":[1792342800000],"start":"2026-10-18T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Raymore Park","address":"93 Raymore Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M9P 1W9","lat":43.696339,"lng":-79.514301},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Raymore Nature Stewards on a guided walk through the park. Learn about plants for ink-making & natural dyes; ecological restoration; foraging for food & flavour; birds of the valley; and the annual salmon migration. \n\nRaymore Park’s dramatic history helped shape Toronto’s conservation movement. In 1954 Hurricane Hazel washed away the suburban neighbourhood where the park now stands. The TRCA’s floodplain management plan makes space for rivers to flow and ravines to flourish. \n","categories":["Cultural","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"K_ZlxNyOikq3jYBHJGTcBQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"458dc6c7-5605-4822-a70e-a7ea682d7e28","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"009382b7-ea34-40a6-afad-2cd5d9cc01c1","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"0627e6dc-1fa4-4144-99a7-fe539be47b1a","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"8f41667b-131c-49ec-b004-4be27f92a2ee","name":"Taste of Downtown Yonge Beverage Tour","dates":[1789320600000,1789925400000,1790530200000,1791135000000,1791739800000,1792344600000,1792949400000,1793557800000,1794162600000,1794767400000,1795372200000,1795977000000,1796581800000,1797186600000,1797791400000],"start":"2026-09-13T13:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T13:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Meeting Point: Daon Cafe","address":"475 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON M4Y 1X7","lat":43.662291,"lng":-79.383096},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Six drinks. Local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots. 90 minutes of discovery.\n\nExplore Downtown Yonge in a whole new way with a special beverage focus.\n\nYou’ll visit a selection of 6 local cafés, tea shops, bakeries and neighbourhood hot spots, sampling six different beverages along the way. Discover hidden gems, hear some of the stories behind the neighbourhood, and find places you may never have thought to try.\n\nIt’s a fun, easy way to explore more of Downtown Yonge and you might just discover your next favourite spot!\n","categories":["Food/Culinary","History","Tour"],"presenter":"Downtown Yonge BIA","image":null,"website":"http://www.downtown.com/foodtours","tickets":"http://www.downtownyonge.com/foodtours"},{"id":"f3a02400-1989-4608-95a5-c62e78542118","name":"2026 Toronto Book Award Winner – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1801612800000],"start":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":28,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall and Toronto Book Awards and Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nJoin the recipient of the 2026 Toronto Book Award for a special discussion celebrating this year's winning book. Recognizing literary excellence and a strong connection to Toronto, the award honours works that contribute to the city's rich cultural and literary landscape. This event offers an opportunity to hear from the award-winning author about their work, creative process and the stories that inspire them. Winning author to be announced November 15.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnic alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book signing and American Sign Language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aa781327-e16b-4746-85a8-0d42659b267c"},{"id":"dc37ba04-d620-403d-8abf-d3da49523ba9","name":"2026 Toronto Book Award Winner – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1801612800000],"start":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-02T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":28,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall and Toronto Book Awards and Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nJoin the recipient of the 2026 Toronto Book Award for a special discussion celebrating this year's winning book. Recognizing literary excellence and a strong connection to Toronto, the award honours works that contribute to the city's rich cultural and literary landscape. This event offers an opportunity to hear from the award-winning author about their work, creative process and the stories that inspire them. Winning author to be announced November 15.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnic alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book signing and American Sign Language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aa781327-e16b-4746-85a8-0d42659b267c"},{"id":"2a222d54-1437-43a2-8ed5-51a0ce3fe47b","name":"Marie Curtis Park - 11a.m. to 1p.m.","dates":[1791039600000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Marie Curtis Park","address":"2 Forty Second St, Etobicoke","lat":43.586761568,"lng":-79.542078498},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Try something new, get moving and connect through sport, Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels.\n\nWith a variety of sports equipment on board, vibrant vans tour neighbourhoods, transforming parks and outdoor spaces into pop-up sport hubs, bringing energy and excitement directly to communities around the city. Proudly powered in partnership with Nike, Play Mobile is committed to the future of youth sport, creating more equitable and inclusive access to play – with a focus on encouraging girls to participate and stay involved in sport.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"JY5NZWRAS6Lt1TXJKw_GWw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=2%20Forty%20Second%20St&lat=43.585755&lng=-79.543804&zoom=17","tickets":null},{"id":"bc128130-8af5-4882-9fb9-b723a51da296","name":"Toronto Sauna Festival 2026","dates":[1790978400000,1791050400000,1791122400000],"start":"2026-10-02T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783348,"lng":-79.365627973},"free":false,"low":89.99,"high":233.99,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for three days of social wellness!\n\nEnjoy over 20 saunas, guided and free-flow cold plunges, international sauna rituals, movement, music, recovery experiences, food and community.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"RNl6kf35RbKeLqeTDr70_g","website":"https://www.torontosaunafestival.com/","tickets":"https://torontosaunafestival.tickit.ca/events/36425?goto=t-178beccf4"},{"id":"e295e407-8fb3-4cd7-a6c7-fd3476f4fb1b","name":"Keeper’s by Kendra Yee, Toronto’s Artist-In-Residence 2025-2026","dates":[1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000],"start":"2026-10-03T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-28T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"1643 Dupont Street","address":"1643 Dupont St, Toronto, ON, M6P 3S9","lat":43.664594972,"lng":-79.455747889},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Kendra Yee, the City of Toronto's Artist-in-Residence (2025–2026), presents Keeper's, a reimagined corner store that draws on the artist’s personal narratives alongside histories uncovered through research with the City of Toronto Archives. Together, these stories and materials honour Toronto’s history of Chinese-founded family businesses, represented as a series of new ceramic sculptures embedded with archival imagery that interpret objects commonly found in convenience stores. Rooted in Yee's exploration of her family's immigration to the Prairies during the era of the Chinese Head Tax and Chinese Exclusion Act, Keeper’s weaves household accounts with records of Toronto's Chinese community from the 1890s to the 1950s. The resulting installation is a journey of discovery, inviting visitors to consider the preservation of stories and the communities who shape them.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"oMF3Qo7-NHppSS-catc3nQ","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"3077ac7d-d2e0-4c45-b3bb-055fc4ce33e6","name":"A Moving Affair: Shelter Movers' 10th Anniversary Gala","dates":[1794006000000],"start":"2026-11-06T18:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-06T18:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Ritz-Carlton","address":"181 Wellington St W, Toronto, ON","lat":43.645377,"lng":-79.387157},"free":false,"low":1000,"high":10000,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Tax receipts are issued for 50% of the individual ticket value.","description":"Shelter Movers' signature annual gala returns with an elegant evening to inspire hope and transform lives for survivors of abuse. \n\nThis year's edition marks the charity's 10th anniversary and brings together community leaders, corporate partners, and compassionate supporters for a luxurious evening that includes cocktail hour, a dinner reception and lively entertainment. \n\nEvery dollar raised directly supports Shelter Movers' no-cost moving and storage services for survivors fleeing abuse, helping them transition to safety with dignity. ","categories":["Charity/Cause"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://sheltermovers.com/a-moving-affair","tickets":"https://sheltermovers.com/a-moving-affair"},{"id":"4c21440c-45ac-4404-a2d5-55753ab9f070","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition in