ommunity in the nearly 200-year-old tavern. Enjoy refreshments from the historic bar and a traditional stew served by the hearth. Gather with friends and community to enjoy music, food, and history.\n\nBread and stew are included with every ticket purchased. \nDrinks are for sale at the event. \n\nTickets are not refundable or transferable. ","categories":["Food/Culinary","Museum","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"9dOP0v02KGJnOe0YD--GeQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/8b34e779-518a-4f76-973d-7e99b7d515ca"},{"id":"5ab4a985-62ef-4adf-9c71-2d7d229365b7","name":"Nuit Talk: Simile Aria with Maggy Hamel-Metsos","dates":[1791081000000],"start":"2026-10-03T22:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T22:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Old City Hall, Room 124","address":"60 Queen St E, Toronto, ON, M5C 2T3","lat":43.65334257,"lng":-79.375635348},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"The artist is present. Maggy Hamel-Metsos stages a sculptural symphony of industrial characters, coming alive. Chat with Maggy directly and ask her about her artistic process in salvaging materials and breathing new life into them. \n\nThe Nuit Talks program includes pop-up artist talks scheduled throughout the night, connecting attendees directly to the artists and deepening their understanding and appreciation of art. Many artists are also in attendance at their projects and able to speak to the public about their work.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"QYZHyvGqGheiaO1T-nPDqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/","tickets":null},{"id":"e4870ca5-52a2-48f6-9184-134f178180b0","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,179