","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"a1762e1e-45fe-49c7-a8f2-544049b51603","name":"International Architectural Design Competition 2026-2027: Persian Garden Suite","dates":[1789444800000,1789531200000,1789617600000,1789704000000,1789790400000,1789876800000,1789963200000,1790049600000,1790136000000,1790222400000,1790308800000,1790395200000,1790481600000,1790568000000,1790654400000,1790740800000,1790827200000,1790913600000,1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000,1796101200000,1796187600000,1796274000000,1796360400000,1796446800000,1796533200000,1796619600000,1796706000000,1796792400000,1796878800000,1796965200000,1797051600000,1797138000000,1797224400000,1797310800000,1797397200000,1797483600000,1797570000000,1797656400000,1797742800000],"start":"2026-09-15T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-20T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto (virtual)","address":"","lat":null,"lng":null},"free":false,"low":10,"high":30,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This international architectural competition invites participants to design a Persian Garden Suite pavilion in Toronto. \n\nThe initiative explores cultural heritage, urban design, and innovative architecture. Detailed competition guidelines, submission criteria and timelines are available for participants.","categories":["Cultural","Other"],"presenter":"Iranian-Canadian Architects and Artists Forum ","image":null,"website":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition","tickets":"https://www.icaaf.ca/competition"},{"id":"fad1ca97-b653-4277-8314-eb6adccfeb70","name":"Rebellion Talks: Booze, Taverns & Rowdy Rebels","dates":[1794528000000],"start":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-12T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651678917,"lng":-79.525658746},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Learn the role Toronto's raucous taverns played in the political tensions leading up to the Rebellion of 1837. In the middle of the 1800s, taverns played a central role in political life. Montgomery’s Inn served as a watering hole during those tense years, making it the perfect place to discuss Toronto’s tavern history and how these places helped set the stage for Mackenzie’s attempted revolution.\n\nFrom October 2026 to April 2027, historian Adam Bunch brings Toronto’s history to life in a series of talks exploring the Upper Canada Rebellion and its lasting impact on the city. From spies and taverns to political reform, rural rebels and the Patriot War, each talk reveals a different story connected to the museum where it takes place.","categories":["History","Museum","Talks"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"A0O8xMO1HPYYT0V405xAJQ","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/montgomerys-inn/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/f6ea7917-5448-4175-8d14-9668c7ed3bb7"},{"id":"45c123dc-82e3-4bf8-b3cd-8235d060feff","name":"Toronto Sauna Festival 2026","dates":[1790978400000,1791050400000,1791122400000],"start":"2026-10-02T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Evergreen Brick Works","address":"550 Bayview Ave, East York, ON, M4W 3X8","lat":43.683783348,"lng":-79.365627973},"free":false,"low":89.99,"high":233.99,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for three days of social wellness!\n\nEnjoy over 20 saunas, guided and free-flow cold plunges, international sauna rituals, movement, music, recovery experiences, food and community.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops","Other"],"presenter":null,"image":"RNl6kf35RbKeLqeTDr70_g","website":"https://www.torontosaunafestival.com/","tickets":"https://torontosaunafestival.tickit.ca/events/36425?goto=t-178beccf4"},{"id":"47e08925-9daa-4fe3-8b62-530129d48962","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Recommended for ages 12 and up. Youth 12-16 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAll ticket sales are non-refundable. Tickets are transferable.","description":"Join us for a chilling tour at Colborne Lodge in High Park. Visit the gravesite of John and Jemima Howard. Delve deeply into ideas about death and the afterlife from the 1800s and hear true tales of paranormal activities. Decide for yourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"14109ea6-fa59-45e4-9d71-766d1feac818","name":"Nuit Blanche 2026","dates":[1791068400000,1791154800000],"start":"2026-10-03T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Various","address":"","lat":43.655115,"lng":-79.388237},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join in a free all-night celebration of contemporary art that transforms Toronto’s public spaces into unexpected landscapes and animates cultural sites throughout the city.\n\nThis year’s theme, Tomorrow’s Memories, invites you to look back to the artists, curators, communities and places that defined Nuit Blanche and its twenty-year history.\n\nNuit Blanche is Toronto’s annual all-night celebration of contemporary art, produced by the City of Toronto in collaboration with Toronto’s arts community. Its locations, theme, curation and artists change from year to year, with a selection of projects extended after the event. Since 2006, this award-winning event has featured almost 1,800 art installations by approximately 6,350 artists and has generated over $550 million in economic impact for Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Nightlife"],"presenter":null,"image":"D9unQ_dL2JAu1TGQVkODBg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/festivals-events/nuitblanche/","tickets":null},{"id":"9db80b03-8746-4c0e-9454-333ecb04a60f","name":"Patterns That Aren't Exhibition","dates":[1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000,1793365200000,1793451600000,1793541600000,1793628000000,1793714400000,1793800800000,1793887200000,1793973600000,1794060000000,1794146400000,1794232800000,1794319200000,1794405600000,1794492000000,1794578400000,1794664800000,1794751200000,1794837600000,1794924000000,1795010400000],"start":"2026-10-24T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-18T09:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Cedar Ridge Creative Centre","address":"225 Confederation Dr, Scarborough, ON, M1G 1B2","lat":43.75743,"lng":-79.207132},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Step into the intricate world of artist David Currie as he explores how humans are hard-wired to seek out patterns as a means of adapting to their environment, whether connecting imaginary lines to stars or writing algorithms that direct a robot’s movements. But once a pattern is understood, interest tends to fade. Here, Currie has developed a refreshingly new visual vocabulary, one built to engage rather than fade into the background in his series of large-scale, mixed media, papercut artworks that combine recent discoveries in mathematics with a lifetime of the artist’s skill, development and commitment.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Cultural"],"presenter":null,"image":"kuVTMxi1tk-BXO-t1GOSLw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/cedar-ridge-creative-centre/","tickets":null},{"id":"287c5617-e05a-460d-b200-55c7f8c02bc2","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,179