ile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Curated by Amber-Dawn Bear Robe, enjoy an immersive exploration of Indigenous design languages and their transformative impact on the fashion landscape of the lands we call Canada and the United States. \n\nThis exhibition emerges from the urgent need to recognize and celebrate Indigenous designers who are reshaping the industry by reclaiming cultural narratives, innovating with ancestral techniques, and challenging colonial frameworks within fashion. \n\nThrough research on Indigenous fashion history, cultural sustainability, and decolonial design practices, the exhibition highlights how contemporary Indigenous couturiers blend ancestral knowledge with cutting-edge innovation to redefine fashion on their own terms.\n\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"azAuMTKhii0Yt5PF3WwMYg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/always-in-fashion/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"48b0dcd9-d968-4d0b-bfd1-22a90349447e","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Recommended for ages 12 and up. Youth 12-16 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAll ticket sales are non-refundable. Tickets are transferable.","description":"Join us for a chilling tour at Colborne Lodge in High Park. Visit the gravesite of John and Jemima Howard. Delve deeply into ideas about death and the afterlife from the 1800s and hear true tales of paranormal activities. Decide for yourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"8cbc2a99-c761-4a09-8cb7-c9e0146d592d","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"dbec34d8-2aa5-4460-b800-940d0c83f8cd","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"bbbb1569-6ad5-4122-8bfb-461ae1afc94a","name":"Haunted ROM Tour","dates":[1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000],"start":"2026-10-03T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIn addition to the cost of museum admission ticket.","description":"Discover the haunted history of the Museum as you walk through the very halls where ghosts are said to roam.  \n\nUncover eerie tales, hear ghostly whispers, and explore hidden corners where shadows play tricks on the mind. Don't miss this unique opportunity to explore the supernatural side of art, culture and nature.  ","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"v01BsJ3lGOfA9VI9Eep9fg","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours"},{"id":"63e56b38-cd8a-4c34-a9eb-e3015b54fd2d","name":"Haunted ROM Tour","dates":[1791000000000,1791086400000,1791172800000,1791259200000,1791345600000,1791432000000,1791518400000,1791604800000,1791691200000,1791777600000,1791864000000,1791950400000,1792036800000,1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000],"start":"2026-10-03T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T00:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":"100 Queen's Park, Toronto, ON, M5S 2C6","lat":43.667795388,"lng":-79.394212289},"free":false,"low":5,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nIn addition to the cost of museum admission ticket.","description":"Discover the haunted history of the Museum as you walk through the very halls where ghosts are said to roam.  \n\nUncover eerie tales, hear ghostly whispers, and explore hidden corners where shadows play tricks on the mind. Don't miss this unique opportunity to explore the supernatural side of art, culture and nature.  ","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"v01BsJ3lGOfA9VI9Eep9fg","website":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours","tickets":"https://www.rom.on.ca/whats-on/special-programs/signature-hunts-and-tours?utm_source=cityoftoronto&utm_medium=listing&utm_campaign=huntsandtours"},{"id":"fa7f8437-8f1b-49c8-835c-807277bf84df","name":"(Sold Out) In Broken Light Artist/Curator Guided Tours at Spadina Museum","dates":[1789682400000,1789851600000,1791057600000,1792101600000],"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-15T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Spadina Museum","address":"285 Spadina Rd, Toronto, ON, M5R 2V5","lat":43.679047,"lng":-79.408181},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Limited tickets now sold out","description":"Join artist Ry Van Der Hout and curator Adrien Sun Hall for a special guided tour of the contemporary art exhibition, In Broken Light. Hear from the artist or the curator their own perspectives on the five glass sculptures spanning the four levels of Spadina Museum. \n\nDiscussion includes themes of rupture, repair and how the art speak to the layered history at Spadina Museum.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Museum","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Y0xDdT14ZflLoRl1dLbL0g","website":"https://toronto.ca/spadina","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d3f62fdc-e7d9-4b86-bc72-6cfd0934e234"},{"id":"df851463-0fe3-4e62-b450-628b48d1d4c8","name":"The Life of a Creature by Nadja Lubiw-Hazard – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1804636800000],"start":"2027-03-09T19:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-03-09T19:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":28,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nThrough interconnected stories, The Life of a Creature explores human-animal bonds. Nadja Lubiw-Hazard examines trauma, grief, healing and connection through characters including a veterinarian, a grieving mother and a woman reflecting on Chernobyl's feral dogs, revealing how all living beings are linked. She'll discuss the collection's themes, her approach to writing these bonds and how loss, resilience and transformation shape the stories.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnic alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"y6UlxWQBrC8Mq4YueQCtaQ","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/8e6d46bc-02a0-4756-9f61-5e366042241f"},{"id":"6412d09f-6379-4c57-9509-317b2dc1e937","name":"Harvest & Pumpkin Carving at Scarborough Museum","dates":[1792339200000,1792944000000],"start":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scarborough Museum ","address":"1007 Brimley Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1P 3E8","lat":43.757624,"lng":-79.25481},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the beauty of the harvest season at Scarborough Museum with a family-friendly pumpkin carving experience. Choose your pumpkin, create a unique design, and explore harvest traditions in one of Toronto's most historic settings.\n\nEnjoy seasonal refreshments while museum staff share stories about autumn customs, harvest celebrations, and fall traditions from the past. Participants will receive a pumpkin and carving materials, with the option to take their creation home or leave it on-site as part of a seasonal display.\n\nThis program is suitable for families, children, and adults looking to enjoy a creative fall activity together. Children ages 5 to 12 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nTickets: $15 per person\n Capacity: 10 participants per session\n Dates: October 18 and October 24, 2026\n Sessions: 12:00 to 1:30 p.m. and 2:00 to 3:30 p.m.","categories":["Artisan","Family/Children","History","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"kOg7jhWxHrSLwUfaPifI8A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/scarborough-museum/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/c283e33d-8e25-4921-9ad4-1bc99c03105f"},{"id":"cedde4e2-4815-41be-9825-c985f7cbfa7b","name":"Harvest & Pumpkin Carving at Scarborough Museum","dates":[1792339200000,1792944000000],"start":"2026-10-18T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scarborough Museum ","address":"1007 Brimley Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1P 3E8","lat":43.757624,"lng":-79.25481},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate the beauty of the harvest season at Scarborough Museum with a family-friendly pumpkin carving experience. Choose your pumpkin, create a unique design, and explore harvest traditions in one of Toronto's most historic settings.\n\nEnjoy seasonal refreshments while museum staff share stories about autumn customs, harvest celebrations, and fall traditions from the past. Participants will receive a pumpkin and carving materials, with the option to take their creation home or leave it on-site as part of a seasonal display.\n\nThis program is suitable for families, children, and adults looking to enjoy a creative fall activity together. Children ages 5 to 12 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nTickets: $15 per person\n Capacity: 10 participants per session\n Dates: October 18 and October 24, 2026\n Sessions: 12:00 to 1:30 p.m. and 2:00 to 3:30 p.m.","categories":["Artisan","Family/Children","History","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"kOg7jhWxHrSLwUfaPifI8A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/scarborough-museum/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/c283e33d-8e25-4921-9ad4-1bc99c03105f"},{"id":"4175e54a-491d-49e3-a56d-eac979d816aa","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"a314ae89-346d-495b-9e80-269561b8cf40","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"8858c071-2f53-48ea-a55b-6bdd778be08b","name":"YSpace Tech Accelerator Demo Day","dates":[1790892000000],"start":"2026-10-01T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-01T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto","address":"Location revealed after registration","lat":43.658884,"lng":-79.386176},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Tech Accelerator Demo Day is the final showcase of the 2026 cohort from YSpace's Tech Accelerator, a four-month program supporting high-potential tech startups. This year's cohort includes 10 founders who have spent the past several months building and scaling their companies. After submitting video pitches, the top 5 will take the stage to pitch live to an audience of investors, industry leaders, and startup supporters — competing for up to $30K in cash prizes.The evening will feature live pitches, networking, and an interactive People's Choice Award where attendees can vote for their favourite founder.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://luma.com/g52pnpxp","tickets":"https://luma.com/g52pnpxp"},{"id":"b04df179-cc48-4b35-9ca9-7e9669479caa","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"0f087cec-eac2-495b-9cf4-5e049abd9c9c","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":n