00,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"7e6da7ee-81f3-42cb-a7c5-905fe8115d48","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"c0489794-768d-401c-87cc-85afd7e99fc5","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"4fa7cd55-c43e-4ba7-88ab-7cf545f601b1","name":"Lantern Tours at Fort York: After Dark","dates":[1792711800000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1793316600000,1793403000000],"start":"2026-10-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"100 Garrison Rd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.638491,"lng":-79.40518},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Hear chilling and eerie tales on a lantern tour of Fort York and its historic surroundings. Learn about a haunted lighthouse and the bloody Battle of York. Explore the military burial ground. Tour the creepy shadows and 200-year-old buildings of Fort York at night and learn of the fort’s history and its many paranormal mysteries.","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"G-eno19UG31sj5aKkgxxQg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/09cc8903-6509-4ac3-9964-74a070bbb946"},{"id":"b430c94c-5f2a-41aa-98fc-caad63c4e594","name":"Remembrance Day at Fort York","dates":[1794411000000],"start":"2026-11-11T10:30:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-11T10:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"100 Garrison Rd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.63813,"lng":-79.408942},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Attend one of the City’s most evocative Remembrance Day ceremonies at Fort York National Historic Site. All are encouraged to take part in honouring and remembering the service and sacrifice of all Canadians, from diverse backgrounds and communities, who came together to serve and defend their homes and country. This year also marks the 100th Anniversary of the Royal Canadian Legion.  The ceremony is delivered in partnership with the IODE.\n\nAll are welcome to join a post-ceremony reception inside the Fort's Blue Barracks, where they can enjoy a hot drink and baked goods, and see the temporary Remembrance installation produced by \"They Walked These Streets\".","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Remembrance Day"],"presenter":null,"image":"9BnWOa2mI-uEVUOC6X7g6g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":null},{"id":"70c69b56-5eae-4ed6-a32c-276f5af47c1f","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"b46d40c5-0237-469e-9cb1-5826c72a45a9","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"a2f1f0ab-42c4-4295-bdb1-6131a8776d6d","name":"Fall Flavours &  Crafts at Scarborough Museum","dates":[1791039600000,1791126000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793458800000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scarborough Museum","address":"1007 Brimley Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1P 3E8","lat":43.757624474,"lng":-79.254809969},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy fall-themed fun at Scarborough Museum throughout October weekends. Sip a warm drink from the museum kitchen and savour a treat prepared on the historic stove. Spark creativity with family-friendly paper crafts, a scavenger hunt, and seasonal activities designed for all ages.\n\nAll ages. Drop-In. FREE. All are welcome. ","categories":["Family/Children","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"BA9dThVY5VHcVGOcWEUaCw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/scarborough-museum/","tickets":null},{"id":"bbda4185-af3a-488c-b565-ca463fbbcc04","name":"BAM! Nuit Blanche Night Market","dates":[1791068400000,1791154800000],"start":"2026-10-03T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Wychwood Barns","address":"601 Christie St, Toronto, ON, M6G 4C7","lat":43.679958839,"lng":-79.424094918},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a night of contemporary art! Our market supports local artists of all career stages! \n\nShop and explore the work of various talents within our diverse community.\n \nOver 35 professional artists will exhibit at BAM!, featuring jewellers, ceramists, poets, print makers and so much more! Meet new and emerging career artists at the BAM! Emerging Artist Centre.\n\nDon’t miss the other Nuit Blanche installations and activities happening all night long during Stories in Place at Wychwood Barns, and participate in a hands on art making experience with One Story, Four Places.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":null,"image":"HvogoSkaDpWEsqM0QYl8nQ","website":"https://wychwoodbarns.ca/bam-nuit-blanche-night-market-on-oct-3","tickets":null},{"id":"ddd12f6c-1c6e-41eb-bedb-95cb1fd9adf9","name":"Piece by Piece: Mosaics for Seniors at East Scarborough Storefront","dates":[1789578000000,1789750800000,1790182800000,1790355600000,1790787600000,1790960400000,1791392400000,1791565200000,1791997200000,1792170000000],"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-16T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join Mural Routes for a free multi-session mosaic art workshop series for older adults. Led by mosaic mural artist Cristina Delago, participants will learn mosaic-making techniques, create a personalized artwork to take home, and contribute to a larger community mosaic installation. A final culminating event held on October 23 will take place after workshops are complete to celebrate all participants and what they have accomplished.\n\nThe project is delivered through two separate cohorts running concurrently at different locations. Please ensure you select your intended workshop series (cohort), as each cohort has its own location and schedule. All materials are provided and advance registration is required.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Mural Routes","image":"F4gQpCvBNPCjggJ5mJPA0g","website":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/","tickets":"https://muralroutes.ca/mosaics-for-seniors-2026-storefront/"},{"id":"afaf55d6-9eb4-451d-955c-10feb9d2e405","name":"Kayaking at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789075800000,1789221600000,1789680600000,1789826400000,1790285400000,1790431200000,1790890200000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-10T17:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Register using the correct link below:\nSat September 26 Kayaking\n10 am, 12 pm, 2:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999635854670\nThursday Oct 1 Kayaking\n5:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2002225124245\n\n","description":"Discover Toronto’s newest waterfront destination from a whole new perspective! Join Don't Mess with The Don for an unforgettable guided kayaking experience at Biidaasige Park. Paddle through calm waters, enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, and connect with nature in one of Toronto’s most exciting new parks.\n\nWhether you’re a first-time paddler or an experienced kayaker, this welcoming session is designed for all skill levels. The DMWTD experienced team will provide equipment, safety instruction, and on-water guidance so you can relax and enjoy the adventure.\n\nBring your sense of exploration, dress for the weather, and get ready to experience the beauty of Toronto’s waterfront at golden hour. Spaces are limited and advance registration is required.\n\nPerfect for: beginners, outdoor enthusiasts, friends, families, and anyone looking for a fun activity on the water.\n\nCome paddle, explore, and make summer memories at Biidaasige Park! 🚣‍♀️🌊☀️","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"Za-23fnhcvn_BacwEju5hw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/kayaking","tickets":null},{"id":"d16c7ff8-ba78-4bbf-bb03-8bb6b2c1f6ba","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"35836a65-34e5-4e6d-b574-bf11db9a1585","name":"Music Toronto - Esmé Quartet","dates":[1802392200000],"start":"2027-02-11T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-11T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nSubscribe and Save up to 40%","description":"Having thrilled Music Toronto audiences in 2022 with their elegance, precision and energy, the Esmé Quartet returns with a program of drama, rhythm, and sweeping lyricism. \n\nSamuel Barber’s Quartet, Op. 11 features the haunting slow movement later arranged as the famous Adagio for Strings. John Adams’s Book of Alleged Dances brims with folk energy and playful rhythm, while Antonín Dvořák’s majestic Quartet in G major, Op. 106 crowns the evening with radiant melody and power.\n","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"l6UBwNWKpBIYe67wb5bfhA","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/esme-quartet","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/esme-quartet"},{"id":"125b3b95-5fa9-40eb-a3a9-800f98b935fe","name":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit","dates":[1790791200000,1790877600000,1790949600000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front Street West, Toronto, ON M5V 2W6","lat":43.64392037329108,"lng":-79.38668733673923},"free":false,"low":275,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Local Delegate – All 4 Days: CA$275.00 (With discount code CA$137.50), Local Delegate – Day 3 Only: CA$140.00 (with code CA$70.00), Local Delegate – Day 4 Only: CA$200.00 (with discount code CA$100.00), Student Admission (Valid Student ID Required): CA$70.00 Marketplace Vendor: CA$250.00 (with discount code CA$125.00), They can use the discount code 2026FOA they can enjoy 50% off expires Sep 12.","description":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit is a four-day hybrid conference, taking place virtually on September 30 - October 1, 2026, and in person on October 2-3, 2026 at the Metro Toronto Convention Centre in Toronto, Ontario. The Summit brings together entrepreneurs, startups, investors, business leaders, and ecosystem partners from Canada and Africa. It features expert panels, workshops, startup pitches, networking, business matchmaking, and a career fair, creating opportunities for investment, partnerships, entrepreneurship, and Canada - Africa economic collaboration.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Friends of Africa Coalition","image":"XOz0W9bL3jJbnbVI5aIgTg","website":"https://friendsofafrica.ca/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/16th-african-economic-summit-friends-of-africa-2026-tickets-1803110374669?discount=2026FOA"},{"id":"65fdaf06-c2c3-4895-a530-45dd844af390","name":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit","dates":[1790791200000,1790877600000,1790949600000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front Street West, Toronto, ON M5V 2W6","lat":43.64392037329108,"lng":-79.38668733673923},"free":false,"low":275,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Local Delegate – All 4 Days: CA$275.00 (With discount code CA$137.50), Local Delegate – Day 3 Only: CA$140.00 (with code CA$70.00), Local Delegate – Day 4 Only: CA$200.00 (with discount code CA$100.00), Student Admission (Valid Student ID Required): CA$70.00 Marketplace Vendor: CA$250.00 (with discount code CA$125.00), They can use the discount code 2026FOA they can enjoy 50% off expires Sep 12.","description":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit is a four-day hybrid conference, taking place virtually on September 30 - October 1, 2026, and in person on October 2-3, 2026 at the Metro Toronto Convention Centre in Toronto, Ontario. The Summit brings together entrepreneurs, startups, investors, business leaders, and ecosystem partners from Canada and Africa. It features expert panels, workshops, startup pitches, networking, business matchmaking, and a career fair, creating opportunities for investment, partnerships, entrepreneurship, and Canada - Africa economic collaboration.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Friends of Africa Coalition","image":"XOz0W9bL3jJbnbVI5aIgTg","website":"https://friendsofafrica.ca/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/16th-african-economic-summit-friends-of-africa-2026-tickets-18031103