00028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"b67194b0-2291-4e15-b4b5-4e3fbab9977f","name":"LUMINOUS 2026: A Photography Exhibit","dates":[1791051300000,1791054900000,1792018800000],"start":"2026-10-03T14:15:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-14T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Heliconian Club","address":"35 Hazelton Ave. Toronto, Ontario  M5R 2E3 ​Canada","lat":43.671854,"lng":-79.393329},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Come see an exhibition of fourteen women photographers. Eight performance artists engage with the spirit of selected photographs.This interaction of art disciplines is called 'ekphrasis.' \n\nPhotographers include Linda Briskin, Brianna Caryll, Lucie Collins, Martha Davis, Kye Marshall, Denise Roberts, Jana Skarecky and Henrietta Walmark, with Taivi, Brianna (Bri) Clarke, Kate Marshall Flaherty, Bianca Lakoseljac, Kye Marshall, Elizabeth Ruth, Jana Skarecky and JC Sulzenko. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Dance","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"Czpl0jvO9kvDifyfex7R2g","website":"https://www.heliconianclub.org/","tickets":null},{"id":"911e90f9-a9c4-46e2-adaf-1f0d34aa486a","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"43ad5649-038d-4a78-9fb7-d295e0bfc6be","name":"TRCA Adventures of Salmon","dates":[1791122400000],"start":"2026-10-04T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Morningside Park","address":"390 Morningside Ave, Scarborough","lat":43.780204048,"lng":-79.191613333},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for a fun, educational day of discovery as you learn about the incredible journey of salmon in the Greater Toronto Area during their annual fall migration.\n\nExplore interactive educational stations to discover:\n• Salmon life cycle and migration\n• Salmon species teachings\n• Learn about The Meadoway project\n• Meet the TRCA Aquatic Monitoring team\n• Indigenous engagement and storytelling\n• Fishing demonstrations\n• Arts and crafts\n• Kids’ games and activities\n\nExplore a Stretch of Highland Creek:\nExperience the salmon migration firsthand as you explore a scenic section of Highland Creek.\n\nVisitors are welcome to enjoy a self-guided walk along the well-signed interpretive trail, where educational signage highlights the incredible journey of salmon, their life cycle, the local watershed, and the important conservation efforts that help protect this ecosystem.\n\nOptional guided walks to view salmon in the creek will be offered approximately every 30 minutes throughout the event. ","categories":["Environmental","Family/Children"],"presenter":null,"image":"vTxsGd1M-XuKFp4QyCj-6g","website":"https://calendar.trca.ca/event/trca-adventures-of-salmon/","tickets":"https://calendar.trca.ca/event/trca-adventures-of-salmo"},{"id":"74c54227-d921-4653-9c8f-330440ef4320","name":"Fall Flavours &  Crafts at Scarborough Museum","dates":[1791039600000,1791126000000,1791644400000,1791730800000,1792249200000,1792335600000,1792854000000,1792940400000,1793458800000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Scarborough Museum","address":"1007 Brimley Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1P 3E8","lat":43.757624474,"lng":-79.254809969},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy fall-themed fun at Scarborough Museum throughout October weekends. Sip a warm drink from the museum kitchen and savour a treat prepared on the historic stove. Spark creativity with family-friendly paper crafts, a scavenger hunt, and seasonal activities designed for all ages.\n\nAll ages. Drop-In. FREE. All are welcome. ","categories":["Family/Children","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"BA9dThVY5VHcVGOcWEUaCw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/scarborough-museum/","tickets":null},{"id":"60fbb971-fac7-4da2-bb10-201510f4a3e7","name":"Falstaff Community Centre - 2:30 to 4:30 p.m.","dates":[1791138600000],"start":"2026-10-04T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-04T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Falstaff Community Centre","address":"15 Falstaff Ave, North York, ON, M6L 2C6","lat":43.715250314,"lng":-79.505996228},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Try something new, get moving and connect through sport, Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels.\n\nWith a variety of sports equipment on board, vibrant vans tour neighbourhoods, transforming parks and outdoor spaces into pop-up sport hubs, bringing energy and excitement directly to communities around the city. Proudly powered in partnership with Nike, Play Mobile is committed to the future of youth sport, creating more equitable and inclusive access to play – with a focus on encouraging girls to participate and stay involved in sport.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"JY5NZWRAS6Lt1TXJKw_GWw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=44%20Tobermory%20Dr&lat=43.762598&lng=-79.512091&zoom=17","tickets":null},{"id":"37754e06-5fdd-404d-95e4-7da38999c49d","name":"Lantern Tours at Montgomery's Inn: Beyond Mourning","dates":[1792879200000,1792886400000,1792965600000,1792972800000,1793311200000,1793318400000,1793397600000,1793404800000],"start":"2026-10-24T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T20:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"This Halloween, uncover eerie tales about the past inhabitants of the Inn and the Old Town of Islington. Journey from the dimly lit historic house to the Islington burial ground, learn about Victorian death practices, and hear new stories connecting to Toronto’s past. \n\nContent warning: Topics include illness, death and related subjects.\nRecommended for ages 14 and up. Anyone under 17 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"OGMQ_a1JowZ9TDZayyn_6Q","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/aae32edb-e8f5-4760-b053-81cb44cc2186"},{"id":"04bfc9da-d1fb-46d3-8bb7-4d2631b42e76","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1796734800000,1796821200000,1796907600000,1796994000000,1797087600000,1797253200000,1797339600000],"start":"2026-09-01T08:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-12-15T08:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery","address":"399 The West Mall, Etobicoke, ON, M9C 2Y2","lat":43.643772026,"lng":-79.565452785},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover the history of art at the Etobicoke Civic Centre with artifacts, prints, images and paintings from City of Toronto’s Fine Art, Artifact and Archival collections. Celebrate the present by witnessing a commissioned piece by early career artist Lise Round. Envision the future with new designs of the updated Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"A6-VIKDNvgJfy1_SuU-UqA","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/etobicoke-civic-centre-art-gallery/?WT.rd_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"d1a47fcc-73b1-45b4-b6b7-fda1adecb131","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,179327520