ourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"81698766-fbfb-4177-b59a-20ecf73ec6fc","name":"The Descent of Orpheus","dates":[1792711800000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1792953000000],"start":"2026-10-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-25T14:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"TELUS Centre for Performance and Learning at Koerner Hall","address":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1W2","lat":43.667856304,"lng":-79.396058814},"free":false,"low":85,"high":250,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy our season premiere with Canada’s first fully-staged production of M.A. Charpentier’s The Descent of Orpheus. \n\nFounding Co-Artistic Directors Marshall Pynkoski, C.M. and Jeannette Lajeunesse Zingg, C.M. direct and choreograph this fresh, contemporary, and emotionally-driven staging of Charpentier’s masterpiece, grounded in the concept of period performance. \n\nThe production is the earliest known French operatic take on the Orpheus myth from Ovid's Metamorphoses. Celebrated American tenor Daniel McGrew is making his Canadian debut with Opera Atelier as Orpheus opposite French-Canadian soprano Mireille Asselin as Eurydice. ","categories":["Dance","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":"Opera Atelier","image":"5Kjgp2yeVCQPw_sKJnSawg","website":"https://www.operaatelier.com/shows/the-descent-of-orpheus/","tickets":"https://www.rcmusic.com/concerts?tps_activeFacetTab=Concerts%20Presented%20By%20Others&fq=eventpresenter%7C%7COpera+Atelier"},{"id":"0563d390-467e-4d9c-a50e-341ed70fd816","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"2a6361d5-cd57-4d4b-891a-3bacbc00ccff","name":"Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale","dates":[1791037800000,1791124200000,1791210600000,1791297000000,1791383400000,1791469800000,1791556200000,1791642600000,1791729000000,1791815400000,1791901800000,1791988200000,1792074600000,1792161000000,1792247400000,1792333800000],"start":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Botanical Garden","address":"777 Lawrence Ave E, North York, ON, M3C 1P2","lat":43.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toront