.734346145,"lng":-79.358667018},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrating art, nature and community! \n\nEnjoy over 100 original artworks created outdoors by 46 talented local artists at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens and participate in artist-led workshops and more!\n\nThis curated, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here, capturing moments of light, movement, and the essence of the natural world.\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"dTOLixZ5zgHzXQkFocfpqg","website":"https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/","tickets":null},{"id":"78c5a4ee-fe0e-4f9a-b093-23f6020e59ac","name":"Community BioBlitz","dates":[1791039600000],"start":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fred Young Park","address":"440 Cook Rd, North York","lat":43.766930284,"lng":-79.505365389},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"To commemorate Ravine Days, Environmental Education for a Better Earth (EEFABE) Canada invite community members, youth, and families to participate in a special Community BioBlitz dedicated to exploring and documenting the rich biodiversity of Black Creek Parkland and Ravine.\n\nUsing the citizen science platform iNaturalist, participants will work together to observe, photograph, and identify plants, birds, insects, fungi, and other wildlife found throughout the park. Guided survey groups will explore different habitats, including riparian areas, wetlands, forested zones, and meadow edges, helping to create valuable biodiversity records while learning directly from nature.\n\nWhether you are an experienced naturalist or simply curious about the environment, everyone is welcome to join. Facilitators and volunteers will be available throughout the event to help participants identify species, improve observation quality, and contribute meaningful data to biodiversity monitoring efforts.","categories":["Charity/Cause","Environmental","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"WY1ufz7Dj0nmdwulTeeJhw","website":"https://eefabecanada.org/event/community-bioblitz-biodiversity-blackcreek/","tickets":"https://eefabecanada.org/event/community-bioblitz-biodiversity-blackcreek/"},{"id":"6b0d121a-ec59-4fa6-817b-e02d2ba9e5c0","name":"Art for Alzheimer’s","dates":[1793894400000,1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000],"start":"2026-11-05T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-29T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361,"lng":-79.360334},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Art for Alzheimer’s brings together an exceptional collection of original artwork by Canadian illustrator Doug Martin in support of the Alzheimer Society. \n\nSpanning 40 years of his career, the exhibition showcases original and commissioned works, offering guests the opportunity to discover, appreciate, and purchase one-of-a-kind artwork while supporting an important cause.\n\nAll proceeds will go to support Alzheimer's Society of York Region.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Charity/Cause"],"presenter":"Wherry and Associates Private Wealth Management","image":"rpynIin-O7Wi-LCJZ7z-Rg","website":"https://www.wherryandassociates.ca/events-and-seminars","tickets":null},{"id":"374ab05f-c819-4ccc-bb89-bbe8b00abbaa","name":"Youth Voices Creative Workshop Series","dates":[1790200800000,1790805600000,1791410400000,1792015200000,1792620000000],"start":"2026-09-23T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766004,"lng":-79.199012},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join a free arts-based program where youth can explore different forms of creative expression while developing original work for a community showcase. Through weekly workshops, participants will experiment with a range of artistic disciplines, build creative skills, and collaborate with peers and facilitators in a supportive environment. Through the program, youth will explore and express their experiences, identities, and perspectives through the arts. The program culminates in the Youth Voices Community Showcase, held on October 22 at Tropicana Community Services 1385 Huntingwood Dr., Scarborough, ON, M1S 3J1, where participants will share their work and celebrate the creativity of local youth.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops","Other"],"presenter":"East Scarborough Storefront","image":"P5CxD-jd5C-8DdRxgpxBRA","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"8005d99c-d1fa-4412-81b3-b7bc5befe321","name":"Youth Voices Creative Workshop Series","dates":[1790200800000,1790805600000,1791410400000,1792015200000,1792620000000],"start":"2026-09-23T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-21T18:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766004,"lng":-79.199012},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join a free arts-based program where youth can explore different forms of creative expression while developing original work for a community showcase. Through weekly workshops, participants will experiment with a range of artistic disciplines, build creative skills, and collaborate with peers and facilitators in a supportive environment. Through the program, youth will explore and express their experiences, identities, and perspectives through the arts. The program culminates in the Youth Voices Community Showcase, held on October 22 at Tropicana Community Services 1385 Huntingwood Dr., Scarborough, ON, M1S 3J1, where participants will share their work and celebrate the creativity of local youth.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot Signature Project.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Seminars/Workshops","Other"],"presenter":"East Scarborough Storefront","image":"P5CxD-jd5C-8DdRxgpxBRA","website":null,"tickets":null},{"id":"bdb43595-1ee8-4bc6-abee-7310a3ed0af3","name":"50 Years of Etobicoke Civic Centre Art Gallery Exhibition - 50th Anniversary","dates":[1788264000000,1788350400000,1788436800000,1788523200000,1788616800000,1788782400000,1788868800000,1788955200000,1789041600000,1789128000000,1789221600000,1789387200000,1789473600000,1789560000000,1789646400000,1789732800000,1789826400000,1789992000000,1790078400000,1790164800000,1790251200000,1790337600000,1790431200000,1790596800000,1790683200000,1790769600000,1790856000000,1790942400000,1791036000000,1791201600000,1791288000000,1791374400000,1791460800000,1791547200000,1791640800000,1791806400000,1791892800000,1791979200000,1792065600000,1792152000000,1792245600000,1792411200000,1792497600000,1792584000000,1792670400000,1792756800000,1792850400000,1793016000000,1793102400000,1793188800000,1793275200000,1793361600000,1793455200000,1793624400000,1793710800000,1793797200000,1793883600000,1793970000000,1794063600000,1794229200000,1794315600000,1794402000000,1794488400000,1794574800000,1794668400000,1794834000000,1794920400000,1795006800000,1795093200000,1795179600000,1795273200000,1795438800000,1795525200000,1795611600000,1795698000000,1795784400000,1795878000000,1796043600000,1796130000000,1796216400000,1796302800000,1796389200000,1796482800000,1796648400000,1