d_id=%2Feccartgallery","tickets":null},{"id":"b6d827a1-7c51-4ea5-a559-702484e6ff61","name":"Toronto International Festival of Authors 2026","dates":[1793212200000,1793298600000,1793385000000,1793455200000,1793547000000],"start":"2026-10-28T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T10:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Victoria University at the University of Toronto","address":"91 Charles St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1K5","lat":43.666951,"lng":-79.392113},"free":false,"low":15,"high":159,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n5-Day, 2-Day, and Single Day Passes available. Masterclasses require separate registration. Box office also available on site during Festival hours.","description":"Welcome to Canada’s largest and longest-running literary festival.! \n\nThis fall, TIFA 2026 brings the world’s most compelling writers into conversation with one another and with you. Join us for over 100 events with some of the world’s most beloved authors.\n\nFrom author conversations to electric readings and intimate masterclasses, the Festival is where stories cross borders, ideas find each other, and readers discover that literature is very much alive. \n\nThis year’s guestlist includes Barbara Kingsolver, Dave Eggers, Marie Ndiaye, Ann-Marie MacDonald, Andrew Sean Greer, Patrick deWitt, David Szalay, Vivek Shraya, Canisia Lubrin and Téa Mutonji.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"xo8dfCMetGe-UyXKAAVoiA","website":"https://festivalofauthors.ca/festival/?utm_source=eventlisting&utm_medium=eventlisting&utm_campaign=fallfestival","tickets":"https://festivalofauthors.ca/festival/?utm_source=eventlisting&utm_medium=eventlisting&utm_campaign=fallfestival"},{"id":"5cb81cd0-1be6-4952-85f8-d9771d58ca13","name":"Toronto International Festival of Authors 2026","dates":[1793212200000,1793298600000,1793385000000,1793455200000,1793547000000],"start":"2026-10-28T14:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-01T10:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Victoria University at the University of Toronto","address":"91 Charles St W, Toronto, ON, M5S 1K5","lat":43.666951,"lng":-79.392113},"free":false,"low":15,"high":159,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\n5-Day, 2-Day, and Single Day Passes available. Masterclasses require separate registration. Box office also available on site during Festival hours.","description":"Welcome to Canada’s largest and longest-running literary festival.! \n\nThis fall, TIFA 2026 brings the world’s most compelling writers into conversation with one another and with you. Join us for over 100 events with some of the world’s most beloved authors.\n\nFrom author conversations to electric readings and intimate masterclasses, the Festival is where stories cross borders, ideas find each other, and readers discover that literature is very much alive. \n\nThis year’s guestlist includes Barbara Kingsolver, Dave Eggers, Marie Ndiaye, Ann-Marie MacDonald, Andrew Sean Greer, Patrick deWitt, David Szalay, Vivek Shraya, Canisia Lubrin and Téa Mutonji.","categories":["Literary","Live Performances"],"presenter":null,"image":"xo8dfCMetGe-UyXKAAVoiA","website":"https://festivalofauthors.ca/festival/?utm_source=eventlisting&utm_medium=eventlisting&utm_campaign=fallfestival","tickets":"https://festivalofauthors.ca/festival/?utm_source=eventlisting&utm_medium=eventlisting&utm_campaign=fallfestival"},{"id":"76d7d5bc-ddd7-4d6d-8aec-37e1cdeaafe8","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"be9854de-e942-492d-824e-6502a25e4bc4","name":"Crothers Woods Trail Stewardship Event","dates":[1792332000000],"start":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-18T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Crothers Woods","address":"200 Pottery Rd, East York","lat":43.68933986,"lng":-79.362775138},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nThis event is not suitable for small children or large groups. All attendees must register. Email us to register.","description":"Help steward, repair and improve the natural surface trails at Crothers Woods. \n\nPlease note, there are no washroom facilities on site. Event site conditions vary. Contact us for more information, including accessibility. If you would like to request accessibility support, contact us as soon as possible.","categories":["Environmental"],"presenter":null,"image":"51pUu7Wc878qRW2n7r34-g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/ge\\t-involved/volunteer-with-the-city/tree-planting-stewardship/","tickets":null},{"id":"2549dd08-cbe8-492d-806c-02b2d28a949a","name":"Night Shift","dates":[1792116000000,1792202400000,1792288800000],"start":"2026-10-15T22:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T22:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Citadel: Ross Centre for Dance","address":"304 Parliament St, Toronto, ON, M5A 3A4","lat":43.659033595,"lng":-79.366104722},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us at The Citadel for an immersive experience like no other. Enjoy nine unique performances programmed by curator BaKari IfaSegun Lindsay.\n\nNight Shift is an annual late-night fest that celebrates the many innovative and thought-provoking dance forms explored and practiced by Ontario-based artists.\n\nThis year, we are excited to welcome the following artists:\nTeagan Ariss, Kimia Farokhzad, Jayden Gigliotti, K.H. Kanna, Kemora Manning, Yvonne Ng, Buyi Philip, Takako Segawa, Winterhawk","categories":["Dance","Live Performances"],"presenter":"Citadel + Compagnie","image":"iYEZ53B9VDErVDghllkkZQ","website":"https://www.citadelcie.com/event/night-shift-2026/","tickets":"https://citadelcie.tickit.ca/events/35294"},{"id":"2311a1e1-2537-4b8e-8b32-77ab88e85823","name":"Early Holiday Market","dates":[1794672000000],"start":"2026-11-14T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-14T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Ground Control","address":"1279 Queen St W, Toronto, ON, M6K 1L6","lat":43.641358725,"lng":-79.431866066},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Nothing beats getting your holiday shopping done well in advance so you can put your feet up, eat shortbread and listen to carols while everyone else is going bonkers.\n\nPlease join us as we host over 35 artists and artisans ready to help you check everyone off your list with the coolest, creepiest gifts imaginable!\n\nOur market is (mostly) kid-friendly and the bar will be open for customers to enjoy a beverage while they shop.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Artisan","Consumer Show/Convention","Winter Holidays"],"presenter":null,"image":"sKI2EWIGAIB6TcD6Py4_VA","website":"https://www.torontodarkartsmarket.com","tickets":null},{"id":"8f41eb55-8904-4866-bb85-6a394e977c4d","name":"Riverdale Park East - 11 a.m. to 1 p.m.","dates":[1791644400000],"start":"2026-10-10T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-10T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Riverdale Park East","address":"550 Broadview Ave, Toronto","lat":43.671456859,"lng":-79.355162656},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Play Mobile is a free touring sports program for all ages and skill levels, no registration or reservations are required to participate. The new soccer Play Mobile is dedicated to the world’s most popular game. All ages are invited to learn and celebrate soccer in a fun, supportive environment with no experience required.","categories":["Sports"],"presenter":null,"image":"D-JBEvzzMMBRxdflGESP0g","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/parks-and-community-recreation-centres-map/#location=2231%20Lawrence%20Ave%20E&lat=43.747352&lng=-79.280467&zoom=11","tickets":null},{"id":"c26b7140-6d93-4d10-b4e8-e6c273bc33dd","name":"Rebirth: The Quiet Becoming Installation at Fort York","dates":[1785938400000,1786024800000,1786111200000,1786197600000,1786284000000,1786543200000,1786629600000,1786716000000,1786802400000,1786888800000,1787148000000,1787234400000,1787320800000,1787407200000,1787493600000,1787752800000,1787839200000,1787925600000,1788012000000,1788098400000,1788357600000,1788444000000,1788530400000,1788616800000,1788703200000,1788962400000,1789048800000,1789135200000,1789221600000,1789308000000,1789567200000,1789653600000,1789740000000,1789826400000,1789912800000,1790172000000,1790258400000,1790344800000,1790431200000,1790517600000,1790776800000,1790863200000,1790949600000,1791036000000,1791122400000,1791381600000,1791468000000,1791554400000,1791640800000,1791727200000,1791986400000,1792072800000,1792159200000,1792245600000,1792332000000,1792591200000,1792677600000,1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000,1793455200000],"start":"2026-08-05T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"250 Fort York Blvd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.637864096,"lng":-79.406314887},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience a bold new outdoor installation on the Gardiner Expressway beside Fort York Visitor Centre. Created by artists Delali Cofie and Yuma Dean Hester, it reimagines the site’s layered histories through contemporary art. An accompanying exhibition inside the Visitor Centre deepens the experience, inviting visitors to encounter the Fort as a living cultural landscape shaped by reflection, dialogue and collaboration.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"_QHlUAQMVyNc88AaSDfQ8A","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":null},{"id":"115b10ab-9c88-4f87-a4d2-2e9c65d3e8da","name":"Lantern Tours: Macabre Tales at Todmorden Mills","dates":[1793226600000,1793313000000,1793399400000,1793485800000],"start":"2026-10-28T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361228,"lng":-79.36033401},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an unforgettable evening of creepy stories spanning the 1890s, 1940s and present. Explore the historic Helliwell House and the Cottage, where local legends and chilling tales come to life. After your enhanced tour, warm up with a cozy drink in the Brewery Building.","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"NX5CLZgv1sVhCnb3c1A40w","website":null,"tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/fa1ecb23-0130-4fb4-bf32-86c11590d459"},{"id":"53ee479f-ab72-4982-ad51-1bfee1a72a3f","name":"Lantern Tours: Macabre Tales at Todmorden Mills","dates":[1793226600000,1793313000000,1793399400000,1793485800000],"start":"2026-10-28T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361228,"lng":-79.36033401},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an unforgettable evening of creepy stories spanning the 1890s, 1940s and present. Explore the historic Helliwell House and the Cottage, where local legends and chilling tales come to life. After your enhanced tour, warm up with a cozy drink in the Brewery Building.","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"NX5CLZgv1sVhCnb3c1A40w","website":null,"tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/fa1ecb23-0130-4fb4-bf32-86c11590d459"},{"id":"634a1a48-6b1b-4b11-aa1e-7feb14fe3f31","name":"Night Shift","dates":[1792116000000,1792202400000,1792288800000],"start":"2026-10-15T22:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T22:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"The Citadel: Ross Centre for Dance","address":"304 Parliament St, Toronto, ON, M5A 3A4","lat":43.659033595,"lng":-79.366104722},"free":false,"low":15,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us at The Citadel for an immersive experience like no other. Enjoy nine unique performances programmed by curator BaKari IfaSegun Lindsay.\n\nNight Shift is an annual late-night fest that celebrates the many innovative and thought-provoking dance forms explored and practiced by Ontario-based artists.\n\nThis year, we are excited to welcome the following artists:\nTeagan Ariss, Kimia Farokhzad, Jayden Gigliotti, K.H. Kanna, Kemora Manning, Yvonne Ng, Buyi Philip, Takako Segawa, Winterhawk","categories":["Dance","Live Performances"],"presenter":"Citadel + Compagnie","image":"iYEZ53B9VDErVDghllkkZQ","website":"https://www.citadelcie.com/event/night-shift-2026/","tickets":"https://citadelcie.tickit.ca/events/35294"},{"id":"0041e5a9-f182-4995-aa76-d7576b8f1719","name":"By the Lake Book Club – 3-Event Package (2027)","dates":[1820962800000],"start":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":55,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nEnjoy the final three By the Lake Book Club events of 2027 for just $55. Join Humber Polytechnic alumni as they dive into conversation with leading Canadian authors. This package features Tyler Pennock, Gillian Deacon and Carrianne Leung. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. \n\nThe signature series features six Tuesday-night events, between February and December. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation.\n\nTyler Pennock - September 14, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nGillian Deacon - October 5, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nCarrianne Leung - December 7, 2027 at 7 p.m.\n\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#multipacks/f89d2f6f-5509-40a1-b58c-a5d199cbe683"},{"id":"8fca5d2d-59ac-4cbc-bdda-80293bceec68","name":"Paddleboarding at Biidaasige Park","dates":[1789223400000,1789828200000,1790433000000,1791037800000],"start":"2026-09-12T10:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Biidaasige Park ","address":"51 Commissioners St, Toronto, ON, M5A 1A6","lat":43.646495807,"lng":-79.348925214},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Please register using the correct link below:\nSat September 12 Paddleboarding\n10:30 am, 12:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999636049252\nSat September 19 Paddleboarding\n10:30 am, 12:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999638061270\nSat September 26 Paddleboarding\n10:30 am, 12:30 pm - https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1999638111420\n\n","description":"Get out on the water and experience Biidaasige Park from a whole new perspective! Join Don’t Mess with the Don for a fun and refreshing paddleboarding adventure along Toronto’s stunning new waterfront park. Whether you’re a first-timer or an experienced paddler, this is a great way to connect with nature, enjoy the river, and take in the park’s unique landscapes from the water. All equipment is provided, including a paddleboard, paddle, and personal flotation device (PFD). \n\nParticipants will have up to 1.5 hours to explore at their own pace. Please wear weather-appropriate clothing and water shoes, and bring water to stay hydrated. Recommended for ages 12+. \n\nCome discover the beauty of Biidaasige Park, build confidence on the water, and enjoy an unforgettable summer morning outdoors!","categories":["Environmental","Sports","Tour"],"presenter":null,"image":"L4b1C942bMoMQdF9ic2Ofw","website":"https://www.dontmesswiththedon.ca/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1998641932823"},{"id":"30cd9aa4-df04-4f04-9474-f71bcfa25b90","name":"4th Annual United Way Haunted Garden Walk","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000,1792936800000,1793023200000,1793109600000,1793196000000,1793282400000,1793368800000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Rosetta McClain Gardens","address":"5 Glen Everest Rd, Scarborough, ON, M1N 1J2","lat":43.697429373,"lng":-79.255632193},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Donations in support of United Way are appreciated.","description":"It's spooky season at the Rosetta McClain Gardens. The gardens are transformed into a fun and spooky Halloween experience for families, children and community members to enjoy a self-guided tour.\nEntry is free but donations of any amount are accepted. All donations collected go directly to the United Way. ","categories":["Charity/Cause","Family/Children","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"-W4ubxPgzvotoaO_DhFMkg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/parks-recreation/places-spaces/parks-and-recreation-facilities/location/?id=19","tickets":null},{"id":"cd4ba9fe-0ae1-49ce-8c1d-6ba7bcc03d35","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"3c67623f-d272-4874-b764-6097a5ee313b","name":"Turning in the Light Exhibition","dates":[1791032400000,1791118800000,1791205200000,1791291600000,1791378000000,1791464400000,1791550800000,1791637200000,1791723600000,1791810000000,1791896400000,1791982800000,1792069200000,1792155600000,1792242000000,1792328400000,1792414800000,1792501200000,1792587600000,1792674000000,1792760400000,1792846800000,1792933200000,1793019600000,1793106000000,1793192400000,1793278800000],"start":"2026-10-03T09:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-29T09:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Clark Centre for the Arts","address":"191 Guildwood Pkwy, Scarborough, ON, M1E 1P5","lat":43.746893127,"lng":-79.193688812},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Be inspired by Katharine Harvey's new body of work which explores the remarkable architectural fragments preserved at Guild Park. Historic stone carvings rescued from demolished Toronto buildings now coexist with forests, gardens and Lake Ontario. Through vibrant paintings, Harvey reveals layered stories that connect built heritatge, nature and memory, inviting viewers to see the park with fresh eyes.\n\nAbout the Artist\nKatharine Harvey is a Canadian conceptual painter and multi-media artist based in Toronto. Throughout her career, she has switched naturally between mediums, allowing her paintings to inform her public artwork and vice versa. This process inspired Katharine to create a body of work that includes multi-layered acrylic paintings, recycled plastic installations, monumental public art, kinetic sculptures and an illuminated drone show.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits"],"presenter":null,"image":"7EEr156fHjrgxMEyH4K5ew","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/clark-centre-for-the-arts/","tickets":null},{"id":"4e36d31d-cb21-4539-996a-3ea58ad63ef6","name":"Lantern Tours: Macabre Tales at Todmorden Mills","dates":[1793226600000,1793313000000,1793399400000,1793485800000],"start":"2026-10-28T18:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-31T18:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Todmorden Mills Heritage Site","address":"67 Pottery Rd, East York, ON, M4K 2B9","lat":43.686361228,"lng":-79.36033401},"free":false,"low":22,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Join us for an unforgettable evening of creepy stories spanning the 1890s, 1940s and present. Explore the historic Helliwell House and the Cottage, where local legends and chilling tales come to life. After your enhanced tour, warm up with a cozy drink in the Brewery Building.","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"NX5CLZgv1sVhCnb3c1A40w","website":null,"tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/fa1ecb23-0130-4fb4-bf32-86c11590d459"},{"id":"f101b40a-1800-4921-b2bc-0ed262cc98dc","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"7f95dab2-dbf5-496d-b09f-7eead73b2fdd","name":"Sala-Manca Group: Like a Bird’s Nest","dates":[1790204400000,1790269200000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790787600000,1790874000000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791392400000,1791478800000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791997200000,1792083600000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792602000000,1792688400000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793206800000,1793293200000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793815200000,1793901600000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794420000000,1794506400000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795024800000,1795111200000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795629600000,1795716000000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000],"start":"2026-09-23T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-29T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNote