","venue":{"name":"PIX FILM Gallery","address":"1411 Dufferin St, Toronto, ON, M6H 4C7","lat":43.670941,"lng":-79.439848},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Enjoy a landmark retrospective from the international artist collective, the Sala-Manca Group.\n\nInstallation, video and photography are exhibited together for the first time, all connected to the ritual object of the sukkah, a temporary hut traditionally erected during the Jewish festival of Sukkot.\n\nOver the last twenty years, Sala-Manca has explored the symbolism and function of the sukkah and related themes of shelter, impermanence, displacement, and liberation. In their hands, the sukkah is interchangeably a ritual structure, an ethnographic object, a work of art, an ephemeral monument, a site of protest, and a performative arena. \n\nThis exhibition traverses unlikely geographies, travelling through time and place, from a small town in Germany where no Jews remain to a Jahalin Bedouin community in Khan al-Ahmar; from the contested streets of Jerusalem to the fraught landscapes of Ontario. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Talks"],"presenter":"Fentster Gallery","image":"T7PtQvwfAsgTqCPeW8LzYw","website":"https://fentster.org/birds-nest","tickets":null},{"id":"f0ce66e1-46ca-4898-90b7-7ed61d731344","name":"Music Toronto - Duo Concertante with the Dior Quartet","dates":[1803429000000],"start":"2027-02-23T19:30:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-23T19:30:00-05:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Jane Mallett Theatre, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts","address":"27 Front St E, Toronto, ON, M5E 1B4","lat":43.647405296,"lng":-79.375214232},"free":false,"low":40,"high":70,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nSubscribe and Save up to 40%","description":"Join us for one of Canada’s pre-eminent chamber ensembles, Duo Concertante, with violinist Nancy Dahn and pianist Timothy Steeves. \n\nCelebrated internationally for its expressive depth and remarkable musical unity. They open the program with Luigi Dallapiccola’s Tartiniana Seconda, a brilliant reimagining of Baroque violin music, and a sonata by Ludwig van Beethoven in this Beethoven anniversary year.\n\nVince Ho’s playful Donut Suite adds dazzling wit before the second half, when they join the dynamic Dior Quartet for the sweeping romanticism of Ernest Chausson’s magnificent Concerto for violin, piano, and string quartet.","categories":["Cultural","Live Performances","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"-R-VR_Pnt2_55m_Vn4TLWg","website":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/duo-concertante-dior-quartet","tickets":"https://musictorontoconcerts.com/2026-27-concerts/duo-concertante-dior-quartet"},{"id":"a68ec349-c09e-4436-9641-326352b0bc95","name":"Double Down with Maria and Deanne at Market Gallery","dates":[1792789200000],"start":"2026-10-23T17:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-23T17:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Market Gallery","address":"95 Front St E, Toronto","lat":43.649145,"lng":-79.371526},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Maria Hupfield invites champion fancy shawl Pow Wow dancer and boxing trained athlete Deanne Hupfield to bring discipline, skill and beauty to her wearable sculpture titled Double Punch (North) 2024, currently on display at Market Gallery. The two performers meet at the intersection of creative expression and recreation through movement and sound for this live engagement. \n\nDeanne first activated Maria's artwork Jingle Spiral (2015), in the two channel video commission One Who Keeps on Giving in 2017 for Maria’s first major solo exhibition of the same name at The Power Plant Contemporary Art Gallery in Toronto.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Dance","Museum"],"presenter":"TD Bank Group","image":"3ou0p0CZhpnh7P_fdr6DiA","website":"http://toronto.ca/marketgallery","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/217b5ccd-9fcf-4b05-b19b-c426ad05ad5c"},{"id":"ad3605c2-f428-4436-8ba5-f917f71ccfd6","name":"ProFusion Expo 2026","dates":[1794412800000,1794495600000],"start":"2026-11-11T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-12T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 2W6 - Hall B","lat":43.644049656,"lng":-79.386720757},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Canada’s biggest celebration of photo, video, filmmaking, and creator culture. This is where the imaging industry comes to see what’s next!\n\nFor two unforgettable days, enthusiasts, brands and industry leaders come together for hands-on access to the latest innovations in an immersive, creator-first environment.\n\nMore than a trade show, ProFusion is a live experience built for today’s creator culture.\n\n","categories":["Consumer Show/Convention","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":"fRndbzbFQ0_wdGuLSSkuvQ","website":"https://profusionexpo.com/","tickets":"https://profusionexpo.com"},{"id":"0d2a50a9-b916-4c49-b2b3-4a765d0c85a4","name":"ProFusion Expo 2026","dates":[1794412800000,1794495600000],"start":"2026-11-11T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2026-11-12T10:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front St W, Toronto, ON, M5V 2W6 - Hall B","lat":43.644049656,"lng":-79.386720757},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Canada’s biggest celebration of photo, video, filmmaking, and creator culture. This is where the imaging industry comes to see what’s next!\n\nFor two unforgettable days, enthusiasts, brands and industry leaders come together for hands-on access to the latest innovations in an immersive, creator-first environment.\n\nMore than a trade show, ProFusion is a live experience built for today’s creator culture.\n\n","categories":["Consumer Show/Convention","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":"fRndbzbFQ0_wdGuLSSkuvQ","website":"https://pr