04800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"f6cab62d-42c1-499c-b978-3ff0d3dfcb25","name":"Agency & Defiance: Exhibit at Montgomery's Inn","dates":[1793980800000,1794067200000,1794153600000,1794412800000,1794499200000,1794585600000,1794672000000,1794758400000,1795017600000,1795104000000,1795190400000,1795276800000,1795363200000,1795622400000,1795708800000,1795795200000,1795881600000,1795968000000,1796227200000,1796313600000,1796400000000,1796486400000,1796572800000,1796832000000,1796918400000,1797004800000,1797091200000,1797177600000,1797436800000,1797523200000,1797609600000,1797696000000,1797782400000,1798041600000,1798128000000,1798214400000,1798300800000,1798387200000,1798646400000,1798732800000,1798819200000,1798905600000,1798992000000,1799251200000,1799337600000,1799424000000,1799510400000,1799596800000,1799856000000,1799942400000,1800028800000,1800115200000,1800201600000,1800460800000,1800547200000,1800633600000,1800720000000,1800806400000,1801065600000,1801152000000,1801238400000,1801324800000,1801411200000,1801670400000,1801756800000,1801843200000,1801929600000,1802016000000,1802275200000,1802361600000,1802448000000,1802534400000,1802620800000,1802880000000,1802966400000,1803052800000,1803139200000,1803225600000,1803484800000,1803571200000,1803657600000,1803744000000,1803830400000],"start":"2026-11-06T11:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-02-28T11:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Montgomery's Inn","address":"4709 Dundas St W, Etobicoke, ON, M9A 1A8","lat":43.651679,"lng":-79.525659},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Experience Agency and Defiance, featuring never-before-seen works by Toronto-based artist Frantz Brent-Harris inspired by Jamaican Junkanoo. Through these figures, the artist shares the enduring legacy of agency, defiance, resilience, joy, love, and cultural expression that sustained enslaved peoples and their descendants, even under inhumane conditions. ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","History","Museum","Black History Month"],"presenter":null,"image":"qZyjxxbPBbXkbmhYN7I9Sg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/montgomerysinn","tickets":null},{"id":"8874b0e0-bcff-425f-8fbc-50d2c3f71161","name":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit","dates":[1790791200000,1790877600000,1790949600000,1791036000000],"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Metro Toronto Convention Centre","address":"255 Front Street West, Toronto, ON M5V 2W6","lat":43.64392037329108,"lng":-79.38668733673923},"free":false,"low":275,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Local Delegate – All 4 Days: CA$275.00 (With discount code CA$137.50), Local Delegate – Day 3 Only: CA$140.00 (with code CA$70.00), Local Delegate – Day 4 Only: CA$200.00 (with discount code CA$100.00), Student Admission (Valid Student ID Required): CA$70.00 Marketplace Vendor: CA$250.00 (with discount code CA$125.00), They can use the discount code 2026FOA they can enjoy 50% off expires Sep 12.","description":"Friends of Africa 2026 - African Economic Summit is a four-day hybrid conference, taking place virtually on September 30 - October 1, 2026, and in person on October 2-3, 2026 at the Metro Toronto Convention Centre in Toronto, Ontario. The Summit brings together entrepreneurs, startups, investors, business leaders, and ecosystem partners from Canada and Africa. It features expert panels, workshops, startup pitches, networking, business matchmaking, and a career fair, creating opportunities for investment, partnerships, entrepreneurship, and Canada - Africa economic collaboration.","categories":["Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":"Friends of Africa Coalition","image":"XOz0W9bL3jJbnbVI5aIgTg","website":"https://friendsofafrica.ca/","tickets":"https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/16th-african-economic-summit-friends-of-africa-2026-tickets-1803110374669?discount=2026FOA"},{"id":"30f983b5-8088-43ca-bc19-ae9cb653bee8","name":"By the Lake Book Club – 3-Event Package (2027)","dates":[1820962800000],"start":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-09-14T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":55,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nEnjoy the final three By the Lake Book Club events of 2027 for just $55. Join Humber Polytechnic alumni as they dive into conversation with leading Canadian authors. This package features Tyler Pennock, Gillian Deacon and Carrianne Leung. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. \n\nThe signature series features six Tuesday-night events, between February and December. Each event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation.\n\nTyler Pennock - September 14, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nGillian Deacon - October 5, 2027 at 7 p.m.\nCarrianne Leung - December 7, 2027 at 7 p.m.\n\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":null,"website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#multipacks/f89d2f6f-5509-40a1-b58c-a5d199cbe683"},{"id":"4a44a800-cae2-4b11-8133-d1572f99db40","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"0cf22890-44a9-4281-9b1c-cbd7e86742de","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth 