inians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"c35bba5d-53c8-4118-8d69-da3449bfad78","name":"Rebellion Talks: Mackenzie's Unlikely Montreal Allies","dates":[1804359600000],"start":"2027-03-06T14:00:00-05:00","end":"2027-03-06T14:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Learn about the rebellion in Lower Canada (Québec) and its connection to the Rebellion of 1837 in Toronto. The rebellion in Toronto wasn't the only one. At the same time revolutionaries were taking up arms here, an even bigger rebellion was breaking out in Lower Canada. Meet the Lower Canadian rebels and learn about Mackenzie's relationship with them. Join the conversation at Colborne Lodge, the historic home in High Park named in honour of the governor those rebels in Québec were trying to overthrow.\n\nFrom October 2026 to April 2027, historian Adam Bunch brings Toronto’s history to life in a series of talks exploring the Upper Canada Rebellion and its lasting impact on the city. From spies and taverns to political reform, rural rebels and the Patriot War, each talk reveals a different story connected to the museum where it takes place.","categories":["History","Museum","Talks"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"7HN-ZAKbhpbHWfR1BNzjBg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/03fae57f-c06d-4655-8879-f4517f89ae22"},{"id":"c5cfc968-5e29-4cef-b192-4ddadf03f9fc","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Recommended for ages 12 and up. Youth 12-16 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAll ticket sales are non-refundable. Tickets are transferable.","description":"Join us for a chilling tour at Colborne Lodge in High Park. Visit the gravesite of John and Jemima Howard. Delve deeply into ideas about death and the afterlife from the 1800s and hear true tales of paranormal activities. Decide for yourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"b163bb49-3d69-43c9-a5c0-7e437ea510d0","name":"Lantern Tours at Colborne Lodge: The Unexplained","dates":[1793143800000,1793145600000,1793149200000,1793230200000,1793232000000,1793235600000,1793316600000,1793318400000,1793322000000,1793403000000,1793404800000,1793408400000],"start":"2026-10-27T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T21:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Colborne Lodge Museum","address":"11 Colborne Lodge Dr, Toronto","lat":43.640347955,"lng":-79.459963485},"free":false,"low":25,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"Recommended for ages 12 and up. Youth 12-16 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAll ticket sales are non-refundable. Tickets are transferable.","description":"Join us for a chilling tour at Colborne Lodge in High Park. Visit the gravesite of John and Jemima Howard. Delve deeply into ideas about death and the afterlife from the 1800s and hear true tales of paranormal activities. Decide for yourself what still lingers in the museum's hidden corners. ","categories":["History","Museum","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"jYeFR8obIPqO2Ysfl0s7ng","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/colborne-lodge/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/d62d8302-c953-40b2-b0b1-11b7e868f2c1"},{"id":"501ad18a-f82a-4890-b0f9-f7097e5c1755","name":"Gibson House 175 Anniversary Celebration","dates":[1792249200000],"start":"2026-10-17T11:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-17T11:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Gibson House Museum","address":"5172 Yonge St, North York, ON, M2N 5P6","lat":43.769686148,"lng":-79.414666941},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Celebrate 175 years through a day of historic demonstrations, hands-on activities, and community gathering. Learn the story of Gibson House from its construction in 1851 to its transformation into a public museum through gallery displays, historic kitchen demonstrations, and engaging interpretation. Enjoy anniversary celebrations featuring cake cutting, ice cream making, family crafts, and activities inspired by the history and traditions of the Gibson family. Join museum staff and community members in celebrating 175 years of local history, memories, and connection.","categories":["Celebrations","History","Museum"],"presenter":"Toronto History Museums","image":"zDzjru010Z8AQpmBs1Lmpw","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/gibson-house-museum/","tickets":null},{"id":"ce68ab84-506b-4328-befd-fa5bce1c8ad8","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nChildren 5 and under visit for free.","description":"Featuring several examples of Palestinian tatreez (embroidery) from the Textile Museum’s collection, most of which will be exhibited for the first time! \n\nRetracing Tatreez highlights what these belongings can tell us about the relationship between Palestinians and their homelands in the twentieth century and beyond.\n\nIn this exhibition, curator Nina Rafique showcases these pieces with restored historical context and invites visitors to re-engage with their ways of storytelling. \n\nIn doing so, Retracing Tatreez highlights what these embroideries can tell us about the unique regional connections between Palestinians and their homelands, as well as the journeys of these objects from the hands of their original creators to today.","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Museum"],"presenter":null,"image":"j37-eBOZLJMeQ8B7zUJpJg","website":"https://textilemuseum.ca/event/retracing-tatreez-palestinian-thobes-through-the-20th-century/","tickets":"https://textilemuseumcanada.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/calendar"},{"id":"883051d4-9c7c-4b4b-ad40-ac84bf97e208","name":"Lantern Tours at Fort York: After Dark","dates":[1792711800000,1792798200000,1792884600000,1793316600000,1793403000000],"start":"2026-10-22T19:30:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-30T19:30:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Fort York National Historic Site","address":"100 Garrison Rd, Toronto, ON, M5V 3K9","lat":43.638491,"lng":-79.40518},"free":false,"low":20,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Hear chilling and eerie tales on a lantern tour of Fort York and its historic surroundings. Learn about a haunted lighthouse and the bloody Battle of York. Explore the military burial ground. Tour the creepy shadows and 200-year-old buildings of Fort York at night and learn of the fort’s history and its many paranormal mysteries.","categories":["History","Museum","Tour","Halloween"],"presenter":null,"image":"G-eno19UG31sj5aKkgxxQg","website":"https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/museums/fort-york-national-historic-site/","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/09cc8903-6509-4ac3-9964-74a070bbb946"},{"id":"d7f710fc-b7d5-4d30-87d1-ec80d573fd3c","name":"Retracing Tatreez: Palestinian Thobes through the Twentieth Century","dates":[1790265600000,1790352000000,1790438400000,1790524800000,1790784000000,1790870400000,1790956800000,1791043200000,1791129600000,1791388800000,1791475200000,1791561600000,1791648000000,1791734400000,1791993600000,1792080000000,1792166400000,1792252800000,1792339200000,1792598400000,1792684800000,1792771200000,1792857600000,1792944000000,1793203200000,1793289600000,1793376000000,1793462400000,1793552400000,1793811600000,1793898000000,1793984400000,1794070800000,1794157200000,1794416400000,1794502800000,1794589200000,1794675600000,1794762000000,1795021200000,1795107600000,1795194000000,1795280400000,1795366800000,1795626000000,1795712400000,1795798800000,1795885200000,1795971600000,1796230800000,1796317200000,1796403600000,1796490000000,1796576400000,1796835600000,1796922000000,1797008400000,1797094800000,1797181200000,1797440400000,1797526800000,1797613200000,1797699600000,1797786000000,1798045200000,1798131600000,1798218000000,1798304400000,1798390800000,1798650000000,1798736400000,1798822800000,1798909200000,1798995600000,1799254800000,1799341200000,1799427600000,1799514000000,1799600400000,1799859600000,1799946000000,1800032400000,1800118800000,1800205200000,1800464400000,1800550800000,1800637200000,1800723600000,1800810000000,1801069200000,1801155600000,1801242000000,1801328400000,1801414800000,1801674000000,1801760400000,1801846800000,1801933200000,1802019600000],"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-02-07T12:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Textile Museum of Canada","address":"55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON, M5G 2H5","lat":43.654578756,"lng":-79.386652476},"free":false,"lo