ree":false,"low":70,"high":105,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"A contemporary opera that combines classical vocals with dark ambient noise and amplified electric guitars. \n\nSet during a fictional wartime blackout, the story follows a rural working-class family attempting to survive amidst military collapse and severe food shortages. The psychological drama explores human resilience, desperation, and moral breakdown when social structures disintegrate.\n\nCritically acclaimed by The New York Times, this breakthrough work from the writing team of composer David T. Little (Soldier Songs, JFK) and Canadian librettist Royce Vavrek (Angel’s Bone, Listen, Quiet) put them on the map. They have since gone on, both together and in collaboration with others, to revolutionize opera in North America.","categories":["Live Performances","Music","Theatre"],"presenter":"Tapestry Opera and Against the Grain Theatre","image":"r3Bej54LjTXdeoVxlHVQ8g","website":"https://tapestryopera.com/performances/dog-days/","tickets":"https://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF000002p2Zh2AI"},{"id":"1a71f3c8-f3ab-4ec1-863e-b03e664f343a","name":"Toronto Coin Expo: Canada's Coin Show","dates":[1792764000000,1792850400000],"start":"2026-10-23T10:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-24T10:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Toronto Reference Library ","address":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON, M4W 2G8","lat":43.671878938,"lng":-79.386669972},"free":false,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":"\nKids 16 and under attend for free. Tickets can be purchased at the door for cash only.","description":"Join us at the Toronto Coin Expo, Canada’s premier coin and banknote show and auction, located in downtown Toronto. \n\nFeaturing over 50 internationally renowned coin and banknote dealers, representing Canada, United States, and the World of collectable currencies. \n\nThis is the place to buy, sell, and appraise your coins, banknotes, tokens, medals, militaria, gold and silver.\n\nYou are sure to find a one-of-a-kind coin or banknote treasures!\n","categories":["Consumer Show/Convention","Seminars/Workshops"],"presenter":null,"image":"9vLYmoiOaoAhcURPQGx8iQ","website":"https://www.torontocoinexpo.ca","tickets":"https://tickets-ca.evvnt.com/events/toronto-coin-expo-canadas-coin-show-10-23-2026"},{"id":"c7cb792e-7e96-4cda-a557-a89090e8cd7b","name":"Places That Stayed: Youth Photography Exhibit","dates":[1792123200000,1792209600000,1792296000000,1792382400000,1792468800000,1792555200000,1792641600000,1792728000000,1792814400000,1792900800000,1792987200000,1793073600000,1793160000000,1793246400000,1793332800000,1793419200000,1793505600000,1793595600000,1793682000000,1793768400000,1793854800000,1793941200000,1794027600000,1794114000000,1794200400000,1794286800000,1794373200000,1794459600000,1794546000000,1794632400000,1794718800000,1794805200000,1794891600000,1794978000000,1795064400000,1795150800000,1795237200000,1795323600000,1795410000000,1795496400000,1795582800000,1795669200000,1795755600000,1795842000000,1795928400000,1796014800000],"start":"2026-10-16T00:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-11-30T00:00:00-05:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"East Scarborough Storefront","address":"4040 Lawrence Ave E, Scarborough, ON, M1E 2R2","lat":43.766003524,"lng":-79.199011833},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Discover Kingston-Galloway-Orton Park (KGO) through the eyes of local youth in this outdoor photography exhibit. Created as part of a youth placemaking and photography project, the exhibit features photographs documenting the places and spaces that make the neighbourhood unique, from familiar gathering spots and busy streets to quiet corners, overlooked landscapes, parks, and community spaces. Installed along the community garden fence at East Scarborough Storefront, the exhibit invites visitors to explore the neighbourhood through the perspectives of local youth and reflect on the places that shape community life.\n\nA City of Toronto Cultural Hotspot SPARK Project.\n","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Cultural","Family/Children"],"presenter":"itsneerby","image":"6qUPh0-04BnPvAhTFhcOaA","website":"https://www.itsneerby.ca/","tickets":null},{"id":"8a92a908-af09-4cca-8d6a-e82ac7ccce2b","name":"A Love Affair with the Unknown by Gillian Deacon – By the Lake Book Club","dates":[1822777200000],"start":"2027-10-05T19:00:00-04:00","end":"2027-10-05T19:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Night Event","venue":{"name":"Assembly Hall","address":"1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr, Etobicoke, ON, M8V 4B6","lat":43.597660441,"lng":-79.515824559},"free":false,"low":10,"high":21,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Presented by: City of Toronto’s Assembly Hall, Humber Polytechnic’s Faculty of Media, Creative Arts and Design\n\nA Love Affair with the Unknown is a personal memoir examining how we navigate uncertainty, loss and transformation. Drawing on her experiences with illness, healing and life-changing challenges, Gillian Deacon, veteran journalist and television/radio host, explores what it means to live with vulnerability while remaining open to possibility, connection and growth. She will discuss lessons learned through periods of upheaval and how embracing the unknown can lead to greater resilience, creativity and meaning.\n\nBy the Lake Book Club offers six Tuesday-night events, between February and December featuring leading Canadian authors in conversation with Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-person event includes a reading, discussion, audience Q&A, book-signing and American sign language interpretation. Virtual events are subtitled live.\n","categories":["Literary","Talks"],"presenter":null,"image":"xOF2hcT4Mkqe17tolrymsg","website":"https://toronto.ca/BookClub","tickets":"https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4e9e6d8b-6a3f-472f-92ec-964c81318da1"},{"id":"4112f5d2-ec74-4c22-9ee4-f2285213a430","name":"Public Pier","dates":[1789768800000,1789837200000,1790373600000,1790442000000,1790978400000,1791046800000],"start":"2026-09-18T18:00:00-04:00","end":"2026-10-03T13:00:00-04:00","allDay":"Day Event","venue":{"name":"Marina Quay West","address":"539 Queens Quay West, Toronto","lat":43.636696,"lng":-79.394687},"free":true,"low":null,"high":null,"pwyc":null,"costNotes":null,"description":"Public Pier is turning Marina Quay West into a day-to-night cultural destination right in Toronto's Waterfront - featuring music, dance, food, public art and immersive nighttime projections\n\nEnjoy day-to-night experiences on the waterfront including food and drink from The Super Yummy Market, local DJs including CYRO Sounds, Introspkt and Nabz, free beginner-friendly dance workshops, and public art including SILO Nights, where each evening the Canada Malting Silos will be illuminated with immersive artworks by local and international artists.\n\n\n ","categories":["Arts/Exhibits","Food/Culinary","Music"],"presenter":null,"image":"c6PLTik8EeSto-SlLgqhKw","website":"https://publicpier.ca/","tickets":null}]